{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition","id":873180,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer - Beast edition.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-24T10:46:26-07:00","id":873180,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer - Beast edition.","content":"This feels like a silly question, but how exactly do you/others access your lair? It talks about giving people access to your lair without you being present, and the &quot;Hold the Door&quot; section talks about your Lair having &quot;entrances&quot; but I don't see any further explanation about how they work. Is the primary way you access your lair by primordial pathways? That seems really weird because when you do that everyone around you gets pulled into your lair, so I don't see how granting permission comes into it. The in game example of how primordial pathways works also implies that you have to leave the current chamber you are in if you want to actually stay in your lair when the pathways closes, which is just strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:58:47-07:00","id":873265,"title":"","content":"Basically the entrance is an area where a chamber was created (or exceptionally similar to it) as those are the places where the Primordial Pathway can be opened. Judging by the fact that Heroes can potentially invade and that the book brings up that the lair can have intruders I would say that other beings can open the pathway or access the lair if the being is able to open portals into other worlds. Hold the door can be interpreted two different ways from that. First granting someone easier access to the lair when they try and open an entrance into it. The more likely one though is making it easier to transition from an open Pathway into one of the actual chambers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:16:46-07:00","id":873885,"title":"","content":"There is also Under the Bed, but that is for the Beast only. And I'm actually not sure where you end up when you use it now that i'm reading it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:24:59-07:00","id":873896,"title":"","content":"I'm going to assume it defaults to the Heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:52:50-07:00","id":873917,"title":"","content":"I suppose that works. Although now I'm thinking, since it says you have access to the Primordial Pathways, maybe you just choose where you go. Anywhere in your Lair. Maybe even anywhere in a shared Lair. It does take more work and the right circumstance to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:50:58-07:00","id":874500,"title":"","content":"If a Hero finds out that Anathema are something that they place on Beasts, do they gain the ability to choose which Anathema they inflict?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T07:32:02-07:00","id":874526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874500#post874500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Hero finds out that Anathema are something that they place on Beasts, do they gain the ability to choose which Anathema they inflict?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it's an instinctual thing. From the Hero's point of view, they don't place an Anathema. They realise that the Beast has a fundamental weakness. I'm not sure. I think that they might <i>try</i> to determine which one gets placed, but I don't know if they would succeed or not. I usually just choose the Anathema which is best for the story that the Beast and Hero have fallen into. Perhaps the hero might learn to manipulate the story so that the Anathema he wants is the one that's most likely to be placed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 09-26-2018, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:35:06-07:00","id":874659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874500#post874500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Hero finds out that Anathema are something that they place on Beasts, do they gain the ability to choose which Anathema they inflict?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Anathema. I mean something like a weak point can easily be justified as having badly injured the Beast there and thus that's a spot to exploit. You might be able to swing some of the mental stuff like burning a collector's hoard causes it to go insane or something. Weaknesses are normally just things the Hero is going to &quot;discover&quot; unless it's pulling weird stuff like &quot;my friend here is a powerful wizard and he has cursed you with a weakness to aluminum foil foul monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that's about as close as a Hero is coming to placing an anathema as a conscious decision. I don't think Heroes would be that big on accepting Anathema as a sort of magic power that they can inflict on Beasts, since that would make them ,and other like them, seem like just a group of people with a convenient magic power. As opposed to how most antagonist Heroes are likely to think of themselves which is &quot;I am so badass I did this to the monster.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:05:09-07:00","id":874923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874526#post874526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think that it's an instinctual thing. From the Hero's point of view, they don't place an Anathema. They realise that the Beast has a fundamental weakness. I'm not sure. I think that they might <i>try</i> to determine which one gets placed, but I don't know if they would succeed or not. i usually just choose the Anathema which is best for the story. perhaps the hero might learn to manipulate the story so that the Anathema he wants is the one that's most likely to be placed.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874659#post874659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Anathema. I mean something like a weak point can easily be justified as having badly injured the Beast there and thus that's a spot to exploit. You might be able to swing some of the mental stuff like burning a collector's hoard causes it to go insane or something. Weaknesses are normally just things the Hero is going to &quot;discover&quot; unless it's pulling weird stuff like &quot;my friend here is a powerful wizard and he has cursed you with a weakness to aluminum foil foul monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that's about as close as a Hero is coming to placing an anathema as a conscious decision. I don't think Heroes would be that big on accepting Anathema as a sort of magic power that they can inflict on Beasts, since that would make them ,and other like them, seem like just a group of people with a convenient magic power. As opposed to how most antagonist Heroes are likely to think of themselves which is &quot;I am so badass I did this to the monster.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I suspected. If a Beast or anyone else said to the Hero that they were placing the weakness instead of discovering it, their inherent stubbornness would eliminate any doubts that might cross their minds. It would be good to have an official answer, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:44:48-07:00","id":874954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874923#post874923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's what I suspected. If a Beast or anyone else said to the Hero that they were placing the weakness instead of discovering it, their inherent stubbornness would eliminate any doubts that might cross their minds. It would be good to have an official answer, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That happens in one of the stories in the fiction anthology. A Beast tries to tell his Hero that she created the weaknesses he was suffering from, and asked why he would live so close to the forest that could kill him.<br /> <br /> She wouldn't believe him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:34:35-07:00","id":878396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874500#post874500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Hero finds out that Anathema are something that they place on Beasts, do they gain the ability to choose which Anathema they inflict?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, Heroes operate under a self-reinforcing delusion that they are the center of the story. Conversely to that delusion, anything that would be more directly attributable to his own action is going to be interpreted as an outside force, be it history, fate, or a god-figure, assuring the righteousness of his course. I imagine that the specifics of Anathema have less to do with the volition of the Hero placing it and more to do with the unconscious biases of the Hero in his interpretation of the powers and habits of the Beast in question, which are born out by whichever processes the Hero uses to place Anathema, be it through the quasi-scientific research of your typical amateur cryptozoologist-styled Hero, the vision-quests and moments of clarity of your Chosen One (tm), or through the panicked anecdotes of your movie-geek-trapped-in-a-slasher-flick. Despite the inherent falsehood of their place in the story, Anathema are generally going to be logically consistent with the first impressions the Hero has of the Beast they're placing the Anathema upon, so more often than not, they fit into a theme rather than just being contrived from whatever is readily at hand. Of course, that's not to stop an ST at higher levels from throwing in a Hero that has just enough self-awareness to know that the resonance a prospective Anathema has with the Beast is not as important as the narrative weight he puts behind it, so such a Hero could do the narrative equivalent of the Sidereal Failure without Fail destiny if that was what the ST wanted to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T04:32:03-07:00","id":878655,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all, I'm going to disagree with everyone else here to start with. While the heroes that Beasts tend to encounter are self-deluded glory seekers, they're not the whole of heroes. I'm also willing to bet that we're going to get a Hunter Conspiracy that effectively turns you into a Hero, much like we have Conspiracies that double as God-Machine cultists, Seer followers, and spirit pawns. Anyways, my point is that while early drafts of the game made heroes into deluded VanHellsing Hate Crime douchy tools, there are a couple of paths that a hero can follow. Some of them are less inclined to kill, and more inclined to other measures, like observing first, or (heaven forbid) actually talking. These more open minded heroes could very well come to understand what they are doing. <i>Especially</i> if they end up on friendly terms with a Beast and sit down to talk about their natures. And, yes, that does happen - social expert Beasts are very good at flipping heroes to the &quot;dark side.&quot; It doesn't take a rocket scientist to realize that a removable and changable weakness has to have a cause.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that there are several ways to place an Anathema. The default is in the middle of combat as part of an attack. A hero can learn a gift to place the weakness through research or through vocally denouncing the Beast (Loremaster and Saint's Whisper). Now, the research method mirrors how one discovers ephemeral being's weaknesses and shred a Demon's cover, so most people with this method aren't likely to realize its creating a weakness instead of discovering it. However, the vocal denouncement? That's very much thematically appropriate for a choice to be made as part of what you're telling the Beast.<br /> <br /> All this is theorycrafting, of course. Chances are this won't come up in play. To be honest, I've had trouble with having PCs actually hang out in the Sated Condition for any reasonable length of time to leave themselves vulnerable enough to be hit with an Anathema, and, frankly, approaching a Beast without an Anathema is suicidal for all but the most tweaked out hero band. But it is theoretically possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:04:19-07:00","id":878733,"title":"","content":"So, when a Beast travels from their lair to the Temenos/Anima Mundi/Onieros via a primordial pathway, do they travel there physically or as a dream form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:21:34-07:00","id":878746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=878733#post878733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when a Beast travels from their lair to the Temenos/Anima Mundi/Onieros via a primordial pathway, do they travel there physically or as a dream form?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Physically, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:57:14-07:00","id":878769,"title":"","content":"No, it's dream form. If they get killed they end up back in their lair with soul-shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T01:11:40-07:00","id":880802,"title":"","content":"In dream form do you loose your skills? That section could use some more clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T01:37:13-07:00","id":880811,"title":"","content":"Why would you? Skills are mental things. They're stuff you know or know how to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T02:51:16-07:00","id":880831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=880811#post880811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you? Skills are mental things. They're stuff you know or know how to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because dream form kind-of uses ephemeral being rules, and they don't have skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:02:05-07:00","id":880834,"title":"","content":"Well, what they have instead is sort of thematic pseudo-skills based on what they're supposed to be good at. <br /> <br /> So what you could do is give a large bonus to rolls for skills the &quot;real&quot; you has at high dots, and a smaller one for those at low dots or untrained. <br /> <br /> Oh, wait. That's what skills do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T10:19:04-07:00","id":881074,"title":"","content":"I thought you physically traveled via primordial pathways. The only times it mentions a dream form is when someone is pulled from a dream into your Lair. Also if you only go there as an Astra projection does that not make you far more vulnerable? You can't just run back to your lair to escape if that was the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T10:32:08-07:00","id":881081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=881074#post881074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if you only go there as an Astra projection does that not make you far more vulnerable? You can't just run back to your lair to escape if that was the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeas you can. Why would being in material form make that any easier?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this has been asked before. that's what the devs said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:31:24-07:00","id":881118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=881081#post881081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeas you can. Why would being in material form make that any easier?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this has been asked before. that's what the devs said.</div> </div> </div> </div>The I guess my question is this: if you do not physically travel to your lair and are instead in a dream form what is the point of primordial pathways? It allows you to travel to other realms and places on earth but you need to go from place to lair to other place rather than just from a to b. By that you could only travel with a dream body to these places and not your real form as my reading of primordial pathways suggests.<br /> <br /> Edit: dream form Pg 99, &quot;At any given time, some visitors to a Beast\u2019s Lair may be physically present or in a dream state, depending on exactly how they gained access....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-03-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:01:31-07:00","id":881193,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's how it works. You're in the material. You <i>are </i>material. You want to go to the astral. You open a pathway into your lair and merge with your horror. Then you open another pathway to the astral and un-merge, but since you're in the astral now you're in dream form and use dream stats. If you then want to go somewhere else, say, the hedge, you go back to your lair, re-merge, open another pathway, un-merge and now you're in the hedge. You're material again because you're <i>not in the astral. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:00:09-07:00","id":881363,"title":"","content":"I realize the reason of our disagreement was in part because I was wrong and because I didn't clarify what aspect I was focusing on.<br /> <br /> I missed that blurb about a beast fusing with their horror on entering their lair, I concede you were right there. I must have missed the blurb because I was skimming. I miss interpretated what you saying that the beast would remain physically where they entered the lair.<br /> <br /> The part I was meaning to focus on but not clear enough in comunicating was how not all being brought into the lair would use dream like stats. Like a vampire brought with a beast via primordial pathways would indeed be physical, hence the section I quoted.<br /> <br /> Thank you however for pointing out where I was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:15:18-07:00","id":881441,"title":"","content":"How come Iron Skin is cheaper in the Beast Corebook than in the Chronicles of Darkness Corebook? Is it a discount for Beasts so as to balance it accordingly with the other stuff they can get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:02:46-07:00","id":881464,"title":"","content":"More likely it's an error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:38:21-07:00","id":889265,"title":"","content":"Can a beast recognize minor templates? I'm specifically thinking about wolf blooded. Maybe its like with Mages and psychics, where its easier to tell if they've used their powers in the scene. That being said, some of the tells are always on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:52:35-07:00","id":889374,"title":"","content":"Dont have the page ref at the moment but quote from the book in t<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">he section on Family Resemblance:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Individuals who are fundamentally human but still wield supernatural power are harder to detect. If the individual has not used any supernatural abilities in the same scene as the Beast encountered him, subtract his Integrity rating from the roll as well as Composure.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> I don't know the wolfblooded tells well, but if they are always on, id say they count as having been used.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:31:09-07:00","id":894041,"title":"","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I don't know if this has been answered before, but I'm not sure what to do when creating my Beast character and the book tells me to select Kinship. Doesn't all Kinship power work on any supernatural creature? Do I have to choose? Why is there a blank space for Kinship in the character sheet? It seems like I'm missing something obvious here, but I'm still halfway through my first reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:42:24-07:00","id":894052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=894041#post894041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> I don't know if this has been answered before, but I'm not sure what to do when creating my Beast character and the book tells me to select Kinship. Doesn't all Kinship power work on any supernatural creature? Do I have to choose? Why is there a blank space for Kinship in the character sheet? It seems like I'm missing something obvious here, but I'm still halfway through my first reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, Kinship works on any supernatural creature (even psychics, thaumaturges etc). Before selecting Kinship though, you should have a setting ready with characters to choose from or choose one with little connection to the overarching workings of the setting, for example choosing a fairly generic fire spirit or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:22:13-07:00","id":894083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=894041#post894041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi!<br /> <br /> I don't know if this has been answered before, but I'm not sure what to do when creating my Beast character and the book tells me to select Kinship. Doesn't all Kinship power work on any supernatural creature? Do I have to choose? Why is there a blank space for Kinship in the character sheet? It seems like I'm missing something obvious here, but I'm still halfway through my first reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you be more specific as to what you are referring to in the text? My character sheets don't have a Kinship section. The 4 page sheet has a Kinship Nightmares section.<br /> <br /> There is one of the starting Satiety questions about whether or not you have any particular Kinship with some supernaturals already that would affect your Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:28:34-07:00","id":894146,"title":"","content":"There's a Condition which you apply to any beings with which you have Kinship on page 87 called Family Ties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:40:27-07:00","id":894328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=894083#post894083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you be more specific as to what you are referring to in the text? My character sheets don't have a Kinship section. The 4 page sheet has a Kinship Nightmares section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I bought my PDF from DriveThru and it didn't include a character sheet, so I downloaded one from MrGone site: <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/BtP/BtP_1-Page_Official.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...e_Official.pdf</a><br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sorry, I thought it said &quot;Kinship&quot; but is &quot;Family Ties&quot; instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":". 05-19-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:31:14-07:00","id":894365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=894328#post894328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I bought my PDF from DriveThru and it didn't include a character sheet, so I downloaded one from MrGone site: <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/BtP/BtP_1-Page_Official.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...e_Official.pdf</a><br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sorry, I thought it said &quot;Kinship&quot; but is &quot;Family Ties&quot; instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right, that makes sense. Family Ties is a kinship related condition you put on specific supernaturals (not type, but indivuduals) that gives both you and the target benefits.<br /> <br /> You would list the indiviudauls you have Family ties with here, they are who you can use Family Dinner and Mother's Blood on and generate Kinship Nightmares from ( there is some others too but I can't think of them off the top of my head)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  More Info 05-19-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:07:52-07:00","id":894386,"title":"","content":"Oh, now that makes sense. I misread something and it snowballed in my head. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:47:50-07:00","id":897983,"title":"","content":"I feel like a crazy person for not being able to find this:<br /> <br /> What creates a Hero, mechanically? Isn't there a roll the Beast does that sparks a Hero, or something? I cannot for the life of me find it in the book, and it is driving me insane, because I was SURE there was something like exceptional success on something or a dramatic failure on something made a Hero. Help please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:52:04-07:00","id":898044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=897983#post897983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a crazy person for not being able to find this:<br /> <br /> What creates a Hero, mechanically? Isn't there a roll the Beast does that sparks a Hero, or something? I cannot for the life of me find it in the book, and it is driving me insane, because I was SURE there was something like exceptional success on something or a dramatic failure on something made a Hero. Help please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember exactly what creates a Hero, but a Dramatic Failure or Exceptional Success on a Feeding roll allows Heroes to pick up a Beast's 'scent' and I have a feeling the rules for Hero creation are somewhere around there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T20:11:18-07:00","id":898539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=897983#post897983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a crazy person for not being able to find this:<br /> <br /> What creates a Hero, mechanically? Isn't there a roll the Beast does that sparks a Hero, or something? I cannot for the life of me find it in the book, and it is driving me insane, because I was SURE there was something like exceptional success on something or a dramatic failure on something made a Hero. Help please.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of the first draft. The final version has Heroes serve as a tangentially related phenomenon to Beasts in terms of their dreams having always touched the Primordial Dream at a broad and shallow level; the Heroes that usually hunt Beasts and gain Gifts are the ones who've lost enough of their independent self-concept to hit Integrity 4 and under.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T21:33:05-07:00","id":898606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=898539#post898539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of the first draft. The final version has Heroes serve as a tangentially related phenomenon to Beasts in terms of their dreams having always touched the Primordial Dream at a broad and shallow level; the Heroes that usually hunt Beasts and gain Gifts are the ones who've lost enough of their independent self-concept to hit Integrity 4 and under.</div> </div> </div> </div>AHA! Thank you very much! Time to go dig up the old draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:15:56-07:00","id":905486,"title":"","content":"What happens to imposed lair traits if the original trait which rendered the location resonant is removed? For example if an Ugallu triggers a fire alarm and then uses the resulting downpour from the sprinkler system to impose Thin Air on the room, does this trait disappear once the sprinkler system is turned off, or remain for the rest of the scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T04:09:00-07:00","id":906315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=905486#post905486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to imposed lair traits if the original trait which rendered the location resonant is removed? For example if an Ugallu triggers a fire alarm and then uses the resulting downpour from the sprinkler system to impose Thin Air on the room, does this trait disappear once the sprinkler system is turned off, or remain for the rest of the scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would remain for the scene. The resonant trait is required to impose - once that's done, there's nothing implying the other trait fades when the resonant one does. In fact, you have have high enough Lair, you could then use the presence of Thin Air to manifest Downpour again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:32:54-07:00","id":906535,"title":"","content":"The satiety expenditure affect of Unbreakable states that <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">His armor (still 4/3) <b>applies to aggravated</b><br /> <b>damage attacks</b>.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Is this a typo? my understanding is that applying to aggravated damage is the default behavior of armor unless otherwise stated. If unbreakable is intended to not normally apply to agg then this is a weird way to say so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:13:09-07:00","id":906619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906535#post906535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The satiety expenditure affect of Unbreakable states that<br /> Is this a typo? my understanding is that applying to aggravated damage is the default behavior of armor unless otherwise stated. If unbreakable is intended to not normally apply to agg then this is a weird way to say so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many forms of aggravated damage ignore mundane armor as part of their being so intensely disruptive to solid matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:03:04-07:00","id":906691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906619#post906619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many forms of aggravated damage ignore mundane armor as part of their being so intensely disruptive to solid matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then shouldn't this say that it applies to aggravated damage affects that would normally bypass armor? It seems to worded awkwardly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:21:14-07:00","id":906706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906691#post906691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then shouldn't this say that it applies to aggravated damage affects that would normally bypass armor? It seems to worded awkwardly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me answer this question with another question:<br /> <br /> Why would you expect aggravated damage to be subject to Armor but not Durability, particularly in a Second Edition gameline where the difference between those two qualities is not as great as it was in First Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:29:48-07:00","id":906713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906706#post906706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me answer this question with another question:<br /> <br /> Why would you expect aggravated damage to be subject to Armor but not Durability, particularly in a Second Edition gameline where the difference between those two qualities is not as great as it was in First Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of this post by Dave on 4chan. <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47059905/#47061173\" target=\"_blank\">http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47059905/#47061173</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:41:19-07:00","id":906720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906713#post906713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of this post by Dave on 4chan. <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47059905/#47061173\" target=\"_blank\">http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47059905/#47061173</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Given that that link brings me to an error page and nothing realistically stops you from transcribing the relevant exchange yourself I find this response uncompelling.<br /> <br /> Further notes: Ballistic armor makes specific note that it downgrades lethal damage to bashing damage and makes no mention of aggravated damage; Unbreakable explicitly stacks with Armor from the Iron Skin Merit chain, Iron Skin begins its progression with Armor that only applies to bashing damage; and even the Epic level of that Merit doesn't frame its effects on aggravated damage as an Armor rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:52:38-07:00","id":906729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906720#post906720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that that link brings me to an error page and nothing realistically stops you from transcribing the relevant exchange yourself I find this response uncompelling.<br /> <br /> Further notes: Ballistic armor makes specific note that it downgrades lethal damage to bashing damage and makes no mention of aggravated damage; Unbreakable explicitly stacks with Armor from the Iron Skin Merit chain, Iron Skin begins its progression with Armor that only applies to bashing damage; and even the Epic level of that Merit doesn't frame its effects on aggravated damage as an Armor rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I don't have a transcript so until 4plebs comes back up you'll have to take my word for it. The jist is that aggravated doesn't explicitly bypass armor it's just that several sources of it do, either explicitly so or by bypassing the combat rules altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:19:42-07:00","id":906747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=906720#post906720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that that link brings me to an error page and nothing realistically stops you from transcribing the relevant exchange yourself I find this response uncompelling.<br /> <br /> Further notes: Ballistic armor makes specific note that it downgrades lethal damage to bashing damage and makes no mention of aggravated damage; Unbreakable explicitly stacks with Armor from the Iron Skin Merit chain, Iron Skin begins its progression with Armor that only applies to bashing damage; and even the Epic level of that Merit doesn't frame its effects on aggravated damage as an Armor rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was able to find it in another archive. <a href=\"https://warosu.org/tg/thread/S47059905#p47061173\" target=\"_blank\">https://warosu.org/tg/thread/S47059905#p47061173</a><br /> <br /> Here's a transcript: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &gt;&gt;47060909<br /> Because it's not true. General Armour works against aggravated damage. As &gt;&gt;47061096<br /> says, it's just that many forms of aggravated damage bypass the combat system entirely. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","user":"cmwatford","date":". 06-03-2016, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T18:59:21-07:00","id":912570,"title":"","content":"How do Heroes avoid getting arrested for killing so much? As far as I know, Beasts can easily be marginalized members of society that few would miss, but even then, a serial killer spouting nonsense and hate would draw the attention of the media.<br /> <br /> Beasts run into this problem too, but they can hide evidence of crimes inside their Lairs, silence people with Nightmares and escape prison with Atavisms. Their supernatural allies can also pull strings to divert the attention of local authorities. Isn't it harder for Heroes to gain the trust of supernaturals that might do the same favor for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-11-2016, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T01:04:40-07:00","id":912687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=912570#post912570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Heroes avoid getting arrested for killing so much? As far as I know, Beasts can easily be marginalized members of society that few would miss, but even then, a serial killer spouting nonsense and hate would draw the attention of the media.</div> </div> </div> </div> Step the first. Do not get caught killing the monsters. Even if these things are clearly horrific abominations against reality itself. The rest of the world is not blessed with your clear superiority that enables you to see the truth, maybe you can convince them of the truth, but it is going to be a pain and it'll be a lot easier just to not get caught. Second, not every Hero has a high body count. No tracking a serial killer if all you've got is one tragic shooting in an alley.There is also the mention of Heroes occasionally gaining a boon that allows them to sway others to their cause. The last is the same as others get someone else to help you with the clean up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=912570#post912570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts run into this problem too, but they can hide evidence of crimes inside their Lairs, silence people with Nightmares and escape prison with Atavisms. Their supernatural allies can also pull strings to divert the attention of local authorities. Isn't it harder for Heroes to gain the trust of supernaturals that might do the same favor for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a Hero does lack the benefits that make it easier for a Beast to find and potentially make friends with other monster splats that is true. However, that isn't to say a Hero might lack methods of covering their tracks. Hunters may not like working with Heroes, but if they know the local vampire group has acquired a powerful new protector then having something able to deal with it is useful. More so a Hero can track Beasts, so anyone who wants to kill a Beast would have cause to throw in with the Hero. (Though that doesn't garuantee the Hero's survival and the dead man does fall down a few rungs on the suspect list.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T11:34:55-07:00","id":912886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=912687#post912687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the mention of Heroes occasionally gaining a boon that allows them to sway others to their cause. The last is the same as others get someone else to help you with the clean up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even &quot;occasionally&quot; anymore \u2014 the True King Gift got replaced with Real World because it got changed into the basis for an innate ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:57:43-07:00","id":913866,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know much about this game, or NWoD in general, but I have a simple question upon which my desire to purchase this book will be based. Can I make a dragon? It doesn't need to be a giant menace that can eat the country side. Just a hatchling, as small as a cat is fine (larger is okay as well).<br /> The general dragony qualities are a must: claws, teeth, a breath weapon, armored scales, and the ability to fly.<br /> Is this possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T22:06:01-07:00","id":913869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=913866#post913866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know much about this game, or NWoD in general, but I have a simple question upon which my desire to purchase this book will be based. Can I make a dragon? It doesn't need to be a giant menace that can eat the country side. Just a hatchling, as small as a cat is fine (larger is okay as well).<br /> The general dragony qualities are a must: claws, teeth, a breath weapon, armored scales, and the ability to fly.<br /> Is this possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory and/or rumor serves correctly, this game was originally going to be about dragons, so yes, absolutely.<br /> <br /> It may take a bit to get the entire set of draconic qualities as a whole, but you can get half of them at character creation and pick up the rest in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T02:10:42-07:00","id":913960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=913866#post913866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know much about this game, or NWoD in general, but I have a simple question upon which my desire to purchase this book will be based. Can I make a dragon? It doesn't need to be a giant menace that can eat the country side. Just a hatchling, as small as a cat is fine (larger is okay as well).<br /> The general dragony qualities are a must: claws, teeth, a breath weapon, armored scales, and the ability to fly.<br /> Is this possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. You can make a character that looks human with a dragon's soul, who can manifest (more or less) all those powers you want. They can even have dragon got within their Lair. <br /> <br /> What you can't have is a small draconid wandering around as it pleases in the physical realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T06:24:19-07:00","id":914051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=913866#post913866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know much about this game, or NWoD in general, but I have a simple question upon which my desire to purchase this book will be based. Can I make a dragon? It doesn't need to be a giant menace that can eat the country side. Just a hatchling, as small as a cat is fine (larger is okay as well).<br /> The general dragony qualities are a must: claws, teeth, a breath weapon, armored scales, and the ability to fly.<br /> Is this possible?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=913960#post913960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no. You can make a character that looks human with a dragon's soul, who can manifest (more or less) all those powers you want. They can even have dragon got within their Lair.<br /> <br /> What you can't have is a small draconid wandering around as it pleases in the physical realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though you could pick a suitably ubiquitous Lair Trait and impose your Lair on reality frequently. That would be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T07:44:12-07:00","id":914086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=914051#post914051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Though you could pick a suitably ubiquitous Lair Trait and impose your Lair on reality frequently. That would be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor Lighting is great for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:16:29-07:00","id":914572,"title":"","content":"Does the horror use dream form rules or ephemeral entity rules? IE: attacks -power+finesse or power+brawl and health -resistance+size or resistance+5?<br /> <br /> How does astral travel interact with the lair? Dave's short in Primordial Feast suggests anyone can travel to and from a chamber as if it were any other Temenos realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:33:09-07:00","id":955413,"title":"","content":"Is there a way for a beast to take the form of another person, mimicking their voice and appearance? Sort of like Envy from full metal alchemist? I thought I saw it but can't find it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:04:16-07:00","id":955431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=955413#post955413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way for a beast to take the form of another person, mimicking their voice and appearance? Sort of like Envy from full metal alchemist? I thought I saw it but can't find it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vocal mimicry is one of the basic effects of Siren's Treacherous Song, but looking like other people is outside the scope of the Atavisms presently available to us unless you get very permissive with From The Shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T01:41:07-07:00","id":955477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=955413#post955413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way for a beast to take the form of another person, mimicking their voice and appearance? Sort of like Envy from full metal alchemist? I thought I saw it but can't find it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I know of in the core book, but I wrote an atavism to do that a while back for the Other Atavism Ideas? thread. Here's a link.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Q_-MIErjfZQ5qpDUL1LnnpPffJ72UMlF6H-kBt-s53Y\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Q_-MIErjfZQ5qpDUL1LnnpPffJ72UMlF6H-kBt-s53Y\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Q_-MIErjfZQ5qpDUL1LnnpPffJ72UMlF6H-kBt-s53Y\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Q_-MIErjfZQ5qpDUL1LnnpPffJ72UMlF6H-kBt-s53Y </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:57:44-07:00","id":955763,"title":"","content":"Someone MAY have asked this already, and if they have I apologize but my question is this: If you have a Kinship, can you remove it and create a new Kinship? I know as a storyteller I can make that available, but if I'd like to make sure I do it inside the bounds of the rules (if possible) or at least consider the metaphysical ramifications of doing so in a way that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:34:38-07:00","id":955797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=955763#post955763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone MAY have asked this already, and if they have I apologize but my question is this: If you have a Kinship, can you remove it and create a new Kinship? I know as a storyteller I can make that available, but if I'd like to make sure I do it inside the bounds of the rules (if possible) or at least consider the metaphysical ramifications of doing so in a way that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not limited to a single Kinship or even type of kinship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:32:24-07:00","id":955849,"title":"","content":"Exactly the answer I was looking for, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T02:03:04-07:00","id":958647,"title":"","content":"So with reading about Beast I saw horrors can occasionally go out and drag people into the lair, my question is when there in dream state can they still use powers, say a mage in dream has access to spells? Or does a sleeping werewolf have access to gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T04:43:38-07:00","id":958689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chaos965</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=958647#post958647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with reading about Beast I saw horrors can occasionally go out and drag people into the lair, my question is when there in dream state can they still use powers, say a mage in dream has access to spells? Or does a sleeping werewolf have access to gifts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that, given that the manifestation of the self in the Astral is based on self-image, they would have access to their powers if they saw them as a part of themselves. So a an elder mage or a veteran werewolf probably would, while one who's just undergone his Awakening or First Change probably wouldn't or would have their powers dampened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:05:58-07:00","id":958937,"title":"","content":"The Horror doesn't go after supernats, only mortals are subject to that particular effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T18:00:25-07:00","id":958984,"title":"","content":"Ty also another question, do Beasts get a bonus attribute point like other supernaturals or do they jsut have standard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T18:19:36-07:00","id":958996,"title":"","content":"Beasts get a bonus dot of occult. Not all supernats get a bonus attribute by default. Vampires do, Mages do, Changelings don't (though their kith might give them one), As far as memory serves Werewolves and Sin Eaters don't, although I've only skimmed those books so don't quote me there. I've yet to look at Mummy, Demon, or Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:44:06-07:00","id":959035,"title":"","content":"Ty again Helms, you are so far ive seen the most knowledgeable about beast. So another question when trying to impose tilts on the enviroment fro myour lair is it the same role if you were to open a pathway or is it a different pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:51:32-07:00","id":959037,"title":"","content":"There's no roll to impose Lair Traits, it succeeds automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:08:44-07:00","id":959041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=959037#post959037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no roll to impose Lair Traits, it succeeds automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Wits + Resolve with Chamber resonance penalties if you're instantiating them from nothing instead of daisy-chaining off of an existing phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T00:51:23-07:00","id":959141,"title":"","content":"New question, Can a beast on there own accord drag a dreamer into there Lair or is that only for the horror when hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:09:01-07:00","id":960189,"title":"","content":"Could you clarify a bit please. Do you mean like when your Horror goes and attacks someone else's dream self and drags it into a nightmare to feed, or do you mean like doing a lair merge with an area and just making it so the person leaves the Pathway and enters the Lair proper?<br /> <br /> <br /> My own question. I recall something about a merit that suspended your satiety decrease so long as you're working on a thing for feeding. Does anyone recall the merit I'm talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:10:36-07:00","id":960629,"title":"","content":"You might be thinking of the Low Satiety effect of Relentless Hunter, which suspends your need to eat or sleep as long as you're actively pursuing Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:24:06-07:00","id":960857,"title":"","content":"I was meaning about how the Horror goes out if on low satiety and attacks a persons dreams, and on excep can bring them to lair, I was just checking if that was horror exclusive and you answered question","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T00:32:16-07:00","id":960933,"title":"","content":"Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Does every chamber of your lair have the same traits?<br /> <br /> 2. Does a chamber have to resemble the place it was formed at? The lair examples all seem nice and fantastic and not very similar to any real world location","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12358-cat-of-many-faces","name":"Cat of Many Faces","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12358_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T00:38:56-07:00","id":960936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cat of Many Faces</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=960933#post960933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does every chamber of your lair have the same traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Chamber can have any or none of your Lair Traits present in it at any given time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Does a chamber have to resemble the place it was formed at? The lair examples all seem nice and fantastic and not very similar to any real world location </div> </div> </div>The conceptual location, at least, should match \u2014 a Chamber formed in an abandoned shopping mall is going to be recognizably a shopping mall in some fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:52:21-07:00","id":961074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cat of Many Faces</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=960933#post960933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Does every chamber of your lair have the same traits?<br /> <br /> 2. Does a chamber have to resemble the place it was formed at? The lair examples all seem nice and fantastic and not very similar to any real world location</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, I'd say that it would resemble the real world location as viewed through the lens of a nightmare. Depending on Lair Traits, it may differ even more. For example, my character has a small abandoned cemetery as a Chamber, with the Maze and Mirages Traits. The result is what seems to be a larger, eternally shifting cemetery with obvious signs of active haunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:21:30-07:00","id":961106,"title":"","content":"I can't find a rule on it anywhere s I have to ask, what happens when Beasts sleep? Do they go immediately to the Primordial Dream and merge with their Horrors? Do they not need sleep? Does visiting the Primordial Dream count as sleep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:35:32-07:00","id":961111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961106#post961106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find a rule on it anywhere s I have to ask, what happens when Beasts sleep? Do they go immediately to the Primordial Dream and merge with their Horrors? Do they not need sleep? Does visiting the Primordial Dream count as sleep?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, they can choose not to possess their Horrors when they sleep, although if they do not they simply sleep dreamlessly, they need sleep (as implied by Relentless Hunter counteracting that need partially) and visiting the Primordial Dream does not count as sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:47:03-07:00","id":961115,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I love Beast, but it's rules are not the clearest out of the game line.<br /> <br /> One more question, is there really no other way to get out of your Lair other then rolling? It would be horrible if a player got stuck in their lair, not able to interact with anything cause they can't get out, especially if they only have a heart and thus no direct location in any other world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:46:07-07:00","id":961140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961115#post961115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, I love Beast, but it's rules are not the clearest out of the game line.<br /> <br /> One more question, is there really no other way to get out of your Lair other then rolling? It would be horrible if a player got stuck in their lair, not able to interact with anything cause they can't get out, especially if they only have a heart and thus no direct location in any other world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too true <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Do you mean physically or mentally? If physically, I think they have to roll if they want to get out, but to make it easier you could open a Pathway into the Temenos close to the surface and just make your way out that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:48:53-07:00","id":961142,"title":"","content":"A question of my own: Can Beasts make Chambers out of parts of supernatural realms, like a Dead Domain in the Underworld or a Hollow in the Hedge? More importantly, can you do it in an Astral Realm like the Temenos, the Anima Mundi or even another part of the Dark Dream (perhaps the Lair of another Beast...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:55:11-07:00","id":961145,"title":"","content":"Physically. I think I'm gonna house-rule that, though, especially in a game I don't want to cross with Mage. It seems silly for a non-mage crossover to have the Temenos the best way out of the lair. Thanks a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:04:48-07:00","id":961147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961142#post961142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question of my own: Can Beasts make Chambers out of parts of supernatural realms, like a Dead Domain in the Underworld or a Hollow in the Hedge? More importantly, can you do it in an Astral Realm like the Temenos, the Anima Mundi or even another part of the Dark Dream (perhaps the Lair of another Beast...)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a sidebar specifically covering this. The answer is yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:05:57-07:00","id":961150,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961142#post961142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question of my own: Can Beasts make Chambers out of parts of supernatural realms, like a Dead Domain in the Underworld or a Hollow in the Hedge? More importantly, can you do it in an Astral Realm like the Temenos, the Anima Mundi or even another part of the Dark Dream (perhaps the Lair of another Beast...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can! It has to still fall by the usual rules which makes some places harder. Sin Eater's/Werewolves losing their &quot;integrity&quot; trait doesn't allow you to create a new chamber so the only option for Underworld/Spirit world is to either take a different supernatural there/bring a human/ or get an exceptional success. Of course a really unstable Mage buddy could suit all those needs, but that isn't too likely. I don't think other Primordial places count since they themselves are based on places, but it outright says Underworld/Hedge/ and astral Realms are good as they can connect to the Primordial Dream. In my book it is on pg 96 under &quot;Unusual Sources of Inspiration&quot; in a side bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:17:20-07:00","id":961300,"title":"","content":"When do the victims of You Can Nevver Rest roll to stay conscious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:44:44-07:00","id":961308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961300#post961300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When do the victims of You Can Nevver Rest roll to stay conscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say shortly after it's triggered considering it wouldn't be that surprising for the target to suddenly find themselves not having slept in at least 72 hours if hit with the high satiety version of the nightmare. <br /> <br /> For the normal or after a success at staying away the fatigue condition says it's stamina+resolve every 6 hours with an additional cumulative -1 to all dice pools (including staying awake) until the subject has actually slept for 8 hours plus an additional hour for every six hours over they've accumulated. Additional notes heavy activity can change the modifier to a -2 or 3 and normal humans can't stay awake more days than the lower of resolve or stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:56:54-07:00","id":961312,"title":"","content":"It's the Normal Satiety version that confuses me as it seems to indicate it won't require the victim to roll before 6 hours? The Nightmare's effect should stop well before that, shouldn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:35:23-07:00","id":961325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961312#post961312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Normal Satiety version that confuses me as it seems to indicate it won't require the victim to roll before 6 hours? The Nightmare's effect should stop well before that, shouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as I said probably when you first trigger the nightmare maybe a few minutes depending on which would be most appropriate. The lower version is less chloroform rag in a movie and movie drugged tea where unless they've got something really big they're likely to try and catch a few Zs of their own volition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:31:37-07:00","id":961387,"title":"","content":"So I'm coming at Beast with fresh eyes after taking one look at the Kickstarter draft and deciding I wanted no part of it. Now I'm seeing something of a game I quite like, but among the many deserved revisions from that draft, two changes seem a little strange to me. Does anyone know why the Homecoming was changed to the Devouring, and why Beast creating Heroes was removed? The former was fun because there are so few monsters in the CofD that tap into the unique horror of &quot;you were never human to begin with,&quot; and the latter was nice because a part of me wants Beast to be an official take on Leviathan and I adored the Ahabs from that fan-game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:58:55-07:00","id":961404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=961387#post961387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm coming at Beast with fresh eyes after taking one look at the Kickstarter draft and deciding I wanted no part of it. Now I'm seeing something of a game I quite like, but among the many deserved revisions from that draft, two changes seem a little strange to me. Does anyone know why the Homecoming was changed to the Devouring, and why Beast creating Heroes was removed? The former was fun because there are so few monsters in the CofD that tap into the unique horror of &quot;you were never human to begin with,&quot; and the latter was nice because a part of me wants Beast to be an official take on Leviathan and I adored the Ahabs from that fan-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes being created by Beasts had the unfortunate issue to some people that it was a case of victim blaming or the like. Essentially Heroes were listed as always okay to destroy by a Beast because of their nature, but since the indication was that the most mitigating factor to arguing that a Hero isn't entirely a Beast's creation is that a low integrity score implies the individual may already be slightly unhinged. I'm guessing it was also adjusted to more easily include the existence of Heroes who aren't violent sociopaths, though that part is just my speculation. <br /> <br /> As for the Homecoming becoming the Devouring I'm not sure there. Maybe it was to deal with the claims that Beasts represented the LGBT and/or minorities which was fine until people pointed out that Beasts are literally monsters and feed by being terrible beings. Or it could have just been to inject a bit more room for mystery and debate in the ranks of the Begotten. Since you'd have Beasts that believe they were never human and you'd have those who believed they'd become monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:31:31-07:00","id":966275,"title":"","content":"I couldn't find it in either character generation or among the Nightmares section, but how many Nightmares do starting characters get? I'm assuming the default is two, given one of the sample characters.<br /> <br /> Additionally, how long do Nightmare effects last? A Scene makes sense most of the time, but the &quot;delay until the next time they sleep&quot; thing makes that weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:10:11-07:00","id":966298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ROMzombie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=966275#post966275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't find it in either character generation or among the Nightmares section, but how many Nightmares do starting characters get? I'm assuming the default is two, given one of the sample characters.<br /> <br /> Additionally, how long do Nightmare effects last? A Scene makes sense most of the time, but the &quot;delay until the next time they sleep&quot; thing makes that weird.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They get two Nightmares and normally lasts a scene or how long it says it lasts after it triggers (which is either instantly or when they next sleep).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 09-10-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:27:59-07:00","id":966818,"title":"","content":"If You Must Obey is activated on a sleeping target, does the victim accomplish the orders while sleeping?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:30:44-07:00","id":966858,"title":"","content":"Not all Nightmares are necessarily useful being delayed to sleep. You Must Obey wouldn't really do anything, unless you woke them up during the scene they went to sleep. Behold My True Form and the like are quite useful either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 09-10-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:33:58-07:00","id":967431,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily directly beast related (it's for a hero I'm building, and I can't find a similar thread in the gen. forum), but do compound bows have an initiative penalty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T19:42:06-07:00","id":967683,"title":"","content":"The Hurt Locker preview lists short bows as a -3 and long bows as a -4. The only difference I see in the text between standard and compound is that compound bows have a larger range increment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T23:31:20-07:00","id":967794,"title":"","content":"I'm having a hard time following how Primordial Pathways work, especially in conjunction with Hold The Door and Be My Guest.<br /> <br /> Just how can people enter and leave a Beast's Lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:14:14-07:00","id":968922,"title":"","content":"Has anything been said of whether or not there are other Families and Hungers out there, or if we'll get more in supplements?<br /> <br /> And how do Beasts usually find each other, if at all? I know some are Devoured by others, but I'm a little fuzzy on the specifics of both how the potential Beast is found and what exactly the Devouring process entails, and that's to say nothing of how a whole Brood comes together.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The Lair table on page 93 says that Lair 1 characters have 3 Chambers, but then the text below says that a starting Beast has the Heart and one more Chamber. Do starting Beasts have two or three Chambers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-13-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:32:36-07:00","id":968927,"title":"","content":"I know additional families was discussed as a possibility for the player's guide, but as far as I know that was the extent of it.<br /> <br /> Beasts automatically recognize one another unless one is specifically concealing their supernatural nature, so typically it's just a matter of coming into close proximity with one another. I'll look back at the Devouring section, but I think a Beast-to-be creates &quot;ripples&quot; in the Primordial Dream that attracts Horrors?<br /> <br /> Beasts start with two extant chambers and a maximum capacity of three. You begin play with the Heart, one regular chamber and one empty slot. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:34:29-07:00","id":968930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=968922#post968922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anything been said of whether or not there are other Families and Hungers out there, or if we'll get more in supplements?<br /> <br /> And how do Beasts usually find each other, if at all? I know some are Devoured by others, but I'm a little fuzzy on the specifics of both how the potential Beast is found and what exactly the Devouring process entails, and that's to say nothing of how a whole Brood comes together.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The Lair table on page 93 says that Lair 1 characters have 3 Chambers, but then the text below says that a starting Beast has the Heart and one more Chamber. Do starting Beasts have two or three Chambers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three is the max number of chambers a lair one Beast can have. A Beast can also choose to start with only their lair's heart and no additional chambers. Basically it's saying that you can't claim an extra chamber after you've gotten to 3 until you've upgraded your lair. <br /> <br /> As far as meeting others goes, Beasts are able to recognize other supernatural species meaning it wouldn't be out of line to say the brood met just because one of them noticed the tell upon the other entering the room and was intrigued and got to chatting. <br /> <br /> There was some discussion on other hungers and families, but the tricky part there is that the existing ones are somewhat archetypal thus new ones need to be figured out as both not being a subset of an existing family/hunger without also being too specific. So might happen, but I haven't seen anything specific yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:46:21-07:00","id":968936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=968930#post968930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three is the max number of chambers a lair one Beast can have. A Beast can also choose to start with only their lair's heart and no additional chambers. Basically it's saying that you can't claim an extra chamber after you've gotten to 3 until you've upgraded your lair.<br /> <br /> As far as meeting others goes, Beasts are able to recognize other supernatural species meaning it wouldn't be out of line to say the brood met just because one of them noticed the tell upon the other entering the room and was intrigued and got to chatting.<br /> <br /> There was some discussion on other hungers and families, but the tricky part there is that the existing ones are somewhat archetypal thus new ones need to be figured out as both not being a subset of an existing family/hunger without also being too specific. So might happen, but I haven't seen anything specific yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's basically saying you can start with two Chambers detailed and then make another in play before you need to raise your Lair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:49:49-07:00","id":968942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=968936#post968936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's basically saying you can start with two Chambers detailed and then make another in play before you need to raise your Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically one of those chambers is the heart, but yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:27:23-07:00","id":968960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast pg. 93</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Chamber, the pocket of the Primordial Dream that forms after the Devouring, is called the Heart, but even a new Beast has the potential to take on up to two more Chambers during play. Starting characters begin with one Chamber besides the Heart, but the player can choose not to define this second Chamber and take two Experiences instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">ten characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:07:44-07:00","id":969643,"title":"","content":"Can Beasts enter the specific Oneiroi of a target? I want to see if you can subject someone to a terrible psychodrama in their dreams.<br /> <br /> And when Beasts enter the Astral, do they merge with their Horrors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:59:28-07:00","id":969660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=969643#post969643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Beasts enter the specific Oneiroi of a target?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, yes, though getting there in the first place might be tricky without assistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when Beasts enter the Astral, do they merge with their Horrors? </div> </div> </div>Nope. Beasts don't even merge with their Horrors in the Primordial Dream if they're not in their Lairs.<br /> <br /> &quot;Premeditated,&quot; Dave Brookshaw's story in the Primordial Feast anthology, addresses this somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:28:47-07:00","id":970371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=967794#post967794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having a hard time following how Primordial Pathways work, especially in conjunction with Hold The Door and Be My Guest.<br /> <br /> Just how can people enter and leave a Beast's Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>So no one had any thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:00:34-07:00","id":970431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970371#post970371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So no one had any thoughts on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you clarify what you mean? Are you confused about the mechanics of opening up a pathway, how the listed powers work, or how they work if the Beast isn't present?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:21:45-07:00","id":970547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970431#post970431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you clarify what you mean? Are you confused about the mechanics of opening up a pathway, how the listed powers work, or how they work if the Beast isn't present?</div> </div> </div> </div>How they work if the Beast isn't present. In particular, Be My Guest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:34:11-07:00","id":970551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970547#post970547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How they work if the Beast isn't present. In particular, Be My Guest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that opening a Primordial Pathway uses no supernatural Traits and normally only works on places conceptually flush with a Chamber, I suspect Be My Guest just works like if you were the hosting Beast and didn't have the ability to daisy-chain Lair Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:44:44-07:00","id":970556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970551#post970551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that opening a Primordial Pathway uses no supernatural Traits and normally only works on places conceptually flush with a Chamber, I suspect Be My Guest just works like if you were the hosting Beast and didn't have the ability to daisy-chain Lair Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you think Be My Guest would allow the person to open a Primordial Pathway to that particular Beast's Lair, without the presence of the Beast required?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:31:45-07:00","id":970567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970556#post970556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you think Be My Guest would allow the person to open a Primordial Pathway to that particular Beast's Lair, without the presence of the Beast required?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Chamber resonance and the metaphysical disposition of most suitable locations applies a pretty hefty penalty to what is already a two-component dicepool, so most long-term guests are likely to use your seed locations or places that you've basically made subchambers in.<br /> <br /> I'd also apply the modifiers from the Beast's Satiety Conditions, on the strength of doing so weighting the Hunger/Kinship dichotomy further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:21:20-07:00","id":970675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970567#post970567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Chamber resonance and the metaphysical disposition of most suitable locations applies a pretty hefty penalty to what is already a two-component dicepool, so most long-term guests are likely to use your seed locations or places that you've basically made subchambers in.<br /> <br /> I'd also apply the modifiers from the Beast's Satiety Conditions, on the strength of doing so weighting the Hunger/Kinship dichotomy further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it... Could a Beast's Horror open up a Primordial Pathway whenever it wants to? <br /> <br /> I can't think of anything that actually prevents a Beast from being in a coffee shop and focusing on being his Horror in its Lair and opening a Primordial Pathway to a location a Chamber is based on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:46:05-07:00","id":970722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970675#post970675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it... Could a Beast's Horror open up a Primordial Pathway whenever it wants to?<br /> <br /> I can't think of anything that actually prevents a Beast from being in a coffee shop and focusing on being his Horror in its Lair and opening a Primordial Pathway to a location a Chamber is based on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had this same question a while ago and there's not been any definite answer so far.<br /> <br /> I don't think anything really breaks, given that the Horror wouldn't be able to leave the area and Pathways are normally open for a pretty short period of time, but it could be there's something I'm overlooking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:14:10-07:00","id":970737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=970722#post970722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had this same question a while ago and there's not been any definite answer so far.<br /> <br /> I don't think anything really breaks, given that the Horror wouldn't be able to leave the area and Pathways are normally open for a pretty short period of time, but it could be there's something I'm overlooking.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only exclusion I can remember about what Horrors can't do without being merged with their Beast, is making use of Nightmares. And we know Horrors can make Primordial Pathways, because isn't that what they do when they hunt on their own? <br /> <br /> One of the concepts I absolutely love about Beast: the Primordial is that you basically get a character that can co-locate and its effectively in two places at once most of the time. <br /> <br /> Think of it! A Beast is having some coffee at a cafe. He gets a phone call from a buddy of his, a changeling that's on the run, is panicked and crying about how they're being chased by something and desperately need help! But the Changeling is across the city from the Beast... <br /> <br /> Ah, but the Beast remembers the Changeling is near an abandoned library that the Beast added a Chamber to his Lair from. So he tells the Changeling he can help, but they have to get to the library fast. And to send him a text when they get there. While the Beast is waiting, he takes a seat in the cafe and focuses on his Horror, sending it to the appropriate Chamber. When he receives the text, he controls his Horror and opens a Primordial Pathway to the library merging the two. He calls out with the Horror, finds the Changeling and then guides the Changeling through the nearest Burrow to another Chamber, letting the Pathway close as they exit. <br /> <br /> The Beast gets up, throws away his empty cup of coffee and heads out of the cafe, having saved the day for his friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:40:07-07:00","id":971146,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea, but I'm gonna say no on the idea that the Horror can open pathways to the material plane. At the very least it should not be able to do so remotely ie no it cannot open a pathway in the library if you're across town. The Horror and the Lair are connected, but not the material world so the Horror has no anchor to other points. The chambers are not their seed locations, so the Horror shouldn't be able to just rip open reality and attack anyone it wants. This would be analogous to playing Demon and getting a major compromise of your cover because one of your other covers told someone about soul pact and when you claimed when you aren't using the cover.<br /> <br /> Not to mention Beasts would need to be obscenely rare or else there can be no masquerade concept about them. Why? Because the Horrors will randomly drag people into Silent Hill and try to murder them. As for not breaking anything well remember damage to your Horror is either on your health or your satiety. If your Horror is opening the Pathway into the material plane and attacking whatever is on that end you open it up to getting mauled because it just manifested in the middle of the camp for some werewolves you're friends with and when faced with a literal nightmare trying to kill them they fought back and was on the receiving end of a 5:1 match against Chrinos garou. I mean maybe it's just me, but I would be seriously peeved if my ST informed me I'm on the outs with allies because I tried to kill them, and/or I either lost a chunk of my satiety or health because it randomly picked a fight with someone who could hurt it on the other side of town.<br /> <br /> Think Nightmare on Elm Street 2. Freddy can't attack anyone in the real world until he's brought out into it. He can get people in dreams because at this point he is a being of dreams, so those are open to him, but he couldn't kill anyone at the party he took over the one guy. Your Beast is the anchor point the Horror has to the material world it can't act in it without you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:06:05-07:00","id":971152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971146#post971146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea, but I'm gonna say no on the idea that the Horror can open pathways to the material plane. At the very least it should not be able to do so remotely ie no it cannot open a pathway in the library if you're across town. The Horror and the Lair are connected, but not the material world so the Horror has no anchor to other points. The chambers are not their seed locations, so the Horror shouldn't be able to just rip open reality and attack anyone it wants</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what's under discussion. The Horror being in a Chamber is a necessary element to opening a Primordial Pathway and you can control your Horror reflexively from outside your Lair.<br /> <br /> The question is not whether the Horror might independently exert the effort of opening a Pathway to a probably-unoccupied place outside the Astral when it's not hungry. The question is whether you need to be in an external location to open a Pathway to it from outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:07:56-07:00","id":971155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971146#post971146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea, but I'm gonna say no on the idea that the Horror can open pathways to the material plane. At the very least it should not be able to do so remotely ie no it cannot open a pathway in the library if you're across town. The Horror and the Lair are connected, but not the material world so the Horror has no anchor to other points. The chambers are not their seed locations, so the Horror shouldn't be able to just rip open reality and attack anyone it wants. This would be analogous to playing Demon and getting a major compromise of your cover because one of your other covers told someone about soul pact and when you claimed when you aren't using the cover.<br /> <br /> Not to mention Beasts would need to be obscenely rare or else there can be no masquerade concept about them. Why? Because the Horrors will randomly drag people into Silent Hill and try to murder them. As for not breaking anything well remember damage to your Horror is either on your health or your satiety. If your Horror is opening the Pathway into the material plane and attacking whatever is on that end you open it up to getting mauled because it just manifested in the middle of the camp for some werewolves you're friends with and when faced with a literal nightmare trying to kill them they fought back and was on the receiving end of a 5:1 match against Chrinos garou. I mean maybe it's just me, but I would be seriously peeved if my ST informed me I'm on the outs with allies because I tried to kill them, and/or I either lost a chunk of my satiety or health because it randomly picked a fight with someone who could hurt it on the other side of town.<br /> <br /> Think Nightmare on Elm Street 2. Freddy can't attack anyone in the real world until he's brought out into it. He can get people in dreams because at this point he is a being of dreams, so those are open to him, but he couldn't kill anyone at the party he took over the one guy. Your Beast is the anchor point the Horror has to the material world it can't act in it without you</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly disagree with this. The physical location that a Chamber is tied to is such a strong connection that you get a bonus to opening a Primordial Pathway there. Further, Horrors are explicitly described as being able to open Primordial Pathways. It's how they can leave their Lairs to feed off of other people's nightmares. A connection from Lair to a target's dream pocket is, in of itself, a Primordial Pathway.<br /> <br /> And keep in mind, in my example, it's not the Horror opening the Primordial Pathway on it's own. It's doing so under the Beast's direction, who is capable of taking full control of it whenever they want to. And there's no explicit mention that a Beast can't do what they can normally do when doing so, except for the mention of not being able to use Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:10:30-07:00","id":971156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971152#post971152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not what's under discussion. The Horror being in a Chamber is a necessary element to opening a Primordial Pathway and you can control your Horror reflexively from outside your Lair.<br /> <br /> The question is not whether the Horror might independently exert the effort of opening a Pathway to a probably-unoccupied place outside the Astral when it's not hungry. The question is whether you need to be in an external location to open a Pathway to it from outside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's missing the important part of the equation. If you're in a Chamber, you can open a Primordial Pathway from inside the Lair out to the external location. That's how a Beast can leave their Lair after they enter it. The Horror is inside the Lair, so that's how they can open a Primordial Pathway to the external location. They just can't leave the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:17:20-07:00","id":971159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971156#post971156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's missing the important part of the equation. If you're in a Chamber, you can open a Primordial Pathway from inside the Lair out to the external location. That's how a Beast can leave their Lair after they enter it. The Horror is inside the Lair, so that's how they can open a Primordial Pathway to the external location. They just can't leave the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026That's what I said.<br /> <br /> The point of ambiguity under discussion is whether it's possible to open a Primordial Pathway in a fashion that does not cause you to merge with your Horror for the duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:24:09-07:00","id":971161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971159#post971159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026That's what I said.<br /> <br /> The point of ambiguity under discussion is whether it's possible to open a Primordial Pathway in a fashion that does not cause you to merge with your Horror for the duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. Misunderstood.<br /> <br /> Well, you can open Primordial Pathways that don't necessarily cause you to merge with your Horror. Because when you open Primordial Pathways to the Primordial Dream (that's not your Lair), there is no merging, nor when you open Primordial Pathways to other dimensions. So that doesn't seem to be a particular requirement for utilizing Primordial Pathways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:32:03-07:00","id":971163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971161#post971161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can open Primordial Pathways that don't necessarily cause you to merge with your Horror. Because when you open Primordial Pathways to the Primordial Dream (that's not your Lair), there is no merging, nor when you open Primordial Pathways to other dimensions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026No?<br /> <br /> You merge with your Horror when you open a Pathway between a relevant Chamber and a resonant location that you occupy. That use of the Pathways works by leveraging the similarity between the two places to treat you as though you were in your Lair while the connection is open. You're still transported or translated into the appropriate state of your human form in most any context that is not &quot;you are in your Horror's hunting grounds and it is awake.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:53:14-07:00","id":971172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=971163#post971163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026No?<br /> <br /> You merge with your Horror when you open a Pathway between a relevant Chamber and a resonant location that you occupy. That use of the Pathways works by leveraging the similarity between the two places to treat you as though you were in your Lair while the connection is open. You're still transported or translated into the appropriate state of your human form in most any context that is not &quot;you are in your Horror's hunting grounds and it is awake.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 97 of Primordial Pathways describes that the Horror is capable of opening Primordial Pathways rather explicitly. The sidebar &quot;The Horror Itself&quot; on page 99 describes details of the Horror and what it cannot do.<br /> <br /> So, considering that Horrors can open Primordial Pathways instinctively and that Beasts know how to open Primordial Pathways on their own... What prevents a Beast from using Soul Communion to control their Horror to open a Primordial Pathway from the Chamber they're in to the physical location the Chamber is linked to?<br /> <br /> No merging seems to be necessary for this process. Merging is just a consequence of the Beast and Horror being in the same location.<br /> <br /> Edit: Maybe I'm still misunderstanding what you said was &quot;the question&quot;, regarding whether the Beast has to be at the external location. I don't think the Beast needs to be, because a Beast can open a Pathway from their Lair. And since the Beast IS their Horror... they're technically in their Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T04:37:34-07:00","id":974989,"title":"","content":"Ive searched but found no answer, so i thought someone here might help me.<br /> <br /> Do beasts not roll breaking points? with no integrity, and no real equivalent like humanity for vampires, i couldnt find anything in the book stating specifically that they dont roll them, but i assume they dont. can someone help me out? it seems a little odd to me to play a character where i dont have to roll breaking points, maybe i completely missed it, but i havent been able to find anything in the beast book that explains when beasts would roll them, and if they do, what consequences they have for beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8728-sethe","name":"Sethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:49:26-07:00","id":975012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=974989#post974989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive searched but found no answer, so i thought someone here might help me.<br /> <br /> Do beasts not roll breaking points? with no integrity, and no real equivalent like humanity for vampires, i couldnt find anything in the book stating specifically that they dont roll them, but i assume they dont. can someone help me out? it seems a little odd to me to play a character where i dont have to roll breaking points, maybe i completely missed it, but i havent been able to find anything in the beast book that explains when beasts would roll them, and if they do, what consequences they have for beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts deliberately don't have breaking points. The only real consequences for being a horrible monster of a character are your own conscience and the risk that others will take exception to it. Of course there're Heroes as well, but that's a different thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:39:39-07:00","id":975027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=974989#post974989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive searched but found no answer, so i thought someone here might help me.<br /> <br /> Do beasts not roll breaking points? with no integrity, and no real equivalent like humanity for vampires, i couldnt find anything in the book stating specifically that they dont roll them, but i assume they dont. can someone help me out? it seems a little odd to me to play a character where i dont have to roll breaking points, maybe i completely missed it, but i havent been able to find anything in the beast book that explains when beasts would roll them, and if they do, what consequences they have for beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. As I understand it beast as sociopathic. They may follow a code or have a conscience, but there is no significant emotional force keeping them in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:56:41-07:00","id":975030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=975027#post975027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't. As I understand it beast as sociopathic. They may follow a code or have a conscience, but there is no significant emotional force keeping them in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts aren't sociopaths: in fact, if they have a conscience they can't be. Integrity systems aren't necessarily something that you can measure in-game (barring a few mind powers): it's an abstraction of how your character <i>has behaved</i>, rather than a measure of how evil/human/spirit/whatever they are. Demons also have a weird Integrity equivalent: the Cover rating is just how in-character they're behaving for a given Cover.<br /> <br /> I was discussing what makes a monster in a Mage thread, and something I said there was that Beasts are the only splat that <i>have</i> to be monsters: everybody else has options, albeit painful ones, that let them avoid being monsters. If a Beast stops being a monster, they unconsciously ruin the lives of people around them until their soul starves and dies. So a Beast has to come to terms with that rather than trying to cling to their old lives, and I think that's the reason they don't have an Integrity equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:04:09-07:00","id":975032,"title":"","content":"Well...you can avoid your hunger thanks to family dinner.<br /> If you befriend a &quot;benign&quot; supernatural, you can increase your satiety without hunt nobody.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:21:20-07:00","id":975039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=975030#post975030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts aren't sociopaths: in fact, if they have a conscience they can't be. Integrity systems aren't necessarily something that you can measure in-game (barring a few mind powers): it's an abstraction of how your character <i>has behaved</i>, rather than a measure of how evil/human/spirit/whatever they are. Demons also have a weird Integrity equivalent: the Cover rating is just how in-character they're behaving for a given Cover.<br /> <br /> I was discussing what makes a monster in a Mage thread, and something I said there was that Beasts are the only splat that <i>have</i> to be monsters: everybody else has options, albeit painful ones, that let them avoid being monsters. If a Beast stops being a monster, they unconsciously ruin the lives of people around them until their soul starves and dies. So a Beast has to come to terms with that rather than trying to cling to their old lives, and I think that's the reason they don't have an Integrity equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be right about beast, but I have encountered sociopaths that are decent people. They believe in doing the right thing and have a conscience, but do not feel any emotional sympathy or what we might call love or compassion for others. Their morality is strictly intellectual rather than emotional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:59:45-07:00","id":975128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=975039#post975039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might be right about beast, but I have encountered sociopaths that are decent people. They believe in doing the right thing and have a conscience, but do not feel any emotional sympathy or what we might call love or compassion for others. Their morality is strictly intellectual rather than emotional.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add my own two cents, I personally think that Beasts, being literally half Horror and half human, can choose - not necessarily consciously - whether they think with their chemical, human meat-brain or with the metaphysical and amoral dream-mind of their Horror. In other words, the more a Beast associates himself with his Horror and the more he acts like it, the more he thinks using its mind, which is utterly sociopathic and has no real capacity to process morality or empathise with humans in a meaningful way. The more a beast associates with his human self, the more he thinks with that mind and, consequently, the more human he tends to act. Thus, as a Beast acts more like a monster, his morality becomes more and more intellectual, less something that he feels and more something that he thinks, as K9ine said.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the human is a sociopath in the first place, finding the difference between the two conjoined psyches becomes more difficult. <br /> <br /> BTW, I myself am slightly sociopathic and sometimes find getting my head around what others seem to find morally clear is quite difficult. I still consider myself to be a relatively good person though, so... yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T21:03:20-07:00","id":975361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=975128#post975128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add my own two cents, I personally think that Beasts, being literally half Horror and half human, can choose - not necessarily consciously - whether they think with their chemical, human meat-brain or with the metaphysical and amoral dream-mind of their Horror. In other words, the more a Beast associates himself with his Horror and the more he acts like it, the more he thinks using its mind, which is utterly sociopathic and has no real capacity to process morality or empathise with humans in a meaningful way. The more a beast associates with his human self, the more he thinks with that mind and, consequently, the more human he tends to act. Thus, as a Beast acts more like a monster, his morality becomes more and more intellectual, less something that he feels and more something that he thinks, as K9ine said.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the human is a sociopath in the first place, finding the difference between the two conjoined psyches becomes more difficult.<br /> <br /> BTW, I myself am slightly sociopathic and sometimes find getting my head around what others seem to find morally clear is quite difficult. I still consider myself to be a relatively good person though, so... yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I think that a Beast the started as a sociopath would have an easier time adjusting. The more emotional they are before the devouring would likely break their mind. On a another note, I am one of those hyper emotional types. I had to adapt to become sociopathic (well sociopathic by todays standards, I guess the ancient greeks would just call me a stoic) just to cope with the real world. This is another way a beast might adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T03:02:17-07:00","id":975449,"title":"","content":"thanks for the answers!<br /> i have to admit i really like the breaking point system, and it makes me a little sad that beast have nothing like it to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8728-sethe","name":"Sethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:17:09-07:00","id":976023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=975449#post975449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks for the answers!<br /> i have to admit i really like the breaking point system, and it makes me a little sad that beast have nothing like it to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of those things where an absence of the system speaks a great deal. In place of the breaking point system, Beasts are meant to waver around on their Satiety scale, which messes with them mentally quite significantly and provides lots of opportunities for Beats similarly to how breaking points do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T02:55:15-07:00","id":977672,"title":"","content":"Can someone help me with the Eshmaki. They confuse me.<br /> <br /> Okay, so they're established as Nightmares of Darkness (although they were once Nightmares of Destruction, which is baffling why they would be changed to Darkness but whatever), they're the Slendermen and Creepers (the Minecraft ones included, I suppose). Okay, got it. Let's take a look at their Atavisms: From the Shadows, makes sense. Limb from Limb, alright. Dragonfire...<br /> <br /> <b>Wat?</b> Dragonfire? As in breathing fire on people? Um, how is that fitting for the whole Darkness theme? Fire was the first thing humans used for light, and that's symbolically linked to creatures in darkness? Shouldn't Dragonfire be an Anakim Atavism? Oh, &quot;<i>a curl of smoke or a dreadful gleam in her eyes is often her victim\u2019s only warning</i>&quot; (taken from Dargonfire's description).<br /> <br /> ...Weak.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look at the fourth one: Relentless Hunter. &quot;<i>Not all Eshmaki strike from the shadows</i>&quot; (from the description). <b>What in the-!</b> I thought Eshmaki were creatures of darkness, aren't they all supposed to strike from the shadows? Isn't that their thing? They're nicknamed the Lurkers for crying out loud! What's worse is that they don't have Shadowed Soul, which allows a Beast to meld into shadows. Y'know, their thing. But actually no, that's for Namtaru, Nightmares of Revulsion, because that's makes much more sense apparently! Oh, &quot;<i>Medusa dwelled in darkness. Not by choice, no, but to hide from her own hideousness. No mirror was allowed within her Lair, and no friendly soul came to visit her. Even the darkness betrayed her in time. It permeated her flesh and filled her eyes, opening itself to her, until there was no more refuge in the dark. Gnashing her teeth, she shut her eyes and lay in wait, listening to the silence of her Lair. She belonged to the darkness and it to her.</i>&quot; (from Shadowed Soul's description).<br /> <br /> ...Weak.<br /> <br /> So I ask again, can somebody please explain this to me? I sure can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:29:02-07:00","id":977700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=976023#post976023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's one of those things where an absence of the system speaks a great deal. In place of the breaking point system, Beasts are meant to waver around on their Satiety scale, which messes with them mentally quite significantly and provides lots of opportunities for Beats similarly to how breaking points do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had not thought of it like that, and suddenly it makes a lot more sense. Thanks so much for helping me with this everyone, it has brought a lot of considerations to mind about how to play a beast, and has made me like them much more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8728-sethe","name":"Sethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:31:50-07:00","id":977805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977672#post977672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wat?</b> Dragonfire? As in breathing fire on people? Um, how is that fitting for the whole Darkness theme? Fire was the first thing humans used for light, and that's symbolically linked to creatures in darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Family has had Blazing Light as a suggested Lair Trait since the Kickstarter draft. Be less literal-minded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's take a look at the fourth one: Relentless Hunter. &quot;<i>Not all Eshmaki strike from the shadows</i>&quot; (from the description). <b>What in the-!</b> I thought Eshmaki were creatures of darkness, aren't they all supposed to strike from the shadows? Isn't that their thing? They're nicknamed the Lurkers for crying out loud! </div> </div> </div>The consistent focus on solitude and loneliness as the Family's thematic and the fact that the paragraph you're quoting goes on to talk about how this healing-booster Atavism makes the Beasts who have it simply unable to be put down for good.<br /> <br /> The Anakim hit on their name as the Nightmares of Hopelessness through the fact that their incredibly direct go-to methods of hunting tend to be too potent to actually stop head-on. Relentless Hunter works best for werewolf-style hit-and-run tactics, which is right in the Eshmaki's wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's worse is that they don't have Shadowed Soul, which allows a Beast to meld into shadows. Y'know, their thing. But actually no, that's for Namtaru, Nightmares of Revulsion, because that's makes much more sense apparently! </div> </div> </div>Things <i>fester</i> in the dark. Things that make your skin crawl just to think about, whether they're out to get you personally or not.<br /> <br /> The Eshmaki are associated with the dark through the sensory deprivation representing a vulnerability to something that might be hunting you down. The Namtaru are associated with the dark because that's where revolting things <i>live</i>.<br /> <br /> Your commentary is weak and orthogonal to your question and can be done without, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:56:54-07:00","id":977982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Family has had Blazing Light as a suggested Lair Trait since the Kickstarter draft. Be less literal-minded.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about being literal-minded, it's that there's a reason Prometheus stole fire from the gods and gave it to humanity. Thematically, fire is light and power, and not just in the physical sense. It's light in that it also represents knowledge and power in that it drove invention as much as it could be used as a weapon. That's why I feel it's more of an Anakim thing, because Anakim represent things that are stronger and smarter than you ever will be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The consistent focus on solitude and loneliness as the Family's thematic and the fact that the paragraph you're quoting goes on to talk about how this healing-booster Atavism makes the Beasts who have it simply unable to be put down for good.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no connection between those concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anakim hit on their name as the Nightmares of Hopelessness through the fact that their incredibly direct go-to methods of hunting tend to be too potent to actually stop head-on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only brought up the Anakim for Dragonfire specifically, but now that you mention it, Relentless Hunter works a lot better for them than for the Eshmaki. Nothing you said here goes against that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relentless Hunter works best for werewolf-style hit-and-run tactics, which is right in the Eshmaki's wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? No seriously, if you can regenerate quickly, why ever employ hit-and-run tactics at all? You employ it to avoid getting hurt in the first place (which is why wolves in real life do it). Quick regeneration makes that unnecessary, unless you're going up against something that can kill you much faster than you can regenerate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things <i>fester</i> in the dark. Things that make your skin crawl just to think about, whether they're out to get you personally or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that makes sense for why a Namtaru might happen to have Shadowed Soul, it does not however, make sense for it to be tied to the entire Family as a whole. I mean think about it, light would make Medusa stronger and darkness would make her weaker, considering her victims have to actually see her face. Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Eshmaki are associated with the dark through the sensory deprivation representing a vulnerability to something that might be hunting you down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't Shadowed Soul enhance the hell out of that, though? Think about it: Let's say someone's in the dark somewhere (in their bed, walking at night, whatever) and they get the sense that they're being watched. They see nothing but darkness, because the Lurker watching them is part of it. That is, until they come out right the second they're about to strike...<br /> <br /> Isn't that supposed to be right up the Eshmaki's alley?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Namtaru are associated with the dark because that's where revolting things <i>live</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same could be said of all the monsters thematically speaking. The game ain't called Chronicles of Darkness for nothing, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977805#post977805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your commentary is weak and orthogonal to your question and can be done without, thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, your quick dismissal is what can be done without, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:42:42-07:00","id":978194,"title":"","content":"One of the two of you is wrong and it's not Satchel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:04:12-07:00","id":978205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977982#post977982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about being literal-minded, it's that there's a reason Prometheus stole fire from the gods and gave it to humanity. Thematically, fire is light and power, and not just in the physical sense. It's light in that it also represents knowledge and power in that it drove invention as much as it could be used as a weapon. That's why I feel it's more of an Anakim thing, because Anakim represent things that are stronger and smarter than you ever will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonfire is a power that lets you burn down someone's house without any prior warning. Light and knowledge have nothing to do with the themes at play in a primal nightmare of fire-breathing monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no connection between those concepts. </div> </div> </div>There's no connection between rapid healing and not dying and being able to keep coming after you while waiting for the point when you are at your most vulnerable. Mhm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? No seriously, if you can regenerate quickly, why ever employ hit-and-run tactics at all? You employ it to avoid getting hurt in the first place (which is why wolves in real life do it). Quick regeneration makes that unnecessary, unless you're going up against something that can kill you much faster than you can regenerate. </div> </div> </div>Cats don't play with their food. The &quot;quick&quot; regeneration you're talking about either costs a precious resource, requires special conditions, or takes half an hour per box to heal lethal damage in a system where most weapons will deal at least two points of damage on a successful hit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While that makes sense for why a Namtaru might happen to have Shadowed Soul, it does not however, make sense for it to be tied to the entire Family as a whole. I mean think about it, light would make Medusa stronger and darkness would make her weaker, considering her victims have to actually see her face. Just sayin'. </div> </div> </div>The Gorgons are not all or even mostly Medusa. They <i>are</i>, however, heavily composed of the kin of cockroaches and cave worms and assorted other hideous things that hide from the light.<br /> <br /> The Eshmaki, for contrast, include stalking predatory cats and storm-dragons among their sample characters and common Horror imagery. Not every Family-affinity Atavism has to be used in every possible Beast of that Family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't Shadowed Soul enhance the hell out of that, though? </div> </div> </div>The same logic applies to Unbreakable with the Anakim or Mimir's Wisdom with the Makara. The Begotten powerset is not strongly divided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same could be said of all the monsters thematically speaking. </div> </div> </div>That's the point of Atavisms being universally learnable, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, your quick dismissal is what can be done without, thanks. </div> </div> </div>The irony abounds.<br /> <br /> If you have a question, ask the question. Spare the repeated stink about how you're unimpressed by the flavor text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:19:55-07:00","id":978250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978194#post978194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the two of you is wrong and it's not Satchel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unsubstantiated claim is unsubstantiated. Considering Satchel's last post, to say that substantiating such a claim is going to be an uphill battle is an understatement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonfire is a power that lets you burn down someone's house without any prior warning. Light and knowledge have nothing to do with the themes at play in a primal nightmare of fire-breathing monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does in an inverse way, that's what makes fire-breathing monsters scary. Humans tend to see fire as a powerful force, for both good and ill. So if a monster has the power to produce fire by merely breathing, that's terrifying because it shows how strong and destructive the monster is.<br /> <br /> There's a reason fire breath is so strongly associated with dragons, which are symbols of greatness and power in and of themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no connection between rapid healing and not dying and being able to keep coming after you while waiting for the point when you are at your most vulnerable. Mhm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be kind and simply leave this alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cats don't play with their food.</div> </div> </div> </div>The overwhelming majority do at least once. Some even do it as a hobby.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;quick&quot; regeneration you're talking about either costs a precious resource, requires special conditions, or takes half an hour per box to heal lethal damage in a system where most weapons will deal at least two points of damage on a successful hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving this alone, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gorgons are not all or even mostly Medusa. They <i>are</i>, however, heavily composed of the kin of cockroaches and cave worms and assorted other hideous things that hide from the light.</div> </div> </div> </div>And cockatrices, and swamp-things, and the Blob. Darkness simply isn't central.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same logic applies to Unbreakable with the Anakim or Mimir's Wisdom with the Makara. The Begotten powerset is not strongly divided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet there's Titanic Blow and Monster from the Deep, both of which are basically attacks, but deviate in the specific things that they do, keeping in line with the concepts of their Families. Why not do the same with other Atavisms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The irony abounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the word you're looking for is &quot;hypocrisy&quot;, not &quot;irony&quot; (don't worry, it's a common mistake). Second, it doesn't apply, &quot;quick dismissal&quot; wasn't my first choice, but I posted it instead to be polite.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Satchel;n978205]If you have a question, ask the question.<br /> <br /> Refer to my original post, I ain't repeating it here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978205#post978205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spare the repeated stink about how you're unimpressed by the flavor text.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a question based on the muddling of themes, the &quot;stink about flavor text&quot; is inevitable and in fact part of the question. Looks like said question has been answered &quot;No.&quot;, so I won't press any further than this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 09-29-2016, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T04:59:31-07:00","id":978311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=977672#post977672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone help me with the Eshmaki. They confuse me.<br /> <br /> Okay, so they're established as Nightmares of Darkness (although they were once Nightmares of Destruction, which is baffling why they would be changed to Darkness but whatever), they're the Slendermen and Creepers (the Minecraft ones included, I suppose). Okay, got it. Let's take a look at their Atavisms: From the Shadows, makes sense. Limb from Limb, alright. Dragonfire...<br /> <br /> <b>Wat?</b> Dragonfire? As in breathing fire on people? Um, how is that fitting for the whole Darkness theme? Fire was the first thing humans used for light, and that's symbolically linked to creatures in darkness? Shouldn't Dragonfire be an Anakim Atavism? Oh, &amp;quot;<i>a curl of smoke or a dreadful gleam in her eyes is often her victim\u2019s only warning</i>&amp;quot; (taken from Dargonfire's description).<br /> <br /> ...Weak.<br /> <br /> Let's take a look at the fourth one: Relentless Hunter. &amp;quot;<i>Not all Eshmaki strike from the shadows</i>&amp;quot; (from the description). <b>What in the-!</b> I thought Eshmaki were creatures of darkness, aren't they all supposed to strike from the shadows? Isn't that their thing? They're nicknamed the Lurkers for crying out loud! What's worse is that they don't have Shadowed Soul, which allows a Beast to meld into shadows. Y'know, their thing. But actually no, that's for Namtaru, Nightmares of Revulsion, because that's makes much more sense apparently! Oh, &amp;quot;<i>Medusa dwelled in darkness. Not by choice, no, but to hide from her own hideousness. No mirror was allowed within her Lair, and no friendly soul came to visit her. Even the darkness betrayed her in time. It permeated her flesh and filled her eyes, opening itself to her, until there was no more refuge in the dark. Gnashing her teeth, she shut her eyes and lay in wait, listening to the silence of her Lair. She belonged to the darkness and it to her.</i>&amp;quot; (from Shadowed Soul's description).<br /> <br /> ...Weak.<br /> <br /> So I ask again, can somebody please explain this to me? I sure can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you, there are several things like this in BtP that seem off to me. It would really benefit from a second edition, or a supplement book that provides some alternative rules/setting stuff. Maybe some of that will be in the Beast players guide, but I'd wait to find out before I would consider buying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:32:12-07:00","id":978383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978250#post978250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsubstantiated claim is unsubstantiated. Considering Satchel's last post, to say that substantiating such a claim is going to be an uphill battle is an understatement.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the two of you has a track record of consistently being right for about a decade, having even been noted several times as someone who clarified subjects in ways that improved writing in the books by writers and has been confirmed as right on track by developers, and it is not you.<br /> <br /> Unsubstantiated, sure. I'm busy with shit right now and I have to decide what to blow my time on. For me, it's enough for me to point out that from where I am standing, Satchel is correct. I don't have the time to share my literary and analytical point of view, and I don't feel like I have to because, well, Satchel is on track. Sure, I might be wrong on that, but history shows the odds are not in your favor on that one.<br /> <br /> Context is important. Jokes about Satchel being all-knowing, all-seeing are not made as satire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:00:52-07:00","id":978404,"title":"","content":"So Question, Maybe silly.<br /> <br /> Mirage + Environmental Immunity VS Illusion Powers. How does this work?<br /> <br /> Ok So I know how Obfuscate VS Auspex / Other Info revealing Powers. Clash of Wills. But I'm not that well versed on Beast, How have yall been doing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:56:26-07:00","id":978438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978404#post978404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Question, Maybe silly.<br /> <br /> Mirage + Environmental Immunity VS Illusion Powers. How does this work?<br /> <br /> Ok So I know how Obfuscate VS Auspex / Other Info revealing Powers. Clash of Wills. But I'm not that well versed on Beast, How have yall been doing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it would depend on whether the illusion was cast upon the Beast themselves, in which case it would be a Clash of Wills as per usual, or whether it's cast upon an area, in which case the Beast would simply see the illusion as a transparent overlay on what was really there. That's how I would run it, anyway. I'm not sure if that's the best way though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:15:21-07:00","id":978490,"title":"","content":"Can a beast effectively immunise itself against anathemas by hiding a weapon which has been used for the weaponbound anathema in the lair?<br /> <br /> After all the rules state that a beast can only suffer from one anathema at a time, any further attempts to place one fail and instead reveal the current one. For most anathemas that is just as dangerous as placing a new one, but the weaponbound anathema is completely harmless for the beast unless the hero has the weapon in question. If it is hidden beyond his reach - for instance in a lair - he cannot exploit the anathema. Even if he has the open gate gift allowing him to enter the lair he has first to deal with the (potentially lethal) environmental tilts there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:57:55-07:00","id":978657,"title":"","content":"Yes if you want to take the risk of it still being used against you at a bad time (read it is used against you while it is still weapon bound to you.) I mean you would need to be careful since if that weapon gets destroyed the anathema is lifted. Otherwise yeah there isn't anything in universe stopping you from going paranoid survivor on it and burying it in a cement block and dropping it in the ocean. Though I would probably play as the thing unsettles and creeps out the Beast in question intensely seeing how the weapon would basically radiate that it exists to murder you specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:56:50-07:00","id":978877,"title":"","content":"Would a Beast be able to form Family Ties with their mirror universe counterpart (as in the ones in the core book, just after the Angels section)? Would they be able to find/form a Chamber in the alternate universe to travel between them via their lair? If so, someone with a narcissistic tendency could get very...kinky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:27:15-07:00","id":978888,"title":"","content":"A mirror double yes, their mirror double no. Though that's less a mechanical barrier and more that the mirror double is not going to be willing to allow the original to stay outside the mirror. Based on the description I kind of picture it like Welcome to Nightvale 19A and 19B when Cecil and Kevin first met up. As far as creating chambers in the mirror world goes, it isn't detailed so what specifically it is would be up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:18:41-07:00","id":978957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978490#post978490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a beast effectively immunise itself against anathemas by hiding a weapon which has been used for the weaponbound anathema in the lair?</div> </div> </div> </div> For the record, I'd like to point out that this is actually a classic trope. Hero finds the dragonslaying sword inside the dragon's own hoard (inside the own Lair, even!) and uses it kill the monster. So, I would argue that we're dealing with a feature here, not a bug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After all the rules state that a beast can only suffer from one anathema at a time, any further attempts to place one fail and instead reveal the current one. For most anathemas that is just as dangerous as placing a new one, but the weaponbound anathema is completely harmless for the beast unless the hero has the weapon in question. If it is hidden beyond his reach - for instance in a lair - he cannot exploit the anathema. Even if he has the open gate gift allowing him to enter the lair he has first to deal with the (potentially lethal) environmental tilts there. </div> </div> </div> I've made a Beast PC that started off with Anathema already on them, and run with it. Dragon collectors that kidnaps &quot;princesses.&quot; I did this more because I wanted to emulate the dragon legend a bit closer, rather than an attempt to immunize myself or anything. I liked the extra compulsion, thought it made the game more interesting. Also, I had fun going out of my way to make all the kidnapped princesses into Kin through some way or another. The one that went Ventrue was especially interseting with the constant attempts of taking over the little pack. Ah, so much fun.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my point is this - Trust me when I say that a good ST will use that against you. The Heroes aren't stupid - at least successful ones aren't. These guys are like hunters, and do their research. They find your &quot;bane&quot; and use it against you. You hide the anathama in the depths of your Lair, the heroes will figure out how to get into the Lair and track your weapon down to use it against your Horror while you're off busy doing other things. Imagine the shock when you suddenly realize that your personal Castlevania has its own Belmont trying to bring down the Heart, using the worst weapon against it. Kidnap people, and you'll find that your victims go Hero Party on you. I don't care how much armor, health and regeneration you think you have, I can attest that several knives in the back when you don't expect it are coming. Coup d'etre rules are vicious. RIP, dragon.<br /> <br /> You will never be immune to your anathema.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Would a Beast be able to form Family Ties with their mirror universe counterpart (as in the ones in the core book, just after the Angels section)? Would they be able to find/form a Chamber in the alternate universe to travel between them via their lair? If so, someone with a narcissistic tendency could get very...kinky.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> You can form Kinship even with your worst (non-Hero) enemies - you can threaten and use as much Hard Leverage / Force as many Doors as you want to get it.<br /> <br /> Kinship doesn't mean best friends or healthy, stable relationships. Its possible, but it doesn't stop the mirror-double from following its nature. You'll need other magics to offset that somehow,</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-30-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:13:58-07:00","id":979092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978957#post978957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can form Kinship even with your worst (non-Hero) enemies - you can threaten and use as much Hard Leverage / Force as many Doors as you want to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Even if the target is willing, the two still must spend considerable time together, endure common hardship, hunt together, or otherwise become close before this Condition can be applied.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is worth noting that the relationship does not have to be affectionate or even friendly for this Condition to apply; all it requires is that the Beast and the target be close. Associates, rivals, or even genial enemies thus potentially qualify for this condition as well, though it will likely be significantly harder to maintain more hostile connections.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:17:21-07:00","id":979282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=979092#post979092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Even if the target is willing, the two still must spend considerable time together, endure common hardship, hunt together, or otherwise become close before this Condition can be applied.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;It is worth noting that the relationship does not have to be affectionate or even friendly for this Condition to apply; all it requires is that the Beast and the target be close. Associates, rivals, or even genial enemies thus potentially qualify for this condition as well, though it will likely be significantly harder to maintain more hostile connections.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Some commentary might be useful with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:42:11-07:00","id":979611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=978957#post978957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For the record, I'd like to point out that this is actually a classic trope. Hero finds the dragonslaying sword inside the dragon's own hoard (inside the own Lair, even!) and uses it kill the monster. So, I would argue that we're dealing with a feature here, not a bug.<br /> <br /> I've made a Beast PC that started off with Anathema already on them, and run with it. Dragon collectors that kidnaps &quot;princesses.&quot; I did this more because I wanted to emulate the dragon legend a bit closer, rather than an attempt to immunize myself or anything. I liked the extra compulsion, thought it made the game more interesting. Also, I had fun going out of my way to make all the kidnapped princesses into Kin through some way or another. The one that went Ventrue was especially interseting with the constant attempts of taking over the little pack. Ah, so much fun.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my point is this - Trust me when I say that a good ST will use that against you. The Heroes aren't stupid - at least successful ones aren't. These guys are like hunters, and do their research. They find your &quot;bane&quot; and use it against you. You hide the anathama in the depths of your Lair, the heroes will figure out how to get into the Lair and track your weapon down to use it against your Horror while you're off busy doing other things. Imagine the shock when you suddenly realize that your personal Castlevania has its own Belmont trying to bring down the Heart, using the worst weapon against it. Kidnap people, and you'll find that your victims go Hero Party on you. I don't care how much armor, health and regeneration you think you have, I can attest that several knives in the back when you don't expect it are coming. Coup d'etre rules are vicious. RIP, dragon.<br /> <br /> You will never be immune to your anathema.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with your points, my only worry was soul communion which would allow a beast to destroy the weapon, thus removing anathema, the moment someone successfully enters the lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:29:05-07:00","id":979822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=979611#post979611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mostly agree with your points, my only worry was soul communion which would allow a beast to destroy the weapon, thus removing anathema, the moment someone successfully enters the lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Beast is opened up to a new anathema if they're in a vulnerable state for it. So nothin's really changed, I'd say. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:49:36-07:00","id":980260,"title":"","content":"Does anybody know if Heroes qualify for Kinship? They're neither included nor specifically excluded (as Demons are) in the sidebar, and it seems like they would probably fall under Fundamentally Human. Besides the possibility of choosing to buck the narrative and befriend supposedly mortal enemies this is relevant for whether Beasts can spot Heroes as supernaturally gifted. One of a Hero's biggest advantages is that they usually see Beasts before the Beasts see them. That would still be the norm, as Fundamentally Human imposes pretty hefty penalties if the target hasn't used a supernatural power, I'm just curious if Beasts get a roll to detect them at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:43:02-07:00","id":980302,"title":"","content":"I would think that Heroes are Fundamentally Human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T21:57:12-08:00","id":1022223,"title":"","content":"Do you have to &quot;distribute&quot; your Lair Traits among your different Chambers, or does every Chamber have every Lair Trait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T22:03:07-08:00","id":1022225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1022223#post1022223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have to &amp;quot;distribute&amp;quot; your Lair Traits among your different Chambers, or does every Chamber have every Lair Trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Chamber has every Trait. You can turn them off though, if you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:09:10-08:00","id":1022314,"title":"","content":"The Lair Traits of the local hive's Apex are added to the Lairs of lesser Beasts, right?<br /> <br /> If so, then do the Apex's Lair Traits conform themselves to each individual Beast's Lair, or are they forced unto the Lairs?<br /> <br /> For example, if the Apex is a demon whose hellish pit drips with boiling water (the Corrosive Trait), then is the local mecha-monster's Lair filled with boiling water from hell or toxic battery acid?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T19:51:01-08:00","id":1022592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1022314#post1022314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lair Traits of the local hive's Apex are added to the Lairs of lesser Beasts, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hive Trait of the local Apex applies to all Chambers in that hive, including those incorporated into a Lair. Notably, this means the Apex still can't access another Beast's Heart without going through an intervening Burrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, then do the Apex's Lair Traits conform themselves to each individual Beast's Lair, or are they forced unto the Lairs? </div> </div> </div>There's a feature in attached Chambers that represents the Hive Trait which Beasts with the appropriate Environmental Immunity and/or permissions can use like Burrows to navigate the hive. A Jenny Greenteeth sort of river-hag might have a stream that runs through the Lairs of her subordinate Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, if the Apex is a demon whose hellish pit drips with boiling water (the Corrosive Trait), then is the local mecha-monster's Lair filled with boiling water from hell or toxic battery acid? </div> </div> </div>There's a feature in the parts of the local mecha-monster's Lair that were drawn from within the hive that drips Corrosive boiling water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T20:49:29-08:00","id":1023091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1022592#post1022592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hive Trait of the local Apex applies to all Chambers in that hive, including those incorporated into a Lair. Notably, this means the Apex still can't access another Beast's Heart without going through an intervening Burrow.<br /> <br /> There's a feature in attached Chambers that represents the Hive Trait which Beasts with the appropriate Environmental Immunity and/or permissions can use like Burrows to navigate the hive. A Jenny Greenteeth sort of river-hag might have a stream that runs through the Lairs of her subordinate Beasts.<br /> <br /> There's a feature in the parts of the local mecha-monster's Lair that were drawn from within the hive that drips Corrosive boiling water.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the non-Heart Chambers of lesser Beasts in the hive have an apparently out-of-setting feature that doesn't jive particularly well with the Beast's own theme, and that alien feature hints at the nature of the Apex of the hive?<br /> <br /> Here's an example made of what I understand: The cave-troll's Lair has places where disorienting will-o-wisps are found, despite it being otherwise a pitch-black underground tunnel. Follow the lights without being bewitched by them, and you find yourself in a gigantic marshland filled with half-decaying corpses that spawn off will-o-wisps, which is the Lair of the Apex of the hive that is a giant man-eating alligator. If the alligator permits you, then you can follow the lights again and find yourself in an undersea grotto of a kraken that has angler fish swimming around it, or the magnificent nest of an ogre-king whose corridors are enlaid with alluring jewels.<br /> <br /> Would the above be an appropriate representation of the mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:42:08-08:00","id":1023107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1023091#post1023091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the non-Heart Chambers of lesser Beasts in the hive have an apparently out-of-setting feature that doesn't jive particularly well with the Beast's own theme, and that alien feature hints at the nature of the Apex of the hive?<br /> <br /> Here's an example made of what I understand: The cave-troll's Lair has places where disorienting will-o-wisps are found, despite it being otherwise a pitch-black underground tunnel. Follow the lights without being bewitched by them, and you find yourself in a gigantic marshland filled with half-decaying corpses that spawn off will-o-wisps, which is the Lair of the Apex of the hive that is a giant man-eating alligator. If the alligator permits you, then you can follow the lights again and find yourself in an undersea grotto of a kraken that has angler fish swimming around it, or the magnificent nest of an ogre-king whose corridors are enlaid with alluring jewels.<br /> <br /> Would the above be an appropriate representation of the mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, although it's worth remembering that the feature is not necessarily symbolically alien and the parts of the Lairs that the Hive Trait appends itself to correspond to discrete locations in the material world \u2014 that cave-troll's tunnel Lair itself runs through the city's infamous Murder Overpass and the crawlspace under a local vampire's Haven. Most of the more fantastical vistas in the Primordial Dream correspond to Hearts or the otherworldly inspiration Kinship opens up, and those are generally outside the hive by definition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T22:03:42-08:00","id":1023116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1023107#post1023107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of, although it's worth remembering that the feature is not necessarily symbolically alien and the parts of the Lairs that the Hive Trait appends itself to correspond to discrete locations in the material world \u2014 that cave-troll's tunnel Lair itself runs through the city's infamous Murder Overpass and the crawlspace under a local vampire's Haven. Most of the more fantastical vistas in the Primordial Dream correspond to Hearts or the otherworldly inspiration Kinship opens up, and those are generally outside the hive by definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T02:00:25-08:00","id":1025343,"title":"","content":"1#: Since beast is happy with crossovers, how does it stack up in terms of narrative and mechanical balancing. From what I've experienced in our young game is that beast starts fairly powerful, atavisms and nightmares being somewhat roughly 3 pip powers from something like vampire. However there is small concern in our group if beasts will get quickly (relatively) overshadowed by the non-beasts since there is really no way to upgrade atavisms and nightmares, so when the changelings and vampires will be buying their 5 dot powers, which by themselves probably unlocked 4 other powers for them to use giving them lot of variety, beasts are stuck with same 3 dot equivalents. So if the games run long, do beasts just get left behind in terms of efficiency, unable to contribute against the more powerful enemies the other lines might end up facing. <br /> <br /> 2#: The game masters section of the book describes the two methods of getting new chambers (crit on nightmare vs breaking point) being quite different. It describes crit on nightmare resulting in a basically exact facsimile of the area the event unfolded in, with hints of the nightmare adding flavour in there. However it describes chambers made from breaking point locales as &quot;almost like a second heart, build from fragments of the soul&quot;, and the example given is more fantastic. The question here then is, are these chambers less effective for pathways since they resemble real places less. Honestly this might need more talking through than simple answer but start is a start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:01:59-08:00","id":1025434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xararion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1025343#post1025343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1#: Since beast is happy with crossovers, how does it stack up in terms of narrative and mechanical balancing.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Roughly equivalent to a three-dot power&quot; is an old not-quite-accurate-anymore description of the power level of werewolf Gift Facets. The front-loaded nature of Begotten abilities is there in part to allow you to focus on more prosaic Traits like Attributes, Skills, Merits, and Lair, but it by no means makes effects like Dragonfire or Looming Presence or You Cannot Kill It stop being effective compared to other supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> Beasts are <i>very</i> efficient, given that the vast majority of their powers are either costless or only cost Willpower and their focus on resilience allows them a respectable capacity to adapt by playing to the scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2#: The game masters section of the book describes the two methods of getting new chambers (crit on nightmare vs breaking point) being quite different. </div> </div> </div>Thematically. It goes on to specify that the outcome is mechanically identical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:20:40-08:00","id":1027166,"title":"","content":"The satiety expenditure effect of Needs Must states you can mentally mark someone and track them to the ends of the earth. However, does that only work while you are low satiety? Will the mark vanish at a certain point, or is it permanent? The language is really vague regarding how long it applies for and what makes it differ from the low satiety effect, outside of the number and how it doesn't need to gather satiety for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:07:17-08:00","id":1027787,"title":"","content":"I hate to double post, but I have another question; if a Beast is in an area that's sympathetic to one of their lair traits (such as a Makara with Currents wading through a river, or an Anakim with Sealed Exits in a locked room), can they impose that same trait but under their control? Could the wading Makara use Currents to direct a river to be stronger against particular individuals, or the Anakim use Sealed Exits so even those with the key door couldn't leave the locked room (at least without those from the other side opening it)? The core book simply specifies that you can apply <i>other</i> lair traits, but not the one the current tilt is sympathetic with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:03:07-08:00","id":1028259,"title":"","content":"Question. I have an unfettered beast in my chronicle that has a point where he was murdered that I want my players to find, and try to force their way into his lair. I was going to have them roll Wits + Resolve to open a primordial pathway, with a +1 bonus for each clue they have collected about the unfettered's death.<br /> <br /> Shouldn't there be penalties associated with breaking into another beast lair? I can't find any in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:58:22-08:00","id":1028288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1028259#post1028259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question. I have an unfettered beast in my chronicle that has a point where he was murdered that I want my players to find, and try to force their way into his lair. I was going to have them roll Wits + Resolve to open a primordial pathway, with a +1 bonus for each clue they have collected about the unfettered's death.<br /> <br /> Shouldn't there be penalties associated with breaking into another beast lair? I can't find any in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>No penalties to the dice pool, but they have to deal with the Lair Traits when they arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T20:18:13-08:00","id":1028396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1028288#post1028288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No penalties to the dice pool, but they have to deal with the Lair Traits when they arrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there not even a merit, weird. I guess I'll need to be creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T22:18:30-08:00","id":1028431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1027166#post1027166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The satiety expenditure effect of Needs Must states you can mentally mark someone and track them to the ends of the earth. However, does that only work while you are low satiety? Will the mark vanish at a certain point, or is it permanent? The language is really vague regarding how long it applies for and what makes it differ from the low satiety effect, outside of the number and how it doesn't need to gather satiety for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>A satiety marked target has several difference to it's lower marked counterpart.<br /> <br /> First, as expenditure is not tied to high or low it ends when you stop marking the target, or something forces it, not because you got too full to track it. Second, you can have as many marks as you want and still mark someone for low satiety if you qualify. Third if your target is a living being a satiety marked target can be sense jacked allowing one to locate the target through their perceptions or just use them as a spy. A low satiety just makes you supernaturally good at tracking the person or thing.<br /> <br /> I'd argue you still need to be able to see the target to mark them in either case though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T18:18:06-08:00","id":1028809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1028396#post1028396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there not even a merit, weird. I guess I'll need to be creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's no rules for purposely breaking into another beasts lair outside of a heroes powers. It'd be weird if there was an official merit which helped you do something you homebrewed into the game :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:11:42-08:00","id":1029317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1028431#post1028431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A satiety marked target has several difference to it's lower marked counterpart.<br /> <br /> First, as expenditure is not tied to high or low it ends when you stop marking the target, or something forces it, not because you got too full to track it. Second, you can have as many marks as you want and still mark someone for low satiety if you qualify. Third if your target is a living being a satiety marked target can be sense jacked allowing one to locate the target through their perceptions or just use them as a spy. A low satiety just makes you supernaturally good at tracking the person or thing.<br /> <br /> I'd argue you still need to be able to see the target to mark them in either case though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that; I've got a Beast I've been wanting to play who starts out with Needs Must, and the satiety expenditure part always confused me. I like the concept of marking something you leave out to be stolen so that you can track someone down through it, or someone you love in case someone steals them.<br /> <br /> ...hmmm. That's got Changeling material there. You undergo the Devouring, and with Needs Must mark someone you don't want to lose. You then find overnight the person's no longer there, but that someone has taken their place, and you get a strange inkling to travel through what should be a closet. Through Skeleton Key, you find a strange land full of thorns that reacts to you, and equally strange people who find you terrifying, but decide having you on their side is better than you wild. You learn of Arcadia, of Changelings, of how your special someone was likely taken there. You break down the doors of the realm and take them back, midway through their own failing escape attempt.<br /> <br /> There's something appealing about a living embodiment of nightmares breaking down the doors of a place that embodies the dreams of a force of personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:35:35-08:00","id":1029328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1029317#post1029317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...hmmm. That's got Changeling material there. You undergo the Devouring, and with Needs Must mark someone you don't want to lose. You then find overnight the person's no longer there, but that someone has taken their place, and you get a strange inkling to travel through what should be a closet. Through Skeleton Key, you find a strange land full of thorns that reacts to you, and equally strange people who find you terrifying, but decide having you on their side is better than you wild. You learn of Arcadia, of Changelings, of how your special someone was likely taken there. You break down the doors of the realm and take them back, midway through their own failing escape attempt.<br /> <br /> There's something appealing about a living embodiment of nightmares breaking down the doors of a place that embodies the dreams of a force of personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember someone (ArcaneArts or Satchel, most likely) posting something in the veins of the True Fae essentially being escapists who are in denial of the harsh, cold reality of the outside world. Living nightmares shattering their precious fantasies goes well with that trail of logic. Of course, the Gentry never tolerate having their Precious be taken away from them, so sooner or later they'll come back...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:27:50-08:00","id":1029396,"title":"","content":"Hey you're not playing a collector right if you just let someone walk away with your stuff. I mean I don't care how the gentry convinced the person to come with them they are your friend. Your is a possessive word and that will be respected if you have to burn their home down and salt the earth with freaking cold iron shavings to do it. (nods)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T01:50:06-08:00","id":1029504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1029328#post1029328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember someone (ArcaneArts or Satchel, most likely) posting something in the veins of the True Fae essentially being escapists who are in denial of the harsh, cold reality of the outside world. Living nightmares shattering their precious fantasies goes well with that trail of logic. Of course, the Gentry never tolerate having their Precious be taken away from them, so sooner or later they'll come back...</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, you came into their home and took something of theirs. What stops them from doing the same to your lair?<br /> <br /> Even worse, what is to stop them from moving in after they turn your Horror into a throw rug?<br /> <br /> (Well, I don't think that the Gentry could sustain themselves in the Primordial Dream, but a Beast's lair would probably make a nice prize)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T05:36:52-08:00","id":1029564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1029504#post1029504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worse, you came into their home and took something of theirs. What stops them from doing the same to your lair?<br /> <br /> Even worse, what is to stop them from moving in after they turn your Horror into a throw rug?<br /> <br /> (Well, I don't think that the Gentry could sustain themselves in the Primordial Dream, but a Beast's lair would probably make a nice prize)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And on that note, who's to say the True Fae and Beasts are any different from each other? They both appear to be sentient manifestations of humanity's consciousness. They both have a reality warping realm that shapes itself based on their experiences and tastes, they both sustain themselves on the emotions of mortals, and they both have a powerful basis in mythological creatures. They also both have the capacity to transform others into monsters (Changelings via Durances, and Beasts via Devouring)<br /> .<br /> <br /> The only real difference seems to be that Beasts have adopted a permanent identity for themselves, while True Fae are content to remain abstract and prone to flights of whimsy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T09:06:08-08:00","id":1029618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1029564#post1029564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on that note, who's to say the True Fae and Beasts are any different from each other? They both appear to be sentient manifestations of humanity's consciousness. They both have a reality warping realm that shapes itself based on their experiences and tastes, they both sustain themselves on the emotions of mortals, and they both have a powerful basis in mythological creatures. They also both have the capacity to transform others into monsters (Changelings via Durances, and Beasts via Devouring)<br /> .<br /> <br /> The only real difference seems to be that Beasts have adopted a permanent identity for themselves, while True Fae are content to remain abstract and prone to flights of whimsy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are quite a few differences actually; for a start, as Beasts don't suffer from Iron unless it's an anathema placed on them by a Hero (and even them its only a weakness to particular iron, rather than iron as a whole), they arent Fae like the Gentry and Changelings are. They also don't have a Mask that hides their true selves - they have their human self, which they always had, and their inner Horror, which isn't hidden away so much as on another plane of reality. Same with their fuel; Changelings and, as far as I know, Fae in general can simply draw from emotional energy from a person or that which is in the air itself (provided there's a lot of people around), and though they may have particular tastes that mitigate how much they get, any Fae can get Glamour from any emotion. Beasts, meanwhile, need to get Satiety from terror specifically, and it has to have an impact on others. Further, the more sated a Beast's Horror is, the harder it is to actually get more satiety, whereas Fae aren't limited in this regard in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Regarding the &quot;changing others&quot; aspect, True Fae capture and change a person's very nature, down to their soul, whereas Beasts can either open up the change for someone willing (or potentially unwilling), or it comes naturally to them, with the Horror coming and outright replacing their soul. That's pretty significant, because it's either with consent (if perhaps not knowledge of what one is getting into), or it's just a natural thing like puberty - either way, it needs to have the potential there in order to happen at all. For True Fae...well, let's just say there are a lot of rape analogies that don't take a lot of effort to make when it comes to them.<br /> <br /> Even how they affect dreams is different. A Beast is, well, a thrashing beast inside of a dream. They don't have fine control a Fae does - even the most rudimentary Fae creature can tear a dream apart and put it together into a new configuration, whereas a Beast can only tear it apart (or, at best, make it nightmarish). Beasts are specifically living nightmares, whereas the Gentry have access to all dreaming. A Beast's Horror is near never clever, whereas a True Fae can run circles around geniuses...if with the danger of dizzying themselves, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> Really, though True Fae and Beasts have a lot similarities, they're more skin deep than anything else. They just happen to be terrifying creatures wh affect the local dreamscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-10-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:44:08-08:00","id":1029798,"title":"","content":"Very stupid question I'm sure. Where in the book does it discuss feeding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","ava