a lot of effort to make when it comes to them.<br /> <br /> Even how they affect dreams is different. A Beast is, well, a thrashing beast inside of a dream. They don't have fine control a Fae does - even the most rudimentary Fae creature can tear a dream apart and put it together into a new configuration, whereas a Beast can only tear it apart (or, at best, make it nightmarish). Beasts are specifically living nightmares, whereas the Gentry have access to all dreaming. A Beast's Horror is near never clever, whereas a True Fae can run circles around geniuses...if with the danger of dizzying themselves, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> Really, though True Fae and Beasts have a lot similarities, they're more skin deep than anything else. They just happen to be terrifying creatures wh affect the local dreamscape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick correction, a horror can be intelligent. It's just really unlikely, but Mimir's wisdom does exist for a reason and it is mentioned that sometimes things like the anakim are terrifying because they appear to have figured you out and you can't think them. (Not the exact words, but it is mentioned briefly in the book.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:31:52-08:00","id":1030725,"title":"","content":"Would you allow the Satiety Expenditure effect of Infestation to count as the Swarms Trait for the purposes of imposing Traits, opening Primordial Pathways, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:39:32-08:00","id":1030728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1030725#post1030725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you allow the Satiety Expenditure effect of Infestation to count as the Swarms Trait for the purposes of imposing Traits, opening Primordial Pathways, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would. The book seems to give a lot of leeway in how the initial environment is created, so I don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:53:04-08:00","id":1031716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1028809#post1028809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's no rules for purposely breaking into another beasts lair outside of a heroes powers. It'd be weird if there was an official merit which helped you do something you homebrewed into the game :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Im just suprised that the book is written in such a way that another beast can just wander into your lair without any clash of wills or some sort of extended action or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:48:57-08:00","id":1031884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1031716#post1031716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im just suprised that the book is written in such a way that another beast can just wander into your lair without any clash of wills or some sort of extended action or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't &quot;just wander into your lair&quot;. You would have to make a primordial pathway to your lair to give the other beast access to your lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T17:11:21-08:00","id":1031890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1031884#post1031884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't &quot;just wander into your lair&quot;. You would have to make a primordial pathway to your lair to give the other beast access to your lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm really confused... So, lets say a antagonistic beast wanted to intrude on your lair. What would happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T17:47:47-08:00","id":1031899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1031890#post1031890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm really confused... So, lets say a antagonistic beast wanted to intrude on your lair. What would happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might stalk you until you open a primordial pathway to your lair and try to sneak in while it's open or it might just visciously attack you until you make a primordial path for the &quot;merge with horror&quot; buff and charge into another chamber of your lair. Once in your lair it follows the intruder rules from page 98. The antagonistic beast has to deal with your lair traits, and moving between the chambers takes a point of willpower and an intelligence + Resolve roll contested by your Horror\u2019s Power + Resistance. But if you never leave the door open for the other beast, then they will never get in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:11:36-08:00","id":1031989,"title":"","content":"Actually the section on Brood Lairs on p. 43 seems pretty relevant. Pretty much all the other Beast needs to do is be a stalker and win a Clash of Wills and then you're hosed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:31:49-08:00","id":1033600,"title":"","content":"With &quot;be my guest&quot; you can enter and leave a beasts lair as a beast can. Does this mean that you can access other realms than the material from a beasts lair by using primordial pathways? <br /> <br /> Sorry if this has already been asked I just realized that this could have interesting implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:59:08-08:00","id":1033621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1033600#post1033600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With &quot;be my guest&quot; you can enter and leave a beasts lair as a beast can. Does this mean that you can access other realms than the material from a beasts lair by using primordial pathways?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this has already been asked I just realized that this could have interesting implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicit statement doesn't currently exist on the books, but my reading is that you use the same mechanics as your host Beast does for opening Primordial Pathways, including bonuses for Lair Traits and penalties for world and Chamber similarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T19:46:07-08:00","id":1035592,"title":"","content":"My table was bit confused about this. How do looming presence and horrors increased size affect health. I've understood that looming doesn't apply to you when you're merged. Or I've been entirely mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:47:52-08:00","id":1035622,"title":"","content":"It does say, 'Greater size produces a commensurate increase in Health.' So since Health is Size + Stamina, and Looming Presence increases Size by Lair, your Health would instead be Size + Stamina + Lair.<br /> <br /> When you're Rampant, you lose your Lair Attribute, which is what most of Looming Presence is based on. I think it's technically possible to get some of the benefits from the Atavism, the 'after any successful attack' bit, but then it's mostly useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T22:41:17-08:00","id":1035631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1035622#post1035622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does say, 'Greater size produces a commensurate increase in Health.' So since Health is Size + Stamina, and Looming Presence increases Size by Lair, your Health would instead be Size + Stamina + Lair.<br /> <br /> When you're Rampant, you lose your Lair Attribute, which is what most of Looming Presence is based on. I think it's technically possible to get some of the benefits from the Atavism, the 'after any successful attack' bit, but then it's mostly useless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looming Presence is an Atavism, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Rampant Beasts can still access their Atavisms, they're allowing their horror to physically enter and merge with their bodies. They lose access to their Nightmare powers, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, one of the example Rampants in the book actually has Looming Presence, although it does nothing to explain how it works for her.<br /> <br /> <br /> My guess is that Looming Presence effectively gives you whatever your lair was at the time of Inheritance, but can't be increased further.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-21-2017, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T22:54:31-08:00","id":1035633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1035631#post1035631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rampant Beasts can still access their Atavisms, they're allowing their horror to physically enter and merge with their bodies. They lose access to their Nightmare powers, though.<br /> <br /> My guess is that Looming Presence effectively gives you whatever your lair was at the time of Inheritance, but can't be increased further.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do still get their Atavisms. But for instance, 'The Beast's actual height and weight are unchanged, but his <i>effective</i> Size is raised by (his Lair dots).' And 'Any opponent whose Size is less than the Beast' effective Size suffers a penalty to all attacks against their character equal to half the Beast's Lair, rounded up.' With no Lair or even Lair 0 you wouldn't get anything from it.<br /> <br /> I don't think a Rampant Beast would keep these benefits as if they still had a Lair. Part of the whole problem with the Rampants is that the Horror has destroyed its Lair, trying to basically Claim its human host so it can run rampant. They can still be big, as the warping effect of Rampancy can justify Size changes, but you're no longer channeling a Horror from the Primordial Dream, it's there in your ill fitting human suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T00:08:29-08:00","id":1035642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1035633#post1035633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do still get their Atavisms. But for instance, 'The Beast's actual height and weight are unchanged, but his <i>effective</i> Size is raised by (his Lair dots).' And 'Any opponent whose Size is less than the Beast' effective Size suffers a penalty to all attacks against their character equal to half the Beast's Lair, rounded up.' With no Lair or even Lair 0 you wouldn't get anything from it.<br /> <br /> I don't think a Rampant Beast would keep these benefits as if they still had a Lair. Part of the whole problem with the Rampants is that the Horror has destroyed its Lair, trying to basically Claim its human host so it can run rampant. They can still be big, as the warping effect of Rampancy can justify Size changes, but you're no longer channeling a Horror from the Primordial Dream, it's there in your ill fitting human suit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And that sounds like a problem. because most, if not all, of their powers are based around how high their Lair rating is at the time. Having a Lair of 0 would effectively mean any of those powers become completely useless. Hence my thoughts on how their Lair is considered to be functionally halted at whatever rating it was prior to going Rampant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> Alien Allure - Adds your Lair dots to Manipulation<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, becoming Rampant does get an optional bonus to Skills and Attributes based on how high your Lair was prior to Inheritance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-21-2017, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T00:47:39-08:00","id":1035654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1035642#post1035642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that sounds like a problem. because most, if not all, of their powers are based around how high their Lair rating is at the time. Having a Lair of 0 would effectively mean any of those powers become completely useless. Hence my thoughts on how their Lair is considered to be functionally halted at whatever rating it was prior to going Rampant.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> Alien Allure - Adds your Lair dots to Manipulation</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a variety of other bonuses that don't work off of Lair. Always starting with a good first impression. And they keep Satiety, so they get those abilities as well. So opening Doors imposes the Charmed Condition, Social roll Exceptional Successes on 3 instead of 5. And so forth.<br /> <br /> Rampant are Beasts at their worst, it seems to be the point. They're not player characters anymore, it's like a draugr or first edition's zi'ir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, becoming Rampant does get an optional bonus to Skills and Attributes based on how high your Lair was prior to Inheritance. </div> </div> </div>There's a variety of bonuses they can get per dot of Lair, I'd suggest you could give them some Dread Powers as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T08:04:02-08:00","id":1037842,"title":"","content":"How do beasts categorize horrors in relation to family resemblance?<br /> <br /> Edit: Chronicles of Darkness horrors, not beast horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:59:32-08:00","id":1037887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1037842#post1037842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do beasts categorize horrors in relation to family resemblance?<br /> <br /> Edit: Chronicles of Darkness horrors, not beast horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, CofD Horrors are such a wide and varied bunch that it probably depends on the specifics. They probably wouldn't consider the evil wishing well Kin because it's a wet hole in the ground, but they'd probably be bros with the Jersey Devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:42:31-08:00","id":1038160,"title":"","content":"This is a bit of a weird question: if a Beast falls in love with someone, and that person has access to their lair, would their Horror also share that love? What if two Beasts in a Brood were to fall in love? I doubt it'd make the monstrous sabretooth tiger into a loveable kitten for your love, but maybe it'd choose not to hunt them down, or even intimidate them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:46:40-08:00","id":1038165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1038160#post1038160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit of a weird question: if a Beast falls in love with someone, and that person has access to their lair, would their Horror also share that love? What if two Beasts in a Brood were to fall in love? I doubt it'd make the monstrous sabretooth tiger into a loveable kitten for your love, but maybe it'd choose not to hunt them down, or even intimidate them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that defies the 'simple' part of 'ask a simple question.' But it gives me an image of two Gorged Horrors cuddling in a Chamber somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T21:36:17-08:00","id":1038263,"title":"","content":"I don't think so. From what I remember of the chapter fictions and the anthology Horrors don't seem capable of love or at all concerned with the social connection a Beast might have to someone it wants to eat. At best giving someone unrestricted access to the Lair means the Horror will treat them as a guest and allow them to visit freely.<br /> <br /> That said, Beasts and their Horrors do share a pretty intimate connection and I could see there being a bit of emotional bleedthrough in rare cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T22:39:21-08:00","id":1038274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1037887#post1037887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, CofD Horrors are such a wide and varied bunch that it probably depends on the specifics. They probably wouldn't consider the evil wishing well Kin because it's a wet hole in the ground, but they'd probably be bros with the Jersey Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny you should bring that up... the Jersey Devil is an example Apex in the book, and Beast try to avoid them nearly as much as mortals do. Probably because the one who's believed to be the Jersey Devil has a habit of strangling people to death if they can't solve her riddles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1038160#post1038160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit of a weird question: if a Beast falls in love with someone, and that person has access to their lair, would their Horror also share that love? What if two Beasts in a Brood were to fall in love? I doubt it'd make the monstrous sabretooth tiger into a loveable kitten for your love, but maybe it'd choose not to hunt them down, or even intimidate them?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the Horror is sated, I think you retain your self control while inside your Lair. So if you love them in your human form, you should be able to love them in your Horror form.<br /> <br /> You just have to work out the mechanics of doing anything romantic while in the form of a monster. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-26-2017, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:51:22-08:00","id":1038394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1038274#post1038274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Funny you should bring that up... the Jersey Devil is an example Apex in the book, and Beast try to avoid them nearly as much as mortals do. Probably because the one who's believed to be the Jersey Devil has a habit of strangling people to death if they can't solve her riddles.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I'm talking about the Jersey Devil Horror written up in the Chronicles of Darkness core book because he's my favorite take on the character in the CofD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T15:40:54-08:00","id":1040249,"title":"","content":"I know I'm corrupting the purpose of this thread, but is there an ETA on the POD version of the Beast condition cards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:13:27-08:00","id":1041553,"title":"","content":"Can Heroes gain access to supernatural Merits (such as psychokinesis), or does their Heroic nature mean they're now considered a supernatural template?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm asking because one idea I had for a Hero is a kid who manifests Geokinesis after waking up from a car accident in which a Beast had been behind the wheel of the vehicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:18:27-08:00","id":1041710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1041553#post1041553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Heroes gain access to supernatural Merits (such as psychokinesis), or does their Heroic nature mean they're now considered a supernatural template?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm asking because one idea I had for a Hero is a kid who manifests Geokinesis after waking up from a car accident in which a Beast had been behind the wheel of the vehicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule the latter and ban Supernatural Merits. It also feels fitting for a Hero to think of himself above such parlor tricks of lesser men.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a Hero getting blessed by some benefactor or channeling a magic item to access supernatural power feels also fitting, only to turn out that those blessings and magic items are actually his own power (in the form of Gifts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:50:02-08:00","id":1041828,"title":"","content":"Whether minor templates can have supernatural merits seems to be a case by case basis. The only real rule is do whatever will make your game more fun, but as far as precedent goes one of the Heroes in Conquering Heroes is also a Proximi.<br /> I'm on the side of allowing template stacking, although I'd limit it to Hero +1. There are a lot of cool powers in Hurt Locker, and expanding your options will keep your players guessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:31:39-08:00","id":1042080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1041553#post1041553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Heroes gain access to supernatural Merits (such as psychokinesis), or does their Heroic nature mean they're now considered a supernatural template?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm asking because one idea I had for a Hero is a kid who manifests Geokinesis after waking up from a car accident in which a Beast had been behind the wheel of the vehicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would get more mileage out of your concept if you have a Hero help the geokinetic kid out of the car and bring them along for the Beast hunt. Don't forget that Heroes frequently will have followers. Direct to the question, I think they are a supernatural template and it then falls to you whether to allow the merit anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T00:05:56-08:00","id":1042259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1041553#post1041553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Heroes gain access to supernatural Merits (such as psychokinesis), or does their Heroic nature mean they're now considered a supernatural template?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Hero can be a Proximus (as Conquering Heroes suggests), I don't see why they couldn't have supernatural Merits. They can't have Advanced/Epic Merits normally, though, since [REDACTED].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:31:52-08:00","id":1042277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1042259#post1042259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Hero can be a Proximus (as Conquering Heroes suggests), I don't see why they couldn't have supernatural Merits. They can't have Advanced/Epic Merits normally, though, since [REDACTED].</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, do they get a powered-up version of their template that can gain Advanced/Epic Merits, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:18:16-08:00","id":1042297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1042277#post1042277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, do they get a powered-up version of their template that can gain Advanced/Epic Merits, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>[REDACTED] until Matt chooses to do some spoilers for the Player's Guide, but you shall see soon enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T05:02:19-08:00","id":1042352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1042259#post1042259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Hero can be a Proximus (as Conquering Heroes suggests), I don't see why they couldn't have supernatural Merits. They can't have Advanced/Epic Merits normally, though, since [REDACTED].</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know what a Proximus is. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T05:35:20-08:00","id":1042356,"title":"","content":"A Proximus is a Mage demisplat. They're able to learn and cast a small handful of Mage spells but they aren't Awakened and can't use creative thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T06:10:34-08:00","id":1042367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1042356#post1042356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Proximus is a Mage demisplat. They're able to learn and cast a small handful of Mage spells but they aren't Awakened and can't use creative thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, then in that case I'd personally rule that Geokinesis was a possibility. Another part of the concept I had for him is that since he's a kid, he perceives himself to be a real life super hero and uses his powers to take down the villains (Beasts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:08:50-08:00","id":1042546,"title":"","content":"Proximi are mortals so if one can be a Hero then Heroes must be mortal also. That would mean they can take supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:43:49-08:00","id":1042942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1042546#post1042546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Proximi are mortals so if one can be a Hero then Heroes must be mortal also. That would mean they can take supernatural merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only hint as to them not being mortal is that their life span eventually begins to increase after killing a certain number of Beasts. It even says they can live for centuries, but they need to keep killing Beasts to sustain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:28:01-08:00","id":1043292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1042942#post1042942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The only hint as to them not being mortal is that their life span eventually begins to increase after killing a certain number of Beasts. It even says they can live for centuries, but they need to keep killing Beasts to sustain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a reference to mortality. Mortals is the term used to describe people that aren't supernatural types. Major and minor templates are not relevant terms in the way they were. A ghoul is a supernatural while a proximi is a mortal. A mage is mortal (grows old and dies just like a muggle) but a supernatural type. I had the impression that Heroes were a supernatural type, but that appears to not be the case. I don't know the rule to distinguish between a supernatural mortal and a supernatural person. Heroes fall into the former category apparently. Mortals are allowed supernatural merits whether they have supernatural abilities or not. The supernatural types are not allowed the merits, unless overruled by ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:38:23-08:00","id":1045552,"title":"","content":"It says Insatiable gain the benefits identical to that of beasts who undergo the merger, but those benefits are purely based on trading away lair that the insatiable doesn't have unless they've stolen a lair and the insatiable statblocks don't have any of the merger benefits at all... So what are the benefit's it's getting from the merger rules?<br /> <br /> Also what action is it for an Insatiable to take their horrible form? It says it works like the Merger, but Rampant cannot change between forms. And then later there is the Terrible Form power which seems to be identical to Horrible Form in all ways except for name so I'm abit confused.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit1</b>: How do Insatiable steal atavisms from beasts that they've taken lairs from? Only thing I can see to steal atavism's is Your Power Is Mine, which isn't limited to beasts you've take the lairs of.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit2</b>: This reminds me, do rampant use their old lair to determine the power of atavisms which scale with lair or do those atavisms now become useless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-07-2017, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T19:16:05-08:00","id":1045567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1045552#post1045552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then later there is the Terrible Form power which seems to be identical to Horrible Form in all ways except for name so I'm abit confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrible Form enhances the normal effect of the Horrible Form from &quot;spending a scene or more in this creature's company gives you Shaken and makes you want to leave&quot; to &quot;looking at this creature gives you Shaken immediately and makes you want to leave by any means necessary.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T17:55:37-08:00","id":1046554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1045567#post1045567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrible Form enhances the normal effect of the Horrible Form from &quot;spending a scene or more in this creature's company gives you Shaken and makes you want to leave&quot; to &quot;looking at this creature gives you Shaken immediately and makes you want to leave by any means necessary.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:33:05-08:00","id":1048422,"title":"","content":"Would it break anything if you could exempt characters you have Family Ties with from your Lair Traits the same way you can exempt other Beasts who share your Lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T04:15:35-08:00","id":1048660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1048422#post1048422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it break anything if you could exempt characters you have Family Ties with from your Lair Traits the same way you can exempt other Beasts who share your Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, making vampires or prometheans immune to burning for example might be a bit over the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:03:46-08:00","id":1048676,"title":"","content":"You can only exempt allies from your Lair Traits specifically, it doesn't protect against any other instance of the tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:41:56-08:00","id":1048697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1048676#post1048676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only exempt allies from your Lair Traits specifically, it doesn't protect against any other instance of the tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And even then, they only gain a resistance to the lair, unless you give them free reign to come and go as they please. And that's an extreme display of trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:56:23-08:00","id":1048750,"title":"","content":"I should clarify: I'm talking about how when imposing Lair Traits (page 101) you can spend a willpower point to exempt your broodmates. This is a really neat trick that can allow a Brood to make fights incredibly one sided but it's pretty useless in a mixed troupe game. I think Be My Guest is probably a better restriction than Family Ties if I open it to being used on other supernats, that's the closest you get to sharing a Lair with a non-Beast and requires more investment and risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T14:10:11-08:00","id":1048923,"title":"","content":"Two Questions:<br /> <br /> Since killing is now always an Integrity Breaking Point, do Heroes still have to roll Breaking Points if they kill a Beast? Or are Beasts an exception, since Heroes see them as pure evil? Actually, do they take Integrity Breaking Points from killing other supernaturals?<br /> <br /> Is there anything else that can make a Beast lose Satiety other than time, Lair Healing or Satiety expenditure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:41:41-08:00","id":1049225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1048923#post1048923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two Questions:<br /> <br /> Since killing is now always an Integrity Breaking Point, do Heroes still have to roll Breaking Points if they kill a Beast? Or are Beasts an exception, since Heroes see them as pure evil? Actually, do they take Integrity Breaking Points from killing other supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't remember the rules (or if there is one at all), but I'd say they get a hefty dice bonus when they kill Beasts or other supernaturals in accordance to their Legend trait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there anything else that can make a Beast lose Satiety other than time, Lair Healing or Satiety expenditure? </div> </div> </div>Once again, no idea on the official rule, but it'd be nice for some Heroes or the Insatiate to have something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:17:05-08:00","id":1049379,"title":"","content":"This might not be such a simple question, but how does the Eye of Heaven Atavism actually manifest in-character? Is it like visions you see in your dreams and only later understand, when you stand in front of whoever it was that you saw? Is it an instinctive certainty that if you strike just <i>here</i>, you'll get through the armour?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:09:23-08:00","id":1054630,"title":"","content":"Do new Beasts instinctively know what Nightmares and Atavisms they have? Or at least instinctively use them at first when they are threatened or hungry for fear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:25:40-08:00","id":1054794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1054630#post1054630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do new Beasts instinctively know what Nightmares and Atavisms they have? Or at least instinctively use them at first when they are threatened or hungry for fear?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well atavisms are actually physical. In the case of most Beasts, and probably the majority of atavisms, you'd know your atavisms by just knowing what your Horror is. &quot;I'm going to assume I have rending claws.&quot; &quot;Why?&quot; &quot;Well my Horror has freaking surgical scalpels embeded into the pads of it's fingers. So call it a hunch.&quot; <br /> <br /> Your starting nightmares I'd say are sort of representative of your own understanding of fear. So a Beast who was always worried about not being in control might start with &quot;You must Obey&quot; because they understand the terror of not being in control and they can use their connection to the dream to spread it to others they can connect with. Not necessarily instinctive, but I'd say one needs a solid grasp of why that is scary, so they would have kind of an understanding about what they can use based on feeling capable of teaching or reminding others of that fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:32:01-08:00","id":1054800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1049379#post1049379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might not be such a simple question, but how does the Eye of Heaven Atavism actually manifest in-character? Is it like visions you see in your dreams and only later understand, when you stand in front of whoever it was that you saw? Is it an instinctive certainty that if you strike just <i>here</i>, you'll get through the armour?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would imagine it's a combination of heightened empathy and psycho analysis. You observe and scan the target and learn what you're looking for based on their body language and actions. Of course if you want to relate it to being scary, you could pull off the Hannibal Lecter approach of dropping deep, personal information about somebody during a conversation with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:36:14-08:00","id":1054802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1054794#post1054794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well atavisms are actually physical. In the case of most Beasts, and probably the majority of atavisms, you'd know your atavisms by just knowing what your Horror is. &amp;quot;I'm going to assume I have rending claws.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Why?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Well my Horror has freaking surgical scalpels embeded into the pads of it's fingers. So call it a hunch.&amp;quot; .</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work with an Atavism like Mimir's Wisdom, though? And where do Atavisms bought after Character Creation come from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:39:21-08:00","id":1054805,"title":"","content":"Could a Collector gain Satiety for playing Bridge Troll and demanding an item of great emotional significance as a toll for entry to a certain place? Or does that come under the &quot;trades don't count&quot; rule","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:16:42-08:00","id":1054825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1054802#post1054802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does that work with an Atavism like Mimir's Wisdom, though? And where do Atavisms bought after Character Creation come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would know things. You might realize that your memory has suddenly improved and that seeing through deception is easy for you now, occasionally you know things you have no possible way of knowing just because you wondered it. If you're low satiety you suddenly know something horrible about anyone you bump into. <br /> <br /> Mind you this would also depend on how it's played. Afterall it would be pretty easy to guess that your insights into people lying to you are in some way derived from your Horror if someone lying to you is met with the phantasmal voice of your Horror in your mind whispering, &quot;It lies. You know why it lies. It thinks no one witnessed it, but we know. We always know.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for where later ones come from. That would depend on how you're playing it again. For example your Horror and you are now feeding much better and have a more significant impact on the world around it which feeds back into the Primordial Dream. Consequently the Horror is affected by it's own legend and how it reverberates in the Primordial Dream and so as your Horror becomes more powerful it evolves in new ways. Suddenly those claws are dripping with some kind of toxin that paralyzes the victims because the nightmares of that thing include people being so scared they couldn't move.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you go a different way. Your Horror is this abomination of a spider monster, massive, chitin that looks like it was forged to be used on a particularly durable tank rather than a living creature, it's fangs drip venom so potent they dissolve the very rocks they drip on, it has no eyes yet it can wrap a gnat in webbing from easily over 200 feet and with such precision that not a single strand of webbing is away from the minimal amount of area to wrap the insect, and it doesn't stick to the walls of it's chamber so much as it punctures the rock with it's legs to climb. So you've got that thing and you're not exactly close to it because that thing has been haunting your nightmares since you were 3 and the knowledge that it might actually be what you have in place of a human soul unnerves you a little so you want to keep your distance as much as possible. As a consequence you only started with Needs Must because this thing is always looking for food and since it's part of you then you are now acutely aware of when you walk past lunch. Of course that venom is always dripping from it's maw, so you have Basilisk's Touch as well owing to your ability to draw on the excess venom and distribute it as needed. You feed when you have to then you get into a few bad scuffles, you get screwed up royally after a a fight with a werewolf (who knew those were a thing) you and it are closer owing to it and you being very much in agreement about not wanting to die. The new closeness allows you to draw on the things monsterous chitin to protect yourself from harm as you gain the Unbreakable atavism. You know that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also to your question on the bridge troll that's called extortion or purchase. You aren't giving anything up and the person is giving it up because they have to in order to advance. At the very least I'd say it would be allowable for lower satiety feeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:23:54-08:00","id":1054938,"title":"","content":"that make senses. About the second question though. What if the place they are trying to get to is a place they want to get into desperately, but don't really need to get into, like the best club in town?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:51:35-08:00","id":1055030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1054938#post1054938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that make senses. About the second question though. What if the place they are trying to get to is a place they want to get into desperately, but don't really need to get into, like the best club in town?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I'd still say it's you charging them. You aren't giving them anything save entrance. Which you're doing in more of a manner of &quot;I step to the side and let them passed,&quot; then &quot;I give them the keys to open the door.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:59:47-08:00","id":1055202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1054805#post1054805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Collector gain Satiety for playing Bridge Troll and demanding an item of great emotional significance as a toll for entry to a certain place? Or does that come under the &quot;trades don't count&quot; rule</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's not a trade, that's protection money. It's like saying &quot;pay up, or bad stuff might happen to you.&quot; when trying to cross the area they're guarding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:36:50-08:00","id":1055252,"title":"","content":"Good to hear. My Anakim Collector is a-go","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T05:55:55-08:00","id":1055609,"title":"","content":"This has probably been answered in the book itself, but I haven't been able to locate it specifically: How do Major Lair traits work? Some of them appear to be new features, while others are just enhanced versions of Minor traits. Do you acquire them as upgrades to lesser traits, or do they cost more to purchase later on?<br /> <br /> I'm curious, because I'm not really sure what's keeping a Beast from loading themselves up with a bunch of Major traits early on, and coming across as being somewhat overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T06:27:27-08:00","id":1055620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1055609#post1055609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been answered in the book itself, but I haven't been able to locate it specifically: How do Major Lair traits work? Some of them appear to be new features, while others are just enhanced versions of Minor traits. Do you acquire them as upgrades to lesser traits, or do they cost more to purchase later on?<br /> <br /> I'm curious, because I'm not really sure what's keeping a Beast from loading themselves up with a bunch of Major traits early on, and coming across as being somewhat overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>you can get either minor or Major Lair Traits (and you can only have very few of them, depending on your Lair ranking) , the difference is the gap in power for one and also the difficulty in invoking them. E.g. getting Burning with the highest amount of damage (really Hot and big flames) would make it really hard to use that tilt to call down Darkness. Absolute darkness likewise is something rarely encountered, Thus it Would Be hard to use that to use the burning tilt.<br /> Generally, one tilt needs to be present so you can call down one of your other tilts. Minor traits are relative common, so make it easier to use the Major ones.<br /> You need to have at least one minor Lair trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:49:42-08:00","id":1055651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1055620#post1055620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you can get either minor or Major Lair Traits (and you can only have very few of them, depending on your Lair ranking) , the difference is the gap in power for one and also the difficulty in invoking them. E.g. getting Burning with the highest amount of damage (really Hot and big flames) would make it really hard to use that tilt to call down Darkness. Absolute darkness likewise is something rarely encountered, Thus it Would Be hard to use that to use the burning tilt.<br /> Generally, one tilt needs to be present so you can call down one of your other tilts. Minor traits are relative common, so make it easier to use the Major ones.<br /> You need to have at least one minor Lair trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, thank you for clearing that up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:09:48-08:00","id":1056863,"title":"","content":"How does the Forum feel about the Dream merits from Tooth and Nail, particularly Dream Avatar and Ephemeral Fetish merits? Personally, Dream Avatar strikes me as risky to include, but does create space for interesting character archetypes, while Ephemeral Fetish opens up lots of stories and is almost a perfect fit for most of the Collectors I've seen on the Character Idea thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:30:32-08:00","id":1059838,"title":"","content":"The beasts can feed from nightmares?<br /> In other words, a beast can go to his lair and then walk around to find a victim? Or just the low-satiety horror can do this?<br /> Also, Atavism and Nightmares work in the physical plane, but they work in the same way in the dreams?<br /> And if a beast can walk thought the dreams, it can change things in a fred grugrer fashion or it's limited by it's powers and capacities?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:18:29-08:00","id":1059940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1059838#post1059838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beasts can feed from nightmares?<br /> In other words, a beast can go to his lair and then walk around to find a victim? Or just the low-satiety horror can do this?<br /> Also, Atavism and Nightmares work in the physical plane, but they work in the same way in the dreams?<br /> And if a beast can walk thought the dreams, it can change things in a fred grugrer fashion or it's limited by it's powers and capacities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay a Beast can feed on people who've ended up in the Lair. So if some group of muggers jumps an Anakim and he overlays his lair with the area and one slips into the lair proper then I'm saying they're fair game for feeding. There is no mechanical support for a Beast sending their Horror out to feed in the Primordial Dream aside from it doing so during the heavy starvation period.<br /> <br /> Providing you aren't suffering the starving or ravenous tilts merging with your Horror allows you to use any level of an atavism, though you still have to pay satiety if you want to use the satiety level of an atavism. I'm not so sure on Nightmares, part of me thinks Nightmares aren't usable in the merged state, but I can't recall if I read that anywhere or not.<br /> <br /> Now as far entering dreams goes. First just because it's been mentioned no altering anything in a dream/lair doesn't alter how it is in the real world even if your lair is of an active location. If you're talking like entering another person's dream of being at the mall and because you're a makara suddenly the sprinklers go off and flood the place, and when they try to escape you make the pipes rip out of the ground and restrain them. Honestly nothing I've read suggests that a Beast enters another person's dreams like that. The stuff I've read suggest more often that it's less infiltrating someone elses' dreams and more dragging them into a part of the Primordial Dream controlled by your Horror. So that would probably be more of an ST decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:24:28-08:00","id":1059943,"title":"","content":"Another one, players have to limit to the merits that is on the beast book? For instance, a beast can have aura reading?<br /> Also, you can use merits to increase skills or just experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T22:33:00-08:00","id":1059948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1059943#post1059943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one, players have to limit to the merits that is on the beast book? For instance, a beast can have aura reading?<br /> Also, you can use merits to increase skills or just experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright generally speaking you'll always want to check with your ST when adding out of splat merits. This is partially a courtesy thing as it can get confusing if your Beast has nonsplat specific merits from a bunch of different lines. Or just in case the ST doesn't have the book the merit is from and so might have problems there.<br /> <br /> A Beast can't have aura reading though. Aura Reading is listed as a supernatural merit in the CoD core and that points out that none of the merits in that subsection are possessable by a supernatural. It specifically says &quot;If the character becomes a vampire, ghoul, mage, or any other supernatural the merit disappears.&quot; Then sanctity of merits kicks in and all, but yeah you'd need a lot more ST permission to get them to let your character have a merit they don't qualify for.<br /> <br /> The last bit can you clarify what you mean? Merits usually say if they add anything to a skill and you don't really spend merits unless sanctity kicks in, so I'm not sure what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:19:10-08:00","id":1060095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1059948#post1059948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright generally speaking you'll always want to check with your ST when adding out of splat merits. This is partially a courtesy thing as it can get confusing if your Beast has nonsplat specific merits from a bunch of different lines. Or just in case the ST doesn't have the book the merit is from and so might have problems there.<br /> <br /> A Beast can't have aura reading though. Aura Reading is listed as a supernatural merit in the CoD core and that points out that none of the merits in that subsection are possessable by a supernatural. It specifically says &quot;If the character becomes a vampire, ghoul, mage, or any other supernatural the merit disappears.&quot; Then sanctity of merits kicks in and all, but yeah you'd need a lot more ST permission to get them to let your character have a merit they don't qualify for.<br /> <br /> The last bit can you clarify what you mean? Merits usually say if they add anything to a skill and you don't really spend merits unless sanctity kicks in, so I'm not sure what you mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>i can convert a merit point in xp?<br /> And i am talking more about the core CoD book merits, like combat styles (it's seems that they really take almost all merits that make sense a beast have, but why they don't take the combat styles?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T09:31:48-08:00","id":1060133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1060095#post1060095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i can convert a merit point in xp?<br /> And i am talking more about the core CoD book merits, like combat styles (it's seems that they really take almost all merits that make sense a beast have, but why they don't take the combat styles?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 43 of the CoD book, dude. By default Sanctity of merits functions a you replace a lost merit at the end of the chapter with another merit. &quot;Cashing in&quot; as the book refers to it is something you do with Storyteller permission and of course when it makes sense. Afterall it's one thing if your character has secured a powerful ally and decides they no longer need their secondary safe house, not so much on deciding you no loner need to know how to speak Spanish. <br /> <br /> As for the second bit, like I said generally you ask your ST as a courtesy. Stuff like the CoD book are rarely going to get ruled out unless the ST feels like it goes against the theme of the planned story. For example the story is the brood have been forced to go to ground hard and have had to flee your hometown, let's say Detroit if needed, so now you're all hiding out in Morocco because you all are at least at the basic conversational level in Arabic, but you don't know anyone, you have no allies, and it's supposed to be isolated and not sure who you can trust outside of the circle. Since isolation is meant to be a theme and point in the story your ST would be justified in saying you can't start out with a set of retainers.<br /> <br /> This is because The CoD book is meant for the setting as a whole, so generally speaking it is meant to be a secondary source of merits, items, and information that would just clutter up a splat book to include all of it. But you'd want to check if you were going to grab Dark Triad social merit from the mage book then your ST might very well decide against letting you have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:01:07-08:00","id":1060150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1060133#post1060133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 43 of the CoD book, dude. By default Sanctity of merits functions a you replace a lost merit at the end of the chapter with another merit. &quot;Cashing in&quot; as the book refers to it is something you do with Storyteller permission and of course when it makes sense. Afterall it's one thing if your character has secured a powerful ally and decides they no longer need their secondary safe house, not so much on deciding you no loner need to know how to speak Spanish.<br /> <br /> As for the second bit, like I said generally you ask your ST as a courtesy. Stuff like the CoD book are rarely going to get ruled out unless the ST feels like it goes against the theme of the planned story. For example the story is the brood have been forced to go to ground hard and have had to flee your hometown, let's say Detroit if needed, so now you're all hiding out in Morocco because you all are at least at the basic conversational level in Arabic, but you don't know anyone, you have no allies, and it's supposed to be isolated and not sure who you can trust outside of the circle. Since isolation is meant to be a theme and point in the story your ST would be justified in saying you can't start out with a set of retainers.<br /> <br /> This is because The CoD book is meant for the setting as a whole, so generally speaking it is meant to be a secondary source of merits, items, and information that would just clutter up a splat book to include all of it. But you'd want to check if you were going to grab Dark Triad social merit from the mage book then your ST might very well decide against letting you have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, ty.<br /> But i am the ST, just get some guidings because i am new to CoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T07:46:06-07:00","id":1061822,"title":"","content":"can astral beings (besides Beasts) manifest physically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:31:32-07:00","id":1061831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1061822#post1061822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can astral beings (besides Beasts) manifest physically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Goetia can't Manifest at all in normal circumstances and usually don't even leave the Astral without magical assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T18:04:20-07:00","id":1062103,"title":"","content":"They don't normally leave the Astral, but one of the mysteries presented in Mage 2E is goetia that do leave the astral and pop out in Los Angeles. Some even possess people despite goetia not normally having any kinds of Manifestations.<br /> But usually all goetia stay in the astral where they belong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T21:55:45-07:00","id":1062167,"title":"","content":"Can Beasts experience fear? Given that they are the embodiment and mankind's nightmares and feed upon their terror, I'm not sure if Beasts are psychologically capable of registering fear anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T22:06:29-07:00","id":1062169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062167#post1062167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Beasts experience fear? Given that they are the embodiment and mankind's nightmares and feed upon their terror, I'm not sure if Beasts are psychologically capable of registering fear anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their abiding terror of the Dark Mother is one of the things the Begotten point to as evidence she's still out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T22:30:31-07:00","id":1062176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062167#post1062167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Beasts experience fear? Given that they are the embodiment and mankind's nightmares and feed upon their terror, I'm not sure if Beasts are psychologically capable of registering fear anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure a Beast can still feel fear. It's just not as easy to scare a Beast because of the aformentioned nightmare status.But stronger Beghotten, powerful supernaturals, potent Heroes, the Insatiable a lot of things can scare a Beghotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T23:39:33-07:00","id":1062194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062167#post1062167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Beasts experience fear? Given that they are the embodiment and mankind's nightmares and feed upon their terror, I'm not sure if Beasts are psychologically capable of registering fear anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep, i will make an adventure envolving beasts and their fears","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T23:57:56-07:00","id":1062199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1061831#post1061831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Goetia can't Manifest at all in normal circumstances and usually don't even leave the Astral without magical assistance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> not just Goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T00:54:16-07:00","id":1062204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062167#post1062167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Beasts experience fear? Given that they are the embodiment and mankind's nightmares and feed upon their terror, I'm not sure if Beasts are psychologically capable of registering fear anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still capable of fear, it's just that they don't have nightmares anymore. When they 'dream', they see through the Horror's eyes in their Lair or, if it's hungry, out in the Temenos, hunting down prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T04:03:21-07:00","id":1062226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062199#post1062199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> not just Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from beasts and goetia I only know of Morpheans, which are mages who have become goetia in an attempt to achieve immortality and/or more power. Since they have access to all the Arcana of the original mage they shoule be able to return to the material, but not necessarily have the right Arcana to gain any Manifestations (aside from being able to possess people with Mind 4).<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually there are other beings in the Anima Mundi, but I don't think they leave their part of the Astral either. But if they do leave the Astral they could very well have Manifestations since the Aeons are Rank 8. But beings that powerful have other kinds of difficulties getting to the material.<br /> <br /> Second edit: You might want to specify what other types of astral entities you're curious about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-14-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T06:55:26-07:00","id":1062268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062199#post1062199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not just Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Goetia&quot; means &quot;Astral beings&quot; in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T07:33:25-07:00","id":1062289,"title":"","content":"How is it that Null Snyper feeds if Insatiables have to not only kill, but physically devour their prey? Is she metaphorically devouring lives?<br /> <br /> Also, do Insatiables have different Hungers, or do they all Hunger for Prey? And do they have Satiety?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:04:11-07:00","id":1062320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062289#post1062289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it that Null Snyper feeds if Insatiables have to not only kill, but physically devour their prey? Is she metaphorically devouring lives?<br /> <br /> Also, do Insatiables have different Hungers, or do they all Hunger for Prey? And do they have Satiety?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insatiables have a Satiety track, it can fill and they can spend it on things like increasing their powers, getting the satiety expenditure on atavisms they've stolen, and even creating temporary lair chambers to bolster their power in a pinch.Though even if they get the track filled they're still hungry and active.<br /> <br /> It's pointed out that Null Snyper is kind of a weird case. First one of her problems is that she isn't physically devouring her prey and this is egging her on and she may eventually go out or try to drag someone in to feed the physical portion of the hunger. She is still gaining Satiety from the emotional feeds, but she's considered starved even by the standards of the Insatiable.<br /> Second she is capable of doing a few things wirelessly that Insatiables are supposed to only be able to do in person, for example camera on phones, laptops, and tablets count as her eyes when she uses a power that requires making eye contact or something like that.<br /> <br /> Yeah they have Hungers. It isn't explained as much as it was with the Beghotten, but they are there. The lovesick girl is a hoarder, the blind man is a ravager, the authority is a tyrant (who'd have guessed), Null snyper is a tyrant, and the clown is a predator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:10:33-07:00","id":1062324,"title":"","content":"so, the lovesick girl has to eventually pull a &quot;if I can't have you, no one can&quot; to feed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:45:31-07:00","id":1062343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062324#post1062324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, the lovesick girl has to eventually pull a &quot;if I can't have you, no one can&quot; to feed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The insatiable don't really seem to have the scaling aspect, or it could just be a side effect of the fact that they go all out in every feeding, or just that they're in the antagonist book so it doesn't describe the scaling of it. <br /> <br /> Though her standard feeding method is pretty much make target fall for her then take devour everything about the person, so I'd say she operates past that point. I mean &quot;If I can't have you no one can&quot; implies losing the target and she's pretty much in the &quot;Oh you love me that's nice&quot; *rips heart out of chest and eats it.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T13:14:35-07:00","id":1062450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1062176#post1062176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure a Beast can still feel fear. It's just not as easy to scare a Beast because of the aformentioned nightmare status.But stronger Beghotten, powerful supernaturals, potent Heroes, the Insatiable a lot of things can scare a Beghotten.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like to imagine that a Beast that exhibits fear has the same connotations as someone drinking their own urine. You're excreting the very nutrients your body (Horror) feeds on.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> What happens to the Hive if the Apex / their Lair is destroyed? It would probably recover in the long term once a new Apex is crowned, but I mean in the immediate, short term effects of having one's influence severed from the collective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:35:26-07:00","id":1063019,"title":"","content":"I have some doubts about the way Incarnates work. They can merge with their Horror at will, right? Does that mean they use the 3 Ephemeral Being Attributes boosted by Lair while in their true form? Can they assume their true form without calling forth their Lair?<br /> <br /> Can they use Nightmares while merged with their Horror? Regular Beasts can't, but since Incarnates are the ultimate Beasts, it makes sense for them to be capable of that.<br /> <br /> If they can open Primordial Pathways at will, could one of them use these Pathways as quick means of transportation through the world by using the Astral/Hedge/Shadow/Underworld as shortcuts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:50:02-07:00","id":1063022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1063019#post1063019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some doubts about the way Incarnates work. They can merge with their Horror at will, right? Does that mean they use the 3 Ephemeral Being Attributes boosted by Lair while in their true form? Can they assume their true form without calling forth their Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adopting the Beast-Shape is a distinct thing from regular merging.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they use Nightmares while merged with their Horror? Regular Beasts can't, but since Incarnates are the ultimate Beasts, it makes sense for them to be capable of that. </div> </div> </div><i>The Horror</i> can't use Nightmares on its own. The Begotten normally suffer no such limitation unless they're Ravenous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they can open Primordial Pathways at will, could one of them use these Pathways as quick means of transportation through the world by using the Astral/Hedge/Shadow/Underworld as shortcuts? </div> </div> </div>They can <i>enter the Primordial Dream from anywhere</i>, which is a bit of a different matter \u2014 think of how archmages can always return to their Golden Road.<br /> <br /> Extradimensional rapid transit is already a function of Primordial Pathways and one of the Incarnate storyhooks suggests they may not be as constrained by the contents of their Lair in navigating to other points in the cosmology \u2014 what Dave's mentioned seems to indicate we'll be getting a slightly better look at the Dream (along with the rest of the Astral) in the Player's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:23:23-07:00","id":1063036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1063022#post1063022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adopting the Beast-Shape is a distinct thing from regular merging.<br /> <br /> <i>The Horror</i> can't use Nightmares on its own. The Begotten normally suffer no such limitation unless they're Ravenous.<br /> <br /> They can <i>enter the Primordial Dream from anywhere</i>, which is a bit of a different matter \u2014 think of how archmages can always return to their Golden Road.<br /> <br /> Extradimensional rapid transit is already a function of Primordial Pathways and one of the Incarnate storyhooks suggests they may not be as constrained by the contents of their Lair in navigating to other points in the cosmology \u2014 what Dave's mentioned seems to indicate we'll be getting a slightly better look at the Dream (along with the rest of the Astral) in the Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still a bit confused. If an Incarnate wants to assume their true form, they have to open a Primordial Pathway connecting to their Lair, which they can do essentially at will, yes? Does that mean they can Adopt The Beast-Shape without opening a Primordial Pathway and thus calling forth their Lair?<br /> <br /> Ah, gotcha. So when they are merged, the Beast can still use Nightmares?<br /> <br /> It's good to know we might see more of the Primordial Dream. It always felt underused. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:53:10-07:00","id":1063053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1063036#post1063036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still a bit confused. If an Incarnate wants to assume their true form, they have to open a Primordial Pathway connecting to their Lair, which they can do essentially at will, yes? Does that mean they can Adopt The Beast-Shape without opening a Primordial Pathway and thus calling forth their Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adopting the Beast-Shape is a separate ability from the normal merging that occurs when they physically enter their Lair \u2014 the former does not require them to open a Pathway, while the latter does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:09:49-07:00","id":1067199,"title":"","content":"Why beasts don't have breaking points or something similar to it? I know beats don't have integrity, but they have emotions, right?<br /> I need to make something similar to it because i will make an adventure where you can take emotional and mental &quot;damage&quot;, there is a &quot;mental health&quot; and a &quot;soul health&quot; our &quot;emotional health&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:16:52-07:00","id":1067247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1067199#post1067199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why beasts don't have breaking points or something similar to it? I know beats don't have integrity, but they have emotions, right?<br /> I need to make something similar to it because i will make an adventure where you can take emotional and mental &quot;damage&quot;, there is a &quot;mental health&quot; and a &quot;soul health&quot; our &quot;emotional health&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because integrity was a measure of the mortals soul not actually emotional health, since beast has a horror instead of a soul the closest equivalent to integrity would be their horror's corpus or satiety. When a human does something wrong their soul might cause them to feel guilty about it, when a beast does something wrong the horror does not care so they don't become guilty to the level that it would be worthy of a condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-23-2017, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:40:12-07:00","id":1067260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1067199#post1067199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why beasts don't have breaking points or something similar to it? I know beats don't have integrity, but they have emotions, right?<br /> I need to make something similar to it because i will make an adventure where you can take emotional and mental &quot;damage&quot;, there is a &quot;mental health&quot; and a &quot;soul health&quot; our &quot;emotional health&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It would be incredibly detrimental to being a Beast if they were worried about such things. But they don't really need breaking points anyways. If a Beast acts without reason, that tends to attract the attention of Heroes and irate family members who want to stage an 'intervention' about their poor behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:44:41-07:00","id":1067263,"title":"","content":"I will point out that the entry in the book says that Beasts don't suffer breaking points in the same way humans do. So one could argue that it is possible for one of the Beghotten to suffer a breaking point just with it being more difficult than a human due to things like, literally being a nightmare monster, closing their eyes and visiting the same nightmarish landscape, being kin with the monsters of old, and that a Beast's mind is apparently set so they can go from zero to room full of flayed corpses at the drop of a hat. (Possibly with intense glee if you're playing a ravager.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:26:33-07:00","id":1068097,"title":"","content":"If a beast is targeted by you must obey what happens if they resist? Normally it would be a breaking point, but beasts have no such thing to break. Are they just imune to that nightmare?<br /> Also what happens to other supernatural creatures. For mage they technically don't have breaking points, just acts of hubis if I recall right. Or for a werwolf where there is no one direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:46:03-07:00","id":1070975,"title":"","content":"Question- is there any way to learn kinship nightmares as common nightmares? Quite a few ( We Know All Your Secrets, Everybody Hates You and Death Is A Prison, most notably) seem to fit common primal fears as much as they fit specific supernatural horrors, and it would be nice if there was a way for my beast to start with them without having to figure out how they became best friends with a promethean/sin-eater/mekhet before the story began.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:07:04-07:00","id":1070984,"title":"","content":"That's up to your ST, but do note that the book explicitly says those are only examples and you can learn the same nightmares from other splats that match the theme. We Know All Your Secrets could just as easily come from a Mind Mage or a Grey Changeling or a human telepath. Death is a Prison could easily be something you learn from a ghost, and so on. Even if the ST isn't comfortable allowing them as common nightmares you have some flexibility in who your contacts are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:29:32-07:00","id":1071341,"title":"","content":"How low would your Satiety have to be to able to fed your Hunger for Power by utterly dominating an opponent in a rap battle? Would making them bet something significant or embarassing to be given away or done if they lose help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:35:23-07:00","id":1071446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1071341#post1071341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How low would your Satiety have to be to able to fed your Hunger for Power by utterly dominating an opponent in a rap battle? Would making them bet something significant or embarassing to be given away or done if they lose help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as always 3-1 definitely works. After that if your horror is of the bend that allows for showing that you are intellectually superior to another then destroying them in a rap battle would work, maybe throw in witnesses to the beatdown just to be safe, but I wouldn't say it would need to be low unless your horror was of a more physical domination bend. I probably wouldn't go above 5 though even if you are dealing with an intellectually craving horror.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:48:30-07:00","id":1071456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1071341#post1071341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How low would your Satiety have to be to able to fed your Hunger for Power by utterly dominating an opponent in a rap battle? Would making them bet something significant or embarassing to be given away or done if they lose help?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want to say making them bet something important to them would constitute being a Collector, but from what I understand, they're not in the habit of bartering. They take what they want, regardless of your willingness to comply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T21:36:48-07:00","id":1071604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1071456#post1071456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I want to say making them bet something important to them would constitute being a Collector, but from what I understand, they're not in the habit of bartering. They take what they want, regardless of your willingness to comply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah it would probably still work, I mean worst case you restrict it to lower satiety feeding there, but there are enough stories of the overconfident protagonist going in on a contest and despairing as they are utterly destroyed and lose the cherished object that they foolishly wagered that I can see it being considered fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T06:02:53-07:00","id":1071689,"title":"","content":"Satiety 5, huh? New character created!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T14:15:07-07:00","id":1073876,"title":"","content":"Is there some sort of merit or Atavism that lets a Beast buy a few Dread Powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T21:14:48-07:00","id":1074010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1073876#post1073876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there some sort of merit or Atavism that lets a Beast buy a few Dread Powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well some of the dread powers are already atavisms. Hunter's sense correlates to Needs Must for example. However for the most part you're gonna need to talk to your ST about taking any of those. I mean some of the them I seriously doubt an ST will allow just because the Beghotten have better. Like homeground is nice, +3 dice while there, but Lair provides so much more not the least of which is the ability to bring it into play wherever as opposed to needing to fight in a specific spot. They aren't really meant for Beasts, so you'd need your ST's permission to grab them as a merit or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T22:42:34-07:00","id":1074022,"title":"","content":"Any dread power you want should probably be converted into an atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T23:08:14-07:00","id":1074025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1074022#post1074022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any dread power you want should probably be converted into an atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably wouldn't be all that hard. You'd have to concentrate on the theme of the thing over the actual effect, though, given how Atavisms work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:47:19-07:00","id":1074716,"title":"","content":"Is there a point on the Satiety meter where somebeast with a Hunger for Prey or Punishment -must- kill or at least permanently and severely maim to get the proper satiety potential?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-07-2017, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T23:25:46-07:00","id":1075023,"title":"","content":"There is no point, but cause death isn't what horrors are about or feed from, that is a sineaters field. The FEAR of death yes, and actually delivering on that fear makes a big spike of fear before they die, but a dead body is of no interest or use to a horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:18:42-07:00","id":1075498,"title":"","content":"Can a Beast with a Hunger for Prey gains Satiety from hunting supernatural creatures?<br /> <br /> More precisely can someone with a Hunger for Prey indulge safely by hunting Hedge-beasts, Hobgoblins or Wights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:43:36-07:00","id":1075507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1075498#post1075498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast with a Hunger for Prey gains Satiety from hunting supernatural creatures?<br /> <br /> More precisely can someone with a Hunger for Prey indulge safely by hunting Hedge-beasts, Hobgoblins or Wights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they can, and it's a High satiety meal. Good eating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:52:44-07:00","id":1075508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1075507#post1075507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they can, and it's a High satiety meal. Good eating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. That confirms what I thought the most moral solution for a Beast with Hungers other than Punishment is to embrace the supernatural and hunt there.<br /> <br /> So the Great Hunter of the Hedge can join the merry Brood<br /> <br /> Makara Tyrant working with the Guardians of the Veil as Labyrinth Keeper. If they can't escape her clutches, they aren't fit to Awaken anyway<br /> Namataru Collector hunting forbidden lore and knowledge: 'Scelesti Grimoire, put in on the shelf on your right with the others<br /> Anakim Ravager foiling the plans of the powerful: 'And now let me describe my diabolical scheme to force you to pay better wages to your workers.&quot;<br /> Eshmaki Hunter hunting what the other supernaturals fear: &quot;Huntsman, check. Wight, check. Gulmoth, check! Idigam? No this one is not on my list. Does it feels fear though?&quot;<br /> Ugallu Nemeses hunting kinslayers and criminals against family: Beleguared sane man.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T11:06:19-07:00","id":1075529,"title":"","content":"what are wights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:46:03-07:00","id":1075700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1075529#post1075529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what are wights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires who have fallen to 0 Humanity. At least that was the name in 1e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:27:16-07:00","id":1075748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1075700#post1075700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires who have fallen to 0 Humanity. At least that was the name in 1e</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are draugr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:19:34-07:00","id":1075816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1075700#post1075700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires who have fallen to 0 Humanity. At least that was the name in 1e</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to milo v3's reply: Wights are Humanity 0 vampires in Masquerade, and Draugr are Humanity 0 vampires in Requiem.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Requiem, I recommend Strix as prey for that Eshmaki Predator. Those things are nasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:24:31-07:00","id":1075818,"title":"","content":"For beasts with an immunity to something, is that even an immunity to supernatural sources of it? If you have darkness as a trait and a vampire causes utter darkness can you see with no problem? Would there be a clash of wills? Or just you are blind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T03:30:09-07:00","id":1075821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bonreu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1075818#post1075818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For beasts with an immunity to something, is that even an immunity to supernatural sources of it? If you have darkness as a trait and a vampire causes utter darkness can you see with no problem? Would there be a clash of wills? Or just you are blind?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it's a Tilt, you're immune. So if a vampire uses a power which inflicts blindness, you're out of luck unless you have the Atavism Shadowed Soul. If the magic creates the Darkness Tilt, you're fine. That's how I remember it, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:26:33-07:00","id":1078037,"title":"","content":"Quite a few questions about lair traits:<br /> <br /> 1- I assume so but just in case- can a beast switch off lair traits in its lair?<br /> <br /> 2- What happens when my lair traits and the Apex's influence openly contradict? Suppose my heart chamber is a pristine forest representing the fear of being far from civilisation, and the local Apex is an Iron Master werewolf whose embodies the fear that you can't escape civilisation and whose influence appears as aspects of the city. Who &quot;wins&quot;?<br /> <br /> 3- How do traits such as maze manifest in the waking world- do corridors literally shift or do people just get lost more? Also, how real are manifested traits- if a mage can control insects, can they control a manifested Infestation?<br /> <br /> 4- Does a trait immunity encompass reasonable related effects, or only what the trait says? For example, if I have the Burning trait, am I immune to smoke inhalation and being blinded by firelight or just being directly burnt? Also, how do non-damaging lair immunities like Sealed Exits work? Can I pick any lock, or do they just do nothing?<br /> <br /> 5- if I have the Engulfing trait, representing quicksand, I presumably can't be caught in quicksand. Am I also immune to being tied by vines, stuck in glue, being pinned down and other possible manifestations of the Engulfing trait, or just quicksand?<br /> <br /> 6- Do lair immunites protect me from the same traits in other beast's lairs? I can't tell if that should be a clash of wills or automatic.<br /> <br /> 7- How much of a physical location is a lair? Like, if my lair is a town, could I map it out and say &quot;oh, the general store is three doors down from the church&quot;, or is it some generic evershifting town? <br /> <br /> (sorry for quite a few questions, I have been re-reading lair traits for running a game and was a little unsure)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","user":"Urbenmyth","date":".  Another question. Sorry. 04-13-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:32:25-07:00","id":1078041,"title":"","content":"even a city can have a park. Just put car noises in the background, but no way to get to them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:12:15-07:00","id":1078166,"title":"","content":"1) Inside the lair is where the traits come from in an overlay, so you can't really turn them off. <br /> <br /> 2) Well Apex traits tend to be kind of faint and not necessarily noticed unless one is looking for them. So like Aquastosic says it might be something like if you climb the trees or end up in a clearing you can barely make out a city in the distant or maybe in quiet moments you can hear the noise of traffic, but can't figure out a way to reach them.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm guessing you're talking about a Beast imposing the maze trait on an area as opposed to how it would appear if you picked a fight with someone in a house of mirrors or a corn maze. The way I see it the overlay drags dream logic into the world. So it could easily go with either angle of the cube films. Either the person just finds it really easy to get lost for some reason, or when they aren't looking everything shifts around causing them to open a door and arrive at a room that was two doors a left fork in the hall and up a flight of stairs. It would really depend more on the lair than anything else.<br /> <br /> 4)Trait immunity primarily works on tilts. As far as a fire goes, unless you open the lair, you would be blinded by smoke not because the smoke stings your eyes but in the same way a shrub blinds a person because it is directly blocking your vision. Sealed exit wouldn't apply unless you pulled an overlay, so if someone locked you in a bank vault you are actually stuck in the vault. That said one the overlay is in place then whatever method your Horror is able to use to bypass sealed exits applies and that the only exit is sealed would no longer prove a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:45:21-07:00","id":1078402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1078166#post1078166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Inside the lair is where the traits come from in an overlay, so you can't really turn them off.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can explicity control what traits are present or not in any given Chamber at anytime in the lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T17:32:24-07:00","id":1080096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1078037#post1078037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5- if I have the Engulfing trait, representing quicksand, I presumably can't be caught in quicksand. Am I also immune to being tied by vines, stuck in glue, being pinned down and other possible manifestations of the Engulfing trait, or just quicksand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick thing, I don't think engulfing is applied the way a lot of your examples are being used. Like pinned is not being engulfed, being tied up with vines is not engulfed, and being stuck in glue is a case by case. (Someone applying glue to the ground and it drying while you stand is not, hurling you into a vat is.) Anyway I lean towards yes on the immunity to a condition applying, but I wouldn't hold it against an ST who argued that you being immune to quicksand doesn't make you immune to countless tentacles just shooting out covering you and dragging you back into the maw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1078037#post1078037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6- Do lair immunites protect me from the same traits in other beast's lairs? I can't tell if that should be a clash of wills or automatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the trait isn't a version yours can't protect against. E.g The burning trait lists levels and your lair is a less intense burn than the other beasts you won't be immune. So a Beast who's lair is in housefire is still going to have problems wandering around the chamber of another Beast who's got a chamber trait that describes as &quot;Hey guys the car tires just evaporated and the bus is melting.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1078037#post1078037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of a physical location is a lair? Like, if my lair is a town, could I map it out and say &quot;oh, the general store is three doors down from the church&quot;, or is it some generic evershifting town?<br /> <br /> (sorry for quite a few questions, I have been re-reading lair traits for running a game and was a little unsure)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lair is a dreamspace. So how it maps out would be open to question based on different Beasts. Like let's say Silent Hill 2 were a Lair the major set piece locations being different chambers, and all that. In that case the different areas would map since those are different chambers. If we're just talking a chamber in the Lair that is a town then it may have landmarks, but I don't think they'll be the easily found, mapped, and locatable type. Of course you could also treat it as a rogue-like dungeon. It can eventually be mapped out <b> this</b> visit. Next visit that map will be useless.<br /> <br /> (Though I'm also reserving the right, if they start mapping out town traits in a Lair, to pull the plug on any point where I think they're getting BS. One thing to be able to go, &quot;I think the Cafe is a few blocks that way, we can use that to get out of the rain.&quot; Another entirely for someone to gain weapons by arguing that they just went into the local gun store and took them out of the display case.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:26:39-07:00","id":1080376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=874954#post874954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That happens in one of the stories in the fiction anthology. A Beast tries to tell his Hero that she created the weaknesses he was suffering from, and asked why he would live so close to the forest that could kill him.<br /> <br /> She wouldn't believe him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read this last night...great story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T00:16:43-07:00","id":1082168,"title":"","content":"how do beasts actually enter their lair ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T00:30:40-07:00","id":1082169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1082168#post1082168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do beasts actually enter their lair ?</div> </div> </div> </div>They open a primordial pathway - basically they intersect a chamber of their lair with a spat of normal reality that in some way matches it. This has to be done in places with their lair traits matching in, though it works if you impose them yourself, and even easier if it's in the room the chamber is based on. The process is done the same way in reverse, from lair to normal reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:37:01-07:00","id":1082232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1082169#post1082169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They open a primordial pathway - basically they intersect a chamber of their lair with a spat of normal reality that in some way matches it. This has to be done in places with their lair traits matching in, though it works if you impose them yourself, and even easier if it's in the room the chamber is based on. The process is done the same way in reverse, from lair to normal reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So do they just touch a door way or can they just open it anyplace at any time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T08:46:06-07:00","id":1082279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1082232#post1082232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do they just touch a door way or can they just open it anyplace at any time?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is covered within the book.<br /> <br /> A Beast whose Horror dwells in a Dark and Flooded Lair with a Chamber based on the space underneath the old bridge on the outskirts of town can enter their Lair from underneath that bridge while it's Dark and/or Flooded, and can likewise do the same with the underside of any other bridge while it's Dark and/or Flooded with a little more difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T10:00:07-07:00","id":1082298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1082232#post1082232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So do they just touch a door way or can they just open it anyplace at any time?</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for doorway, but the place has to resemble their Lai","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T10:42:06-07:00","id":1082309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1082232#post1082232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So do they just touch a door way or can they just open it anyplace at any time?</div> </div> </div> </div>As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> noted, it is covered in the book, but think of it more like the Beast is imposing their lair over reality. It's dark and wet under the bridge, but the Beast manages to succceed their roll, opens a primordial pathway, and suddenly things start changing. The bridge arches higher, and strange lichen forms along its edges. The waters become darker, deeper than they should, and rise along the riverbanks. Even the riderbanks change, becoming waterlogged mud intersperced with the gravel that was there originally.<br /> <br /> It's not a complete transition, more a halfway point - the bridge isn't nearly as gothic as it is in your chamber, nor is the river nearly as wide. It's just as imposing, sure, but it's got mundane reality mingled in - your chamber doesn't have gravel in its mud, nor does the bridge have graffiti. It's just this bridge does, so the pathway will too.<br /> <br /> The bridge's entire structure doesn't change of course; even if it becomes larger in perspective, it's just that: perspective...well, dream perspective anyways, since for that space of time, the underside of that bridge is, for all intents and purposes, part of your lair. The top of the bridge is the same hieght, even if its arch seems larger from below, and the river isn't actually flooding anywhere other than where the pathway is set. I'm not even entirely sure whether people could see that the bridge has changed if they were looking from down the river. It's all temporary, though. Notably, this also means a Beast becomes their Horror; within their Lair, even if it's imposed on reality via a primordial pathway, they become their Horror. They retain their mind, but their body changes.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I imagine it; other people may make it a more immediate transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T05:18:52-07:00","id":1082975,"title":"","content":"Can a Beast choose to not merge with their Horror when they invoke their Lair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:20:34-07:00","id":1083022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1082975#post1082975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast choose to not merge with their Horror when they invoke their Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, not unless the Horror is Slumbering, in which case the Beast cannot merge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:48:47-07:00","id":1083943,"title":"","content":"two more lair questions- <br /> <br /> 1. If I steal a chamber from another beast, does it keep its old lair traits or gain mine?<br /> <br /> 2. Can I alter lair traits mundanly? (for example, if I'm dragged into a Burning lair with a fire existinguisher, can I put the firey rookery of the Firebird out?) <br /> <br /> Also, lastly<br /> <br /> 3. Insasiates don't have kinship powers or nightmares,right? I'm reading that correctly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:59:59-07:00","id":1084065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1083943#post1083943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">two more lair questions-<br /> <br /> 1. If I steal a chamber from another beast, does it keep its old lair traits or gain mine?<br /> <br /> 2. Can I alter lair traits mundanly? (for example, if I'm dragged into a Burning lair with a fire existinguisher, can I put the firey rookery of the Firebird out?)<br /> <br /> Also, lastly<br /> <br /> 3. Insasiates don't have kinship powers or nightmares,right? I'm reading that correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>First the insatiables are the only things that can flat out steal chambers. Everyone else is stuck with creating a merged chamber or flat out destroying the other beast's chamber and putting in their own. <br /> <br /> As far as mundane solutions to lair traits goes, I'd say it might work on it but it's not going to alter the trait. So basically your fire extinguisher can put out some flames, but unless the Beast decides to suppress the burning trait there will just somehow always be more fire to swarm back into areas you've previously put out.<br /> <br /> Yeah Insatiables aren't really things Beasts can get powers off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:18:26-07:00","id":1084072,"title":"","content":"Kinship requires a real, trusting close relationship. Any alliance with an Insatiable lasts until they get Hungry enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:50:19-07:00","id":1084087,"title":"","content":"&quot;A Beast attacking another Beast\u2019s Lair may instead steal a Chamber for his own use. If he has not added a Chamber this story and has a free slot, he may pay 1 Satiety while the Chamber is collapsing to add it to his own Lair.&quot; Beast page 100. Unless that was retconned out?<br /> <br /> (also thanks for answering my many qusetions everyone!)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T17:48:27-07:00","id":1084218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1084087#post1084087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A Beast attacking another Beast\u2019s Lair may instead steal a Chamber for his own use. If he has not added a Chamber this story and has a free slot, he may pay 1 Satiety while the Chamber is collapsing to add it to his own Lair.&quot; Beast page 100. Unless that was retconned out?<br /> <br /> (also thanks for answering my many qusetions everyone!)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nah just a detail I bit I forgot about. It doesn't come up with my group, so it got forgotten as a thing Beasts could do. Moreso as Insatiables have the ability to steal Lairs from a Beast as one of their major threat attributes, you know how it goes.<br /> <br /> If we're taking a Chamber then I think I'd rule it based on how adaptable the Beast can be and the nature of the Chamber. Basically if the player has extra traits available then they can use subsuming the Chamber as an excuse to gain those traits , you know incorporating another myth into their own, if they can't then those traits will just melt off and you get a sort of theme that can be noticed with close study. Like a metric crap ton of holes in walls that eliminate a corridor's ability to function as a labyrinth, but all the debris makes it so you can't find the exit and can't move very easily through the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T01:07:27-07:00","id":1084924,"title":"","content":"Would beast with <i>Storm-Lashed </i>ignore effects of natural cold and heat. It says they could comfortably walk through a blizzard. The obvious way to take that is that they're not bothered by the wind and the snow blown around, but since it does say comfortably and that they ignore weather, you could also take it as them just ignoring the extreme cold condition of the weather. Similarly would they be able to go without suitable environmental clothing to desert, technically overbearing sun is still extreme environment and a weather condition.<br /> <br /> Would beast be able to use the satiety expenditure version of the same ability to summon a level 0 environmental storm, say if you happen to want rain to open your <i>downpour </i>lair more easily, but without actually starting a damaging/flooding storm.<br /> <br /> How on earth do you get defense vs lightning bolt from the sky in the low satiety version. Okay that one is more a personal nitpick than question. Guns just seem like much better option than any atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T09:55:31-07:00","id":1085062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xararion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1084924#post1084924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would beast with <i>Storm-Lashed </i>ignore effects of natural cold and heat. It says they could comfortably walk through a blizzard. The obvious way to take that is that they're not bothered by the wind and the snow blown around, but since it does say comfortably and that they ignore weather, you could also take it as them just ignoring the extreme cold condition of the weather. Similarly would they be able to go without suitable environmental clothing to desert, technically overbearing sun is still extreme environment and a weather condition.<br /> <br /> Would beast be able to use the satiety expenditure version of the same ability to summon a level 0 environmental storm, say if you happen to want rain to open your <i>downpour </i>lair more easily, but without actually starting a damaging/flooding storm.<br /> <br /> How on earth do you get defense vs lightning bolt from the sky in the low satiety version. Okay that one is more a personal nitpick than question. Guns just seem like much better option than any atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regards to lightning bolts... They're not very subtle, as people have stated they've felt odd sensations prior to a lightning strike. I'd also argue that they're probably hard to aim.<br /> <br /> Guns are useful! But let's be honest, you're not taking Storm-lashed because it's the most mechanically effective ability. You're taking it because you want to be the epicenter of a terrifying storm and throw lightning bolts. That's kind of it's own reward, isn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:48:09-07:00","id":1085286,"title":"","content":"Guns don't scale and the high damage ones are difficult to carry inconspicuously. Since many of the offensive Atavisms scale off Lair they equal or exceed all but the largest, most attention garnering weapons by Lair 3. <br /> <br /> And if you're using Cyclopean Strength with Limb from Limb it's possible to do a reliable 6+ lethal every turn by Lair 3 when you're low satiety (assuming you have at least one to burn on CS)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T08:02:47-07:00","id":1085786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xararion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1084924#post1084924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would beast with <i>Storm-Lashed </i>ignore effects of natural cold and heat. It says they could comfortably walk through a blizzard. The obvious way to take that is that they're not bothered by the wind and the snow blown around, but since it does say comfortably and that they ignore weather, you could also take it as them just ignoring the extreme cold condition of the weather. Similarly would they be able to go without suitable environmental clothing to desert, technically overbearing sun is still extreme environment and a weather condition.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;He suffers no adverse effects from wind and weather <b>of any kind</b>, including Environmental Tilts&quot; so I would rule yes, they are immune to desert heat/ice-cap cold (although not, like, an oven or meat-locker)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T18:11:20-07:00","id":1085979,"title":"","content":"I'm running my very first Beast game (go me!) and a player wanted to know: can you create a Chamber in, say, the Hedge or the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T19:37:46-07:00","id":1086007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1085979#post1085979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running my very first Beast game (go me!) and a player wanted to know: can you create a Chamber in, say, the Hedge or the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can explicitly create Chambers whose basis is in other worlds if one of the formative criteria is met, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T07:19:32-07:00","id":1086183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1086007#post1086007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can explicitly create Chambers whose basis is in other worlds if one of the formative criteria is met, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! THANK YOU!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T23:05:58-07:00","id":1088118,"title":"","content":"This is probably listed somewhere in the rulebook but I couldn't find definite answer on it. Does the dream form of beast which only has 3 stats share the human maximum of 5 until your lair goes above that. I just started wondering this because you get lair x 2 points to divide to stats + size for your beast form, and your stats go by the highest of your physical/mental/social. Thus you can very reasonably expect 3 in every score (or at very least 2) before lair, 4 in one if you are really willing to take the hit. <br /> <br /> I just figure that if your beast isn't the type to be imposingly huge, your hit the cap of increasing your stats way before you actually get to breach the limit. At 3 lair you can have all stats at 5, and if you can't ignore the limit you are bound to just increase size, whether it fits your concept or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12705-xararion","name":"Xararion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:58:14-07:00","id":1088229,"title":"","content":"Add on to that Question. Do you have to distribute those Lairx2 dots the way every time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:22:46-07:00","id":1088491,"title":"","content":"An Apex question:<br /> Which native supernatural is the Apex? I'm a little confused: is it the most influential? Or the most powerful? The most feared? Or something else entirely.<br /> Thanks, guys!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:35:42-07:00","id":1088523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1088491#post1088491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Apex question:<br /> Which native supernatural is the Apex? I'm a little confused: is it the most influential? Or the most powerful? The most feared? Or something else entirely.<br /> Thanks, guys!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking, it's the one who has the most influence on the local primordial dream- spreading nightmares, creating chambers or chamberable places, etc. In practical terms, it's a combination of the most powerful, most feared and most interactions with mundane humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T20:19:45-07:00","id":1088608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1088523#post1088523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically speaking, it's the one who has the most influence on the local primordial dream- spreading nightmares, creating chambers or chamberable places, etc. In practical terms, it's a combination of the most powerful, most feared and most interactions with mundane humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably, the trajectory of a lot of 2e Supernatural Tolerance Traits is such that more powerful monsters tend to cycle through their fuelstat more rapidly without a careful dance of catspaws, courtesies, and conservation, and most of those sources of fuel tend to be gotten in proximity to humans or humanlike entities.<br /> <br /> What this tends to mean is that the highest correlation between being the Apex and being a powerful supernatural entity goes up dramatically if you regularly have to personally defend yourself and/or don't have a social network to lean on and/or can't limit most of your spendier behaviors to empowering weaker monsters who don't get too hungry too fast.<br /> <br /> (Astute readers will notice that this scans pretty directly to how the contrasting competencies of Gorged and Starved Begotten emerge.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:19:50-07:00","id":1111392,"title":"","content":"Are successive uses of the You Can Nevver Rest nightmare on the same target cumulative? Do they each add 24h without sleep after the 1st casting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T13:43:23-07:00","id":1112321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1111392#post1111392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are successive uses of the You Can Nevver Rest nightmare on the same target cumulative? Do they each add 24h without sleep after the 1st casting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be wrong, but I don't think most nightmares allow you to subject a person to more than one at a time if they have a duration of longer than instant. Which would mean that you can't stack the power on a person since they would wear off after the scene. Though multiple sources might work then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:28:33-07:00","id":1112841,"title":"","content":"A mortal character I've been playing for a bit is getting devoured soon, but I can't seem to find rules for devouring in play. What should I know? How much satiety should I start with? Would you give the character the bonus dot in occult, or the extra merit dots for only starting with 1 chamber? (And is it even possible for a freshly devoured Beast to have more than one? She's been to a few locations that qualify.)<br /> <br /> I'm a little bit confused by hive traits. Assuming my character doesn't personally have the hive trait, how can she utilize it, if at all? Is an area with the hive trait resonant with her lair? Can she impose the hive trait?<br /> <br /> What's the benefit of Fist of Nightmares? Apparently any beast can already cause a nightmare through touch without that merit, so...<br /> <br /> Can a Beast use a nightmare on themselves?<br /> <br /> Can I use Direction Sense (Advanced) to track someone or something I perceived before I took the merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:15:59-07:00","id":1112949,"title":"","content":"Building a Legend actually explains Hive Traits better than the core book. The gist: Apex imposes the Hive Trait on everyone's Lair. You can't really do anything with the Hive Trait--in fact, you don't get automatic immunity to it the way you do your own Lair Traits, so the Hive Trait could be a real pain in the ass if it doesn't already jive with your existing Lair Traits. If the Hive Trait is the same as one of your Lair Traits, otoh, it's a non-issue.<br /> <br /> Assuming the Hive Trait is not one of you own Lair Traits, you can't impose it or use its resonance to impose a LT. The core book (p. 97) says that resonance with LTs grants a one-die bonus to opening a Primordial Pathway, and I don't think it would be a stretch to include the HT in that as a house rule.<br /> <br /> I don't think there are rules for an in-play Devouring, so you'll have to house-rule this one. Personally, to me it makes sense to gain the dot of Occult but to otherwise start with bare minimums--Satiety 2 and no Chambers besides the Heart. Of course, you can always have the Chamber acquisition happen somewhere &quot;off-stage&quot; (maybe it was something she instinctively did the first time she returned to one of those locations) if you don't want to make a fuss over it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:28:13-07:00","id":1112957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mortal character I've been playing for a bit is getting devoured soon, but I can't seem to find rules for devouring in play. What should I know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first and easiest is that a lot of this is going to be things you'll probably want to verify with your ST, as the book doesn't really give rules for the change to my knowledge. Second, this is a rare case where your character will be going to sleep and waking up a new species, so feel free to play this as if sufferering from the worst hangover ever if it fits the chronicle's atmosphere and feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much satiety should I start with? Would you give the character the bonus dot in occult,</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually get the bonus dot in occult due to being hooked into the nightmare portion of humanity's collective unconcious. So unless your ST feels like that connection wouldn't be sufficient for an increase, say your occult would go up to 5 or even go to 6, you'll probably get it though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or the extra merit dots for only starting with 1 chamber? (And is it even possible for a freshly devoured Beast to have more than one? She's been to a few locations that qualify.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's very much an ST call. However, the rule for starting characters who choose only to have the Heart chamber is that they get 2xp not a merit or something. That said I would say you only start with the Heart as that forms when they undergo the Devouring/Homecoming leaving the new Beast the potential to claim the two new chambers out of those areas you think qualify to become Chambers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little bit confused by hive traits. Assuming my character doesn't personally have the hive trait, how can she utilize it, if at all? Is an area with the hive trait resonant with her lair? Can she impose the hive trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay this part is actually easy. The Hive trait comes from the most powerful entity that has a an active influence on the area. IE you do not have a Hive Trait that's just something that bleeds in from the thing that infects the fears the surrounding area. So don't worry about that as, unless you become the Apex being for the city, the Hive trait will be something from an ST controlled character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the benefit of Fist of Nightmares? Apparently any beast can already cause a nightmare through touch without that merit, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fist of Nighmares has the advantage that it actually weakens resistance against the nightmare. Normally a Nightmare is just straight opposed, but with fist the stored Nightmare only loses a success for every 2 dots of resistance the target has against it. Meaning the target would need their resistance to be double your stored successes to negate it as opposed to normal whereby they can theoretically resist with a lower dice pool.<br /> <br /> You are also technically supposed to say something when invoking a nightmare normally, and what you say has to be relevant to the invoked nightmare. While it isn't a certainty that a person might hear you invoking a nightmare the possibility that someone <b>might</b> hear is a potential grounds for conflict down the line if you go for immediate release on the nightmare. Whereas fist allows one to just brush the person and the nightmare spreads.<br /> <br /> Also probably wouldn't hurt if you could use Fist of Nightmares to inflict the kindred nightmare of You are Infected on a person. Though you are really going to need to talk with the ST about that as it does say the target normally needs to have ingested the Beghotten's blood. Might not fly, but god knows I'd ask if the situation was available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast use a nightmare on themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to say no, but I'll also raise the question of why would you want to? At the very least I'm pretty sure behold the true form doesn't work on the Beast inflicting it since they see that Horror pretty much anytime they close their eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112841#post1112841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use Direction Sense (Advanced) to track someone or something I perceived before I took the merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd ask your ST I don't have any sort of reference to say yay or nay on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 07-07-2017, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T20:26:46-07:00","id":1113077,"title":"","content":"Alright, thank you so much for the answers, everyone. I kind of figured most of this would be up to my ST but he's as new to Beast as I am so I thought I'd see if I could dig up official answers before throwing all this in his lap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1112949#post1112949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building a Legend actually explains Hive Traits better than the core book. The gist: Apex imposes the Hive Trait on everyone's Lair. You can't really do anything with the Hive Trait--in fact, you don't get automatic immunity to it the way you do your own Lair Traits, so the Hive Trait could be a real pain in the ass if it doesn't already jive with your existing Lair Traits. If the Hive Trait is the same as one of your Lair Traits, otoh, it's a non-issue.<br /> <br /> Assuming the Hive Trait is not one of you own Lair Traits, you can't impose it or use its resonance to impose a LT. The core book (p. 97) says that resonance with LTs grants a one-die bonus to opening a Primordial Pathway, and I don't think it would be a stretch to include the HT in that as a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if the Hive Trait is thin air, does my character take the penalty to physical actions/get harmed by the extreme environment in her own Lair? Can she switch it off or decide who it affects like with her own lair traits?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to say no, but I'll also raise the question of why would you want to?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not ever come up and I realize it qualifies as a bad idea by most metrics, but some of them do have positive side effects. For example, if I took Run Away and found a ticking time bomb under my bed, I might decide the extra speed is worth the horrible panic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":13652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","user":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","date":". 07-07-2017, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:18:46-07:00","id":1113095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1113077#post1113077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the Hive Trait is thin air, does my character take the penalty to physical actions/get harmed by the extreme environment in her own Lair? Can she switch it off or decide who it affects like with her own lair traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if the Apex is imposing Thin Air, your Beast suffers from the Thin Air tilt inside their own Lair. It can't be switched off or applied selectively. Your can gain resistance to Thin Air by a) cozying up to the Apex (if they're a Beast) and hoping they grant you immunity; b) forming a brood with another Beast who already had Thin Air in order to get the shared immunity, or c) spending the Experience to buy Thin Air for your own Lair. As long as the Hive Trait is Thin Air, having Thin Air for your own Lair is kind of redundant, but if the Apex (and thus the Hive Trait) changes, you'll still have Thin Air.<br /> <br /> If you're the only Beast in the game, I'd say the easiest thing for both you and the ST to do is either have the Hive Trait duplicate one of your Lair Traits, or chose a minor Hive Trait like Poor Lighting or Echoing - something that might be an annoyance but won't potentially kill you or any visitors to the Lair. Again, if it's not something that you want to focus time or energy on, it's okay to handwave the details. You can always decide later that the Apex has changed if you want to explore this part of the game in more detail.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:21:39-07:00","id":1113096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1113077#post1113077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the Hive Trait is thin air, does my character take the penalty to physical actions/get harmed by the extreme environment in her own Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can she switch it off or decide who it affects like with her own lair traits? </div> </div> </div>Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T01:00:53-07:00","id":1113144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1113077#post1113077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might not ever come up and I realize it qualifies as a bad idea by most metrics, but some of them do have positive side effects. For example, if I took Run Away and found a ticking time bomb under my bed, I might decide the extra speed is worth the horrible panic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of get the idea, although I'll point out I don't recall any of the Nightmares providing bonuses to anything. At least not in a capacity that you probably wouldn't have inherently by recognizing the situation. Like lets face if you're in a situation where the blind terror of a high satiety run away nightmare would benefit you're probably justified just going into a blind panic and running.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:47:39-07:00","id":1113711,"title":"","content":"On the matter of the Hive Trait, if it becomes something you can't afford to deal with, you can also simply close your Lair off from the Hive, as detailed in the BtP corebook. Which will reduce your range of action in the Primordial Dream, but also ensures your Lair isn't affected by the Apex's influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T16:57:29-07:00","id":1113942,"title":"","content":"Ooh, yes, that's right -- though the corebook doesn't really provide any mechanics for that, and it's not mentioned at all in BaL (which is odd, since it delves so deeply into Lairs and Chambers otherwise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T18:02:12-07:00","id":1113965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1113942#post1113942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, yes, that's right -- though the corebook doesn't really provide any mechanics for that, and it's not mentioned at all in BaL (which is odd, since it delves so deeply into Lairs and Chambers otherwise).</div> </div> </div> </div>It does have mechanics for it. It limits how far the horror can do when hunting to lair/2 miles, and it removes the Hive trait from your lairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T22:08:34-07:00","id":1114056,"title":"","content":"But how does a Beast actually -do- it? There's no mention of rolls or costs to cut off your Lair, but if it's just player fiat I'd rather that was stated outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T22:34:15-07:00","id":1114062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1114056#post1114056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how does a Beast actually -do- it? There's no mention of rolls or costs to cut off your Lair, but if it's just player fiat I'd rather that was stated outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would there be rolls or costs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T23:49:22-07:00","id":1114074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1114056#post1114056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how does a Beast actually -do- it? There's no mention of rolls or costs to cut off your Lair, but if it's just player fiat I'd rather that was stated outright.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The implication here seems to be that cutting off your Lair from the Hive is something easily done for any Beast who knows how to do it (since dice pools by default represent actions that require effort and have a chance to fail), and the loss of hunting ground is a sufficient trade-off for the advantage of blocking an unwanted Hive Trait (thus needing no additional cost)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T09:34:33-07:00","id":1114184,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for beast to have different hungers? the regular entries are kind of &quot;meh&quot; for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T09:54:26-07:00","id":1114189,"title":"","content":"Homebrew makes anything possible. Besides that, one of the upcoming books, I think the Player's Guide, is going to introduce a couple of new Hungers. One previewed one is a Hunger for Secrets, which sounds like playing a Mage to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:32:18-07:00","id":1121686,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know where to find the explanation on the rate satiety is burned up normally? I know Beasts can expend it to fuel other abilities. The only chart I can find is on 338 which denotes how long it takes for different lair levels at Starving or Ravenous to not feed before the Horror goes out on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:43:40-07:00","id":1121691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1121686#post1121686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know where to find the explanation on the rate satiety is burned up normally? I know Beasts can expend it to fuel other abilities. The only chart I can find is on 338 which denotes how long it takes for different lair levels at Starving or Ravenous to not feed before the Horror goes out on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 111, &quot;Time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:07:38-07:00","id":1121699,"title":"","content":"What happens when two Anakim Tyrants arm wrestle each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:42:46-07:00","id":1121706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1121699#post1121699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when two Anakim Tyrants arm wrestle each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Furniture gets broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:01:38-07:00","id":1122173,"title":"","content":"Does Skeleton Key allow you to access your Lair without worrying about narrative similarities? It says it can open to the Primordial Dream instead of the gate's normal exit, but it doesn't specify if that means the Lair or what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T00:42:28-07:00","id":1122257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1122173#post1122173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Skeleton Key allow you to access your Lair without worrying about narrative similarities? It says it can open to the Primordial Dream instead of the gate's normal exit, but it doesn't specify if that means the Lair or what.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that it could, but you'd still need some kind of magical/occult doorway/passage/portal, and (most of them) don't grow on trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T04:45:41-07:00","id":1122294,"title":"","content":"They do if you're friends with Changelings. Hedgegates are real easy to make. <br /> <br /> But then, that's kind of my experience with Beast as a whole. A lot of limiting factors are just a matter of bringing the right two splats together to render trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:43:14-07:00","id":1122778,"title":"","content":"So.. with an initial tilt in place, if I call another trait in can I merge with my horror (as per the example with the school)? Or do I need to use a nightmare/back door, skeleton key, or other method?<br /> <br /> Lair Traits are cool but I'm not sure how the Lair interacts with the material world (or is travelled to on the regular) and that's assuming the risks involved are pretty high, if your horror dies you die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T14:16:00-07:00","id":1122806,"title":"","content":"Just calling down the tilts only requires one naturally occurring tilt. If you want to open the Lair and merge you need to open a primordial pathway (You'll note in the example that the school is the real world basis for one of the chambers).<br /> <br /> I don't find the risks to be that high, or at least not as high as fighting outside the Lair where you can still die the regular way. Rolls to destroy chambers happen on multiple minute intervals and are resisted by an active Horror, so the odds of some Hero destroying your Heart without first dispatching your Horror (and thus killing you anyway) aren't that high. Meanwhile the Horror has all your atavisms and significantly higher attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T18:11:42-07:00","id":1122866,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression when I bring a Lair Trait into effect, if anyone leaves the scene they enter my Lair. So that isn't the case? Or it's only the case when actually at a Chamber's creation point (creating a chamber is particularly difficult, too.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T18:46:43-07:00","id":1122871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1122866#post1122866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression when I bring a Lair Trait into effect, if anyone leaves the scene they enter my Lair. So that isn't the case? Or it's only the case when actually at a Chamber's creation point (creating a chamber is particularly difficult, too.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Bringing lair traits into an area is a different ability to overlapping your lair with an area. The &quot;if anyone leaves they enter the lair&quot; is part of the ability to open a primordial pathway to your lair which causes it to overlap with the current environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T19:40:16-07:00","id":1122875,"title":"","content":"If someone is so inspired by your Legend that they actually want you to scare them for a thrill or bragging rights, can you still get Satiety from them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T20:07:46-07:00","id":1122884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1122875#post1122875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone is so inspired by your Legend that they actually want you to scare them for a thrill or bragging rights, can you still get Satiety from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though they'll probably regret being so willing once you damage their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T04:07:49-07:00","id":1122961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1122871#post1122871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing lair traits into an area is a different ability to overlapping your lair with an area. The &quot;if anyone leaves they enter the lair&quot; is part of the ability to open a primordial pathway to your lair which causes it to overlap with the current environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>So opening a pathway is what superimposes it, with the pathway can I inflict as many tilts than since I'm &quot;in my lair&quot; as it were? Cool, thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:50:44-07:00","id":1131430,"title":"","content":"How do brood lairs work during inheritance?<br /> <br /> Since one form involves destruction of a Beast's lair, would that not mean the entire brood goes rampant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:33:57-07:00","id":1131441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131430#post1131430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do brood lairs work during inheritance?<br /> <br /> Since one form involves destruction of a Beast's lair, would that not mean the entire brood goes rampant?</div> </div> </div> </div>An unfettered leaves an empty lair behind assuming a success or a the kind of grand failure that leaves a lair behind.<br /> <br /> A rampant beast technically absorbs their lair back into themself, the book says it happens quickly, so it wouldn't destroy the other Lairs due to one chamber being in an overlay with another chamber. At worst I'd argue it might destroy the overlapped chamber, but that wouldn't cause Rampancy since even if that happened with every chamber the Heart can't be overlapped. Most likely I'd say there might be some minor damage to the overlaid chamber as the Lair of the Rampant breaks down and fades away.<br /> <br /> Incarnates I couldn't say probably vary based on the legend of the Incarnate in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 08-20-2017, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:15:16-07:00","id":1131539,"title":"","content":"Do Lair traits require an action? Every instance I've seen it's X/Scene but they don't go into detail as to how you actually put one into play outside of &quot;turn on the sprinklers&quot; &quot;burn the house down&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T00:09:51-07:00","id":1131642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131539#post1131539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Lair traits require an action? Every instance I've seen it's X/Scene but they don't go into detail as to how you actually put one into play outside of &quot;turn on the sprinklers&quot; &quot;burn the house down&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To my knowledge this tends to be done by just opening a pathway (pg 97 Beast Core) which says its an instant action. Though if there's another way I'm not aware of that might not hold true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T01:47:43-07:00","id":1131654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131642#post1131642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my knowledge this tends to be done by just opening a pathway (pg 97 Beast Core) which says its an instant action. Though if there's another way I'm not aware of that might not hold true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordial Pathways are a different ability to Imposing Traits. It doesn't say what action imposing traits is, but it can be assumed to be an instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:49:42-07:00","id":1131711,"title":"","content":"One other question. A mage in the group failed the Clash of Wills against my Needs Must Atavism (marking / satiety expenditure) and decided to &quot;analyze/scrutinize it&quot; and gave it an opacity of 3.<br /> How would you rule things like that where it's &quot;arcana dots&quot; difficult or something. My highest resistance trait is Stamina at 4, so I suggested that should be the substitute for Arcana but they waived it. Earlier they tried to say I use the lowest of my resistance traits (treating them like arcana for some spell or effect) for contesting against a counter spell but I said no because it's not strictly arcana + I -always- use the highest according to the CoW page.<br /> <br /> Can anyone give any insight? Because as it stands My Stamina 4, Lair 4 beast's secrets are just laid out bare to this mage whenever I want to use -anything- lol. It was a tad frustrating at the time. Are there more in-depth crossover rules considering Beast is &quot;The Crossover Chronicle&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a tad disconcerting and a huge deterrent if the mage just &quot;knows everything&quot; about anything used on them (within a turn or two, no less)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 08-20-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:33:03-07:00","id":1131730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131711#post1131711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other question. A mage in the group failed the Clash of Wills against my Needs Must Atavism (marking / satiety expenditure) and decided to &quot;analyze/scrutinize it&quot; and gave it an opacity of 3.<br /> How would you rule things like that where it's &quot;arcana dots&quot; difficult or something. My highest resistance trait is Stamina at 4, so I suggested that should be the substitute for Arcana but they waived it. Earlier they tried to say I use the lowest of my resistance traits (treating them like arcana for some spell or effect) for contesting against a counter spell but I said no because it's not strictly arcana + I -always- use the highest according to the CoW page.<br /> <br /> Can anyone give any insight? Because as it stands My Stamina 4, Lair 4 beast's secrets are just laid out bare to this mage whenever I want to use -anything- lol. It was a tad frustrating at the time. Are there more in-depth crossover rules considering Beast is &quot;The Crossover Chronicle&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a tad disconcerting and a huge deterrent if the mage just &quot;knows everything&quot; about anything used on them (within a turn or two, no less)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does the Mage even <i>know </i>he has been Marked? The write-up gives no indication the target is somehow aware of it. Routinely checking his Sympathy Connections? If he didn't do that beforehand, this seems a bit like a IC Knowledge/OOC knowledge seperation failure.<br /> <br /> Regarding Clash of Wills: The Book clearly states<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP p 222</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Beasts,<b> lacking both dot-ranked powers </b>and secondary Traits driving their powers, roll Lair + their highest Resistance Attribute.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>, emphasize mine. As such, since Arcana are dot-ranked powers, it is pretty clear that they instead use their highest resistance attribute for clash of wills. Anything that deviates from that is a house rule and should be made clear as such, imo. Otherwise, people are not on the same page, which harms the game.<br /> <br /> Regarding withstanding a Mage Spell: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw p 127</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Living (or undead) subjects usually Withstand spells with Stamina (for physical transformations or afflictions), Resolve (for attempted mind control or other mental effects), or Composure (for emotional manipulation or effects that target sanity, perception, or the soul).&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> This is what you do outside a Clash of Will, usually. No Lair specifically.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding opacity: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw p 94</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Supernal Phenomena Are More Opaque: A mage can Scrutinize the site of a Wasteland created by a Promethean and learn a great deal, but the Opacity rating should be higher (roughly 1.5 times higher, as a suggestion) than a similar effect created by Awakened magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Opacity of 3 seems appropriate to me, seeing how Scrying is Space 2. Even then, to track it down to the Beast would take more than just Scrutiny. He learns <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether the Mystery is the result of Awakened magic.<br /> \u2022 If so, what Arcana were involved and the Signature Nimbus of the caster (unless it was cast using a Rote).<br /> \u2022 <b>Roughly how old the Mystery is (hours, days, months,years, centuries).</b><br /> \u2022 Optionally, what Practice created the Mystery (<b>if a non-Supernal Mystery, then what Practice the Mystery most closely resembles</b>). </div> </div> </div> and with Deep Knowledge <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Awakened magic cast using a Rote, or the effects of an Attainment, the Signature Nimbus of the mage involved.<br /> \u2022 For Awakened spells, the spell factors involved (including the remaining duration), whether the spell caused a Paradox (and if so whether that Paradox was released or contained), and whether the spell has been relinquished.<br /> \u2022<b> Identification of a phenomenon as being linked to one the mage has Scrutinized before.</b><br /> \u2022<b> If not Awakened magic, the power level of the creator relative to the mage\u2019s Gnosis (if applicable).</b><br /> \u2022 Whether the Mystery is related to the Supernal Realms or Abyss.<br /> \u2022 <b>How the Arcanum used relates to the Mystery \u2014 for example, using Death Sight to scrutinize a vampire\u2019s ghoul will reveal Deep Information relating to the undead blood in the subject\u2019s system, and any powers the ghoul has gained from it. Using Fate Sight to assess a changeling\u2019s powers will reveal that they are formed by mystical bargains.</b> </div> </div> </div> It certainly would not automatically &quot;lay out bare&quot; all your secrets to the mage whenever you use anything. Could you give some more information with how the Mage does that? Not to mention that Scrutinizing yourself is probably a bit harder than an object or other person, and that it pours magic into the area, meaning anyone able to sense magic notices - not always (what am I saying, not USUALLY) a good thing.<br /> <br /> Why do you Mark you teammates, though? Or are you opposing each other in this Chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T13:47:01-07:00","id":1131864,"title":"","content":"He has the keen periphery merit, and is as he puts it &quot;aware whenever as supernatural power is used in his presence&quot; and he chose to scrutinize the effect instead of &quot;unravelling it&quot; which is basically spamming counter after counter accumulating successes or something like that. He rolled twice and said he knows how my Atavisms work, and every detail about Needs Must. Essentially unraveling a mystery as he put it, for arcane beats.<br /> <br /> The last one I think is how he said he knows everything. He gave an example saying he'd know every discipline a ghoul ever learned &quot;from their blood&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> Barring that, his retainer - another player - has a custom devotion that is called The Hills Have Eyes, and it's basically Lord of the Land level stuff for Auspex. He is aware of everything within the domain, and gets a few more questions for free than he normally would afaik, but it isn't strictly relevant for this case.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure he was using the Revelation/Scrutiny rules from M:tA2E, but now that I have the PDF learning how it relates to an arcanum is different than just &quot;I know how your atavisms work, and what this one does at each level including that you can borrow my senses.&quot; -sigh- he has a habit of finding sidebars in the backs of books for things so unless this is hidden away somewhere I'll be bringing this up next session with as many citations as possible.<br /> edit: And he's only supposed to get 1 piece of deep information per exceptional, not extra per mana it's just an extra success per mana from what I've read on p93-94.<br /> <br /> One last thing, he treated it as mind, not space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 08-20-2017, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T14:52:11-07:00","id":1131892,"title":"","content":"Well, all i can say is that is not how that skill works. I cannot find keen periphery merit, so I assume it's homebrew? If you mean peripheral mage sight, yeah, it makes you notice *something* supernatural happened. Not what, how, why, in what manner shape or form, or how he might find out. The example given in the PDF on Page 90 explicitly stats so. The example mage would get a sense of supernatural powers being used, but lack of Death means He'll never find out what it is. So no. He has no way of knowing he was targeted, and unless his natural response to &quot;something supernatural happened&quot; is a complete Screening of himself, I. Call. Bullshit. Which I hardly ever do. So yeah, serious, major-league bullshit.<br /> <br /> Yes, he could do that with a ghoul *kinda, by using the correct Arcana and focused mage sight, which, as I said, has the problem of pouring Mana into the area, thus possibly alerting/attracting magic - sensitive things. While he is very focused and unaware, for some time. But to do so with the Atavism, he'd have to study the source of it. So he'd have to know what the source is. Which he cannot without tracing the Sympathetic connection back. Which he cannot without being aware of it. Which he purely and simply is immesely unlikely to be. Otherwise all he could learn is &quot;dude making this was about my strength/stronger/weaker. I have (never) Seen something similar before. It works kinda like Scrying and Locate Object. It's a few hours/days old&quot;.<br /> <br /> Treating it as mind would not let him understand that he is Marked and traced by someone, but that there is an open channel to his senses imo.<br /> <br /> Your teammate Seems needlessly hostile. And it looks like he makes mages greater than they are (no small task in itself). A mage is not a 'roll dice - you win!' Character. Playing A mage is Being a supernatural batman. Be smarter, better prepared than the others. <br /> <br /> *it would be more a &quot;What powers does that blood give him?&quot;, not &quot;which disciplines ever did he learn?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T16:27:56-07:00","id":1131937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131892#post1131892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, all i can say is that is not how that skill works. I cannot find keen periphery merit, so I assume it's homebrew?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's previewed material from Signs of Sorcery and, surprising nobody, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\">it also doesn't work like that</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T16:58:05-07:00","id":1131949,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell the mage would, at best, be able to determine Needs Must as an effect belonging the arcana of space( connections, distance, and all.) Its an offshoot periphreal mage sight ,as previously stated by Wormwood, so if the Beast wasn't trying to conceal the effect then the mage would know something supernatural had happened in the general vicinity without knowing specifically what. Granted the effect would only work to begin with if the Mage could perceive the Beast doing it. So if the Beast had been just hanging out in line at a mall food court and used Needs Must and the Mage was in front of them looking over the menu the Mage wouldn't get to know unless the Beast did something while using the Atavism to cross it over into another sense beyond sight. If they could see the Beghotten then with Keen Periphreal they could possibly determine that it did something supernatural and it tied into the Space arcanum (assuming I've got the arcanum right, I'm more used to the old spheres) for the effect, but wouldn't be able to determine more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:09:31-07:00","id":1131952,"title":"","content":"Huh. The write up is curiously different from core. Specifically, this contradicts Core in so far that Mages DO know where the power originated. As in, something casts from across the Shadow, and even Mages without Spirit and Death instinctively know where the spell came from. IF within the Mage's sensual range.<br /> So with Keen Periphery, the Mage could tell this would be a Space-Arcanum related occurence. Far cry from the claim.<br /> Thanks for the information, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T17:32:35-07:00","id":1131958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131952#post1131952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. The write up is curiously different from core. Specifically, this contradicts Core in so far that Mages DO know where the power originated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, the corebook says nothing about not being able to place the location of supernatural activity, only that existing in Twilight is usually concealment enough for a ghost to avoid pinging the Periphery without a more definite action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:09:38-07:00","id":1131974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131949#post1131949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can tell the mage would, at best, be able to determine Needs Must as an effect belonging the arcana of space( connections, distance, and all.) Its an offshoot periphreal mage sight ,as previously stated by Wormwood, so if the Beast wasn't trying to conceal the effect then the mage would know something supernatural had happened in the general vicinity without knowing specifically what. Granted the effect would only work to begin with if the Mage could perceive the Beast doing it. So if the Beast had been just hanging out in line at a mall food court and used Needs Must and the Mage was in front of them looking over the menu the Mage wouldn't get to know unless the Beast did something while using the Atavism to cross it over into another sense beyond sight. If they could see the Beghotten then with Keen Periphreal they could possibly determine that it did something supernatural and it tied into the Space arcanum (assuming I've got the arcanum right, I'm more used to the old spheres) for the effect, but wouldn't be able to determine more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was in a keep/castle set up on an island. He's a left-path lich with body-mods calling himself The Dragon King. As myself and the vampire were the only non-staff people on the island other than him he could safely assume I was the source of something supernatural - to which he decided to scrutinize the effect on himself since he failed the clash. But to make a couple rolls and just flat out go &quot;I know how your atavisms work, basically - oh and I know every detail of Needs Must.&quot; is the part I'm contesting it seems the rules are on my side.<br /> <br /> We literally re-rolled to make sure we follow the rules (plus our characters were just stupid levels of overpowered) and we've got this to deal with lol.<br /> At least it seems like it's a preview of something that's going to be released officially. But still, so far what I gather is that all he knows is it's a space-sorta thing happening and it's likely my fault, and he knows I have 1 more dot of Lair than he does Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 08-20-2017, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:41:35-07:00","id":1131988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131958#post1131958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, the corebook says nothing about not being able to place the location of supernatural activity, only that existing in Twilight is usually concealment enough for a ghost to avoid pinging the Periphery without a more definite action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just re-read it, and you are right - the Core didn't specify anything about the place. Still, from the writeup <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor does Peripheral Mage Sight give any clues as to what just<br /> happened \u2014 only that magic is afoot. </div> </div> </div> I assumed that it was a less informative ability than it's apparently meant to be, more of an &quot;Time to investigate!&quot; kind of marker rather than a pinpointer of &quot;Here be Magic!&quot;.<br /> I liked the less powerful (and yeah, to me having the additional information of where exactly the sensation originates is much more powerful) version better, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Ahwell!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11492\" data-vbnamecard=\"11492\">Arduras</a> &quot;since he failed the clash&quot; is not really a reason, because the character is not aware of the CoW.<br /> The &quot;only non-staff&quot; is a way better reason, but there are still hundreds of things one could do with Space-related abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:06:58-07:00","id":1132015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1131988#post1131988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the less powerful (and yeah, to me having the additional information of where exactly the sensation originates is much more powerful) version better, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not a whole lot that the process benefits from by forcing you to triangulate and the existence of nonvisual Peripheries doesn't really obviate the fact that <i>if you are seeing something, you can generally tell where it is</i>. It's your magical nature acting as a filter on your normal perception of the world, and most perceptible magical phenomena are things that exist in the world \u2014 it would be kind of goofy if &quot;perceiving magical occurrences through the lens of your Path and Nimbus&quot; didn't actually let you perceive <i>a magical occurrence</i> without dropping into the specialized lenses of Active Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:19:52-07:00","id":1132022,"title":"","content":"Plus if I recall supernaturals seeing a Beast use an Atavism tend to see a shadow form or an overlay or something of the Beast's Horror, might tip off a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T01:43:07-07:00","id":1132121,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> yeah, I Get that. I suppose. This makes it more of a spider sense, though, no? Or does it really exclusively Apply To sight? Because then the mage would have to be looking at the marking in progress to even qualify for noticing something magical. Huh. I should hit the mage board with mah questions, dont wanna derail.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> indeed, as long as youre looking at the beast in that moment that is the case!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T09:01:49-07:00","id":1132233,"title":"","content":"The peripheral tells him something happened, the keen merit tells him &quot;something spacey happened&quot; can he then scrutinize the details of the power used? Learning the powers a ghoul gains from dead blood with death as the example, he'd learn that someone can &quot;scry&quot; him via space. Or can use his senses briefly if he scrutinized with mind. That about sums it up?<br /> <br /> Regarding supernatural senses constantly registering beasts and their atavisms, all I can say is it must be pretty messy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 08-27-2017, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T16:19:05-07:00","id":1134654,"title":"","content":"Can a Beast use You Must Obey to make someone forget what just happened to them? This was brought up in our last game and was kind of a point of contention. I personally think you can't but my friend thinks it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T11:28:35-07:00","id":1134885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1134654#post1134654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast use You Must Obey to make someone forget what just happened to them? This was brought up in our last game and was kind of a point of contention. I personally think you can't but my friend thinks it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can order a person to yes, and they might even try to forget like you tell them to, but I don't think it allows one to start mucking around with memories. Look at the base level it specifically says that attempts to ignore or countermand the Beast's orders provoke a breaking point. That speaks to the general flavor of the nightmare in question. This isn't a power that turns people into a will-less thrall who's mind can be freely shaped, this is body control specifically to evoke the horror of a person not being able to control themself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T13:41:19-07:00","id":1140302,"title":"","content":"So I'm very confused on the Unbreakable Atavism: How exactly does it work combined with Iron Skin at the Highest Levels? What attacks go through it? How as a storyteller in a mechanical combat fight would you challenge these creatures since their armor supposedly applies to aggravated damage? Is it only through Anathemas &amp; Armor Piercing? The whole numbers confuse me as it seems like Unbreakable is impossible to fight along with the fact General Armor applies to all attacks. Clarification would be nice - Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T14:29:29-07:00","id":1140314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1140302#post1140302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm very confused on the Unbreakable Atavism: How exactly does it work combined with Iron Skin at the Highest Levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the highest levels of Iron Skin, the character has the greatest amount of Stamina a character can get without supernatural assistance, Armor 2 against non-aggravated damage, the ability to spend a point of Willpower to downgrade two points of lethal damage into two points of bashing damage, the ability to spend a point of Willpower to downgrade one point of non-Anathema aggravated damage into one point of lethal damage, and the ability to ignore the first point of non-Anathema damage from a given instance of damage.<br /> <br /> The Unbreakable Atavism adds 3 to your general Armor rating and 2 to your ballistic Armor rating as its base effect, rising to +4/+3 at low Satiety (which comes with all the problems that Low Satiety normally represents).<br /> <br /> If you've got a character with those advantages at their disposal on top of the usual resilience Environmental Immunities afford you, then the threats to such a character are chiefly in weapons and resources that ignore Armor, hazards you are not immune to, Killing Blows, social/mental/perceptual offenses, and generally putting powerful weaponry in the hands of extremely skilled users of those weapons.<br /> <br /> It's supposed to be hard to overcome that kind of damage reduction without &quot;cheats&quot; \u2014 that's part and parcel of being on the higher end of resilience in a class of monster that specifically corresponds with legendary nightmare creatures from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T08:45:05-07:00","id":1140526,"title":"","content":"Satchel is correct, but to add some concrete examples for clarity: High powered guns can have weapon modifiers of +3, 4, even 5, and armor piercing ammo can ignore 1 to 3 points of armor. Yeah, handguns and probably even shotguns are nearly worthless against a fully armored Beast, so you bring an elephant gun, or a sniper rifle with specialty ammunition. <br /> <br /> Beasts themselves have a number of armor negating abilities at their disposal. Basilik's Touch inflicts poison (although you probably need to be a low satiety to reliably use it on someone with stamina 5+) Siren's Treacherous Song ignores most forms of armor. Cyclopean Strength combined with Limb From Limb just wins by sheer dint of numbers for Beasts with Lair 4 or higher. Advanced Killer Instinct is a major advantage against armor, and so on.<br /> <br /> There are a million other ways for other splats to deal with armor, and I don't have the comprehensive knowledge or patience to get into all of them, but Changelings alone have Renders and Razorhands, who can take Potent Kith to get pretty respectable amounts of armor piercing (well, Razorhands cancel it out with weapon modifier, but the end result is the same) even at relatively little exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T08:08:54-07:00","id":1141752,"title":"","content":"Satchel is mostly correct. You reduce Bashing Damage by 2, Lethal Damage by 2, and all non-Anathama damage by 1. This is important for firearms, because the ballistic armor reduces the incoming damage. Combine with Relentless Hunter and Infestation for ultimate survivability.<br /> <br /> What is effectively 7/3 armor against most attacks (8/6 with a concealable bulletproof vest or 10/4 with modern chainmail) is powerful, but not insurmountable. A hypothetical 5L, 3AP gun will only deal Successes -1 damage while a 5L, 3AP sword will deal Successes +1. Killer Instinct is another +3 damage. Called shot the head to avoid mundane armor. Then there is all the various non-damage ways affect a Beast, or damage ways that avoid armor all together. In Beast you have: Basilisk' s Touch, Siren's Song, Cyclopean Strength, Limb from Limb, and Behold! MY TRUE FORM that can help you ignore or outpace the opponent's armor. With the right fighting styles, a plain Jane mortal has a chance of getting through it.<br /> <br /> As for STing that sort of monster, understand that the player is signaling to you that they want to play the Juggernaught. Let them do that, give them chances to shine, challenge them in other area, and give them threats that only they can survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:20:10-07:00","id":1141945,"title":"","content":"Spending Satiety on Unbreakable makes bashing damage no longer apply, and most sources of Lethal damage turn into Bashing. Furthermore, his armor now applies to aggravated damage. That makes them quite Juggernaut-y, but as one of my beasts just had to experience, fighting something like a Mosquito-Host (Zhibesi from this forum) can still be a pain in the ass. Combining Unbreakable with Relentless Hunter and Looming Presence constitutes the defensive trifecta (More health + low satiety reduces the attackers dice pool by half your Lair rounded up, which is like bonus Defense that you do not lose when using All-Out attacks. As long as you are the taller, of course.) Adding Infestation makes this only more crazy as low Satiety Infestation reduces most Sources of Lethal damage to Bashing. Pair this up with Satiety spending on Unbreakable, and you are nearly invulnerable except for Aggravated damage (still reduced by armor). Now add Iron Skin all the way up to Epic, and even that can be downgraded/outright soaked.<br /> <br /> Creating a Beast like that WOULD eat up 7 xp for the Atavisms, at least 4 for the attributes and another 2 for Epic Iron Skin, though, so long as you build towards this in character creation with 4 stamina, and Dropping 4 merit points on advanced/Iron Skin.<br /> Total of 13 xp.<br /> <br /> Also yes, listen to SoulGambit's advice: let them Occasionally revel in their tankiness, give them Threats only they can survive or make it a point to challenge the group so that them tanking allow the others to do their thing (deal damage, steal, discuss, etc ). Then throw them into a Situation where they are totally out of their waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  sleep y 09-19-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T12:42:54-07:00","id":1146127,"title":"","content":"Excluding the ones that affect traits unique to humans like speech, could you use Nightmares, or even some more subtle Atavism like Alien Allure or Siren's Treacherous Song, on animals by RAW?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T08:48:23-07:00","id":1146351,"title":"","content":"Don't see why not. The Sound of a voice can help calming animals (or so the opposite) if done correctly, and alien Allure was started to be just as likely looks as it is postures or pheremones.<br /> Nightmares would be more restricted imo. They need to have the capacity to comprehend/experience the fear the Nightmare is based on. I would not accept You deserve this on most animals, except social advanced beings like Gorillas for example.<br /> you are lost makes sense for every territorial animal Bugs everywhere makes sense for many, but not all. Etc. Case by case imo.<br /> <br /> <br /> Phone scrambled some words will correct when at computer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 10-03-2017, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T09:11:51-08:00","id":1156708,"title":"","content":"Can a beast replace their Lair Traits? I'm finding that they can just add new Traits when their Lair increases to applicable heights, but are there any rules for them replacing extant Traits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T05:23:39-08:00","id":1161131,"title":"","content":"A simple, and potentially stupid, question. Can a beast enter a dream and deliberately feed on a victim in that dream. I know the Horror can do that when left at Starving for too long, but can a PC feed this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T16:57:47-08:00","id":1162575,"title":"","content":"possibly a really dumb question but: Can Beasts form kinships with Heroes? Besides the obvious logistical problems that i assume can be potentially overcome, i couldn't find anything that says they can't (as far as i can tell, only G-M things and Insatiables can't), but I'm afraid there might be something that I super missed like an idiot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T23:09:03-08:00","id":1162645,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1752_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1752\" data-vbnamecard=\"1752\">mofous</a> From what I've seen there aren't any listed merits or powers to allow a Beghotten to feed by deliberately releasing their Horror upon the dreamscape.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13001_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13001\" data-vbnamecard=\"13001\">SdeSpencer</a> I didn't see anything that explicitly says that its impossible for a Beast to become kin with a Hero, but in my mind this would be an ST call that borders on a houserule. I mean the Hero in Conquering who was most amiable to Beasts pretty much had the rule of pass through and don't cause trouble and I won't kill you. So while I wouldn't say its explicitly against the RAW it feels less like a thing that would happen in a Chronicle on the player's side and very much like something that would be more of a story hook based on, &quot;Wait why would a Hero go out of their way to save a Beast?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T00:10:27-08:00","id":1162653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1161131#post1161131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple, and potentially stupid, question. Can a beast enter a dream and deliberately feed on a victim in that dream. I know the Horror can do that when left at Starving for too long, but can a PC feed this way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take control of your horror, have them travel through the local hive of the primordial dream. The horror can potentially then travel into the dream of someone, in which it can then attempt to terrify the individual in a manner appropriate for your hunger. Finding the dream of someone specific could be rather difficult though and there are no rules for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T09:45:18-08:00","id":1162741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1162645#post1162645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13001_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13001\" data-vbnamecard=\"13001\">SdeSpencer</a> I didn't see anything that explicitly says that its impossible for a Beast to become kin with a Hero, but in my mind this would be an ST call that borders on a houserule. I mean the Hero in Conquering who was most amiable to Beasts pretty much had the rule of pass through and don't cause trouble and I won't kill you. So while I wouldn't say its explicitly against the RAW it feels less like a thing that would happen in a Chronicle on the player's side and very much like something that would be more of a story hook based on, &quot;Wait why would a Hero go out of their way to save a Beast?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T20:50:43-08:00","id":1173680,"title":"","content":"I know you merge and take control of your Horror if you enter your lair, but if you physically travel to a chamber of the primordial dream do you also merge with your horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T21:12:41-08:00","id":1173685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1173680#post1173680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you merge and take control of your Horror if you enter your lair, but if you physically travel to a chamber of the primordial dream do you also merge with your horror?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if it's within or merged with your own Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T20:18:25-08:00","id":1176681,"title":"","content":"Here's a question: does the Beast have to be the direct cause the fear in order to potentially gain Satiety from it? In other words, can a Beast feed by witnessing &quot;natural&quot; (or otherwise incidental) trauma? <br /> <br /> All of the instances I could find of a Beast feeding would seem to suggest the affirmative, but I don't see anywhere that it is explicitly specified that the Beast <i>must </i>be the instigator to feed from someone. The obvious exception is Family Dinner, in which they don't even have to directly participate, but that seems to operate on different metaphysical rules than normal feeding.<br /> <br /> The character concept I had in mind was storm-chaser with a Hunger for Ruin, who would hypothetically feed primarily off the despair and destruction felt by the storms he chases, which he doesn't (necessarily) have any hand in causing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T22:25:00-08:00","id":1176696,"title":"","content":"Considering there's a sample character that gains satiety by unleashing her social media followers into doxxing folk to feed from that, signs point to no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T04:11:30-08:00","id":1176743,"title":"","content":"She's an Insatiable though, so the normal rules may not apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T05:16:14-08:00","id":1176750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1176696#post1176696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering there's a sample character that gains satiety by unleashing her social media followers into doxxing folk to feed from that, signs point to no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that she has to see a video or live feed of the victim killing themselves to feed, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T15:11:57-08:00","id":1176843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1176681#post1176681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: does the Beast have to be the direct cause the fear in order to potentially gain Satiety from it? In other words, can a Beast feed by witnessing &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot; (or otherwise incidental) trauma? </div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have an idea for a hack that deals with that very idea. I won't go too far into that, here, but I will say that it should be a very intense source of fear if you're going to allow the character to feed from it. For example, if your character creates a storm that destroys someone's home, you should be able to feed from it. If the same storm is naturally occurring, it should require devastation on at least a neighborhood level, if not citywide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T15:22:54-08:00","id":1176844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1176696#post1176696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering there's a sample character that gains satiety by unleashing her social media followers into doxxing folk to feed from that, signs point to no.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't quite what I meant. She's still the impetus behind the events that lead to her feeding. What I want to know is what happens if a Beast comes across a situation they had no hand in causing. For example, if a Tyrant witnesses a mugging, could they feed on the helplessness of the victim, despite not being the cause of the helplessness? I guess this kind of comes down to the nature of the Hunger. Do Beasts feed off of fear itself, or do they feed off of <i>causing</i> fear? Are they driven to monstrous acts in order to sate their hunger, or is performing the act itself what fills them? This is my question (which is starting to sound not-so-simple).<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1176843#post1176843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have an idea for a hack that deals with that very idea. I won't go too far into that, here, but I will say that it should be a very intense source of fear if you're going to allow the character to feed from it. For example, if your character creates a storm that destroys someone's home, you should be able to feed from it. If the same storm is naturally occurring, it should require devastation on at least a neighborhood level, if not citywide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is what I'm talking about. I'd be very interested to see what you come up with.<br /> <br /> Edit again: I'm now picturing a merit, or perhaps an atavism, for a &quot;scavenger&quot; type of Beast that makes this type of feeding possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 01-17-2018, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T13:24:16-08:00","id":1177032,"title":"","content":"Okay, different question, this time it's about Family Dinner. The wording on &quot;hunting&quot; seems imprecise enough to me that I'd like to see what everyone else thinks. So the text makes it quite clear that there are two independent activities that could each provide 1 Satiety, &quot;hunting&quot; and &quot;feeding&quot; (and they aren't exclusive). It's easy enough to picture a &quot;hunt&quot; without &quot;feeding&quot; (say, Iron Masters who don't generally eat their sacred prey), but then further down the text makes the stipulation that targets that &quot;allow themselves to be 'hunted' do not qualify as proper targets for Family Dinner&quot;. Now hang on, are they not valid targets, period? Or do they just not qualify for the first point of Satiety for &quot;hunting&quot;? Because if it's the former, which it seems pretty emphatic about, then what <i>would</i> qualify as a &quot;feeding&quot; without a &quot;hunt&quot;? Because the first thing that comes to mind, a vampire feeding from thralls, is expressly excluded. I can understand why they wouldn't want to make Family Dinner too easy (themes of the game and all that)...but it's explicitly defined that &quot;hunting&quot; isn't required (and then later says that &quot;the hunt must be genuine&quot;)! Someone please tell me what I'm missing. The longer I look at it the more frustrated I get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T13:50:28-08:00","id":1177038,"title":"","content":"The hunt needing to be genuine means it can't be a staged event. Like a vampire feeding on a person who's volunteered to be fed on wouldn't count as a hunt just because they agreed to run since the vamp wanted a chase.<br /> <br /> As for feeding without a hunt, I'd say it would be an impersonal thing. Just random action that leads to the necessary actions of a feeding. A vampire grabbing a random person walking by and sinking their fangs in to the person's neck, a changeling making a glib/offhand comment that just happens to set the mood properly for a feeding, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:27:26-08:00","id":1177051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177038#post1177038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hunt needing to be genuine means it can't be a staged event. Like a vampire feeding on a person who's volunteered to be fed on wouldn't count as a hunt just because they agreed to run since the vamp wanted a chase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I think I get that part...but would it still count as a &quot;feeding&quot; or not? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T17:22:09-08:00","id":1177095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177051#post1177051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I think I get that part...but would it still count as a &quot;feeding&quot; or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially this is an ST thing. (It does expressly say ultimately comes down to the ST's call.) The way I see it a volunteer would still need to be a free target. Like if I recall there was a clan in vampire ,Salurbi I think, who couldn't feed off unwilling targets. All their food had to be coerced, bargained, etc from the target. So one of them making the exchange of &quot;I'll fix your relative and I get to take some of your blood.&quot; would be fair game. <br /> <br /> I think the idea is that family dinner would be the metaphysical equivalent of the hyena or jackals waiting for the lion to finish eating its food to grab its own lunch from the scraps. So, it doesn't work if the family member basically went to the refrigerator and pulled out beer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:58:52-08:00","id":1177344,"title":"","content":"That section could certainly do with a bit of clarification, but I view the restriction on tame targets applying to the Hunt aspect, not Family Dinner as a whole. After all, it doesn't bar any of the numerous &quot;Feeding&quot; options that don't involve sapient prey at all, just notes that they need to be dealing with hunger of a supernatural origin. Many of the CofD splats replenish fuel primarily from non human(like) sources, making &quot;Tame&quot; a hard to apply distinction. If a Changeling gets glamour from a goblin fruit, is it tame because it didn't put up a fight? Or is it not, because it's an inanimate object incapable of agreeing to anything? (There are probably goblin fruits that are exceptions to that but for the sake of this question I'm assuming one of the less strange ones)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:52:12-08:00","id":1177362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177344#post1177344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Many of the CofD splats replenish fuel primarily from non human(like) sources, making &quot;Tame&quot; a hard to apply distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is perhaps a sign that &quot;regaining fuel&quot; is not the operative definition of &quot;feed&quot; that Family Dinner works on \u2014 I would let a Beast piggyback on a Promethean regaining Willpower from their Torment or a mage pursuing their Obsessions, but not the former drawing Pyros from a fusebox or the latter performing a quiet oblation at a Hallow to gain Mana.<br /> <br /> The thematic tone of Family Dinner is &quot;this is bad for <i>somebody </i>involved in the process,&quot; and it feels dishonest to read it in ways that defy that tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T11:51:29-08:00","id":1177377,"title":"","content":"can a beast enter a dream to influence it or is it just impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T09:55:27-08:00","id":1177628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177377#post1177377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can a beast enter a dream to influence it or is it just impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is presently nothing that allows a Beast to go full Freddy Krueger, or Inception. The only ways I finding another splat with an ability that might allow it and asking them to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T11:40:25-08:00","id":1177650,"title":"","content":"Nothing in the RAW. But we know the Horror can enter dreams in order to feed, so I feel like it's not unreasonable to let the merged Beast do the same thing -- there just hasn't been any discussion of mechanics. I feel like Changeling 2nd's oneiromancy rules could be adapted for use in a Beast game, but that's obviously not helpful unless you backed the Kickstarter for that and have access to the manuscript previews.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T16:24:12-08:00","id":1177710,"title":"","content":"A Primordial Pathway will get you into someone's dreams easy, but once it actually closes and drops you there you're separated from your Horror again and don't have any special powers to influence the dream beyond what you could do in meatspace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T22:27:53-08:00","id":1177998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177710#post1177710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Primordial Pathway will get you into someone's dreams easy, but once it actually closes and drops you there you're separated from your Horror again and don't have any special powers to influence the dream beyond what you could do in meatspace.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be coming down to a different of interpretation, but--a Beast in meatspace can impose Lair Traits, use Atavisms and inflict Nightmares. Why wouldn't a Beast in someone's dream be able to do the same things? Granted, using Nightmares when you're already <i>in </i>a nightmare might have some very weird effects, and a Beast still wouldn't have the level of granular control over the dream that a Changeling would.<br /> <br /> I'm personally hoping the Player's Guide discusses this more explicitly (along with other stuff related to Hives and Pathways.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T00:06:56-08:00","id":1178006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177998#post1177998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may be coming down to a different of interpretation, but--a Beast in meatspace can impose Lair Traits, use Atavisms and inflict Nightmares. Why wouldn't a Beast in someone's dream be able to do the same things? Granted, using Nightmares when you're already <i>in </i>a nightmare might have some very weird effects, and a Beast still wouldn't have the level of granular control over the dream that a Changeling would.<br /> <br /> I'm personally hoping the Player's Guide discusses this more explicitly (along with other stuff related to Hives and Pathways.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I tend to run it - a Beast loose in the Temenos or an Oneiros has the same powers it does in meatspace, although I generally make it so that the flash of the Horror that supernaturals witness in Twilight when a Beast uses an Atavism is visible to anyone and sticks around for longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T04:45:38-08:00","id":1178032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1177998#post1177998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't a Beast in someone's dream be able to do the same things?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can: &quot;don't have any special powers to influence the dream beyond what you could do in meatspace.&quot; Means you can do the things you could do in the waking world there, which includes atavisms/lair traits/etc., you just don't get anything special for travelling into a dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T17:14:41-08:00","id":1178600,"title":"","content":"so they just scare people in the waking world then? that's a bit disappointing and a missed opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T17:40:22-08:00","id":1178615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1178600#post1178600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so they just scare people in the waking world then? that's a bit disappointing and a missed opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? We just said that they can do anything they can do in the waking world in the dreams.... So they can use their nightmares/atavisms/open primordial paths/lair traits. and they can feed on people's fears in dreams. They just don't get any special systems for influencing dreams beyond &quot;travel into dream and do stuff in it using their various abilities&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-23-2018, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:42:35-08:00","id":1178762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1178615#post1178615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? We just said that they can do anything they can do in the waking world in the dreams.... So they can use their nightmares/atavisms/open primordial paths/lair traits. and they can feed on people's fears in dreams. They just don't get any special systems for influencing dreams beyond &quot;travel into dream and do stuff in it using their various abilities&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>oooooooh. dang sorry. i must i've misread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T22:05:43-08:00","id":1179110,"title":"","content":"Technically, a person's head is full of Goetia if you pull from Mage, and eating a person's Goetia can have some profound narrative consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T02:02:49-08:00","id":1179140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1179110#post1179110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, a person's head is full of Goetia if you pull from Mage, and eating a person's Goetia can have some profound narrative consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Beasts enter someone\u2019s Oneiros from their dreams, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T11:41:52-08:00","id":1179269,"title":"","content":"They can open a Primordial Pathway directly to someone's Oneiros (BtP, p. 97).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T21:45:40-08:00","id":1180602,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I'm sure some of this has been asked before and I think it's already in the books. I'm thinking of running a Beast / Golden Age of Piracy chronicle, and have a few basic questions.<br /> <br /> 1. Can some remind me how feeding and feasting works? beasts feed on fear, is it only fear or more emotions? do they have to kill? is there some benefit to killing? what's the benefit of having non beasts involved?<br /> 2. Sometimes in dreams the landscape can change suddenly, or things can loop, etc, but my reading of beast is that there are basically different rooms, is there a way to emulate some of the weird effects one might experience in dreams? what about falling? you know that dream where you're falling, how can you handle that in your lair?<br /> 3. When a beast attacks someone, they are in their dreams? do they have any more control over that environment, and directing it? can beasts easily roam about the primordial dream, and other parts of the dream, outside of their lair?<br /> 4. how much of what beasts know is learned vs innate? how much do they understand about what they are when it first happens? how much do they then understand about their ... cousins.. the other splats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T06:12:58-08:00","id":1180685,"title":"","content":"1) It is fear, shock, and terror, as well as family dinners. Killing is a bonus to the feeding dice pool, but not required. Family dinners are what happens when more supernaturals get involved.<br /> 2) Beasts have The Primordial Dream, which works on the small statistics as other ephemeral realms, but have some slight dice bonus. The lairs they inhabit are specific nightmares, usually tied to terrifying events and locations in the material world. The lair chambers are entirely in the hands of the beast. Lair traits help define them, and what's going on.<br /> <br /> 3) The Horror may roam the natural chambers of an areas Hive, which are other locations like it's own chambers that naturally form. You have some bonuses to combat in the PD, and can open portals to and from it with some stringent rolls.<br /> <br /> 4) That is up to the player and ST.<br /> <br /> I'm on my phone, so that's the short version. Will get you some more details in a few hours if no one beats me to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:17:01-08:00","id":1180815,"title":"","content":"To go into more detail regarding Feeding, family dinner is basically a sort of Voyeurism where a Beast can get a little bit of Satiety by watching one of their cousins feed (from an unwilling victim, though. Blood dolls dont count). Neither Victim nor Cousin need to be aware of the Beast watching, though. The main benefit of Family Dinner is the Beast doesn't need to do anything other than watch, so it's ideal for the lazy or out-of-options. On the other hand, it's not as satisfying, so there is less Satiety to be gotten.<br /> Regarding the Fear, a Beast needs to cause a certain type of fear, as indicated by their Family and Hunger. Their Hunger also tells you a bit more about what they do to feed: Collectors collect, Tyrants exert dominance, Ravagers destroy etc(not limited to physical acts: destroying someone's confidence or belief certainly would count).<br /> <br /> Regarding how much they understand: At least some - they get a free dot of Occult to represent a certain innate understanding/connection. So while they might not know much about their cousins, they are aware that there are other supernatural creatures that are different from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:33:50-08:00","id":1181006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1180685#post1180685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The Horror may roam the natural chambers of an areas Hive, which are other locations like it's own chambers that naturally form. You have some bonuses to combat in the PD, and can open portals to and from it with some stringent rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>right, the hive, other members of the beasts family, but what about outside of that even, the general dream realm? or the person they are attacking's dreams? and what about things like the ever falling? or I even remember BtP mentioning doing things like dreams with teeth falling out. How does that work? if it's PC's being affected by a beast antagonist how does that work? to simplify I'm trying to figure out the exact limitations of beasts in a &quot;dream scape&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T22:45:39-08:00","id":1181023,"title":"","content":"So a thing, it would appear the Horror is reluctant to leave the Lair, so exploring the dreamscapes outside of the Lair might require some work if you want to do it in a way that isn't walking in your street form. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Beast core pg 99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bBeasts exploiting Kinship<br /> with mages or changelings sometimes find themselves wandering<br /> the greater dream-realms beyond their Lairs, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now onto the next part.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1181006#post1181006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> right, the hive, other members of the beasts family, but what about outside of that even, the general dream realm? or the person they are attacking's dreams? and what about things like the ever falling? or I even remember BtP mentioning doing things like dreams with teeth falling out. How does that work? if it's PC's being affected by a beast antagonist how does that work? to simplify I'm trying to figure out the exact limitations of beasts in a &quot;dream scape&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A merged Beast* does not have access to it's Nightmares. So, while a Beast can use All Your Teeth Fall Out on a random person walking the streets in the real world they would not be able to do so merged with the Horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Unified, completed, whole, what are we calling a Beast that's entered their Lair and temporarily become one with Horror?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T00:21:45-08:00","id":1181034,"title":"","content":"You read that wrong, it's the Horror on its own that can't use Nightmares. They work just fine while merged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:36:17-08:00","id":1181094,"title":"","content":"Seconding <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a>: by my reading, merging with their Horror gives the Beast access to everything at their usual disposal plus a neat little buff. Atavisms are still restricted by actual Satiety, while on their own (read: not merged), a Horror can use every aspect of their Atavisms as it pleases (albeit still needs to expend Satiety for the Expenditure part) but not use any Nightmares.<br /> <br /> This differenciation matters because during your story, the Horror might come under attack by an invading Hero (or Changeling/Mage/Hunter...), while the Beast - as in, the human body of the trinity (Physical Human Body, Dreamscape Lair, Metaphysical Horror 'Body') that makes up the Beast- is not merged with it. And killing the Horror does kill the Beast, as does collapsing the Heart of the Lair.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T21:34:05-08:00","id":1185013,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone. I have a query on your opinion of this rules interpretation. Near the section about low Satiety where it describes the Horror seeking sustenance in its own in intervals based on Lair there is a sidebar called the horror itself. Based on a statement in this section that says the Horror only leaves the Lair if it is Starving or Ravenous my storyteller has made the following decision: if the character leaves thier Lair while Starving or Ravenous they leave as thier horror and behave like an ephemeral entitiy. I do not believe this is true, however I cannot find a definitive statement either way. I personally interpret this as an extension of the rule governing when the Horror leaves in search of sustenance and feeds on people close to the character. What are your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T21:51:00-08:00","id":1185016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1185013#post1185013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone. I have a query on your opinion of this rules interpretation. Near the section about low Satiety where it describes the Horror seeking sustenance in its own in intervals based on Lair there is a sidebar called the horror itself. Based on a statement in this section that says the Horror only leaves the Lair if it is Starving or Ravenous my storyteller has made the following decision: if the character leaves thier Lair while Starving or Ravenous they leave as thier horror and behave like an ephemeral entitiy. I do not believe this is true, however I cannot find a definitive statement either way. I personally interpret this as an extension of the rule governing when the Horror leaves in search of sustenance and feeds on people close to the character. What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>No: the Begotten (the mortal shell) and Horror (Beastly soul) are technically separate entities. In a way similar to how the Sin Eater and Geist are separate entities.<br /> <br /> So when the rule is referring to the Horror leaving its Lair, they're talking about the entity that gives the Begotten their power, and not the Begotten themselves. So in this case, your ST's interpretation would technically be untrue since the Horror entering and leaving the Lair isn't completely dependent on the Begotten entering or leaving their Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T04:56:18-08:00","id":1185109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1185016#post1185016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No: the Begotten (the mortal shell) and Horror (Beastly soul) are technically separate entities. In a way similar to how the Sin Eater and Geist are separate entities.<br /> <br /> So when the rule is referring to the Horror leaving its Lair, they're talking about the entity that gives the Begotten their power, and not the Begotten themselves. So in this case, your ST's interpretation would technically be untrue since the Horror entering and leaving the Lair isn't completely dependent on the Begotten entering or leaving their Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<br /> Additionally, they probably hunt through the Primordial Dream (think Astral as opposed to the &quot;normal&quot; world, but in Twilight). Since they attacking other dreamers, unless you want to import the Dream Bastion rules from Changeling, ephemeral traits probably don't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T14:58:13-08:00","id":1185736,"title":"","content":"If a Beast is in their lair, do they instantly morph into their Horror or is it more like a changing breed situation where they can (mostly) control the transformation?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, can a Beast and a Horror be in the lair at the same time? I ask because the mental image is really cool in my mind. (smol botanist standing with what is essentially godzilla)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T16:03:11-08:00","id":1185755,"title":"","content":"It's an almost instantaneous merging unless the Horror is Gorged and thus asleep. That's also the only time they can be in the Lair at the same time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T16:25:44-08:00","id":1185764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1185736#post1185736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Beast is in their lair, do they instantly morph into their Horror or is it more like a changing breed situation where they can (mostly) control the transformation?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, can a Beast and a Horror be in the lair at the same time? I ask because the mental image is really cool in my mind. (smol botanist standing with what is essentially godzilla)</div> </div> </div> </div>What Master Aquatosic said. <br /> <br /> Still, it would be incredibly thematic for a Beast to slowly transform into what she really is in front of people, after having discretely opened a Pathway so that they\u2019re all already in her Lair. (In this interpretation, the instant transformation rule is there to prevent merging from being a possible vulnerability, rather than strict enforcing instant-ness.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T23:19:39-08:00","id":1185834,"title":"","content":"Could someone remind me, a Beast, a Mage, and a Demon walk into a room. Does the beast know that the mage is such immediately? would it immediately roll contested for the demon? or does the beast actually have to be trying to notice the other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T23:46:43-08:00","id":1185838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1185834#post1185834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone remind me, a Beast, a Mage, and a Demon walk into a room. Does the beast know that the mage is such immediately? would it immediately roll contested for the demon? or does the beast actually have to be trying to notice the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the mage: Assuming nothing supernatural has been done yet in the scene, the Beast reflexively rolls Wits + Occult + Lair - the mage's Composure + Wisdom; apart from a heightened chance of failure, this works as normal.<br /> <br /> For the demon: Assuming the demon is in Cover, before anything else, the demon may roll their Cover rating as an unresisted and uncontested reflexive action; if this roll succeeds, Family Resemblance detects nothing, and if it fails, the Wits + Occult + Lair - Composure roll proceeds as normal except without the possibility of exceptional success; after a successful roll, the Beast and the demon engage in the Clash of Wills to determine who gets a complicating Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T16:06:20-08:00","id":1186114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1185838#post1185838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the mage: Assuming nothing supernatural has been done yet in the scene, the Beast reflexively rolls Wits + Occult + Lair - the mage's Composure + Wisdom; apart from a heightened chance of failure, this works as normal.<br /> <br /> For the demon: Assuming the demon is in Cover, before anything else, the demon may roll their Cover rating as an unresisted and uncontested reflexive action; if this roll succeeds, Family Resemblance detects nothing, and if it fails, the Wits + Occult + Lair - Composure roll proceeds as normal except without the possibility of exceptional success; after a successful roll, the Beast and the demon engage in the Clash of Wills to determine who gets a complicating Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks that mostly tells me what I need to know, except more complicated, 4 beasts (PCs) walk on to a ship with say 12 other splats (nothing obvious going on, everyone in cover, blushed, etc), and 100 mortals... now as the GM doing 4*12 rolls seems like a terrible idea, is there a better way to resolve this? and to complicate it more, what if one of the other splats is a vampire in torpor in a box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T16:46:23-08:00","id":1186124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1186114#post1186114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks that mostly tells me what I need to know, except more complicated, 4 beasts (PCs) walk on to a ship with say 12 other splats (nothing obvious going on, everyone in cover, blushed, etc), and 100 mortals... now as the GM doing 4*12 rolls seems like a terrible idea, is there a better way to resolve this? and to complicate it more, what if one of the other splats is a vampire in torpor in a box.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roll for the characters who're paying attention when they're paying attention to characters for whom this would matter \u2014 this is otherwise the epitome of a white-room circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T18:43:07-08:00","id":1186149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1186124#post1186124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roll for the characters who're paying attention when they're paying attention to characters for whom this would matter \u2014 this is otherwise the epitome of a white-room circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>is it really white room if I'm planning on dumping a bunch of Beasts on a Merchant vessel with a handful of other splats tossed in? I'm going to run Beast during the Golden age of Piracy, so trying to figure out the best way to handle such things. I figure I put a few PC beasts onto a ship that has other supernatural tenants and they're all going to be bumping into each other very quickly. Probably in the first few minutes when the ship is getting underway. I was going to dump a vampire in the cargo hold, headed to America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T20:36:05-08:00","id":1186169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1186149#post1186149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it really white room if I'm planning on dumping a bunch of Beasts on a Merchant vessel with a handful of other splats tossed in? I'm going to run Beast during the Golden age of Piracy, so trying to figure out the best way to handle such things. I figure I put a few PC beasts onto a ship that has other supernatural tenants and they're all going to be bumping into each other very quickly. Probably in the first few minutes when the ship is getting underway. I was going to dump a vampire in the cargo hold, headed to America.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I am saying is that you are literally not going to be in the situation where <i>all four Beasts</i> are encountering <i>all twelve monsters</i> at the <i>same exact point in the narrative</i>, unless your goal is to have the exact story beat of &quot;the four of you each saw all twelve of these other monsters within seconds of each other, and it is significant that you all come to separate conclusions about each of them despite being in a context where they can communicate.&quot; Most pacing structures parcel out that many characters over the course of the story rather than dumping them all in front of the camera at the start.<br /> <br /> The roll for Family Resemblance matters when you need more information than the automatic basic success provided for unveiled kin. Anything that's not an Unchained or in the &quot;fundamentally human&quot; category can be pinged as a basic member of their species without a roll as long as they aren't magically hiding what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:29:44-08:00","id":1186673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1186149#post1186149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it really white room if I'm planning on dumping a bunch of Beasts on a Merchant vessel with a handful of other splats tossed in? I'm going to run Beast during the Golden age of Piracy, so trying to figure out the best way to handle such things. I figure I put a few PC beasts onto a ship that has other supernatural tenants and they're all going to be bumping into each other very quickly. Probably in the first few minutes when the ship is getting underway. I was going to dump a vampire in the cargo hold, headed to America.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it is really going to be one single big moment than just do a pooled rolls system. Only roll once for the Beasts, use the highest and assume they will share what they notice with the others. That could cut it down a whole lot.<br /> <br /> If you want to reduce it even more then you could group the others by supernatural type, again use the highest. If they succeed on the roll against the highest Composure+Wisdom mage then they notice all of them, etc. It may not be perfectly mechanically accurate but it works for that narrative moment when they start to notice how every third person seems to be a Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T15:16:14-08:00","id":1189026,"title":"","content":"Let's say a Beast has a phobia of something prior to their Homecoming/Devouring. After the Homecoming, do they still have that phobia or are they less scared of it?<br /> <br /> (I'm asking mostly because the idea of what amounts to Godzilla being afraid of the ocean is fucking hilarious)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:03:20-08:00","id":1189064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1189026#post1189026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say a Beast has a phobia of something prior to their Homecoming/Devouring. After the Homecoming, do they still have that phobia or are they less scared of it?<br /> <br /> (I'm asking mostly because the idea of what amounts to Godzilla being afraid of the ocean is fucking hilarious)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that's 100% up to the player and/or Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T13:36:37-08:00","id":1189455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1189026#post1189026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say a Beast has a phobia of something prior to their Homecoming/Devouring. After the Homecoming, do they still have that phobia or are they less scared of it?<br /> <br /> (I'm asking mostly because the idea of what amounts to Godzilla being afraid of the ocean is fucking hilarious)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much what Wardragon says. I'd imagine certain phobias would probably clear up like a fear of drowning would probably clear up after discovering you were having the drowning dream because you're actually a nightmare piranha swarm, but this would probably not do a thing towards clearing up your arachnaphobia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:10:55-08:00","id":1193506,"title":"","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> Beast Player Guide: at Ravenous Maw, low Satiety effect... can you eat, A.K.A. instant kill, a victim after you engulf them?<br /> <br /> The other Atavism, Enemy Within, can change your clothes too? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:47:09-08:00","id":1193599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1193506#post1193506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello.<br /> <br /> Beast Player Guide: at Ravenous Maw, low Satiety effect... can you eat, A.K.A. instant kill, a victim after you engulf them?<br /> <br /> The other Atavism, Enemy Within, can change your clothes too?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the satiety expenditure on the atavism allows you to choose to inflict lethal damage I would say low satiety probably doesn't include autokill unless the target is out cold. That said I would also posit that said courtesy only applies to PCs (because otherwise where's the fun) or significant enemies. Extras are SOL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:53:32-08:00","id":1193602,"title":"","content":"Got a question (or rather, a fetch quest) because I can't find it: Where was it explained what Chambers looked like? I somehow keep thinking they resemble the actual physical space, but with additional changes due to Lair Traits. That seems at odds with me thinking they can easily be whatever you want them to be. Anyone got a page for me? Pretty please? ^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:44:11-08:00","id":1193621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1193602#post1193602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a question (or rather, a fetch quest) because I can't find it: Where was it explained what Chambers looked like? I somehow keep thinking they resemble the actual physical space, but with additional changes due to Lair Traits. That seems at odds with me thinking they can easily be whatever you want them to be. Anyone got a page for me? Pretty please? ^^&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the general thing a lot of people have gone with since there wasn't a ton of explanation on the appearance. Plus the player's guide now saying the chambers sort of tells the Beast's story would make some sense to view the chambers as distorted versions of the seed location.<br /> <br /> That said page 151 of the player's guide does imply it a bit more when the example chamber of a church near a mall is used since it says the Beast could leave the church to explore the fragile dream mall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:48:45-08:00","id":1193625,"title":"","content":"Thank you !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:05:29-08:00","id":1193630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1193621#post1193621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the general thing a lot of people have gone with since there wasn't a ton of explanation on the appearance. Plus the player's guide now saying the chambers sort of tells the Beast's story would make some sense to view the chambers as distorted versions of the seed location.<br /> <br /> That said page 151 of the player's guide does imply it a bit more when the example chamber of a church near a mall is used since it says the Beast could leave the church to explore the fragile dream mall.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks a bunch, that helped a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:41:22-08:00","id":1193649,"title":"","content":"So one way of gestating a Horrorspawn is to carry it with you (as opposed to leaving it in your Lair until it's ready). Would a Beast gestating a Spawn look visibly pregnant in normal, human form? Or, since the Spawn is part of the Primordial Dream, is it more like a Fettered spirit superimposed on the human Beast when viewed through the right lens?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T13:37:17-08:00","id":1193689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1193602#post1193602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a question (or rather, a fetch quest) because I can't find it: Where was it explained what Chambers looked like? I somehow keep thinking they resemble the actual physical space, but with additional changes due to Lair Traits. That seems at odds with me thinking they can easily be whatever you want them to be. Anyone got a page for me? Pretty please? ^^&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on what nalak42 said, Chambers are definitely based on whatever physical location they were formed in, but also take on characteristics that befit the dreamlike and psycoreflective nature of the Primordial Dream. <i>Beast</i> is a very figurative game; things often look like what they do because &quot;that's how this sort of thing is supposed to look.&quot; So in this case, I'd say start with the physical location and then overlay features based on the nature of the event that created the Chamber, the Family and Hunger of the controlling Beast and the controlling Beast's (or Beasts') traits.<br /> <br /> For example, an old warehouse that gets turned into a Chamber for a Talassii spider Horror might be filled up with giant spiderwebs. And if the Beast has Lair traits such as Maze and No Exit, then the warehouse might be filled with boxes that create a maze-like obstacle course for intruders to struggle through, unable to find a door or window to get out. BUT. If instead, a Namtaru whose Horror is a living pile of industrial effluent and who has Lair traits like Heat and Toxic (are those real? I don't have access to my books at work...) might instead turn the very same warehouse into insufferable cesspool with chemicals flowing down the walls and across the floor, and an oppressive heat sapping the strength of anyone who enters. And an Ugallu might have a warehouse that seems to be a mile across, utterly empty no cover or shade and bright lights shining down on intruders, who run and run toward the distant doors while <i>something</i> swings though the rafters far overhead...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:22:36-08:00","id":1193695,"title":"","content":"Do horrors choose there beast or they just get stuck with what a random smruck no matter how unfitting they are","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:29:14-08:00","id":1193697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1193695#post1193695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do horrors choose there beast or they just get stuck with what a random smruck no matter how unfitting they are</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much always the former.<br /> <br /> The Horrors are depicted as being the ones to seek out a potential Begotten. The Player's Guide does describe some Beasts that end up regretting and disappointed when they discover what the source of their nightmares actually are, and act unsatisfactorily in a way that the Horror also regrets their choice, but that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T14:36:16-08:00","id":1193701,"title":"","content":"I find that kinda of funny !maybe they can try to mold them into a more fitting form what methods what they use to do that do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T02:30:53-08:00","id":1193856,"title":"","content":"The Extreme Heat Lair Trait wouldn't provide immunity to mundane fires, would it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T03:27:06-08:00","id":1193868,"title":"","content":"Nope, only to Extreme Heat, like wandering in the desert or in coal mines or other places. You could argue that they wouldn't suffer from the heat a fire gives off, so if they were in a burning building in a room that's not on fire, they'd be fine, but that's a very specific scenario.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am still slightly sad that Razoured does not provide immunity to bladed weapons, despite being aware of the balancing issues that would cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T08:58:30-07:00","id":1194548,"title":"","content":"This may not be a simple enough question, but what would be appropriate starting Lair Traits for an Inguma Horror that is 'the Queen of the Other Kind' - the faerie queen, the witch-ruler, the queen of the criminal underworld. I'm thinking definitely Minions, but I'd like something else comparatively easy to bring about in the physical world. Would Dim Light work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:12:39-07:00","id":1194576,"title":"","content":"Maze, Sealed Exits, Fog, Swarms, Undergrowth, Engulfing, Mirages, and Razored would all work for a faerie queen. I'd say sealed exits, fog, and maybe maze are the easiest to find analogs to in the real world. Sealed exits could be any condemned building. Fog for obvious reasons. Maze would be a warehouse or even a hospital.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:28:05-07:00","id":1194585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194576#post1194576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maze, Sealed Exits, Fog, Swarms, Undergrowth, Engulfing, Mirages, and Razored would all work for a faerie queen. I'd say sealed exits, fog, and maybe maze are the easiest to find analogs to in the real world. Sealed exits could be any condemned building. Fog for obvious reasons. Maze would be a warehouse or even a hospital.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of something like a proliferation of thorny brambles (that is, Razored and Undergrowth), but would it be possible to create the conditions for Razored with, say, broken glass which becomes thorns growing out from subterranean vines, then manifesting Undergrowth draws up the vines. Does that sound workable, or is broken glass too far from that brand of Razored?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:45:32-07:00","id":1194591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194585#post1194585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of something like a proliferation of thorny brambles (that is, Razored and Undergrowth), but would it be possible to create the conditions for Razored with, say, broken glass which becomes thorns growing out from subterranean vines, then manifesting Undergrowth draws up the vines. Does that sound workable, or is broken glass too far from that brand of Razored?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you had a bunch of jagged glass around, I'd allow it in my game. It could be a pile of smashed windows and frames, walls topped with broken glass, etc. Also, keep an eye out for things like razor wire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T11:46:41-07:00","id":1194592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194591#post1194591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you had a bunch of jagged glass around, I'd allow it in my game. It could be a pile of smashed windows and frames, walls topped with broken glass, etc. Also, keep an eye out for things like razor wire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, razor/barbed wire would definitely work. It's just that it's often easier to break a window than it is to lug around a bundle of barbed wire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T12:16:36-07:00","id":1194598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194592#post1194592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, razor/barbed wire would definitely work. It's just that it's often easier to break a window than it is to lug around a bundle of barbed wire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I would say it takes more than a broken window to be able to invoke your trait. The example the book uses for Downpour is to activate a building's sprinkler system. A water faucet wouldn't work. So, just one broken window wouldn't either. However, something like the scene in Die Hard when they shoot out all the glass to keep the barefoot John from moving around easily would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T12:20:22-07:00","id":1194601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194598#post1194598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but I would say it takes more than a broken window to be able to invoke your trait. The example the book uses for Downpour is to activate a building's sprinkler system. A water faucet wouldn't work. So, just one broken window wouldn't either. However, something like the scene in Die Hard when they shoot out all the glass to keep the barefoot John from moving around easily would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T12:28:16-07:00","id":1194605,"title":"","content":"Smoke grenades make a fine Tool for invoking Fog, but it's costly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T18:35:17-07:00","id":1194691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1193649#post1193649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one way of gestating a Horrorspawn is to carry it with you (as opposed to leaving it in your Lair until it's ready). Would a Beast gestating a Spawn look visibly pregnant in normal, human form? Or, since the Spawn is part of the Primordial Dream, is it more like a Fettered spirit superimposed on the human Beast when viewed through the right lens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Related: this section claims that you can't just conceive and give birth to a Horrorspawn, and states that <i>all</i> Horrorspawn must be incubated in the Lair. It then proceeds to describe two different methods of creating Horrorspawn (one of which is highly similar to 'just' conceiving, though the act required is obviously more complex than that) both of which allow the Beast to carry the spawn around in their physical body if they choose instead of incubating it in their Lair, and the fluff that follows <i>definitely</i> makes it seem like a physical birth in the material world is going to happen.<br /> <br /> The section on physical bodies describes that, after incubating in the Lair, the Horrorspawn don't have physical bodies and goes on to describe how one can be procured for them. Does this also apply to Horrorspawn that are carried by the Beast herself? Are they 'born' somehow bodiless? This isn't clear.<br /> <br /> These sections kind of read as if the ability to carry and birth the Horrorspawn was a last-minute addition without further adjustments being made to the text to fully accommodate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T19:22:01-07:00","id":1194702,"title":"","content":"I mean, I assumed that that the &quot;birth&quot; happens with the Beast in her Lair (and probably looks more like an alien chestburster than anything). I'm just speculating on whether it makes sense for the Beast to look pregnant outside the Lair -- it potentially introduces some fun complications for the duration of the gestation (especially for men and male-passing Beasts) but it also runs into the very problems you're pointing out of the Spawn basically being a goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:46:54-07:00","id":1194835,"title":"","content":"Does imposing Minions/Thralls allow the entities in question to manifest as if they were in the Lair, or are they restricted to Twilight Form?<br /> <br /> Minions have the option to impose various tilts - what dice pools should be used for this? I understand it could happen kind of 'at random' but that doesn't work well for my table. Would you let them have the opportunity to do such if the trait was imposed?<br /> <br /> I'm a little torn on these questions because, on one hand, I want to stick with the general rules around how Goetia and other astral phenomena manifest in the physical world, but on the other hand, I'm a firm believer that there should never be any Lair traits that have no effect when imposed (and ideally, all of them should function at 'full power' when imposed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T08:13:29-07:00","id":1194841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194835#post1194835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does imposing Minions/Thralls allow the entities in question to manifest as if they were in the Lair, or are they restricted to Twilight Form?<br /> <br /> Minions have the option to impose various tilts - what dice pools should be used for this? I understand it could happen kind of 'at random' but that doesn't work well for my table. Would you let them have the opportunity to do such if the trait was imposed?<br /> <br /> I'm a little torn on these questions because, on one hand, I want to stick with the general rules around how Goetia and other astral phenomena manifest in the physical world, but on the other hand, I'm a firm believer that there should never be any Lair traits that have no effect when imposed (and ideally, all of them should function at 'full power' when imposed).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably have them roll Power + Finesse - Defense to inflict a Tilt on someone. And I'd also probably have them manifest if imposed, as a special case (though obviously they can't leave the affected area).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T08:16:34-07:00","id":1194842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194841#post1194841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd probably have them roll Power + Finesse - Defense to inflict a Tilt on someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you handle actually calculating those for Minions specifically? There's no guidance on stating them out that I can see. I actually don't know if Actors have Attributes at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T09:19:07-07:00","id":1194865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194842#post1194842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you handle actually calculating those for Minions specifically? There's no guidance on stating them out that I can see. I actually don't know if Actors have Attributes at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn that something in the book stated that Actors in the Lair have the Horror's Attributes divided by two, but now I can't seem to find that. Huh. Maybe the implication is that, like other scaling traits, you're supposed to stat them yourself, which affects your immunity/imposition?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, so this is in the rules for the Thralls Trait:<br /> <br /> &quot;As dream creatures, the thrall's traits are half the Horror's, rounded down, and each thrall may use one of the Beast's Atavisms.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I guess that's what I was thinking of. My first intuition is that Actors should use half the Horror's Attributes, rounded down, and don't have access to any Atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 03-13-2018, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T10:43:19-07:00","id":1194887,"title":"","content":"I think the minions/thralls should definitely be considered to be &quot;physically&quot; present. One feature of imposing Lair traits is that the magic is in the summoning, not material effect. Imposing Downpour makes <i>real </i>water fall from the sky; Blazing Light makes <i>real </i>sunlight shine in the area. (it explicitly says that you can hurt vampires this way, which would only happen if the light truly is sunlight)<br /> <br /> Carrying that over to Minions and Thralls, the magic is giving them purchase in the real world temporarily; you're not creating false bodies for them or anything, they're now <i>there </i>just as much as they are in the Lair. So I would say that there's no mechanical difference between an imposed minion/thrall and one in the Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","user":"Gellydog","date":". 03-13-2018, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T16:42:49-07:00","id":1195029,"title":"","content":"This may have been asked before oh well,<br /> <br /> Can a Begotten bring things into their Lair? For example, a Collector keeping their ill gotten gains in their Lair. Or a Beast hides a weapon they can use later in the Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","user":"AdorableChou","date":". 03-13-2018, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T16:58:46-07:00","id":1195033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1195029#post1195029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may have been asked before oh well,<br /> <br /> Can a Begotten bring things into their Lair? For example, a Collector keeping their ill gotten gains in their Lair. Or a Beast hides a weapon they can use later in the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly a thing that they can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T18:00:47-07:00","id":1195055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1195029#post1195029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may have been asked before oh well,<br /> <br /> Can a Begotten bring things into their Lair? For example, a Collector keeping their ill gotten gains in their Lair. Or a Beast hides a weapon they can use later in the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's actually recommended as a storage place in Doppleganger atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T19:08:31-07:00","id":1195072,"title":"","content":"Can a beast keep animals children or plants in there lair physical unharmed because I\u2019m thinking about a beast that loves puppies and kittens. But humans just kinda of meh and uses there lair to take care of puppy mill rescues . And of course brutulty maims the humans running it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T19:24:08-07:00","id":1195078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1195072#post1195072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a beast keep animals children or plants in there lair physical unharmed because I\u2019m thinking about a beast that loves puppies and kittens. But humans just kinda of meh and uses there lair to take care of puppy mill rescues . And of course brutulty maims the humans running it</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends in part on the Lair Traits, but the BPG has a merit that lets you make one Chamber of your Lair into a sort of &quot;guest bedroom&quot; where visitors can safely reside.<br /> <br /> There is also art of some kind of squid-woman with a Lair full of cats and it is adorable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T19:27:56-07:00","id":1195079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1195078#post1195078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends in part on the Lair Traits, but the BPG has a merit that lets you make one Chamber of your Lair into a sort of &amp;quot;guest bedroom&amp;quot; where visitors can safely reside.<br /> <br /> There is also art of some kind of squid-woman with a Lair full of cats and it is adorable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the squad women\u2019s art is in the players guide? Meow meow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T04:07:33-07:00","id":1195214,"title":"","content":"Quick question(s) regarding the Feign Death Kinship Merit from BPG:<br /> It basically turns the Beast into a walking corpse for one 1WP, right?<br /> As the heart stops beating, not only are poison and diseases suspended (effectively making them immune to poison attacks and, let's say, Atavisms like Basilisk's Touch and Plague Bearer), they <i>should </i>be bleeding out a lot slower, right? I mean, the heart stopped beating, so there's nothing actively pushing the blood out. So the rate at which they acquire Agg damage when Full Lethal should be, I dunno, 2 turns instead of 1 turn?<br /> In addition, playing dead in the right circumstances is quite useful (an be that to lull the Hero in a false sense of victory to ambush them one more time) - IF the opposite party buys it. Which brings me to the question: Would they appear alive or dead to Mages with Life Sight or Death Sight, respectively?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T07:52:31-07:00","id":1195296,"title":"","content":"Are there any limitations on who can become the Apex of the area? Can ephemerals, extremely rad humans (with or without supernatural qualities) and/or non-kin such as demons become the Apex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T08:24:29-07:00","id":1195302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1195296#post1195296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any limitations on who can become the Apex of the area? Can ephemerals, extremely rad humans (with or without supernatural qualities) and/or non-kin such as demons become the Apex?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only requirement is &quot;inspires the most fear in the area,&quot; and the core book mentions that an independent ghoul is the Apex of Tokyo, so minor templates are fair game. But I'm not sure a 100% baseline mortal would inspire the <i>kind </i>of fear necessary to penetrate the Primordial Dream. Horrible things happen to people all the time, even things that cause Integrity loss, but it takes a supernatural twist to create a Chamber. I'd say the same limit applies to the Apex.<br /> <br /> The problem with a Demon being Apex isn't so much that they're not Kin, but that the Apex has to <i>personally </i>inspire a lot of fear. Since Demons operate undercover (and under Cover) and indirectly, it's pretty unlikely they'd be the focus of enough fear to gain Apex status. Again, the core book gives the example of a powerful elder vampire who mostly operates through minions and catspaws as a character unlikely to become Apex; Demons generally fit a similar description.<br /> <br /> But then again, these two points together could be a plot hook -- a seemingly powerless mortal (or weirder, a <i>group </i>of mortals) has gained Apex status, but when the brood investigates they realize it's actually a Demon.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T08:26:23-07:00","id":1195303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1195296#post1195296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any limitations on who can become the Apex of the area? Can ephemerals, extremely rad humans (with or without supernatural qualities) and/or non-kin such as demons become the Apex?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Chambers in a hive, though, all share some similarity, some small aspect granted by who- or whatever <b>supernatural</b> figure looms largest in the area\u2019s <b>Primordial Dream</b>. The Children call this being the Apex. </div> </div> </div> (Emphasis mine.)<br /> <br /> Demons have no connection to the Primordial Dream. So, they cannot be an Apex. Humans with a supernatural quality would have the potential since they are supernatural and connected to the PD, but unlikely since pretty much any other supernatural being is going to be more powerful. As for ephemera... Ghosts, maybe, since they were once human. Spirits could be the subject of fears, which make up the PD. So... Maybe? Angels depends on if Demons don't have a connection to the PD because they are of the God Machine or because they cut their connection to the God Machine. I'm not sure which it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:49:13-07:00","id":1195339,"title":"","content":"On page 283, the corebook explicitly states that a demon can be the Apex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:38:50-07:00","id":1195368,"title":"","content":"This is me, standing corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:39:44-07:00","id":1195545,"title":"","content":"As I interpret it, the demon has no connection, but if a demon somehow is the most feared by people (despite that public recognition is BAD for them), the people supply the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:46:38-07:00","id":1195547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1194835#post1194835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little torn on these questions because, on one hand, I want to stick with the general rules around how Goetia and other astral phenomena manifest in the physical world, but on the other hand, I'm a firm believer that there should never be any Lair traits that have no effect when imposed (and ideally, all of them should function at 'full power' when imposed).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't keep track of how Twilight stuff works. I envision the beast's Lair as a place where normally Twilight creatures are fully solid and that simply imposing said traits would put them into Twilight, but as far as I can tell there'd be no rule against them spamming Atavisms invisibly and invincibly. Demons and mages in astral twilight also seem to be able to spam powers at will.<br /> <br /> You could turn it around and let the beast's player define it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T18:08:03-07:00","id":1195555,"title":"","content":"Well an area also doesn't require an Apex, and an Apex need not be an individual either. So if one of the Demon's covers achieved the qualifications for Apex then the demon would be the Apex, just those tracking the Apex link through the hive would associate the Apex trait of little minion critters running around as the result of the number of informants and operatives Mr. Camera employs in the city. The same would apply to an Agency due to it being a collection of demons should said Agency gain the proper influence and insinuation with the local populace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:19:50-07:00","id":1196339,"title":"","content":"What kind of immunities do the Minions &amp; Thralls Lair traits provide?<br /> <br /> What about Hunting/Stalking grounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T20:34:00-07:00","id":1196345,"title":"","content":"I don't think they do provide an immunity to anything specific. Minion and thrall seem less like something you have protection for and more something that when the overlay happens a lot of other things start to happen at your bidding.<br /> <br /> Stalking/hunting grounds I might give a bonus to protecting or noticing you're in someone else's, but that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:13:45-07:00","id":1196357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1196345#post1196345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\Minion and thrall seem less like something you have protection for and more something that when the overlay happens a lot of other things start to happen at your bidding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean I get that, but until BPG ever available Lair trait also provided you with a meaningful immunity that you could employ in the material without manifesting your trait, though these immunities were naturally easier to utilize for more common (Minor) traits.<br /> <br /> The Core Book explains that &quot;Minor: Lair Traits are always possible in the physical world without the use of magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Following that line of thought through to its conclusion, there should be some sort of phenomena in the physical world that Minions, for example, should make you immune to, just like every other one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T22:09:30-07:00","id":1196368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1196357#post1196357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean I get that, but until BPG ever available Lair trait also provided you with a meaningful immunity that you could employ in the material without manifesting your trait, though these immunities were naturally easier to utilize for more common (Minor) traits.<br /> <br /> The Core Book explains that &quot;Minor: Lair Traits are always possible in the physical world without the use of magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Following that line of thought through to its conclusion, there should be some sort of phenomena in the physical world that Minions, for example, should make you immune to, just like every other one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but pg 101 phrases it as being immune to the environmental tilts which those traits lack a corresponding tilt. <br /> <br /> I don't think these are the same vein as the first set of lair traits, more things to help flesh out the nightmare monster aspect. For example Stalking and Hunting ground points out that it can only be applied to one chamber and the real world analogue of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T22:24:09-07:00","id":1196372,"title":"","content":"What if minions made you immune to bring harried be large crowds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T11:56:46-07:00","id":1196554,"title":"","content":"Minions aren't a tilt directly, but they can impose the Knocked Down, Stunned, or Immobilized tilts, so it stands to reason that a Beast with that Trait can't be knocked down or restrained by a Hero's followers or the like.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, maybe Heroes can't benefit from followers against a Beast with this Trait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T12:01:59-07:00","id":1196556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1196554#post1196554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minions aren't a tilt directly, but they can impose the Knocked Down, Stunned, or Immobilized tilts, so it stands to reason that a Beast with that Trait can't be knocked down or restrained by a Hero's followers or the like.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, maybe Heroes can't benefit from followers against a Beast with this Trait?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see manifested minions dealing with/incapacitating a Hero's mooks, but I don't see how it would work when not manifested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T15:05:16-07:00","id":1196619,"title":"","content":"I think making the Beast immune to Minion-imposed tilts is a little OP (it's a Minor Lair Trait, after all) but providing some extra resistance to rolls that would impose them would be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T18:02:16-07:00","id":1196666,"title":"","content":"What can you actually do after using Shadow Stalker to eat someone's shadow? Can you talk? Can you move while remaining attached? Can you use Nightmares without Fist of Nightmares?<br /> <br /> Minions, per the lair trait, can inflict tilts. What are the mechanics for doing this? Does it just happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T18:04:09-07:00","id":1196667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1196619#post1196619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think making the Beast immune to Minion-imposed tilts is a little OP (it's a Minor Lair Trait, after all) but providing some extra resistance to rolls that would impose them would be appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players Handbook stealth erratas lair immunity. If its an attack, you just get +2 to your resistance/contested roll.<br /> <br /> Minions helps you against Actors in the various astral realms, whiel Thralls help you against Goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T19:32:59-07:00","id":1196686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1196667#post1196667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Players Handbook stealth erratas lair immunity. If its an attack, you just get +2 to your resistance/contested roll.<br /> <br /> Minions helps you against Actors in the various astral realms, whiel Thralls help you against Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only if another supernatural is using some form of magic to replicate the effect.<br /> <br /> Let's say we have a Beast with the blinding lair trait. High beams, or a flashbang won't bypass a Beast's blinding lair trait. Another Beast dragging the world into their lair of blinding lights won't work on the first Beghotten either. A mage casting a spell to basically pull the concept of a blinding light into existance and conceal it in their hand to fling into the Beast's face when it get's too close then there's a roll off on the subject.<br /> <br /> Still a bit of a nerf for rebalance, but not as severe as removing a Beast's immunity just because someone is attacking them with the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T15:47:03-07:00","id":1196931,"title":"","content":"Do an Atavism's &quot;persistent&quot; effects need to be activated and does having them reveal the Horror to the supernaturally inclined?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T00:53:53-07:00","id":1197075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1196931#post1196931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do an Atavism's &quot;persistent&quot; effects need to be activated and does having them reveal the Horror to the supernaturally inclined?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and I'd say that they'd only be revealed when they come into effect - e.g. if an insectoid Namtaru with Unbreakable is hit by an attack they seem for a moment to have a rigid carapace covering them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T03:39:30-07:00","id":1197114,"title":"","content":"What kind of action sequence is using touch to activate a nightmare? Is that two separate instant actions or one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:02:03-07:00","id":1197195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1197114#post1197114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of action sequence is using touch to activate a nightmare? Is that two separate instant actions or one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would allow either the touch or the nightmare activation to be reflexively rolled into the other action in this case.<br /> <br /> RAW, I think it would be 2 instant actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/