":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T09:37:15-07:00","id":1198009,"title":"","content":"Hunger-wise, you can easily go for predator, tyrant or nemeses. The First ist obvious, as a tyrant it enforces the lesson of cooperation (alone, you are weak and helpless!) And as a nemeses it would punish straying from the group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:09:39-07:00","id":1198110,"title":"","content":"They probly have kinship with the storm wolves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:12:01-07:00","id":1198112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1198110#post1198110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probly have kinship with the storm wolves</div> </div> </div> </div>If they met some, I suspect that they'd get along, yes, provided that personalities didn't clash. Kinship works on a personal level, not just through mythic association. It would definitely be fitting, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:32:34-07:00","id":1198123,"title":"","content":"amarok Does seem to be a form/avatar of winter wolf like destorary wolf is fernis ur","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:27:13-07:00","id":1198227,"title":"","content":"Couple questions:<br /> \u200b Can a character start the game with multiple Kinships established?<br /> \u200bCan Nightmares affect creatures in Twilight if the Beast isn't herself in Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T22:50:32-07:00","id":1198253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1198227#post1198227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple questions:<br /> \u200b Can a character start the game with multiple Kinships established?<br /> \u200bCan Nightmares affect creatures in Twilight if the Beast isn't herself in Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say A) ask your Storyteller and B) yes, if the Beast can perceive and speak in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T01:50:54-07:00","id":1198270,"title":"","content":"How do the automatic successes from Cyclopean Strength interact with dice pool penalties in general, and with Defense in specific?<br /> <br /> Say I'm a Giant with Strength 4, Brawl 2, Lair 2 who spends a point of Satiety to beat up a vampire with Defense 5. Do I just roll (4+2)-6=1 die and add two automatic successes to the attack? Or do I subtract the Defense from the successes first, negating them altogether and ultimately rolling 3 dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T06:44:19-07:00","id":1198312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1198270#post1198270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the automatic successes from Cyclopean Strength interact with dice pool penalties in general, and with Defense in specific?<br /> <br /> Say I'm a Giant with Strength 4, Brawl 2, Lair 2 who spends a point of Satiety to beat up a vampire with Defense 5. Do I just roll (4+2)-6=1 die and add two automatic successes to the attack? Or do I subtract the Defense from the successes first, negating them altogether and ultimately rolling 3 dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to treat them like a weapon bonus that happens to also apply to Strength rolls besides attacks, because that is the existing precedent for how &quot;automatic successes&quot; are handled and the book makes no reference to any special way to approach them otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:27:11-07:00","id":1198624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1198312#post1198312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to treat them like a weapon bonus that happens to also apply to Strength rolls besides attacks, because that is the existing precedent for how &quot;automatic successes&quot; are handled and the book makes no reference to any special way to approach them otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting interpretation that I would have never come up with. One problem I immediately see with it is that it actually contradicts the text of the power, as the Satiety effect of CM says &quot;The Beast gains automatic successes equal to his Lair dots <b>on all Strength related rolls</b> for the remainder of the scene (...)&quot; whereas treating them as a weapon bonus would mean they only apply to <b>successful</b> attack rolls, rather than all rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:37:17-07:00","id":1198626,"title":"","content":"I think that ruling comes from where automatic successes were introduced in first edition. My group also goes with the interpretation that the roll needs to succeed before adding automatic successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:17:07-07:00","id":1198701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1198624#post1198624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting interpretation that I would have never come up with. One problem I immediately see with it is that it actually contradicts the text of the power, as the Satiety effect of CM says &quot;The Beast gains automatic successes equal to his Lair dots <b>on all Strength related rolls</b> for the remainder of the scene (...)&quot; whereas treating them as a weapon bonus would mean they only apply to <b>successful</b> attack rolls, rather than all rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Tessie says above. The phrasing of the mechanic is not optimal, but to be frank there's the simple fact that the way ChroD dice math is set up to work means there would be little reason not to have framed it as &quot;these rolls <i>automatically succeed</i>, with [Lair] successes in cases where this matters.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Anakim wheelhouse is already full of stuff that effectively reduces the number of successes you would need to accomplish a Strength-related task that doesn't require the standard one success to complete; like with Fate boons in Mage 2e <i>technically </i>being readable as allowing a character with the right near-basic rote to automatically succeed at any spellcasting roll, the broader context of the mechanic in question makes a particular reading come across as obviously unintended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-23-2018, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:04:36-07:00","id":1198726,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong, your interpretation is certainly way <i>saner</i> than anything my more rigorous approach to parsing rules can offer, I just wish it wasn't &quot;it's clearly not what's written, but it's the closest thing that makes sense&quot;. Well, that and not actually make the Satiety effect of CM poor man's version of Limb From Limb, but you can't have it all, can you?<br /> <br /> Thank you both for your answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T03:50:53-07:00","id":1198993,"title":"","content":"So I'm running a Beast/Werewolf 2nd ed crossover game. In one of the more beast focused sessions an NPC love intrest to one of the players murdered another NPC slumbering Makara collector causeing him to become unfettered and changeing his horror's hunger to punishment. Now it feeds upon the love intrest every few nights with growing intensity. I am planing on having the beast/werewolf pack enter the love intrest soulscape or dreamscape by way of the player beasts lair and doing battle with the unfettered in the bright dream. This particular unfettered is quite powerful at rank 4 and so I've got to ask but what happens when someone dies in the bright dream? I know the book mentions they wake up with the soul shocked condition but that dosen't make sense to me seeing as they've physically entered via the lair. Where exactly would they have a body to wake up? This is more in regards to what happens to the Werewolves, I would assume the Beast just wakes up in their lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24014-winterchangeling","name":"WinterChangeling","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T07:13:37-07:00","id":1199037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WinterChangeling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1198993#post1198993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm running a Beast/Werewolf 2nd ed crossover game. In one of the more beast focused sessions an NPC love intrest to one of the players murdered another NPC slumbering Makara collector causeing him to become unfettered and changeing his horror's hunger to punishment. Now it feeds upon the love intrest every few nights with growing intensity. I am planing on having the beast/werewolf pack enter the love intrest soulscape or dreamscape by way of the player beasts lair and doing battle with the unfettered in the bright dream. This particular unfettered is quite powerful at rank 4 and so I've got to ask but what happens when someone dies in the bright dream? I know the book mentions they wake up with the soul shocked condition but that dosen't make sense to me seeing as they've physically entered via the lair. Where exactly would they have a body to wake up? This is more in regards to what happens to the Werewolves, I would assume the Beast just wakes up in their lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Chamber is the only place in the Astral with physical presence and getting to the Bright Dream without a Pathway requires going through the Primordial Dream, which is the job for a Dream Form. The werewolves follow suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T18:14:52-07:00","id":1199270,"title":"","content":"How would you stat a Beast based on my husbundo Konrad Curze/night haunter from warhammer 40k?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T20:16:14-07:00","id":1199289,"title":"","content":"Conferring with my actual husband who knows a thing about Warhammer, it sounds like he'd be an Eshmaki Nemesis and absolutely has the Limb from Limb atavism. More than that is hard - are you looking for a starting character or an experienced one? Do you want to stick with the default for mortals in CofD, or try to model him like a Space Marine? In short, I don't think this is a &quot;simple question&quot; so you might want to try making a separate thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T22:01:27-07:00","id":1199299,"title":"","content":"Or ask about it on the existing &quot;Think of Exi