a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a joke about how it\u2019s ether snoozing or hungry do th might more aurutely describe cats</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, my apologies. I don't always recognize jokes for what they are. But yes, they do sound like cats when I put it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:03:37-07:00","id":1202099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1202065#post1202065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, my apologies. I don't always recognize jokes for what they are. But yes, they do sound like cats when I put it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my friends also sometimes have trouble understanding metaphors sarcasm ectc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:38:14-07:00","id":1203638,"title":"","content":"So...Skin Deep is really cool. I'm thinking of picking it up on my existing character, but a lot of the stuff it might do seems like it's done better by the Atavisms I already have.<br /> <br /> Having the wings sounds cool - but I have Wings of the Raptor. So do the claws, but I have Limb from Limb. Scaly hide, but I have Unbreakable...<br /> <br /> Would you allow Skin Deep to provide boosts/bonuses to other Atavisms? For example, letting the wings provide a +2 bonus on the roll to take flight with Wings of the Raptor, or the one to swoop upwards / dive bomb? Would you let the extra damage from physical claws stack with Limb from Limb, or have it give a bonus to the attack rolls? What about the armor and Unbreakable?<br /> <br /> I really want this Atavism because it's very thematic for this character, but I want it to be useful, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:37:34-07:00","id":1203733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1203638#post1203638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...Skin Deep is really cool. I'm thinking of picking it up on my existing character, but a lot of the stuff it might do seems like it's done better by the Atavisms I already have.<br /> <br /> Having the wings sounds cool - but I have Wings of the Raptor. So do the claws, but I have Limb from Limb. Scaly hide, but I have Unbreakable...<br /> <br /> Would you allow Skin Deep to provide boosts/bonuses to other Atavisms? For example, letting the wings provide a +2 bonus on the roll to take flight with Wings of the Raptor, or the one to swoop upwards / dive bomb? Would you let the extra damage from physical claws stack with Limb from Limb, or have it give a bonus to the attack rolls? What about the armor and Unbreakable?<br /> <br /> I really want this Atavism because it's very thematic for this character, but I want it to be useful, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a low level part of the thing with Skin Deep is that it visibly modifies the human form when in use. Like if my character uses Limb from Limb to slice open an enemy's chest all anyone without supernatural senses witnesses is that my character's freaking fingernails just tore a hole in this person. Skin Deep though, the person may not end up seeing what those talons are, but they are seeing my character suddenly growing fracking Nosferatu claws. So you know intimidation bonus there.<br /> <br /> Course the next advantage is that Skin Deep isn't set, so you can move between shaped for speed and scaly hide as needed. (If you can't manifest multiple ones.)<br /> <br /> Limb from Limb I'd probably allow as the two don't do the same thing, same with Scaly Hide. Fleshy Wings does have some overlap, but not enough that I wouldn't allow it unless it started to become a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T07:08:57-07:00","id":1204851,"title":"","content":"I know the default with merits is that you can only have up to 5 dots maximum; is that the intent behind Primordial Cult? Because I don't see it breaking if the separate benefits are the same as the old Haven/Sanctum merits (with the Size/Security ratings purchased with separate dots) with the abilities not prohibiting you from the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T13:38:09-07:00","id":1204962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1204851#post1204851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the default with merits is that you can only have up to 5 dots maximum; is that the intent behind Primordial Cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the third dot and beyond go toward the extra effects and Influential can explicitly be purchased up to five times, I can't think of any reading where that <i>isn't</i> the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T02:05:44-07:00","id":1207201,"title":"","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> I have some questions about the Caught in the Webs atavism (Player's Guide). When using it as a thrown weapon attack, we need a bit more information than what is given in the atavism itself. Is it aerodynamic? What about it's size? Also how does the Immobilized condition work in this situation? To resolve that, normally one can attempt to tear through it (for this we need a Durability, which we don't have) Or does the atavism ignore this, and keeps the target Immobilized for the scene? (since the dexterity technically stays 0, no way to resolve that, which is strange)<br /> <br /> Would appreciate some help understanding the mechanics behind this one.<br /> <br /> And as a bonus question, would you allow this to work with Lightning-Strike? It technically requires you to deal damage (so by RAW it doesn't work), but using the touch attack with L-S sounds pretty fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T09:52:41-07:00","id":1207307,"title":"","content":"Hello, I've got questions about a few things:<br /> \u200b-Does Smashing Current allow to use Defense against surprise attacks?<br /> \u200b-Does Enemy Within allow to mimic the mien of a Changeling?<br /> \u200b-For the purpose of Illusion of Safety's Satiety Expenditure option, do doors and other mundane openings count as portals or is it only referring to magical portals?<br /> \u200b-Can a Horrorspawn hold a conversation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T14:02:13-07:00","id":1207406,"title":"","content":"Can a claimed have the devouring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T14:03:30-07:00","id":1207408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I've got questions about a few things:<br /> \u200b-Does Smashing Current allow to use Defense against surprise attacks?<br /> \u200b-Does Enemy Within allow to mimic the mien of a Changeling?<br /> \u200b-For the purpose of Illusion of Safety's Satiety Expenditure option, do doors and other mundane openings count as portals or is it only referring to magical portals?<br /> \u200b-Can a Horrorspawn hold a conversation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is what ever is best for your game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T01:47:12-07:00","id":1207582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207201#post1207201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some questions about the Caught in the Webs atavism (Player's Guide). When using it as a thrown weapon attack, we need a bit more information than what is given in the atavism itself. Is it aerodynamic? What about it's size?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea how that matters. It\u2019s a supernatural attack that follows the rules as presented. It has whatever appearance is appropriate to the Beast\u2019s Horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207201#post1207201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how does the Immobilized condition work in this situation? To resolve that, normally one can attempt to tear through it (for this we need a Durability, which we don't have) Or does the atavism ignore this, and keeps the target Immobilized for the scene? (since the dexterity technically stays 0, no way to resolve that, which is strange)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike mundane versions of the Immobilised Tilt, you can\u2019t simply break out by breaking the substance. It disappears at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207201#post1207201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a bonus question, would you allow this to work with Lightning-Strike? It technically requires you to deal damage (so by RAW it doesn't work), but using the touch attack with L-S sounds pretty fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t, but whatever works for your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I've got questions about a few things:<br /> \u200b-Does Smashing Current allow to use Defense against surprise attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, if you\u2019re aware of an attacker, your Horror tries to help. But surprise can still surprise you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b-Does Enemy Within allow to mimic the mien of a Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally not, but if it works for your game, I\u2019d allow it with Satiety expenditure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b-For the purpose of Illusion of Safety's Satiety Expenditure option, do doors and other mundane openings count as portals or is it only referring to magical portals?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2018Portal\u2019 was just a shorthand way of saving wordcount from saying \u2018doors, windows, trapdoors, hatches, portholes...\u2019 etc. Mundane is what\u2019s intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b-Can a Horrorspawn hold a conversation?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make an appropriate Horrorspawn, I don\u2019t see why not. It\u2019s likely to be a strange conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:27:11-07:00","id":1207600,"title":"","content":"First of all, thanks for the input!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207582#post1207582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how that matters. It\u2019s a supernatural attack that follows the rules as presented. It has whatever appearance is appropriate to the Beast\u2019s Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the rule:<br /> &quot;Applying the snares requires a thrown weapon or touch attack (Beast: The Primordial, pp. 164-165), but activating the Atavism itself is reflexive&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe I misinterpreted it, and you actually have to throw something &quot;real&quot; at them? (The thrown weapon attack needs the aerodynamic trait and the size of the thrown object for it's own rules)<br /> What confuses me is that the touch attack does no damage, so why would they want the thrown to work differently?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b-Does Smashing Current allow to use Defense against surprise attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't the Horror who does the protecting with the atavism (but these &quot;phantom forces&quot;, flavor it as you will, I'm planning on a spider-web-esque variant), and most importantly, it is persistent. Also, it is specifically mentioned that the defense is applied to &quot;all&quot; attacks, so I think it works for surprises as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207307#post1207307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b-Does Enemy Within allow to mimic the mien of a Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can see it at all. (so you shouldn't be able to)<br /> And in case you do, see Bunyip's response. It IS a supernatural thing, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:38:00-07:00","id":1207603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207600#post1207600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, thanks for the input!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207600#post1207600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the rule:<br /> &amp;quot;Applying the snares requires a thrown weapon or touch attack (Beast: The Primordial, pp. 164-165), but activating the Atavism itself is reflexive&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe I misinterpreted it, and you actually have to throw something &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; at them? (The thrown weapon attack needs the aerodynamic trait and the size of the thrown object for it's own rules)<br /> What confuses me is that the touch attack does no damage, so why would they want the thrown to work differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now I understand where this comes from. Right, this answer has two parts - the mechanical, behind-the-scenes answer, and the cinematic, in-front-of-the-camera answer.<br /> <br /> Mechanics - you\u2019re not actually \u2018throwing\u2019 anything through the air so aerodynamics etc. don\u2019t matter. You need to make a thrown or touch attack because you don\u2019t automatically hit your target. If you\u2019re standing right next to him, or in melee, you can try to reach out and touch him and he can defend to get out of the way. If you successfully touch him, he suffers the effect. Same with the thrown attack. If you\u2019re at range, you \u2018line up\u2019 the supernatural effect and try and tag him with it. He can defend and try to get out of the way. If you succeed, he suffers the effect. Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> Cinematic answer - what it looks like depends on your Horror. You might literally fling sticky webbing at him, binding his limbs. The ground might reach up and grab him with stony hands, holding him in place. Or it might turn to mud and suck at his feet as he sinks further into it. But no matter how it appears, you don\u2019t have to worry about the weight, balance, or other traits of the \u2018weapon\u2019. The act of succeeding in the attack roll essentially tags the victim with sufficient resonance between the physical world and Primordial Dream to let the manifestation of the atavism through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:47:59-07:00","id":1207605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207603#post1207603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re at range, you \u2018line up\u2019 the supernatural effect and try and tag him with it. He can defend and try to get out of the way. If you succeed, he suffers the effect. Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it has a defined range? I don't have the Guide so I don't know (but I'm guessing it doesn't since IceBen wouldn't have a reason to ask otherwise) but unless it has a defined range the range would be calculated using the object's Size and whether it's aerodynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-16-2018, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T04:56:33-07:00","id":1207607,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is the basis of my problem.<br /> <br /> I have two solutions in my mind, one is where you throw an object, and on a successful hit you reflectively activate the atavism, or the other, since there is no range listed, you have to do it point blank. (But instead of touch, you &quot;throw&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:02:12-07:00","id":1207609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207605#post1207605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it has a defined range? I don't have the Guide so I don't know (but I'm guessing it doesn't since IceBen wouldn't have a reason to ask otherwise) but unless it has a defined range the range would be calculated using the object's Size and whether it's aerodynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Sorry, it seems to have fallen off the final, published version. 2 x Lair dots yards, same as the Satiety expenditure version, except you don\u2019t get to simultaneously attack everyone in range.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: So yes, beginning Beasts with low Lair ratings will generally be in touch range, but the range grows pretty rapidly, and soon you\u2019ll be able to \u2018hit\u2019 and slow down victims further away, to help you catch up to them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-16-2018, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T06:24:26-07:00","id":1207633,"title":"","content":"I see, thank you!<br /> <br /> Just to clear up everything that could come in play; does it increase per the normal throwing rules (*2 range for -1 die), or is it more like a special attack roll?<br /> <br /> (also, I just see that you are one of the writers, thanks for that on a separate level <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) &gt; Does that mean that the intended mechanism of the Smashing Currents is that surprise negates it? (since you explained it that way)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:28:06-07:00","id":1207727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1207582#post1207582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea how that matters. It\u2019s a supernatural attack that follows the rules as presented. It has whatever appearance is appropriate to the Beast\u2019s Horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Unlike mundane versions of the Immobilised Tilt, you can\u2019t simply break out by breaking the substance. It disappears at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t, but whatever works for your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, if you\u2019re aware of an attacker, your Horror tries to help. But surprise can still surprise you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Generally not, but if it works for your game, I\u2019d allow it with Satiety expenditure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Portal\u2019 was just a shorthand way of saving wordcount from saying \u2018doors, windows, trapdoors, hatches, portholes...\u2019 etc. Mundane is what\u2019s intended.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you make an appropriate Horrorspawn, I don\u2019t see why not. It\u2019s likely to be a strange conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThank you for answering!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T00:17:27-07:00","id":1208351,"title":"","content":"Did anyone ever figure out the mechanics behind the Minions Minor Lair Trait? It's supposed to inflict Tilts, but there's not really any mechanics behind how they do that last I checked (which was shortly after the book got. . pre-released?). Any help would be appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:38:04-07:00","id":1208357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1208351#post1208351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone ever figure out the mechanics behind the Minions Minor Lair Trait? It's supposed to inflict Tilts, but there's not really any mechanics behind how they do that last I checked (which was shortly after the book got. . pre-released?). Any help would be appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know of any official mechanics for it. I personally roll half the Horror's Power or Finesse to inflict Tilts with them, depending on how it's being done (rats just barrelling over someone is Power, goblins tripping them finesse) but that's only me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:43:46-07:00","id":1208360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1208357#post1208357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know of any official mechanics for it. I personally roll half the Horror's Power or Finesse to inflict Tilts with them, depending on how it's being done (rats just barrelling over someone is Power, goblins tripping them finesse) but that's only me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I had some vague ideas on how to do it, but I figured I would ask around. Thankfully I won't be playing this character until probably the Summer, so plenty of time to either get an official word about it or iron out some homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T21:11:12-07:00","id":1210267,"title":"","content":"Not a simple question but. What would happen if a Mage tries to replicate a lair? Or claim chambers in the primordial dream with Mind?<br /> Note I'm not saying they can have lair with a spell I'm just curious as to what would happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T02:38:00-07:00","id":1210340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1210267#post1210267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a simple question but. What would happen if a Mage tries to replicate a lair? Or claim chambers in the primordial dream with Mind?<br /> Note I'm not saying they can have lair with a spell I'm just curious as to what would happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure the closest you could get would be making a demiplane maybe. Claiming would likely be temporary, but allow the mage some amount of base control over the chamber- if it was even possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:00:12-07:00","id":1210522,"title":"","content":"Hi, I have another question!<br /> \u200bDoes Enemy Within allow to change the clothes the beast wears to match the new form they take?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:15:22-07:00","id":1210534,"title":"","content":"I'd say no, because nothing in the write-up indicates to me that anything other than the physical appearance of the victim is mimiced - without expending Satiety, you cannot even mimic their capabilities. I don't consider someone's clothes to be part of them, but then, that's maybe just me. Also, it would remove some things I like about the ability (being chased --&gt; shapeshift when walking around a corner --&gt; chill --&gt; be grabbed by those who give chase due to the same clothes, only for them to realize 'oops, wrong dude', you know this scene from the movies --&gt; walk away like a boss) so obviously I am biased.<br /> (Also, consider this - people that KNOW there's a shapeshifter will keep an eye out for the clothes more than the person, which raises the stakes and creates drama - it's important to have a spare set of outfits on you =P)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:22:25-07:00","id":1210537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1210522#post1210522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I have another question!<br /> \u200bDoes Enemy Within allow to change the clothes the beast wears to match the new form they take?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do as Wormwood says, at least by default. I look at it like I would look at an Atavism for the Thing (the John Carpenter's one, not poor Ben Grimm), where having to change clothes/discard previous one is part of the nuisances a shapeshifter has to deal with. But it's also one of those elements I consider to be easily open to customization by Storytellers and players, depending on the Horror.<br /> <br /> And now I want to do something with a Thing-like Inguma","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:50:48-07:00","id":1210550,"title":"","content":"Adding onto the other side of that question, the book only talks about shapes and appearances, so nothing permits it either. In my opinion it depends on how you want it to work. Do you want the horror to &quot;push out&quot; your physical form? Change it like a clay? Or do you want it to coat with your new outlook? Either works, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T15:15:51-07:00","id":1210625,"title":"","content":"CofD is generally pretty lenient with clothing when it comes to shapeshifting. Vampires with Protean always subsume the clothes, and werewolves only rip clothes as a penalty for bad Harmony. For most werewolves the clothes can actually change to fit them when shifting to their near-human form. Skinthieves, on the other hand, requires an additional Merit in order to keep their clothes when transforming. But that's also a minor template that puts much more focus on the details around shapeshifting than even werewolves.<br /> <br /> When a power doesn't specify you should look to two things: What is the purpose of the power, and how does the power work? The purpose is to look like someone, and clothes can definitely be considered part of that. The power is an Atavism, so it works by channelling the nightmarish symbols of the Primordial Dream into the Beast. That means shifting the clothes isn't really an issue, unlike The Thing which shapeshifts through a biological process. Therefor I'd definitely allow the clothes to change too. It fits the purpose of the Atavism, and it definitely fits the theme of Inguma who has it as an In-Family Atavism. Just look to their Birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T15:28:50-07:00","id":1210634,"title":"","content":"I admit a lot of that is because of my worship for John Carpenter, so that colors my interpretation. But overall I'd rule it as a &quot;I picture it in my mind as what The Thing does, but we can change it depending on the character without thinking about it twice&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T17:07:02-07:00","id":1210685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1210625#post1210625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires with Protean always subsume the clothes</div> </div> </div> </div>Brief aside: Where does it say this? I can't find any reference to it in VtR2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T20:28:11-07:00","id":1210779,"title":"","content":"Skin Deep and similar bonuses to strength, dexterity, stamina -- should a horror or horrorspawn be able to benefit from these to boost power, finesse, and resistance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T01:08:07-07:00","id":1210861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1210779#post1210779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skin Deep and similar bonuses to strength, dexterity, stamina -- should a horror or horrorspawn be able to benefit from these to boost power, finesse, and resistance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as written, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:32:51-07:00","id":1211158,"title":"","content":"I have Dexterity 4, Manipulation 1, Wits 2. I am a master thief with very little intersocial capacity or something, I put all my social dots in Composure.<br /> <br /> I enter my Lair and begin to compose a revolutionary speech, relying on incisive wordplay and clever jokes. Because my Finesse is 6, I'm really good at this, even though I'm actually terrible at this. My Horror is a giant squid. It doesn't do a lot of revolutionary speeches.<br /> <br /> Is this valid? Does the game talk about this kind of thing anywhere? Inside a Lair, you're smart and charming as long as you're strong, which you could use for research or architectural engineering or whatever else. What if I don't even want to bother with the speech myself, does my Horror have my Skills normally? Can I tell it to do the copywriting while I hit the pool? How about my Merits? Do I have access to those things while merged, can I make use of kung-fu as a monster that isn't humanoid?<br /> <br /> I keep going over page 99 but I can't figure out what the interpretation is supposed to be, what a Horror is capable of without me and what I'm capable of while merged with it. It all seems like blank space that has to just be houseruled into something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 04-24-2018, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:56:31-07:00","id":1211168,"title":"","content":"...possibly a dumb question but:<br /> <br /> So if through happenstance a Beast gets kidnapped by the Gentry and they attempt to turn them into a changeling...nothing happens, due to their soul being so irreversibly altered that they can't be fae'd, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:05:55-07:00","id":1211199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1211168#post1211168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...possibly a dumb question but:<br /> <br /> So if through happenstance a Beast gets kidnapped by the Gentry and they attempt to turn them into a changeling...nothing happens, due to their soul being so irreversibly altered that they can't be fae'd, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Though it's probably also true that a Beast wouldn't be taken by the Gentry for conversion, due to ancient contracts with either the Primordial Dream or the Dark Mother. They could be kidnapped to torture or kill, if the Beast pissed off the Fae bad enough, but will usually just be left alone, as they belong to a different dream.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:22:45-07:00","id":1211207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1211199#post1211199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. Though it's probably also true that a Beast wouldn't be taken by the Gentry for conversion, due to ancient contracts with either the Primordial Dream or the Dark Mother. They could be kidnapped to torture or kill, if the Beast pissed off the Fae bad enough, but will usually just be left alone, as they belong to a different dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could wonder as to how the Hedge interacts with Beasts as being something that might make Gentry hesitant to act against a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:36:31-07:00","id":1211238,"title":"","content":"The thing about Hedge interactions -- in Changeling 1e, the Hedge reacted to the presence of a Changeling based on their Wyrd, and only at very high Wyrd could a changeling actively manipulate the Hedge. 2e has thrown that out in favor of the Hedgespinning subsystem, where any Changeling can attempt to actively manipulate the Hedge, but there's no hard-and-fast passive effects from just being there. (At least, I couldn't find any mention of the Hedge reactivty subsystem in the Kickstarter previews for CtL2, and I looked pretty carefully.)<br /> <br /> But the Beast corebook stilll points to the 1e subsystem, using Lair instead of Wyrd. The intended effect of which, I guess, was that Beasts and Changelings would be indistinguishable from each other in their effect on the Hedge...but, unless this is errata'd, they now look pretty distinct from one another. (Which, for the record, I like better for fluff reasons--Beasts are the dreams, changelings are the dreamers).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T18:26:12-07:00","id":1211252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1211158#post1211158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this valid? Does the game talk about this kind of thing anywhere? Inside a Lair, you're smart and charming as long as you're strong, which you could use for research or architectural engineering or whatever else. What if I don't even want to bother with the speech myself, does my Horror have my Skills normally? Can I tell it to do the copywriting while I hit the pool? How about my Merits? Do I have access to those things while merged, can I make use of kung-fu as a monster that isn't humanoid?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit in Book of Spirits that points out the common-sense meaning of this, but the short version is: No, the PFR Attribute Spread does not translate to all of the things in its subset being equally effective at the tasks they correspond to \u2014 a Horror with Power 5 is not in practice the equivalent of a mortal with Strength 5, Presence 5, and Intelligence 5. The concept of the entity in question takes precedence over any computer-dumb literalistic reading of the mechanics when it comes to framing what it can and can't do within the story.<br /> <br /> A Beast with the Strength of an Olympic medalist is more effective at imposing their raw will in the Primordial Dream when merged with their Horror, but they don't <i>actually get</i> the equivalent of Intelligence 5 just because they're rolling for Intelligence-based rolls as though that part of their dicepool was 5.<br /> <br /> High Attributes are only going to compensate so much for low Skills and lack of usable tools, is the other thing \u2014 the effect is more comparable to you just spending Willpower on a bunch of rolls to do the thing you're not good at than it is to suddenly becoming a virtuoso in the dreamscape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T03:33:53-07:00","id":1212194,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm back with new questions!<br /> Is the weapon damage causes by the Dig Deep merit of the Relentless Assault style Lethal or Bashing?<br /> Does Ravenous Maw allow a Beast to gain sustenance from eating normally inedible stuff?<br /> Is imposing a Lair Trait an Instant or Reflexive action?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:12:03-07:00","id":1212205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1212194#post1212194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the weapon damage causes by the Dig Deep merit of the Relentless Assault style Lethal or Bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every weapon is considered lethal so I think it adds lethal by default. (otherwise it could have said 1 automatic success)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1212194#post1212194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Ravenous Maw allow a Beast to gain sustenance from eating normally inedible stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the point? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1212194#post1212194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is imposing a Lair Trait an Instant or Reflexive action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will check this, but if I remember correctly, then an instant action. &lt;edit: yeah, I can't find it xD&gt;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","user":"IceBen","date":". 04-27-2018, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T06:47:53-07:00","id":1212255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1212194#post1212194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the weapon damage causes by the Dig Deep merit of the Relentless Assault style Lethal or Bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same type of damage as you would do normally.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1212205#post1212205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">otherwise it could have said 1 automatic success</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing weapon damage by one <i>is</i> adding one automatic success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:51:53-07:00","id":1212473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1212255#post1212255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Increasing weapon damage by one <i>is</i> adding one automatic success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing the existing weapon damage by one is indeed adding one success. Here, however, the wording is <b>adding</b> one weapon damage. That's why I think you sacrifice a die for a point of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> edit: Also, it fits thematically with &quot;Dig Deep&quot; and it's flavor text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","user":"IceBen","date":". 04-27-2018, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:57:30-07:00","id":1212477,"title":"","content":"Adding one weapon damage is also the same thing as increasing weapon damage by one. And even if it weren't, why would you default to lethal damage instead of the type of damage the attack already inflicts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:47:24-07:00","id":1212565,"title":"","content":"That's what confuse me a bit: damage from any weapon is always lethal, but is Weapon damage the same as damage from a weapon? Does using Dit Deep make someone's body the equivalent of a weapon the way the Martial Art merit does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:08:46-07:00","id":1213268,"title":"","content":"&quot;Weapon modifier&quot; is a slightly misleading term. Normal unarmed attacks have a &quot;weapon&quot; modifier of +0 bashing. Dig Deep changes it to +1 bashing. If you have enough martial arts to deal lethal, it adds one lethal to the total (1 at four dots of MA, 3 at five).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:16:50-07:00","id":1213270,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: The human bite has a modifier of -1B, meaning it can potentially deal zero damage even if successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T08:34:26-07:00","id":1213441,"title":"","content":"Because in GMC weapon equals to lethal damage, thats my reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If anything you will convince me that the whole attack should do lethal damage, but I'm certain that it is written to only affect one point.<br /> Also, bite is a special action during grapple, not a weapon (for humans). And I don't really remember it having a die penality either, but I'll check that again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:02:37-07:00","id":1213449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1213441#post1213441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because in GMC weapon equals to lethal damage, thats my reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If anything you will convince me that the whole attack should do lethal damage, but I'm certain that it is written to only affect one point.<br /> Also, bite is a special action during grapple, not a weapon (for humans). And I don't really remember it having a die penality either, but I'll check that again.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Bite<br /> A human\u2019s teeth have a -1 weapon modifier and deal<br /> bashing damage. Animals and some other creatures treat<br /> their teeth like weapons, dealing lethal damage to mortals.<br /> Animal bites have a weapon modifier depending on the kind<br /> of animal: a wolf applies +1, while a great white shark gets +4.<br /> Humans can only bite as part of a grapple, using the<br /> Damage move (see below).&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 89 of Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It clearly states that biting does have a weapon modifier, and despite including &quot;weapon&quot; in &quot;weapon modifier&quot; it does not actually include a weapon and it only deals bashing. Similarly Claws of the Unholy has a weapon modifier of +0 aggravated damage. Weapon modifier is the gameplay term used for all attacks regardless of what type of damage that attack deals. Despite its name it does not imply that a weapon is used for the attack.<br /> Also, since weapon modifier modifies the amount of successes, not the dice pool, a weapon modifier of -1 wouldn't be a one die penalty. It would simply deal successes -1 damage. For example, if someone wins a grapple with 3 successes and chooses to bite, the bite would deal 2 bashing. If they would instead only win by 1 success the bite attack would deal 0 damage despite actually hitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-30-2018, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:16:28-07:00","id":1213454,"title":"","content":"I read only beast, and there is no -1B weapon rating, if you wish I can copy the appropriate parts (when I get to my computer), or you can check: Bite BtP 165, Weapons and Armor BtP 167. Bite works mechanically as you wrote, but the wording is different. BtP was written with GMC rules, not basic CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T10:01:08-07:00","id":1213473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1213454#post1213454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BtP was written with GMC rules, not basic CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>BtP did copy some GMC rules which is unfortunate because GMC uses the term &quot;damage rating&quot; which comes from the Storytelling System (aka first edition) because GMC was supposed to modify the rules of first edition. BtP as a whole is instead supposed to use the revised Storytelling System (aka second edition) where the term instead is &quot;weapon modifier/damage&quot; (which is why we have a new Merit that increases &quot;weapon damage&quot; despite that not being properly defined by the copy-pasted rules). That means CofD is basically errata because it has printed the actual rules for the system BtP is supposed to use.<br /> <br /> You can willingly ignore CofD (especially if you don't own the book, and you shouldn't have to buy it since BtP is supposed to function on its own) that properly defines what &quot;weapon modifier&quot; means and come up with a creative solution of your own, but my original answer still stands because that's without a doubt how the rules are supposed to be interpreted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-30-2018, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:03:16-07:00","id":1213556,"title":"","content":"Can there be a unicorn horror <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/megamitensei/images/5/53/UnicornSMT.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20080801225707\" target=\"_blank\">https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/...20080801225707</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":".  Add pics 04-30-2018, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:05:53-07:00","id":1213559,"title":"","content":"yes<br /> <br /> like so<br /> <img src=\"https://images.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=http%3A%2F%2F3.bp.blogspot.com%2F-jAXfPLWnSP4%2FUWmuVeLtGuI%2FAAAAAAAADck%2F7eK4zf5r4k0%2Fs1600%2Fscary%2Bunicorn.jpg&amp;f=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:06:37-07:00","id":1213560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1213556#post1213556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can there be a unicorn horror <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/megamitensei/images/5/53/UnicornSMT.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20080801225707\" target=\"_blank\">https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/...20080801225707</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but expect less \u201cpeaceful and holy animal who heals ills\u201d of modern depictions and more \u201cprideful and kingly beast who gores the unworthy\u201d of older depictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:13:45-07:00","id":1213564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1213560#post1213560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but expect less \u201cpeaceful and holy animal who heals ills\u201d of modern depictions and more \u201cprideful and kingly beast who gores the unworthy\u201d of older depictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact, the whole &quot;only virgin maidens can tame unicorns&quot; thing probably started as a joke, along the lines of &quot;it would take an impossible being to do this impossible task&quot;. Classic unicorn are truly wild beasts<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok, so it was really more like &quot;takes one mythical being to catch another&quot;, but that's in our world, not the CoD, where Hobgoblin Narwhal-Horses probably were a real thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.c