9#post1213619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but if we\u2019re talking about Horrors specifically, I really doubt one would look like a \u201cmodern\u201d unicorn. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, a story hook; A unicorn-Beast still isn\u2019t proud of his Horror despite it not looking like the fluffy modern unicorns, so he decides to shape the Bright Dream. All of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s the bright dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:57:42-07:00","id":1213658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1213655#post1213655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What\u2019s the bright dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>The collective soul of humanity. Mages know it as the Temenos. See also the real-life concept of the Collective Unconscious in Jungian psychology. If you\u2019re familiar with the Persona series, then the Sea of Souls too. <br /> <br /> Astral Realms, a Mage 1E book, contains the myriad of realms and creatures found within. Mage 2E core has 2E mechanics for mages to travel to it. Beast Player\u2019s Guide gives us mechanics for Beasts to travel to it... and to shape it, which can be done by anyone who gets there. Shaping the Temenos/ Bright Dream basically changes the noosphere, and thus can change local humans\u2019 beliefs and perceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:46:21-07:00","id":1214737,"title":"","content":"If you cut your lair form the Hive because of an harmfull Apex trait or for any other number of reason, can you link your lair back to thze Hive at some point ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T01:56:21-07:00","id":1214969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1214737#post1214737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cut your lair form the Hive because of an harmfull Apex trait or for any other number of reason, can you link your lair back to thze Hive at some point ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as far as I understand it, cutting your lair off requires you to destroy all chambers in said hive, but you can build new ones there the normal way. (also, the Apex trait only affects the chambers in the hive, or in case the Apex is a beast, the heart as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:29:40-07:00","id":1215037,"title":"","content":"It doesn't say anytbing about destroying your chambers at all and the huve trait never affect the hearth from what i've been reading, even if the apex is a Beast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:50:17-07:00","id":1215054,"title":"","content":"Player's Guide talks about the apex trait affecting the heart when it originates from a beast, and how to handle overlapping traits (reflexive action to select one).<br /> And the destroying isn't described, but how else do you severe your lair from a hive? It is not like you can just will the chamber not to be part of a hive (it is literally a part of it), you have to get rid of it to wall off your lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:17:24-07:00","id":1215068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215054#post1215054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player's Guide talks about the apex trait affecting the heart when it originates from a beast, and how to handle overlapping traits (reflexive action to select one).<br /> And the destroying isn't described, but how else do you severe your lair from a hive? It is not like you can just will the chamber not to be part of a hive (it is literally a part of it), you have to get rid of it to wall off your lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that there are mechanical effects for walling off your Lair that make no sense to include if that process is simply removing every Chamber connected to the hive from your Lair? No. You make the narrative efforts to negate the Apex's thematic tie to the parts of your Lair that it holds dominion over and constrict your feeding range accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:24:40-07:00","id":1215069,"title":"","content":"Is the mechanical effect only the feeding range, or is there something else? The range is easily explained by you not having a way to easily navigate the hive. (So your horror can't just roam in there without having the benefit of the existing primordial pathways) It has to be addressed either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:39:57-07:00","id":1215074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215069#post1215069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the mechanical effect only the feeding range, or is there something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having a Chamber in the local hive doesn't alter your feeding range, but keeping the Apex from being able to enter your Lair at will does, and the Apex's ability to enter your Lair at will is contingent upon your Lair containing a Chamber from their hive. The Heart only becomes accessible to the Apex through your gaining Chambers within their hive, so the hive shouldn't become harder to navigate just because you're in the same position as a newcomer in town; the hive contains &quot;spacial&quot; shortcuts across the Primordial Dream that the Horror has no difficulty navigating the dreamscape without to feed normally, which is why the hive can allow the Horror to range further in the first place, but the dreamscape only touches the hive through its Chambers, not the entire region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:53:01-07:00","id":1215083,"title":"","content":"Ok, sadly that just confused me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> -So chamber in the hive = apex access to you,<br /> -Severing = half feed range + stripping the trait<br /> is what you are saying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:09:55-07:00","id":1215090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215083#post1215083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, sadly that just confused me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> -So chamber in the hive = apex access to you,<br /> -Severing = half feed range + stripping the trait<br /> is what you are saying?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Player's Guide made it clear that there's more to the Primordial Dream than its Chambers, and the parts of it that are not Chambers adhere to material geography in a way that attaches logically to &quot;your Horror roams within a set radius from your physical location.&quot; Walling off your Lair means your Horror is essentially <i>avoiding the rest of the hive</i>, hence the narrower range of feeding area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:26:10-07:00","id":1215099,"title":"","content":"I see. How does the apex work thematically then? I assumed they affect the chambers in their territory within their hive, but they aren't. So instead they affect the people, and the Horror picks up these while feeding? Brings them itself to the Lair, so has to avoid potential sources? That would have other constraints as well, so probably not. Right now it isn't too clear to me how it actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:37:52-07:00","id":1215111,"title":"","content":"I've always treated it as &quot;As long as you close off burrows to the Hive&quot; you are not a part of the Hive. Otherwise, if you have chambers in say, Chicago, New York, and Los Angeles, you have three separate hives to contend with.<br /> <br /> If you do leave up a burrow to the Hive, the Hive trait only affects chambers directly connected to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:56:28-07:00","id":1215119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215111#post1215111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always treated it as &amp;quot;As long as you close off burrows to the Hive&amp;quot; you are not a part of the Hive. Otherwise, if you have chambers in say, Chicago, New York, and Los Angeles, you have three separate hives to contend with.<br /> <br /> If you do leave up a burrow to the Hive, the Hive trait only affects chambers directly connected to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hive doesn't have burrows. It has primordial pathways; shortcuts, as Satchel mentioned above.<br /> The problem is that your claimed chamber is governed by you, but it is in the Hive, right under the Apex' image. Why can't it affect the chamber just because you don't go that far away to feed? I mean you can do that on the other side of the world, and it still counts. Why, what is happening in the background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:36:10-07:00","id":1215141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215099#post1215099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. How does the apex work thematically then? I assumed they affect the chambers in their territory within their hive, but they aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are. &quot;The hive&quot; is &quot;all the Chambers in a region,&quot; but the wider geographical territory a hive's Chambers occupy is not itself subject to the rules of Chambers \u2014 the dreamscape is simply the fragile reflection of the material world in which the Begotten's homes exist, which itself neighbors the Temenos and the Anima Mundi by approaching places with more or less association with the presence of people; the overlap between population centers as a Horizon in the Dream and the common basis of hives in the material world suggests a certain amount of difficulty navigating to human dreams while avoiding the territory of an ever-present avatar of subconscious fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215119#post1215119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hive doesn't have burrows. It has primordial pathways; shortcuts, as Satchel mentioned above.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hive is all the Chambers in a region and the Burrows connecting them to Lairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:57:44-07:00","id":1215151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215141#post1215141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...navigating to human dreams while avoiding the territory of an ever-present avatar of subconscious fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>This still doesn't help me much. What does it have to do with chambers?<br /> The only plausible thing I can think of is the Horror cleaning the Chamber constantly, so it doesn't have time to wander off that much -.- Other things don't really make even this much sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215141#post1215141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The hive is all the Chambers in a region and the Burrows connecting them to Lairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant specifically the unconnected chambers. The hive includes chambers, and no burrows, then the beasts claim chambers, and create their burrows. Otherwise the Horror just opens pathways between all these chambers to hunt.<br /> <br /> \u200bOr... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a>, do you mean keeping the chamber but rewiring the Lair so you won't have any burrows leading to it? Like an island? That, I can see working. &lt;the chamber would still have the apex trait, but not the heart, and it wouldn't connect with other hives&gt; You would need pathways to navigate there, sure, but manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:25:35-07:00","id":1215168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215151#post1215151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This still doesn't help me much. What does it have to do with chambers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chambers occupy the physical location they were made from in the larger dreamscape and thus serve as the entry points from the dreamscape into the hive itself. Places where a lot of people are around are both more likely to have Chambers in them (and thus within the reach of the Apex) and more able to serve as entrances to the part of the Astral where individual human souls can be reached. The Horror having to navigate around the former to find prey while hungry and agitated is going to be less choosy and range less far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:31:04-07:00","id":1215172,"title":"","content":"He doesn't have any chance there, this chamber you are describing is <b>in his lair. </b>No matter where the Horror goes, the chamber stays in the lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:32:47-07:00","id":1215174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215119#post1215119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hive doesn't have burrows. It has primordial pathways; shortcuts, as Satchel mentioned above.<br /> The problem is that your claimed chamber is governed by you, but it is in the Hive, right under the Apex' image. Why can't it affect the chamber just because you don't go that far away to feed? I mean you can do that on the other side of the world, and it still counts. Why, what is happening in the background?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. I run it as requiring a burrow out into the Hive instead. This provides a cleaner mechanic for my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:37:50-07:00","id":1215175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215174#post1215174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. I run it as requiring a burrow out into the Hive instead. This provides a cleaner mechanic for my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that would definitely solve my problem as well xD Will keep it in mind!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:49:40-07:00","id":1215182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215172#post1215172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't have any chance there, this chamber you are describing is <b>in his lair. </b>No matter where the Horror goes, the chamber stays in the lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Restate the question, then, because I have no idea what you're asking and I haven't been talking about a singular Chamber. The Apex of a region applies the Hive Trait to any Chambers within the area, whether they're part of a Lair or not, because &quot;any Chambers within the area&quot; is what the hive is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T11:52:58-07:00","id":1215183,"title":"","content":"Soooo, to reconnect to the hive, a beast would just have to claim a new chamber belonging to the hive ? or can she just choose to reconnect it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:03:11-07:00","id":1215187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215183#post1215183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo, to reconnect to the hive, a beast would just have to claim a new chamber belonging to the hive ? or can she just choose to reconnect it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my read, you could do either, but they would require you to technically add a &quot;new&quot; chamber. But take it with a grain of salt, we are still arguing about how exactly it goes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also see <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a>'s post, it makes things mechanically easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:04:10-07:00","id":1215188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215183#post1215183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo, to reconnect to the hive, a beast would just have to claim a new chamber belonging to the hive ? or can she just choose to reconnect it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine the descriptive legwork to be closer to the latter than the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:12:37-07:00","id":1215189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215182#post1215182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Restate the question, then, because I have no idea what you're asking and I haven't been talking about a singular Chamber. The Apex of a region applies the Hive Trait to any Chambers within the area, whether they're part of a Lair or not, because &quot;any Chambers within the area&quot; is what the hive is.</div> </div> </div> </div>What counts as being connected to a Hive?<br /> <br /> What I think: Having a chamber in the hive<br /> What I assume this means: The chamber has the shared trait<br /> How I think you stop this: Collapse the chamber<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> What I think you are presenting (correct me by all means, if you meant these differently):<br /> <br /> A hive is a collection of chambers /no question here/<br /> The apex forces the lair traits on the chambers /no question here/<br /> Your chamber gains protection from this by you forcing your horror not to go that far while feeding /I utterly fail to understand why/<br /> <br /> I have some other questions connected to that last one, but lets stay with this for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","user":"IceBen","date":".  Separated the two parts 05-04-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:21:57-07:00","id":1215193,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, the entire chapter about lairs, hives, lair traits, Apex, and Primordial pathways in the core book feels like it needs a big clarity rewrite. Or we just need a separate FAQ thread we can keep the op updated just for this series of topics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:24:02-07:00","id":1215195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215189#post1215189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your chamber gains protection from this by you forcing your horror not to go that far while feeding /I utterly fail to understand why/</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> You <i>alter your Lair so that the features the Apex uses to have access to your Lair do not persist, mechanically removing the Hive Trait from those Chambers.</i> This change cuts your Lair off from the hive and its assortment of Pathways and Chambers as part of the process of denying the Apex access to your Lair and Horror, <i>which results in the Horror having less room to wander without reestablishing a connection to the hive</i>.<br /> <br /> Why on earth would you assume I was saying <i>the feeding consequences of cutting off your Lair from the hive</i> were the <i>cause of</i> cutting off your Lair from the hive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:35:34-07:00","id":1215200,"title":"","content":"&quot;Connected to a Hive&quot; means &quot;in the same general geographical location.&quot; My Lair can have Chambers that are connected to different Hives, and a Hive is (of course) made up of lots of different Chambers belonging to different Lairs, plus some unclaimed ones.<br /> <br /> Not every Beast has Chambers in more than one Hive, which is why your solution to the Apex Trait problem doesn't always work. If all my Chambers are located in St. Louis, and the Apex of St. Louis is a dick, I can't just collapse my whole Lair and leave town -- or rather, that's a nuclear option/last resort.<br /> <br /> Instead, I can isolate my Lair from the rest of the Hive. This cuts the Apex off from my Lair, so it can't impose an Apex Trait on me, but it also fences in my Horror. If I fall to Ravenous, the Horror can't range as far from my physical location to feed itself, which makes this situation extra fraught (as it's more likely to target people I like, more likely to repeatedly feed on the same person, and generally more likely to attract a Hero.) Still, isolating my Lair can buy me time to either unseat the troublesome Apex or put my RL affairs in order so I can move to a new city -- then I can gradually collapse the old, St. Louis chambers as I claim new ones in my new Hive.<br /> <br /> If I have just one Chamber in St. Louis and the rest are in another Hive, I might decide that the Chamber isn't worth putting up with the Apex Trait and just collapse it, or I might decide I want to hold onto it as a last resort (a backdoor/emergency exit, maybe). I admit I'm not sure if a Beast is allowed to isolate just the one Chamber from its Hive without isolating the whole Lair from all Hives it might be connected to -- my intuition is yes but I don't have time for a close re-read of the RAW.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T12:39:43-07:00","id":1215206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215195#post1215195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> You <i>alter your Lair so that the features the Apex uses to have access to your Lair do not persist, mechanically removing the Hive Trait from those Chambers.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, this is much clearer.<br /> Meanwhile I got home, so I will start reading on this matter in the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T13:22:03-07:00","id":1215218,"title":"","content":"Ok, I didn't find it straight up explained, but the intended mechanism is most definitely what you wrote. I didn't know the Apex (and those who are immune to the trait) can freely move to chambers within the hive. Sadly it wasn't mentioned that this only includes chambers WITH the trait, but yeah, probably intended that way :/<br /> <br /> Also, it wasn't stated that you can decide if you want the Hive Trait there or no, but &quot;removing the connection to the Apex&quot; must be referencing to removing this common Trait, even if it was yours to begin with.<br /> <br /> In this case you just reapply the Trait you removed, and you are instantly connected to the Hive again.<br /> <br /> This is clear now, but I still have problems understanding why exactly does this reduce your Horror's feeding range, does the Trait provide some kind of a map? So without it the Horror can only move only so far away, but if the area shares some kind of similarity to him, he can go further out, and yet again, if that similarity means it is his home turf, he can just go wherever he wants in it.<br /> Or is it plainly just the same mechanism as opening Pathways? Dissimilar is hard, the Horror is pretty much stuck near you, but the closer it gets to mach your style (even if given to you), the easier it gets.<br /> <br /> This answers one other question of mine, a horror can indeed go to the other side of the planet, if it is the same &quot;region&quot;, and he shares the immunity of the Hive Trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:08:43-07:00","id":1215521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215218#post1215218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is clear now, but I still have problems understanding why exactly does this reduce your Horror's feeding range, does the Trait provide some kind of a map? So without it the Horror can only move only so far away, but if the area shares some kind of similarity to him, he can go further out, and yet again, if that similarity means it is his home turf, he can just go wherever he wants in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine you have gained a mall store as a Chamber. Your Horror, the Mall Rat, has the freedom to run all over town. Then one day, a new Apex takes over, and suddenly the town begins to fill with bothersome shambling zombies as it imposes the Minion trait. Now, the Mall Rat doesn\u2019t like these zombies one little bit. They\u2019re just too different from the faceless crowds it usually prefers (moaning instead of laughing, etc). The zombies are now starting to fill the mall, though, and it can\u2019t stand that. So you lock the doors and take care of the zombies already inside. Now the Mall Rat doesn\u2019t have to deal with zombies, but the only places it can hunt zombie free are now the other stores in the mall. If it wants to expand its hunting grounds, it will need to either tolerate zombies or find a way to get rid of them from the town. Getting rid of the current Apex would be a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T09:52:43-07:00","id":1215538,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> That does sound logical, but sadly mechanically a completely different thing happens.<br /> <br /> So there is this mall, in the physical world, in one end of the city, and it's corresponding Chamber is cleared from the Hive Trait (Minions), so the Horror's Lair isn't connected to the Hive.<br /> The Beast, your character, sleeps in the other end of the city, physically far away from it. (miles away)<br /> <br /> When the Horror starts roaming on it's own, it will only move Lair/2 miles from your physical location, nowhere near said mall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T14:12:12-07:00","id":1215590,"title":"","content":"I think I may have missed in the corebook and it's in the players guide (having it shipped) but what's an obascus rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:44:51-07:00","id":1215611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215590#post1215590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I may have missed in the corebook and it's in the players guide (having it shipped) but what's an obascus rite?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Obcasus Rites, are on page 103 of the player's guide, so if yours is in transit you haven't got them yet don't worry.<br /> <br /> In the brief bit they're kind of magic rituals Beasts get due to their own nature. Largely a way to attempt to connect and commune with the Dark Mother. There's stuff like trying to coax prophetic visions,find potential Beasts, lock an area away from baseline mortal access, force open a planar gate, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T17:58:40-07:00","id":1215635,"title":"","content":"Ahh ok, thanks! So it's meant to be used in non combat situations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T18:03:42-07:00","id":1215637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215635#post1215635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh ok, thanks! So it's meant to be used in non combat situations</div> </div> </div> </div>Most ritual magic is, generally speaking, but Obcasus Rites especially fall into that category, on account of how they can only be performed in consecrated locations with nobody present who isn't a participant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T18:24:35-07:00","id":1215640,"title":"","content":"Murdering people who try to interrupt the ritual is explicitly a valid form of participation though, which I think is a nice touch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:27:45-07:00","id":1215778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215538#post1215538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> That does sound logical, but sadly mechanically a completely different thing happens.<br /> <br /> So there is this mall, in the physical world, in one end of the city, and it's corresponding Chamber is cleared from the Hive Trait (Minions), so the Horror's Lair isn't connected to the Hive.<br /> The Beast, your character, sleeps in the other end of the city, physically far away from it. (miles away)<br /> <br /> When the Horror starts roaming on it's own, it will only move Lair/2 miles from your physical location, nowhere near said mall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, fair point. So instead, look at your mortal flesh as basically functioning like an armored vehicle used to transport your Horror through hostile territory. When it stops, the Horror may come out to forage, but it\u2019s not going to go too far from safety while doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T21:37:51-07:00","id":1215983,"title":"","content":"As we're now several books into the line, an old question re-asked:<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any idea what difficulties Hold the Door and Be My Guest actually circumvent re: entering the Lair, given that the most consistent means of entry (opening Primordial Pathways) in no way limits who can and cannot wind up inside the Lair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T03:54:12-07:00","id":1216029,"title":"","content":"Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1 Does anyone know about the satiety expenditure of Vengeful Earth from the players guide? It mentions summoning some limbs, but not how long they last for? Is it intended they last for a scene, or the turn? Also could it be used to attack multiple targets?<br /> <br /> 2 Death. I vaguely remember reading something about reforming in the lair but I couldn't find it again (or whether I misread it). But are there any mechanics for avoiding (permanent) death in the game that Ive missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24187-farm_ecology","name":"farm_ecology","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T04:06:30-07:00","id":1216033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>farm_ecology</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1216029#post1216029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1 Does anyone know about the satiety expenditure of Vengeful Earth from the players guide? It mentions summoning some limbs, but not how long they last for? Is it intended they last for a scene, or the turn? Also could it be used to attack multiple targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Limbs last for the scene. The can\u2019t be used to make multiple (separate) attacks in a turn, but I\u2019d allow characters to make sweeping attacks that could hit multiple targets in a single motion. I\u2019d probably use something like the auto fire rules, but applied to a melee attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T04:17:51-07:00","id":1216038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>farm_ecology</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1216029#post1216029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 Death. I vaguely remember reading something about reforming in the lair but I couldn't find it again (or whether I misread it). But are there any mechanics for avoiding (permanent) death in the game that Ive missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the reforming in the lair only applies when killed during an astral travel(BPG pg:156, when dieing in the mother\u2019s land wakes up in the lair).<br /> As for general death avoidance, most things die when killed.I can only recall Mummies and the 1e purified having reliable self resurrection. Some have easier time circumventing death by old age, but I cant recall any by Beasts.(apart from the +50 years lifespan per Lair above 5).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24185,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","user":"Zsarnok","date":". 05-07-2018, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24185-zsarnok","name":"Zsarnok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T04:44:40-07:00","id":1216045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1215983#post1215983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we're now several books into the line, an old question re-asked:<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any idea what difficulties Hold the Door and Be My Guest actually circumvent re: entering the Lair, given that the most consistent means of entry (opening Primordial Pathways) in no way limits who can and cannot wind up inside the Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entering a Burrow isn't an uncontested action, and does take time, so if a Pathway is opened, then the Beast has to let people in the Pathway go into his Lair, otherwise they just stay behind when it closes.<br /> (Doing this gives them a way out as well, but iirc you can revoke that part)<br /> <br /> I guess this method applies to Mages and such (including other Beasts as well?) when THEY try to open a way into your Lair, so they can get in uncontested &lt;preferably when you go with them&gt;, but that is just speculation from my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:24:48-07:00","id":1216168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1216045#post1216045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entering a Burrow isn't an uncontested action, and does take time, so if a Pathway is opened, then the Beast has to let people in the Pathway go into his Lair, otherwise they just stay behind when it closes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is as close to an answer as I've gotten as well \u2014 the contested roll, the Willpower cost, and the fact that forcing your way through takes success and multiple turns combined with a Pathway normally staying open for not much longer than that, combined with those timers being on neighboring pages seems like supporting evidence, at least \u2014 but the example of someone trying to leave the external location while the Pathway is open lacks the details to indicate whether its outcome is deliberate or not; the phrasing of Hold the Door doesn't refer to that section save through the use of the word &quot;guest&quot; (and vice versa) and the guest-based mechanics talk about their subjects being <i>unable</i> to enter the Lair rather than encountering the same resistance as an intruder would.<br /> <br /> Pending more direct statements it's probably what I'll go with, but it's a tricky mechanical tangle even after the introduction of Trap Room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T11:00:03-07:00","id":1216219,"title":"","content":"My book should be coming today and be there once I'm back home from school. Can I have a quick summary of the societies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T20:45:49-07:00","id":1216466,"title":"","content":"So since Legendary Horror gives a Horror Influence, does that theoretically mean it could function as a Totem now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:54:51-07:00","id":1216506,"title":"","content":"You don't seem to need Influence to count as a totem, but sure. There's a sidebar in the Pack that suggests alternative totems. And the Player's Guide suggests 'The Final Peace' as a Beast or Horror that acts as a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-08-2018, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T23:34:54-07:00","id":1216514,"title":"","content":"Beast's Horror as a pack's Totem...<br /> <br /> Sounds messy, complicated, and could invite a whole lot of unintended trouble for the Uratha in said pack.<br /> <br /> I love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:33:04-07:00","id":1217183,"title":"","content":"Is there anything about beasts allies to the seer of throne","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join D