detriment, where's the fun in that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T09:50:32-07:00","id":1217997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1217980#post1217980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, if the PCs consists of a group of a major splat, I really, really can't see the player losing the major template on their character have much fun. Playing low-powered mortals can be great fun, but when completely overshadowed in competency on most, if not all, fronts by your coplayers' characters, I'd rather just create a new character of the major template. How story focused the game is doesn't really change anything because individual mortals don't really have much impact on supers, and they don't share major themes with any other gameline. Hence why I think it should only be used on NPCs in stories where the PCs are major splats, or only in games where the PC doesn't have a template to lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie, PN you don't lose your template, you're still a Beast in this scenario. The Horror is diminished because the Horrorspawn is basically like using a recording of a person to substitute the whole person, but that's it. You don't suddenly become a mortal. You get the Soulless condition yes, but that's not that bad. As Satchel said the primary penalty is surrendering and sleep can no longer be used to regain willpower, but that's it. You don't lose your powers, you don't lose the ability to gain experience and grow. *<br /> <br /> Soulless, as explained on page 326 in the Beast core, gives the following penalties and benefits. You get a -2 penalty on any attempts made to possess your character and you do not gain willpower through surrender or rest. You may now gain willpower once a scene by upholding your Virtue without risking yourself, you may completely refill your willpower once a chapter by fulfilling your vice in a way that does pose a risk to you. Though unless you're at integrity 1 fulfilling your vice like that is now a breaking point that gets a -5 penalty on the check. <br /> <br /> *Outside of the replacement period, but that's basically a few days where you need to feed enough to get the amount of food into your Horrorspawn to make it function as a new Horror or die. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T09:54:11-07:00","id":1217999,"title":"","content":"Ahh I see, well I guess I could see it happening. How do I use up experience without being able to spend it while my character sleeps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T10:09:15-07:00","id":1218001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1217999#post1217999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh I see, well I guess I could see it happening. How do I use up experience without being able to spend it while my character sleeps</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't regain willpower from sleep. That's all that changes on that front. Also technically speaking you aren't supposed to be limited to sleep as a means of spending xp, you just save up the xp and then you have your training time, or whatever to justify that you've spent the xp to gain whatever benefit you're going with, This isn't Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T10:48:25-07:00","id":1218015,"title":"","content":"Wrong thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-12-2018, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T11:37:12-07:00","id":1218025,"title":"","content":"I see the &quot;well, what next?&quot; part of using a Horrospawn to save a Beast as a fantastic hook for Storytellers and groups to come up with their own content. Just because the text doesn't give a way to reclaim &quot;full&quot; Beast status doesn't mean we can't come up with our own!<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head...<ul><li>The Brood has to go on a pilgrimage to the Mother's Land, deep within the Primordial Dream, so that their diminished member can attempt to plead directly with Her to restore them. (the Road Trip Option)</li> <li>The Brood enlists the services of a Mage with experience with the dream realms to figure out a way restore their friend's Horror. This leads to an ancient Obcasus Rite that would heal them...but it requires materials and participants that won't be easy (or pleasant) to acquire. (the Scavenger Hunt Option)</li> <li>The Brood discovers that by devouring a Beast Incarnate/Insatiable while in the Primordial Dream, the lesser Horrorspawn can absorb enough power to become a full Horror. Now they have to track down a suitable target, and decide if they're willing to eat another sentient being just to feel whole again... (the You Are What You Eat Option)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T11:46:26-07:00","id":1218029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1218025#post1218025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the &quot;well, what next?&quot; part of using a Horrospawn to save a Beast as a fantastic hook for Storytellers and groups to come up with their own content. Just because the text doesn't give a way to reclaim &quot;full&quot; Beast status doesn't mean we can't come up with our own!<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head...<ul><li>The Brood has to go on a pilgrimage to the Mother's Land, deep within the Primordial Dream, so that their diminished member can attempt to plead directly with Her to restore them. (the Road Trip Option)</li> <li>The Brood enlists the services of a Mage with experience with the dream realms to figure out a way restore their friend's Horror. This leads to an ancient Obcasus Rite that would heal them...but it requires materials and participants that won't be easy (or pleasant) to acquire. (the Scavenger Hunt Option)</li> <li>The Brood discovers that by devouring a Beast Incarnate/Insatiable while in the Primordial Dream, the lesser Horrorspawn can absorb enough power to become a full Horror. Now they have to track down a suitable target, and decide if they're willing to eat another sentient being just to feel whole again... (the You Are What You Eat Option)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you could go through a second devouring, a completely other Horror eating your &quot;soul&quot; again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T17:48:50-07:00","id":1218108,"title":"","content":"Cool idea <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12970_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12970\" data-vbnamecard=\"12970\">Gellydog</a>! Sort of like the beast version of a prometheans journey","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T17:51:18-07:00","id":1218110,"title":"","content":"Another question, is the fabulist a person? It sounds like he is just the guy that makes creepypastas, and like slenderman, he can effect other people into spreading creepy stories the internet. I am really confused by the fabulist description","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T20:39:30-07:00","id":1218141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1218110#post1218110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, is the fabulist a person? It sounds like he is just the guy that makes creepypastas, and like slenderman, he can effect other people into spreading creepy stories the internet. I am really confused by the fabulist description</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's an Incarnate class Beast. From how the description goes it seems like Fabulist basically forged a memetic hunting ground, it targets those who have a copy of the original stories, as those can still be spread about then its hunting ground can continue to exist. As no powers are listed for it then its up for debate, but presumably the creepy effects are things it has learned how to do and used in the stories and then again on the victims. Like imposing a lair trait on an area to cause it to exhibit properties that the area shouldn't be able to exhibit. <br /> <br /> The original story archive is debatable as it can be a number of things from just exceptionally well crafted fiction, to actual events retold in such a manner and with the proper details that allow the stories to fall into the category of wavering back and forth over the audience's willingness to believe the veracity of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T05:47:04-07:00","id":1218181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1218141#post1218141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it's an Incarnate class Beast. From how the description goes it seems like Fabulist basically forged a memetic hunting ground, it targets those who have a copy of the original stories, as those can still be spread about then its hunting ground can continue to exist. As no powers are listed for it then its up for debate, but presumably the creepy effects are things it has learned how to do and used in the stories and then again on the victims. Like imposing a lair trait on an area to cause it to exhibit properties that the area shouldn't be able to exhibit. <br /> <br /> The original story archive is debatable as it can be a number of things from just exceptionally well crafted fiction, to actual events retold in such a manner and with the proper details that allow the stories to fall into the category of wavering back and forth over the audience's willingness to believe the veracity of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who\u2019s Fabulist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T07:56:00-07:00","id":1218204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1218181#post1218181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who\u2019s Fabulist?</div> </div> </div> </div>An example Incarnate Beast with a cult in the Player's Guide. The Fabulist created their Legend online via creepypasta, apparently because they had no other choice; little is known of what they're like in real life, but they appear to harbor a deep rage, a deep sense of betrayal, towards their physical body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T16:15:12-07:00","id":1218355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1218204#post1218204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An example Incarnate Beast with a cult in the Player's Guide. The Fabulist created their Legend online via creepypasta, apparently because they had no other choice; little is known of what they're like in real life, but they appear to harbor a deep rage, a deep sense of betrayal, towards their physical body</div> </div> </div> </div>Body Dysphoria? Or a really fucked up illness like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrodysplasia_ossificans_progressiva\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrod...ns_progressiva</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":".  Typo 05-13-2018, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T23:39:59-07:00","id":1218427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1218355#post1218355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Body Dysphoria? Or a really fucked up illness like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrodysplasia_ossificans_progressiva\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibrod...ns_progressiva</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Something really fucked up happened to their body - maybe accident, maybe illness, maybe something they were born with. No-one knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date