ctions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:29:23-07:00","id":1220738,"title":"","content":"what do you think on Beast traveling to other planets through astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:37:27-07:00","id":1220740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1220738#post1220738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you think on Beast traveling to other planets through astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand the Astral, that's not how it works. It's a world of souls and meaning. It doesn't correspond to physical distance like the Shadow does. Beasts can use it to travel via their Lairs and Primordial Pathways, but I don't think they could reach the real-world planets. They could venture out into the Sidereal Wastes and find the Astral planet-souls, but I don't <i>think</i> they could get to the real ones. It is a very interesting question, though. If they could get there, immunity to Lair Traits could help them survive, provided the Beast has the appropriate ones - Suffocating and Extreme Cold come to mind for Mars, for instance.<br /> <br /> That said, I am not an expert here. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> , do you have a couple of cents to give us?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T06:48:28-07:00","id":1220817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1220740#post1220740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand the Astral, that's not how it works. It's a world of souls and meaning. It doesn't correspond to physical distance like the Shadow does. Beasts can use it to travel via their Lairs and Primordial Pathways, but I don't think they could reach the real-world planets. They could venture out into the Sidereal Wastes and find the Astral planet-souls, but I don't <i>think</i> they could get to the real ones. It is a very interesting question, though. If they could get there, immunity to Lair Traits could help them survive, provided the Beast has the appropriate ones - Suffocating and Extreme Cold come to mind for Mars, for instance.<br /> <br /> That said, I am not an expert here. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> , do you have a couple of cents to give us?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Cinder, but this could, theoretically, be possible, but probably not for Beasts.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Wastes have the Astral reflections of other planets, etc in them. It's no unreasonable to think that Astral Irises in these locations may well lead out onto the planets themselves. But Beasts would have a very hard time actually getting far enough in this space to take advantage of it, since iirc they don't have any equivalent of an Amnion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T12:10:52-07:00","id":1220898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1220740#post1220740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That said, I am not an expert here. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> , do you have a couple of cents to give us?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit late and you people pretty much already said what I was going to say, but here's my take.<br /> <br /> My answer would be: yes, a Beast can travel to other planets through the Astral...technically. It's not gonna be easy<br /> <br /> Inodiv said this better than I will, but the Sidereal Wastes are the Astral reflection of astronomical concept and places as they appear on the cosmic layer of the dreamworld and and Irises that open there might lead there without stretching things too much. Given that and the Begotten innate ability to travel around and unlock passages, they should be able to exploit those openings if needed.<br /> <br /> But it's here that things get more complex.<br /> <br /> The Anima Mundi is what the Begotten call Mother's Land. It's described in the last chapter of the PG but, long story short, the soul of the world is also the Dark's Mother turf, the place where the progenitors of the various Families might snooze and the birthplace of larval Horrors (which gain identity and structure later while travelling in the Primordial Dream and being shaped by human thoughts and myths).<br /> <br /> Things get a little murky here. The Player's Guide speaks of it in Beast terms while Mage's Core does it in Awakened terms and we can argue for days on what's supposed to be the right answer while in reality I'm convinced it's mostly the various gamelines looking at the same thing with different perspectives. To make an example, if you got, say, draconic or insect-like eyes you perceive the Ecstatic Wind as the Dark Mother calling, while if those eyes burn with Supernal might that pierces the Lie, you perceive it as your consciousness being absorbed into the cosmic majesty of the soul of the World. And while perception is reality and that's even more true in the Astral, I think there's no need for any sterile answer there. Perhaps it's the Dark Mother's home, perhaps it's the Anima Mundi, perhaps it's both or probably it's the two things being one and the same, at least to some degree. I might run a game that ends with a Brood travelling there to say hi to Nightmare Mom and I still would leave some questions unanswered, even in my personal table's canon.<br /> <br /> Mystery, wonders and nightmares, after all.<br /> <br /> What matters to the topic is that Beasts are in dire danger when travelling to the Mother's Land, because the stronger and more connected to the Dark Mother their Horror is (how high their Lair is), the more they are in danger of their identity dissolving. Mage have a degree of protection with the Amnion, because them having strong willpower and ego is kinda their thing. Beasts, on the other hand, have to fight to preserve their own identity against the world, the monomyth and the tapestry of the Astral as always and here their Primordial side is in danger of reverting back to something removed from humanity. Either that, or the Dark Mother wants to hug them/devour them (same thing, really) with such a ravenous desire that the proximity hurts.<br /> <br /> So you don't have much time to travel to the portion of the Mother's Land that Mages call Sidereal Wastes and find a passage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Having said that, the topic also leads to a lot of interesting story hooks, from Beasts creating chambers in space, to others recovering ancient ones from the depths of the Astral whose existence begs the question of how they came into being in the first place, a community of Begotten creating a web of Primordial Pathways that allows them to travel around the cosmos through Burrows and so on. Plus all that can happen to non-Beast characters that stumble upon these shenanigans.<br /> <br /> It's the sort of thing that likely has no reason to be in most chronicles, but go for it if there's a cool story behind. I have a character whose Devouring happened while she was on the International Space Station and that still keeps a connection to it so she can travel up from time to time and look at Earth from above, so I don't see anything wrong with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: One can also argue that Mother's Land is &quot;only&quot; the portion of the Anima Mundi called Dreaming Earth, considering how it's described and how often you have to roll for damage. That reasoning has a solid basis, but on the other hand the PG also says the interval depends on where you are and makes no distinction between the realms of the Mother's Land. Again, things are a bit murky here. I would not care much while running Beast while I'd follow what Mage says while running Awakening, but I admit that's a solution some find flawed and I have no defense against such criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-21-2018, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:46:58-07:00","id":1220930,"title":"","content":"Do female bodied beasts still have periods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:53:38-07:00","id":1220931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1220930#post1220930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate