mg itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T14:25:46-07:00","id":1239438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1239434#post1239434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> , the ghosts would be a good way of illustrating how people, Beasts and Heroes are meant to work. The first ghosts show Scrooge the 'gentle' way, and when that doesn't work the Ghost of Christmas Future is there with the harsh truth to scare him straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who would represent heroes, the first 2 ghost?<br /> <br /> As for the 3rd ghost, very true, but doesn't the present ghost literally melt into a skeleton and have 2 human creatures, representing he is running out of time for redemption? Because that's pretty scary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:10:45-07:00","id":1239445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1239438#post1239438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who would represent heroes, the first 2 ghost?<br /> <br /> As for the 3rd ghost, very true, but doesn't the present ghost literally melt into a skeleton and have 2 human creatures, representing he is running out of time for redemption? Because that's pretty scary</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall; it's been a long time since I read A Christmas Carol. I can only really remember the general 'shape' of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:22:54-07:00","id":1239575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1239438#post1239438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who would represent heroes, the first 2 ghost?<br /> <br /> As for the 3rd ghost, very true, but doesn't the present ghost literally melt into a skeleton and have 2 human creatures, representing he is running out of time for redemption? Because that's pretty scary</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're only operating on what they do then I would actually say Marley would fit the role of Hero as he's the one who flat out tells Scrooge what he needs to do to avoid his fate. <br /> <br /> As for the Ghost of Christmas Present, he aged as the visit went on and died at the end of it. The only iteration I've ever seen or heard of him becoming a skeleton was the Jim Carrey 3D version, and while that did surprisingly well on adaptation points I don't think that was one of them. The two spirits under his robe were Ignorance and Want, they represented the dangers/horrors/and harm mankind could do through choosing to be oblivious to the things around us in favor of our selfish desires. At most their relationship to Scrooge would have been a &quot;physical&quot; manifestation of his own sins. <br /> <br /> Hmm thinking it over I do have a question, do we have a Nightmare that forces something like a hallucination of a person's transgressions on them, probably homebrew? It seems like a nemesis power, maybe a whisperer trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T12:12:20-07:00","id":1240161,"title":"","content":"So one of the new Inheritances in the Player's Guide is the Division, where the Begotten and Horror are turned into separate beings, but remain linked by a satiety pool. Let's say a Begotten manages to divide themselves' from their Horror, only to realize the huge mistake they've made in doing so.<br /> <br /> Is it within the realm of possibility for the Begotten and Horror to become one being again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T12:39:29-07:00","id":1240170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1240161#post1240161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of the new Inheritances in the Player's Guide is the Division, where the Begotten and Horror are turned into separate beings, but remain linked by a satiety pool. Let's say a Begotten manages to divide themselves' from their Horror, only to realize the huge mistake they've made in doing so.<br /> <br /> Is it within the realm of possibility for the Begotten and Horror to become one being again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words: Storyteller fiat. Another two words: plot fodder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:18:55-07:00","id":1240366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1240161#post1240161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of the new Inheritances in the Player's Guide is the Division, where the Begotten and Horror are turned into separate beings, but remain linked by a satiety pool. Let's say a Begotten manages to divide themselves' from their Horror, only to realize the huge mistake they've made in doing so.<br /> <br /> Is it within the realm of possibility for the Begotten and Horror to become one being again?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Officially it is an Inheritance, which leads me to say no. Granted I see the Inheritance as the end of a character's role in the campaign considering what most of them are. Other than that well as ajf says if the ST thinks it would be fun to run then it'll be fun to see how it plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T02:53:49-07:00","id":1240371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdorableChou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1240161#post1240161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of the new Inheritances in the Player's Guide is the Division, where the Begotten and Horror are turned into separate beings, but remain linked by a satiety pool. Let's say a Begotten manages to divide themselves' from their Horror, only to realize the huge mistake they've made in doing so.<br /> <br /> Is it within the realm of possibility for the Begotten and Horror to become one being again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Officially, no. The Beast is out of luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T01:54:40-07:00","id":1240768,"title":"","content":"Do we have a name/tagline for the 'featured' chronicle? Something like the Strix Chronicle, the Idigam chronicle, the Fallen World chronicles, the Firestorm chronicle, the Huntsman chronicle, the Slasher chronicle or the chronicle of the dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:03:00-07:00","id":1240869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1240768#post1240768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have a name/tagline for the 'featured' chronicle? Something like the Strix Chronicle, the Idigam chronicle, the Fallen World chronicles, the Firestorm chronicle, the Huntsman chronicle, the Slasher chronicle or the chronicle of the dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Feast would be the closest equivalent as it's the title of the accompanying fiction anthology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T14:31:06-07:00","id":1242059,"title":"","content":"Edit: I'm tired and responded to an old old post mistakenly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 08-02-2018, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:52:39-07:00","id":1242570,"title":"","content":"Does anyone use the legendary horror merit, I've been thinking about getting it for an upcoming chronicle, but I find merits like it risky with a fear the reward ain't worth it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T01:04:51-07:00","id":1242651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1242570#post1242570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone use the legendary horror merit, I've been thinking about getting it for an upcoming chronicle, but I find merits like it risky with a fear the reward ain't worth it</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is cool, especially as a sort of hereditary merit.<br /> Also, one way to use it: a Player decides they do not like their Current beast, but still Loves their horror and wants to see it included in the chronicle further on. By buying the merit, it can serve e.g. as a pack's totem. If they want to reincorporate the horror into a Current character, obcasus Rites are your friends.<br /> Can make for awesome scenes.<br /> Use it more for NPC's, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T08:02:39-07:00","id":1242720,"title":"","content":"So it has pretty story potential is what I'm understanding. Would you say it's pretty useful mechanically though (but honestly I'll probably get it for the story)<br /> <br /> Also a horror totem sounds awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T14:53:35-07:00","id":1242793,"title":"","content":"Has it ever been addressed if horrors have a maximum/minimum size? Its something ive always wondered, especially considering how it would effect inheritance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T22:59:16-07:00","id":1244389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1242793#post1242793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it ever been addressed if horrors have a maximum/minimum size? Its something ive always wondered, especially considering how it would effect inheritance</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not. They are created by the primordial dream. However their &quot;effective&quot; size that is responsible for creating their pull of health is not infinite, they start from size 5(if I recall correctly), and can go higher by some atavisms, having points in lair trait and such. <br /> I believe that their seize in the dream is just visual, It does not really correspond with their health and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24520-crazybeard","name":"CrazyBeard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T23:01:16-07:00","id":1244390,"title":"","content":"A quick question for Collector Beasts. Can they collect abstract things? Like feelings, names, or memories? If so, how would they? Would they need some magical deals, or could they do it all by themselves? As RAW, is it possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24520-crazybeard","name":"CrazyBeard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T13:20:35-07:00","id":1244600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrazyBeard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1244390#post1244390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question for Collector Beasts. Can they collect abstract things? Like feelings, names, or memories? If so, how would they? Would they need some magical deals, or could they do it all by themselves? As RAW, is it possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collector's need a trophy for their hoard. So if you were collecting names you would need something to function as a trophy of the name you took.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T21:56:04-07:00","id":1244721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1244600#post1244600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Collector's need a trophy for their hoard. So if you were collecting names you would need something to function as a trophy of the name you took.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... would like a book with them. Which would store them could be describes as such a trophy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24520-crazybeard","name":"CrazyBeard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T22:13:48-07:00","id":1244723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrazyBeard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1244721#post1244721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... would like a book with them. Which would store them could be describes as such a trophy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of this is going to need explanation on the thing you're collecting. Like an obvious one would be you can't just collect names by meeting people and getting their names to write in the book, whereas a scrapbook full of contract envelopes for the unchained you've helped seal these deals* on would probably work well.<br /> <br /> *It isn't easy and everyone thinks you're nuts for working with one of those life swapping weirdos, but hey no one else in the neighborhood has an album literally containing the deeds to human souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T07:22:10-07:00","id":1246642,"title":"","content":"when merging with horror, do you just use it's stats or merge like with spirit-claimed?<br /> <br /> Also, how do beasts detect supernatural portals? like Avernian gates, hedge portals, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, 'well stocked lair' merit. How do you divide the merit points for minions? 1 merit point gives 2 pt to spend on minions, but no instructions for strength/number distribution and how about it's ability to house lair dot's number of guests in EACH room? related question is Thralls lair trait. What are those things? a type of a horrorspawn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 08-16-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T19:48:27-07:00","id":1246847,"title":"","content":"Merging with the Horror you just use highest of Power Finesse and Resistance attributes and then assign bonus dots equal to 2xLair.<br /> <br /> Beasts have no inherent ability to detect portals. They have to see someone else use it (or at least get an accurate description of its location).<br /> <br /> Well stocked Lair gives you merit points, which would translate into minions by way of the usual social merits: Staff, Retainer, etc. The way I read the merit, you can make as many rooms as you want habitable, but you can only manifest enough food and other necessities to support 3xLair people per dot. It's mostly just a question of do you cram all of your guests into one chamber or let them spread out as much as the Lair allows. It's not clear whether making a room habitable allows hostiles to traverse it safely, but given Beasts' inherent ability to apply traits with complete selective discretion inside their domain I'm guessing you can have your eternally burning desert provide a picnic for your supernat buddies and still scorch Heroes to a crisp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T01:45:47-07:00","id":1248355,"title":"","content":"I have a question. Does blood generated by lair feed blood drinkers? like vampires.<br /> For an example a lake of blood, a bloody rain, or even a reflection of underworlds blood river in the chamber.<br /> with the same logic, would water and food (fish from Makara) feed a human? should it be a part of well stocked lair merit?<br /> <br /> On one hand I understand that it's a valuable 'free' resource to exploit, on the other, it's already quite easy to open the pathway into underworld with a bit of roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 08-21-2018, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T01:47:59-07:00","id":1248356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrazyBeard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1244390#post1244390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick question for Collector Beasts. Can they collect abstract things? Like feelings, names, or memories? If so, how would they? Would they need some magical deals, or could they do it all by themselves? As RAW, is it possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>if you play it through the Astral, sure why not. Abstract things become quite tangible there. Doing the same in waking world would be problematic though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T18:21:16-07:00","id":1248583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1248355#post1248355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question. Does blood generated by lair feed blood drinkers? like vampires.<br /> For an example a lake of blood, a bloody rain, or even a reflection of underworlds blood river in the chamber.<br /> with the same logic, would water and food (fish from Makara) feed a human? should it be a part of well stocked lair merit?<br /> <br /> On one hand I understand that it's a valuable 'free' resource to exploit, on the other, it's already quite easy to open the pathway into underworld with a bit of roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the merit of Well-stocked is meant to handle things like having fish or things to allow people to live in there for a while. So I'd say you'd need that if you wanted edible fish in the lair. As for blood, that's very much an ST call since I don't think I personally would allow it, but I can definitely see a few interesting stories coming out Beasts making friends with other supernaturals just because, &quot;Hey this nightmare hellscape of yours freely produces stuff that is really helpful to me, mind if I hang out a bit more?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T18:34:19-07:00","id":1248587,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I feel like it's loose enough to allow for wiggle room depending on the style of story you want to tell, though I can't actually imagine it easily providing Vitae equal to a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T19:50:44-07:00","id":1248601,"title":"","content":"&quot;Live comfortably&quot; suggests to me that it would probably be reasonable to assume it could provide enough blood to keep a vampire out of Torpor, but 1 Vitae per night is rarely hard to find by other means. <br /> <br /> Besides, Beasts already have an extremely useful power for courting vampires if that's what you want to do: Pick up the Relentless Hunter Atavism and they'll be all over you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T22:26:21-07:00","id":1248626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1248601#post1248601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Live comfortably&amp;quot; suggests to me that it would probably be reasonable to assume it could provide enough blood to keep a vampire out of Torpor, but 1 Vitae per night is rarely hard to find by other means. <br /> <br /> Besides, Beasts already have an extremely useful power for courting vampires if that's what you want to do: Pick up the Relentless Hunter Atavism and they'll be all over you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a totally guilt- and violence - free source of vitae you do not have to fight over, though, so especially high - humanity kindred would go &quot;Yes please!&quot;<br /> Huh, chronicle material...<br /> <br /> Also, there is a difference between being a bottomless blood Doll and a host providing your needs. Both work, differently well for different reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T03:48:18-07:00","id":1248673,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the interesting answers guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T14:47:29-07:00","id":1248774,"title":"","content":"Okay, sorry if these were answered explicitly elsewhere in this topic but after 7-8 pages I wasn't prepared to search the entire thread for this.<br /> <br /> If I understand things right:<br /> <br /> If I have a Lair Trait present, then I may freely impose my other lair traits (one per turn, or all at once?)<br /> If I do not have a Trait available and I'm in an area corresponding to a chamber, then I can spend Satiety OR make a Wits + Resolve roll to impose one.<br /> If it's not the exact location I can still make that roll, but with an increasing difficulty based on just how different the place is.<br /> <br /> I can roll with all this, I'm pretty sure I've got the right of it.<br /> <br /> Where I get confused is where the difficulty descriptors say they apply for Primordial Pathways. There's already a -3 penalty in place for trying to open one to or from anywhere in the material world that isn't reflected by a chamber. Do these stack?<br /> <br /> Those two sections seem to be at odds with each other and don't seem to reference each other like it seems they should; I'm drawing a blank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T18:14:08-07:00","id":1248798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1248774#post1248774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I get confused is where the difficulty descriptors say they apply for Primordial Pathways. There's already a -3 penalty in place for trying to open one to or from anywhere in the material world that isn't reflected by a chamber. Do these stack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. This is why you hunt in places that resemble your Chambers and make use of your Lair Traits and get Gorged if you plan to shortcut through your Lair a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T14:14:28-07:00","id":1249009,"title":"","content":"Some prior information first, I've been familiar with the Chronicles of Darkness books for a while although for one reason or another, I've never been able to play in a game. I started with Geist, then went to Changeling because the concepts in both looked interesting to me and when I saw that 2nd ed was coming out, Beast appealed to me most. I love the lore and the idea of both playing an actual monster where the details are more or less left up to the player and being able to infect people with nightmares sounded very interesting. <br /> <br /> Where I'm getting hung up, though, is the Lair and, specifically, the Chambers.<br /> <br /> So, let's say I'm playing a literal Gorgon. The Heart of my Lair is a cave adorned with statues fitting what my Horror is. Over the course of play, I add a Chamber using an abandoned hospital and then later on, I'm able to add another Chamber based on an old, 19th century factory. The Burrows between them are simple. The cave is the basement of the Hospital, stairs leading down into natural, rocky corridors and there's a road connecting the hospital to the factory. As a Medusa-esque figure, my Namtaru glides easily from nightmare-scape to nightmare-scape, hunting the unwary in her home. From what I understand, the real-world places that those Chambers are based on heavily influence the place within the Lair that they exemplify, so while my Medusa may alter the hospital so that it, too, has statues of doctors or patients, maybe being dark or maze-like in it's construction, it still has to look like a hospital and same goes for the factory.<br /> <br /> Now, let's say that instead of a Namtaru, I want to play an Anakim. Perhaps a 20-foot titan of moss and stone with a mouth colored brown from it's ground-up victims. It's Heart is a dense, rocky forest, but otherwise, over the course of play, I still accumulate the aforementioned hospital and factory. There's still the road, but maybe the hospital is set deeper into the forest, closer to the Heart with a path leading into the woods. However, the Anakim is 20 feet tall. How does this giant navigate the insides of the hospital? How does he even get into the factory?<br /> <br /> Lastly, what about a Makara? Some huge leviathan the size of the hospital or the factory itself. How does that thing stalk the hospital's corridors or the rickety machinery of the factory? In addition to it's size, the massive whale-like creature needs an ocean to swim in.<br /> <br /> So, my ultimate question is this. How do I reconcile a Horror that doesn't seem to suit the area a Chamber is in with the Chamber itself? Does it actually have to be connected thematically to the real-world location? If not, how much can I alter it?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this is too long winded. I didn't want to create another thread to busy the forum. I'm also sorry that this is so long-winded. I feel like the core question is simple, but maybe I went overboard, here.<br /> <br /> Any help would be much appreciated, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24563-op3999","name":"Op3999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T15:02:47-07:00","id":1249013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Op3999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249009#post1249009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some prior information first, I've been familiar with the Chronicles of Darkness books for a while although for one reason or another, I've never been able to play in a game. I started with Geist, then went to Changeling because the concepts in both looked interesting to me and when I saw that 2nd ed was coming out, Beast appealed to me most. I love the lore and the idea of both playing an actual monster where the details are more or less left up to the player and being able to infect people with nightmares sounded very interesting.<br /> <br /> Where I'm getting hung up, though, is the Lair and, specifically, the Chambers.<br /> <br /> So, let's say I'm playing a literal Gorgon. The Heart of my Lair is a cave adorned with statues fitting what my Horror is. Over the course of play, I add a Chamber using an abandoned hospital and then later on, I'm able to add another Chamber based on an old, 19th century factory. The Burrows between them are simple. The cave is the basement of the Hospital, stairs leading down into natural, rocky corridors and there's a road connecting the hospital to the factory. As a Medusa-esque figure, my Namtaru glides easily from nightmare-scape to nightmare-scape, hunting the unwary in her home. From what I understand, the real-world places that those Chambers are based on heavily influence the place within the Lair that they exemplify, so while my Medusa may alter the hospital so that it, too, has statues of doctors or patients, maybe being dark or maze-like in it's construction, it still has to look like a hospital and same goes for the factory.<br /> <br /> Now, let's say that instead of a Namtaru, I want to play an Anakim. Perhaps a 20-foot titan of moss and stone with a mouth colored brown from it's ground-up victims. It's Heart is a dense, rocky forest, but otherwise, over the course of play, I still accumulate the aforementioned hospital and factory. There's still the road, but maybe the hospital is set deeper into the forest, closer to the Heart with a path leading into the woods. However, the Anakim is 20 feet tall. How does this giant navigate the insides of the hospital? How does he even get into the factory?<br /> <br /> Lastly, what about a Makara? Some huge leviathan the size of the hospital or the factory itself. How does that thing stalk the hospital's corridors or the rickety machinery of the factory? In addition to it's size, the massive whale-like creature needs an ocean to swim in.<br /> <br /> So, my ultimate question is this. How do I reconcile a Horror that doesn't seem to suit the area a Chamber is in with the Chamber itself? Does it actually have to be connected thematically to the real-world location? If not, how much can I alter it?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this is too long winded. I didn't want to create another thread to busy the forum. I'm also sorry that this is so long-winded. I feel like the core question is simple, but maybe I went overboard, here.<br /> <br /> Any help would be much appreciated, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Dream Logic. Space is a lie we tell ourselves, the giant is more terrifying because he <i>can't</i> fit in here and yet he <i>does</i>.<br /> <br /> (Also Lair Traits infect chambers, so going with a Makara whom say, has the trait for dimly lit and flooded, so long as that hospital is dimly lit while you claim the place, Flooding gives you oceans to swim in.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T15:36:39-07:00","id":1249021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249013#post1249013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dream Logic. Space is a lie we tell ourselves, the giant is more terrifying because he <i>can't</i> fit in here and yet he <i>does</i>.<br /> <br /> (Also Lair Traits infect chambers, so going with a Makara whom say, has the trait for dimly lit and flooded, so long as that hospital is dimly lit while you claim the place, Flooding gives you oceans to swim in.)</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I don't think that's a very satisfying answer in this case. For the giant, it'd definitely work, but for the leviathan, a new problem is caused.<br /> <br /> For example, saying that the size of the Horror depends on the location makes a huge difference when the size of the monster is supposed to be part of what's so frightening about it. The leviathan being small enough to fit changes part of what makes it scary.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, saying, &quot;Yes, the monster is the size of the hospital and yes, it's inside the hospital with you.&quot; Is all fine and good dream-logic-wise, but while a bit of that logic can help reinforce the strange reality of a situation (a door on one side of a bent hallway opening to the start of said hallway for an endless room), if you set up a situation that can't even be realistically imagined (what does the leviathan occupying a space far too small for it to fit in even look like), then it doesn't really help describe what's going on.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously, it works better for the giant. Realistically, even if it stooped, it wouldn't fit into a twelve foot tall corridor, but when that thing's chasing you, you're not super worried about the approximation that is the four or so feet in size that'd make a difference. It's not the same for the building-sized leviathan, the house-sized dragon or the truck-sized eagle (especially when that last one predicates it's fear on the target being exposed, not in small, maze-like hallways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24563-op3999","name":"Op3999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T15:57:55-07:00","id":1249026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Op3999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249021#post1249021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I don't think that's a very satisfying answer in this case. For the giant, it'd definitely work, but for the leviathan, a new problem is caused.<br /> <br /> For example, saying that the size of the Horror depends on the location makes a huge difference when the size of the monster is supposed to be part of what's so frightening about it. The leviathan being small enough to fit changes part of what makes it scary.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, saying, &quot;Yes, the monster is the size of the hospital and yes, it's inside the hospital with you.&quot; Is all fine and good dream-logic-wise, but while a bit of that logic can help reinforce the strange reality of a situation (a door on one side of a bent hallway opening to the start of said hallway for an endless room), if you set up a situation that can't even be realistically imagined (what does the leviathan occupying a space far too small for it to fit in even look like), then it doesn't really help describe what's going on.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously, it works better for the giant. Realistically, even if it stooped, it wouldn't fit into a twelve foot tall corridor, but when that thing's chasing you, you're not super worried about the approximation that is the four or so feet in size that'd make a difference. It's not the same for the building-sized leviathan, the house-sized dragon or the truck-sized eagle (especially when that last one predicates it's fear on the target being exposed, not in small, maze-like hallways).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this runs into the problem of expecting a storyteller to convey too much in play. You present the contradiction and let the players brain spasm as it tries to reconcile it.<br /> <br /> There's an infinite ocean in the tiny closet, and a thing of serrated mountains and colossal spines appraises you hungrily on you between your hung shirts. Do you hold your breath or not? You're not drowning, but ya ain't breathing either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T16:47:29-07:00","id":1249032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249026#post1249026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this runs into the problem of expecting a storyteller to convey too much in play. You present the contradiction and let the players brain spasm as it tries to reconcile it.<br /> <br /> There's an infinite ocean in the tiny closet, and a thing of serrated mountains and colossal spines appraises you hungrily on you between your hung shirts. Do you hold your breath or not? You're not drowning, but ya ain't breathing either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good to make the players' brains spasm as they try to reconcile the contradiction, but expecting the storyteller to describe it is asking too much?<br /> <br /> I don't get that, sorry. Creative descriptions are good, but when you're throwing something at the players that can hardly be imagined, if at all, that's something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24563-op3999","name":"Op3999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T17:28:01-07:00","id":1249039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Op3999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249032#post1249032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's good to make the players' brains spasm as they try to reconcile the contradiction, but expecting the storyteller to describe it is asking too much?<br /> <br /> I don't get that, sorry. Creative descriptions are good, but when you're throwing something at the players that can hardly be imagined, if at all, that's something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just described it. I even went more absurd than the original suggestion. It's not any harder than &quot;the midget towers over you&quot; or &quot;infinite ocean.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are in a tiny closet that is also an infinite ocean. It's easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T17:39:00-07:00","id":1249040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249039#post1249039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just described it. I even went more absurd than the original suggestion. It's not any harder than &quot;the midget towers over you&quot; or &quot;infinite ocean.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are in a tiny closet that is also an infinite ocean. It's easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to start a fight here, it just doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Making a tiny closet in the hospital and making that lead to the ocean does not make the hospital a suitable hunting ground for a leviathan. You just created a non-hospital section of it where the leviathan can be and if you do that, what's the point of maintaining the hospital in the first place? Why not have that Chamber be disconnected from the real-world location and a flooded basement leads to some open ocean Chamber or something? Maybe you start with the Dimly Lit trait and from then on, the basement is always &quot;mysteriously flooded&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24563-op3999","name":"Op3999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T18:43:17-07:00","id":1249043,"title":"","content":"If you want something a bit easier on the imagination, the hospital is underwater and the leviathan is outside, always peering through the windows with its enormous eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T20:49:49-07:00","id":1249050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Op3999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249009#post1249009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, what about a Makara? Some huge leviathan the size of the hospital or the factory itself. How does that thing stalk the hospital's corridors or the rickety machinery of the factory? In addition to it's size, the massive whale-like creature needs an ocean to swim in.</div> </div> </div> </div>You want the straightforward answer to this?<br /> <br /> It's Size 5, m<i>aybe</i> Size 10 if you squint and the customization's been funneled just so. It can fit in a building.<br /> <br /> Creatures that pull double duty as scenery are the demesne of greater Dreamborn sharing real estate with the Mother's Land proper. Being rooted in the human experience means Horrors make full use of their mastery of the environment that they are a part of instead of relying on being an ecosystem in themselves.<br /> <br /> It is necessary to rein in the scope of your imagination if you aren't prepared to make the requisite allowances for it to still make sense - a Chamber is a suitable location for its resident Horror to hunt within, and a Horror is a suitable creature to stalk the dreams of humanity. You're playing sea serpents, not Bahamut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T08:28:41-07:00","id":1249144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249050#post1249050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creatures that pull double duty as scenery are the demesne of greater Dreamborn sharing real estate with the Mother's Land proper. Being rooted in the human experience means Horrors make full use of their mastery of the environment that they are a part of instead of relying on being an ecosystem in themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dreamborn and Mother's Land? I've been reviewing my book trying to find answers, but those terms aren't super familiar to me. Could you give me some page numbers?<br /> <br /> But also, if there's one thing that's hammered home about the Makara, it's their general size. I mean, one of the phrases used in the Looming Presence Atavism (an Anakim Atavism, but it is also meant to help simulate the size of giant Makara) is &quot;the square-cube law be damned.&quot; Maybe it's just poor word choice on the part of the writers, but that law allows for real creatures like the Blue Whale, the biggest animal to have ever lived. Granted, that Atavism doesn't change the actual size of the Beast, it is implied that it's the Horror's size that inspires the use of the Atavism and if it's more indicative of the actual Horror, then size 10 is not unreasonable to achieve, even more when Lair dots are increased over 5 or if the Beast took size increasing Merits to start with.<br /> <br /> Plus, that &quot;effective&quot; size increase affects real health dots and with satiety expenditure, speed as well. It doesn't seem that mutable by Dream Logic if it's reinforced in such a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24563-op3999","name":"Op3999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T11:27:34-07:00","id":1249181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Op3999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249144#post1249144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreamborn and Mother's Land? I've been reviewing my book trying to find answers, but those terms aren't super familiar to me. Could you give me some page numbers?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dreamborn&quot; is Beast's name for what Mage calls &quot;goetia&quot; \u2014 natives of the Astral Realms. The Mother's Land is Beast's name for what Mage calls the Anima Mundi \u2014 the soul of the wider world, which the collective human soul is divided from/connected to by an edifice of stone and fog and language that exists in the depths of the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> The Mother's Land is where you find the souls of deserts and forests and oceans, and also where the Dreamborn that claim an empty Chamber to become Horrors come from. Things there feel more real than anywhere else, and its residents often possess a goodly measure of actual influence over the physical world. The thing is, the protean fear-goetia that take shape as they pass through human legend and language are Rank 2 \u2014 roughly equivalent to the average sentient ghost, conversational spirit, or low-level angel.<br /> <br /> They develop their starting Atavisms and their first dot of Lair as the seed of starting characters' magical aspects in a place where size is often correlated with power and significance, and \u2014 despite theories to the contrary \u2014 generally die with their human halves unless they are freed by Inheritance. Most Horrors' size is &quot;just&quot; a function of their fearsomeness, particularly at the lower end of the scale; being Actually Bigger comes at the opportunity cost of being stronger, defter, or more resilient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it's just poor word choice on the part of the writers, but that law allows for real creatures like the Blue Whale, the biggest animal to have ever lived. </div> </div> </div>It is an incredible stretch to go from &quot;as semi-imaginary creatures giant Horrors don't have to worry about the material/biological constraints of a massive form&quot; to &quot;a thing whose powers include 'scary because it's big' can conceivably have actual trouble moving through a place that is part of it and responds to its needs,&quot; particularly when &quot;orders of magnitude bigger than a human&quot; does not actually contradict &quot;can fit into a building that they're allowed to damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, that &quot;effective&quot; size increase affects real health dots and with satiety expenditure, speed as well. It doesn't seem that mutable by Dream Logic if it's reinforced in such a way. </div> </div> </div>That &quot;effective&quot; Size does not affect Dream Health, is the thing. You're dealing with a psychic construct that draws its power from the soul of the world \u2014 that suggests <i>more</i> viability for nightmare-logic movement options, not less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T11:46:10-07:00","id":1249182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1249181#post1249181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dreamborn&quot; is Beast's name for what Mage calls &quot;goetia&quot; \u2014 natives of the Astral Realms. The Mother's Land is Beast's name for what Mage calls the Anima Mundi \u2014 the soul of the wider world, which the collective human soul is divided from/connected to by an edifice of stone and fog and language that exists in the depths of the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> The Mother's Land is where you find the souls of deserts and forests and oceans, and also where the Dreamborn that claim an empty Chamber to become Horrors come from. Things there feel more real than anywhere else, and its residents often possess a goodly measure of actual influence over the physical world. The thing is, the protean fear-goetia that take shape as they pass through human legend and language are Rank 2 \u2014 roughly equivalent to the average sentient ghost, conversational spirit, or low-level angel.<br /> <br /> They develop their starting Atavisms and their first dot of Lair as the seed of starting characters' magical aspects in a place where size is often correlated with power and significance, and \u2014 despite theories to the contrary \u2014 generally die with their human halves unless they are freed by Inheritance. Most Horrors' size is &quot;just&quot; a function of their fearsomeness, particularly at the lower end of the scale; being Actually Bigger comes at the opportunity cost of being stronger, defter, or more resilient.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are covered in the Beast Players Guide, pp. 155-158.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T12:22:44-07:00","id":1249191,"title":"","content":"As regards the original Hospital question, Ithink there's some confusion about what is happening when.<br /> <br /> If you are simply invoking your Lair Trait of Dimly Lit and then bring in Flooded and what not, then you are still floating around in your flesh bubble and therefore handle things as a physical being, except for where your effective size matters in which case you follow Looming Presence as written(and probably make a mage very upset.)<br /> <br /> If you have a hospital as a Chamber, then a) you can bridge over to your lair at pretty much any place that resonates with the essence the place you nabbed the Chamber, so the more like Creepy Operating Room 3 you are in, the easier it is to bridge in, but more on point, b) when you bridge over reality with a Chamber and you therefore merge with your Horror, you have also merged realtiy with your Chamber, so physical laws are superseded by psychospiritual/dream rules, in which case it doesn't matter that a Blue Whale can't fit into an operating room, You fit in your Chambers and are unimpeded by things like doorframes, so you exist and operate in that hospital normally.<br /> <br /> Now, if a Hospital is not really a prime place for your Hunger-Sating and Legend-Building, then you have a problem-but there's no actual limitation in operating in a hospital as a leviathan. The world bends around you, not the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T13:43:47-07:00","id":1249206,"title":"","content":"Okay, so things seem to be getting hung up on a combination of lore justification and mechanics, here.<br /> <br /> Just discarding the implications of Looming Presence makes no sense. Atavisms are supposed to be representative qualities of the Horror that the Beast can draw on wherever they are. We can't just toss this one away because it's inconvenient. We wouldn't do that with Wings of the Raptor or Dragonfire, would we? Saying that there's some quality that gets added in the translation between Horror and Beast that neither actually have makes no sense at all.<br /> <br /> And here's my problem with Dream Logic. If the Primordial Dream in which the Beasts operate in is based off of the deep, collective mentality of all of humanity, then it still has to be possible for a human to conceive of. If it stretches the imagination too much (for example, if it's asking too much of a Storyteller to describe), then that goes beyond Dream Logic.<br /> <br /> My initial reaction would be to say that the Chamber is influenced first by the Horror's themes and then second by the physical location itself. In this case, that hospital becomes undersea ruins, broken and submerged. That felt too much like providing a homebrew solution to a problem in the book, but now I can see that I'm not the only one to do that. I guess I did find my answer, in a weird way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24563-op3999","name":"Op3999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T13:47:57-07:00","id":1249210,"title":"","content":"I was re-reading family resemblance and i have a doubt, do you think it can recognize undevoured beast and/or heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T00:38:24-07:00","id":1252982,"title":"","content":"I've a question regarding Cyclopean Strength.<br /> <br /> The Satiety Expenditure states: &quot;The Beast gains automatic successes equal to his Lair dots on all Strength related rolls for the remainder of the scene, not just feats of strength.&quot; Considering Unarmed Combat uses Strength + Brawl, and is therefore a Strength related roll, how do the automatic successes interact with the results of the roll?<br /> <br /> Does this make any Unarmed Combat check never miss the target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T00:43:53-07:00","id":1252985,"title":"","content":"I would say yes but the opponent could still dodge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T05:04:43-07:00","id":1253023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1252982#post1252982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've a question regarding Cyclopean Strength.<br /> <br /> The Satiety Expenditure states: &quot;The Beast gains automatic successes equal to his Lair dots on all Strength related rolls for the remainder of the scene, not just feats of strength.&quot; Considering Unarmed Combat uses Strength + Brawl, and is therefore a Strength related roll, how do the automatic successes interact with the results of the roll?<br /> <br /> Does this make any Unarmed Combat check never miss the target?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW:<s>Unambiguously yes</s> (see Satchel's post below)<br /> RAI: Really, really hotly contested.<br /> <br /> It's also weaponry, not just unarmed.<br /> <br /> I allow the successes on combat rolls because that's just not a big deal for me or my table (and we weren't aware of the permutation rules described below).<br /> As Neos mentioned, if it's truly problematic in a specific circumstance, dodging is an option.<br /> For tables that are more concerned about balanced combat, or who read the intent differently, they tend to rule in the other direction.<br /> <br /> I've heard convincing arguments for both approaches, and it's very possible it was not intended to work for combat rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 09-12-2018, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T06:37:31-07:00","id":1253036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1252982#post1252982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Unarmed Combat uses Strength + Brawl, and is therefore a Strength related roll, how do the automatic successes interact with the results of the roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>As the &quot;Extra Successes&quot; Permutation on Page 161.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T01:05:07-07:00","id":1253825,"title":"","content":"Beasts can recognize other potential beasts meeting them in the primordial realm while they are dreaming, but do you think more reliable methods exists (like family resemblance)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T04:31:40-07:00","id":1253840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1253825#post1253825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts can recognize other potential beasts meeting them in the primordial realm while they are dreaming, but do you think more reliable methods exists (like family resemblance)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there's an Obascus Rite for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T05:22:50-07:00","id":1253848,"title":"","content":"True, seek the child rite, thank you \ud83d\udc4d<br /> My only doubt now is if an undevoured beast would register as some kind of psychic to family resemblance, even if he doesn t possess a supernatural merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T01:34:27-07:00","id":1254419,"title":"","content":"In player guide i found this:<br /> &quot;Brushing up against the Primordial Dream alerts these Beasts to their potential brethren, and draws their established brothers and sisters to the newcomer. Dormant Beasts are beacons to those that have already endured their Devouring, es-pecially as their nightmares pull them to the Primordial Dream. &quot;<br /> <br /> But no actual mechanics are given.<br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T01:48:47-07:00","id":1254420,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it's a narrative hook rather than a mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T02:12:22-07:00","id":1254423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254420#post1254420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like it's a narrative hook rather than a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably yes, but i m going to run a devouring for a new player and i need to know if her &quot;mentor&quot; could recognise her potential on sight or if he need to meet her in dreams","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T09:24:44-07:00","id":1254526,"title":"","content":"They can either meet then in the Dream and find out who they are there, or they can use Seek the Child to find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T10:14:35-07:00","id":1254551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254526#post1254526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can either meet then in the Dream and find out who they are there, or they can use Seek the Child to find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately the would be mentor has no access to rites.<br /> In fact until now i believed casual dream meeting the only way for a mentor to find the undevoured.<br /> The strange phrase about the &quot;beacon effect&quot; puzzles me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T12:32:08-07:00","id":1254590,"title":"","content":"Just think of it as a subconscious feeling in the primordial dream, leading beast to that dormant beast ready to go off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T13:00:53-07:00","id":1254600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254590#post1254590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just think of it as a subconscious feeling in the primordial dream, leading beast to that dormant beast ready to go off</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds nice, but do you think that once the beast see her it s &quot;love at first sight&quot; or some more investigation is needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T13:11:10-07:00","id":1254604,"title":"","content":"If by love at first sight you mean &quot;I'm gonna wake that boy up&quot; then I believe so. Beast, to my understanding, want to have a dormant be what they truly are, and will instantly try to have it happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T13:12:32-07:00","id":1254605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254600#post1254600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds nice, but do you think that once the beast see her it s &quot;love at first sight&quot; or some more investigation is needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to go with a mixture of &quot;I saw that person in my dreams and want to know if that actually meant something&quot; and &quot;Something tells me I know him/her from a previous life but they can't recall me yet so I'll stick around until the epiphany happens&quot; tropes.<br /> <br /> The younger Beast is still diving into the Primordial Dream while the Horror is rising to the surface. A mentor's presence mostly facilitates the process and gives explanations that are sorely lacking in a spontaneous Devouring: he is a beacon because, being Family, it grants some guidance just by being there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T14:20:56-07:00","id":1254613,"title":"","content":"Very good, my thoughts are more clear now.<br /> Thanks a lot to everyone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T15:24:22-07:00","id":1254636,"title":"","content":"Do heroes see beast as for what there horrors are? I'm just wondering due to Candy's origins seeing as as his horror form (and seemingly unaware of it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T19:27:15-07:00","id":1254674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254636#post1254636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do heroes see beast as for what there horrors are? I'm just wondering due to Candy's origins seeing as as his horror form (and seemingly unaware of it)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Heroes are included in the supernatural category that means that if a Beast uses an atavism in front of them then they see a sort of phantasmal image of the Horror. That said it has also been a thing in the various fictions of Heroes becoming aware of a Beast gives them a vision of some sort that usually gives them an idea of what the Horror is even if they can't identify the Beast it is part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T19:38:53-07:00","id":1254676,"title":"","content":"But what about the dude candy killed? It says he just saw her walk in, smile and beckoned her over like he was in human form, then get killed by her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T21:59:18-07:00","id":1254689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254676#post1254676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about the dude candy killed? It says he just saw her walk in, smile and beckoned her over like he was in human form, then get killed by her</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was this scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T00:50:18-07:00","id":1254705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1254676#post1254676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about the dude candy killed? It says he just saw her walk in, smile and beckoned her over like he was in human form, then get killed by her</div> </div> </div> </div>An exeptional success on heroic stalking roll give heroes the ability to identify a beast on sight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T06:50:33-07:00","id":1254760,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> it's page 23 for night horrors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T10:55:58-07:00","id":1257997,"title":"","content":"Run today first Beast session. We had simple question on this - How many times each Beast can use Nightmare or Atavisms each scene? Because if you not spent Satiety, theoretically, you could spam the same 'You Must Obey' on each target as long as you can, if scene is circle 1 hour of game time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T14:26:53-07:00","id":1258034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1257997#post1257997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Run today first Beast session. We had simple question on this - How many times each Beast can use Nightmare or Atavisms each scene? Because if you not spent Satiety, theoretically, you could spam the same 'You Must Obey' on each target as long as you can, if scene is circle 1 hour of game time...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well scenes are variable in length so the 1 hour of game time thing isn't really a good metric to use. As for how many times you can use an atavism or nightmare, there's not really a limit on them as written. Atavisms are technically just letting your Horror bleed out into the material world a bit ie rending claws isn't creating claws its just letting the claws out and slashing stuff with them.<br /> Nightmares also lack a limit to number of uses in a scene, however, you do have to manage eye contact with the victim before you can make them deal with the check to see if it takes hold. I would also say that your ST is free to start making it more difficult to get that eye contact once its known that you need it (someone sees you lock eyes with their allies and each ally starts following orders the beast's orders after the eye contact is not necessarily a subtle thing.) Not counting other potential restrictions like just not allowing a person to continually spam the nightmare until the target fails, or as soon as the person breaks out of the nightmare, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T22:10:03-07:00","id":1258107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258034#post1258034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well scenes are variable in length so the 1 hour of game time thing isn't really a good metric to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scene being up up to 1 hour time in <b>CoD </b>games is official rule in gamelines. Of course, scene can end before from story logic stand-point, but for use of powers '1 scene = up to 1 hour' is handy shorting, <i>especially</i> for <b>Mage </b>games. It is both in 1E and 2E <b>Mage. </b>Other 2E corebooks copy-paste scene complicated definition from ( 2E ) <b>CoD Rulebook</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Equation of '1 scene = up to 1 hour' is, for example, on <b>Mage</b> 1E, page 119, on <i>Prolonged spells </i>section and on <b>Mage</b> 2E, page 113 of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T22:25:17-07:00","id":1258110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258034#post1258034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for how many times you can use an atavism or nightmare, there's not really a limit on them as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Nightmare there is some limit putted but I question is it really a limit of usage on it. Here is rule quote I'm refering to, on Success part of <i>Invoking Nightmares</i> section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP, page 134</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Success: The Nightmare takes effect either immediately or when the victim next sleeps, as the Beast desires. If the victim is subject to multiple \u201cdormant\u201d Nightmares, he suffers one Nightmare each time he sleeps, in order of when the Nightmares were applied.<br /> <br /> <b>An individual can only be subject to one active Nightmare at a time. If the Beast invokes a second Nightmare on the same target, the new Nightmare supersedes the old one. </b>If a different Beast does so, the attempt triggers a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my reading, it should limit the things like 'You Must Obey' as only one usage per one target in the same scene. However, if Nightmare were simple Failure player can retake activation, paying next Willpower point with cumulative -1 penalty, as always. But once Nightmare is in effect, it's only one usage per scene of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258034#post1258034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">however, you do have to manage eye contact with the victim before you can make them deal with the check to see if it takes hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <b>BtP</b> corebook points you can use Nightmares on touch only and that <i>the victim</i> needs only to see you, not even yourself. ( <i>Eye Contac</i>t sidebar )<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP, page 133</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmares require a Beast to make eye contact with her victims in order to invoke their effects. That contact is one-way \u2014 the victim needs to see the Beast\u2019s eyes, but not vice versa. This contact is possible through simple barriers like sunglasses (even mirrored) or tinted windows, but does not work when looking at a video feed rather than the Beast herself. Nightmares work on touch, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T22:50:47-07:00","id":1258114,"title":"","content":"I got also question of Feeding of Beasts - As I understand rules on page 108, Beast declarers his feeding action. Then ST judges if it should start from 1-3 Satiety Potential dices, based on action general liknes for Horror's Hunger. Then ST assign bonus/penalties dices to Satiety Potential dicepool. <b>And <i>only</i> when Satiety Potential is <i>greater</i> than now Satiety level of Beast, players roll it, yes?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T22:52:27-07:00","id":1258115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258107#post1258107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is both in 1E and 2E <b>Mage. </b>Other 2E corebooks copy-paste scene complicated definition from ( 2E ) <b>CoD Rulebook</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like most gamelines don't deal with powers whose timescales are granular enough that &quot;this lasts until this event has played out&quot; is sufficient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1257997#post1257997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you not spent Satiety, theoretically, you could spam the same 'You Must Obey' on each target as long as you can, if scene is circle 1 hour of game time...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258110#post1258110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if Nightmare were simple Failure player can retake activation, paying next Willpower point with cumulative -1 penalty, as always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the fact that the Successive Attempts rule doesn't cost Willpower, this and the loss of a turn that failure imposes are essentially all the limiting factors necessary for a two-trait roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T22:54:29-07:00","id":1258117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258114#post1258114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got also question of Feeding of Beasts - As I understand rules on page 108, Beast declarers his feeding action. Then ST judges if it should start from 1-3 Satiety Potential dices, based on action general liknes for Horror's Hunger. Then ST assign bonus/penalties dices to Satiety Potential dicepool. <b>And <i>only</i> when Satiety Potential is <i>greater</i> than now Satiety level of Beast, players roll it, yes?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Base Satiety Potential runs the range from one to five dice, but yes, that's how the mechanic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T23:38:33-07:00","id":1258124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258110#post1258110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <b>BtP</b> corebook points you can use Nightmares on touch only and that <i>the victim</i> needs only to see you, not even yourself. ( <i>Eye Contac</i>t sidebar )</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the sidebar again, the victim needs to see your eyes, if they're looking at your shoes its not working. Touch is a bit of a tricky one since the Fist of Nightmare merit is a thing that exists and the purpose of that merit is to allow one to store a nightmare to inflict on a person via touch. Either way this doesn't really stop the ST from imposing restrictions if you start going with the idea of &quot;Well the nightmare lasts a scene and the core gives a scene's length as about an hour, so every 59 minutes I start spamming You Must Obey on my target to ensure I maintain control for another hour.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T08:14:27-07:00","id":1258391,"title":"","content":"Hi! I have this very simple question, but I couldn't find a definitive answer in the core book. Does a Nightmare always affects a single target, or it can affect everyone who makes eye contact with the Beast?<br /> <br /> P.S.: Context: a Beast PC tried to scare a whole mob with the 'Run Away' Nightmare, and his player argued that he could affect everyone in the mob as long as they made eye contact with his character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":".  Example 10-01-2018, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T09:39:04-07:00","id":1258404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258391#post1258391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! I have this very simple question, but I couldn't find a definitive answer in the core book. Does a Nightmare always affects a single target, or it can affect everyone who makes eye contact with the Beast?<br /> <br /> P.S.: Context: a Beast PC tried to scare a whole mob with the 'Run Away' Nightmare, and his player argued that he could affect everyone in the mob as long as they made eye contact with his character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmares affect a single target. There is a specific meta-Nightmare, &quot;Fear is Contagious,&quot; for affecting multiple targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T15:31:12-07:00","id":1258436,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> I have read the atavism Vengeful earth (player guide pag 88) and i don t understand what is the duration of the satiety expenditure effect.<br /> One scene, one turn or until the beast dismiss it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T16:36:13-07:00","id":1258443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258436#post1258436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi,<br /> I have read the atavism Vengeful earth (player guide pag 88) and i don t understand what is the duration of the satiety expenditure effect.<br /> One scene, one turn or until the beast dismiss it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not explicit, but at a cursory glance, a scene seems reasonable. I could see arguments for less, but not more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T19:10:11-07:00","id":1258466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258404#post1258404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmares affect a single target. There is a specific meta-Nightmare, &amp;quot;Fear is Contagious,&amp;quot; for affecting multiple targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That's exactly what I was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T18:56:50-07:00","id":1258639,"title":"","content":"Depending on the context of the scene he might be able to use it on multiple enemies in succession (one per turn), although somebody screaming and running away is probably enough of a distraction for the rest to break eye contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T19:16:53-07:00","id":1258646,"title":"","content":"Does Hunger Management modify Satiety Potential directly (thus keeping the cap of 10 dice rolled, and allowing it to qualify you for meals at higher satiety levels than you normally would)?<br /> <br /> Or does it add a bonus to the pool when you roll (thus allowing a max of 13 dice to be rolled, but meaning that it wouldn't qualify you to feed on a meal with a potential lower than your Satiety)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T20:15:36-07:00","id":1258658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258646#post1258646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Hunger Management modify Satiety Potential directly (thus keeping the cap of 10 dice rolled, and allowing it to qualify you for meals at higher satiety levels than you normally would)?<br /> <br /> Or does it add a bonus to the pool when you roll (thus allowing a max of 13 dice to be rolled, but meaning that it wouldn't qualify you to feed on a meal with a potential lower than your Satiety)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter seems to fit the wording of the Merit better, with the caveat that I'm pretty sure &quot;under no circumstances&quot; still means what it means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T17:16:28-07:00","id":1258972,"title":"","content":"Probably stupid question, and I swear I've seen the topic come up before but I can't find it after several pages of searching:<br /> Can Beasts benefit from Family Dinner when helping other Beasts (eg Broodmates) Feed? I had it in my head that it was only for other supernaturals, but I'm not so sure lately...<br /> <br /> It'd be a good way to avoid excessive feeding scenes with a large Brood without handwaving them, if it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T22:53:41-07:00","id":1259016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258972#post1258972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably stupid question, and I swear I've seen the topic come up before but I can't find it after several pages of searching:<br /> Can Beasts benefit from Family Dinner when helping other Beasts (eg Broodmates) Feed? I had it in my head that it was only for other supernaturals, but I'm not so sure lately...<br /> <br /> It'd be a good way to avoid excessive feeding scenes with a large Brood without handwaving them, if it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>If i remember it correctly the kinship abilities works only on other supernatural","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T22:56:44-07:00","id":1259018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1258972#post1258972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Beasts benefit from Family Dinner when helping other Beasts (eg Broodmates) Feed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to treat it as such, given the thrust of the &quot;Are you a social predator?&quot; Satiety question on page 80 of the corebook, but that same page highlights Family Dinner from other kin as an additional source of food.<br /> <br /> Beasts can't have Family Ties with other Beasts, so there's already a reduced impact compared to accompanying &quot;cousins&quot; without having to outright declare a Beast whose only supernatural contacts are Begotten to be out of luck re: metaphysically simpler hunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T09:50:21-07:00","id":1259246,"title":"","content":"I agree with Satchel's interpretation here. Family Dinner would be pointless in a Beasts-only game otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T12:26:58-07:00","id":1260004,"title":"","content":"Do y'all recommend the primordial feast anthology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":