I haven't read anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T08:49:11-07:00","id":1260678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1260656#post1260656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading Thousand Years of Night apparently Beasts reincarnate? How does that work I don't remember anything like that in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some implications, ideas and in-character perspectives that talk about what happens to a dead Beast and a Horror that survives her. Enough to speculate on the implications of mythic cycles and if there's a connection between all those who inherit the same Horror.<br /> <br /> It pretty much depends on you, but the option is there. Personally, I go for &quot;some do, some don't and other immortals who recognize your Horror might think you're an ancient Beast reborn or just hold you accountable for what your ancestors did (whether they're right or not is not a question with only an answer)&quot;<br /> <br /> Sorry about the rushed, &quot;it's your call&quot; reply, but I'm outside and writing on a stupid phone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T12:29:26-07:00","id":1260732,"title":"","content":"Adding on, the BPG includes an epic-level Obcasus Rite to bind a Horror with a new human host after the original Beast has undergone the Retreat or the Merger, resulting in a new Beast with the same Horror as the old (and occasionally &quot;dreams, intuitions, and occasional recollections of the life of&quot; the prior Beast).<br /> <br /> Pages 234-235 of the corebook, when discussing the Retreat, also notes that &quot;death is not necessarily the end. It may be <i>an </i>end, but the Horror is not so easily set aside. It can persist, living on in the Primordial Dream.&quot;<br /> <br /> So TYoN didn't pull this out of nowhere, but it's not framed as something that's particularly common or likely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T15:03:47-08:00","id":1267426,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's explicitly explained how the thicker than water social ability works lore wise? is it basically a supernatural aura Beast have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T16:10:44-08:00","id":1267438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1267426#post1267426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's explicitly explained how the thicker than water social ability works lore wise? is it basically a supernatural aura Beast have?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're metaphysically descended from the <i>universal idea of fear.</i> There's a kind of baseline like-attracts-like affinity at play between them and other monsters in a setting where witnessing the supernatural causes most humans to recoil in their souls. A better analogue would be how in 2e a vampire's Beast imparts upon them a sort of intrinsic understanding of how to place themselves to avoid being clearly reflected in mirrors or captured in media. The Begotten get on the same wavelength as other monsters in the absence of complicating social factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T17:05:56-08:00","id":1267453,"title":"","content":"ahh I understand, thanks Satchel!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:17:51-08:00","id":1269049,"title":"","content":"in the beast players guide, it mentions that some talassi believe that their ancient anathema can be broken through reaching incarnation, yet then states that many talassi seeking Incarnate actually play up to their anathema. is there something in missing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:59:24-08:00","id":1269091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1269049#post1269049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the beast players guide, it mentions that some talassi believe that their ancient anathema can be broken through reaching incarnation, yet then states that many talassi seeking Incarnate actually play up to their anathema. is there something in missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire bit between those sentences, for starters. There is not a contradiction in &quot;Really stubborn Talassi looking to break off the Anathema of their Family pursue Incarnation, but every failure sets them all that much further back; a lot of Incarnate Captors actually get there by leaning into the twist instead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T21:07:53-08:00","id":1269097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1269049#post1269049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the beast players guide, it mentions that some talassi believe that their ancient anathema can be broken through reaching incarnation, yet then states that many talassi seeking Incarnate actually play up to their anathema. is there something in missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Incarnate is hardly an easy state to reach, so a lot of Beasts will leverage whatever advantage they've got in getting them there. Not unreasonable that many a Talassi who seeks Incarnation would play up the aura that the Family Anathema gives them. Plus you'd also be dealing with Talassi who don't think it would work for one reason or another, remember the hypothesis isn't even that an Incarnate Talassi would be able to free itself just that if a sufficient number of Talassi &quot;flipped the script&quot; then the Anathema would break. There's no evidence to suggest it would work, just a hypothesis, so you can't really blame some Talassi for not believing it would work and falling back on a useful tool. This is also not counting Talassi who don't give a crap about getting rid of the thing and thus wouldn't really be going out of their way to help with the project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:17:21-08:00","id":1269239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1269097#post1269097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Incarnate is hardly an easy state to reach, so a lot of Beasts will leverage whatever advantage they've got in getting them there. Not unreasonable that many a Talassi who seeks Incarnation would play up the aura that the Family Anathema gives them. Plus you'd also be dealing with Talassi who don't think it would work for one reason or another, remember the hypothesis isn't even that an Incarnate Talassi would be able to free itself just that if a sufficient number of Talassi &amp;quot;flipped the script&amp;quot; then the Anathema would break. There's no evidence to suggest it would work, just a hypothesis, so you can't really blame some Talassi for not believing it would work and falling back on a useful tool. This is also not counting Talassi who don't give a crap about getting rid of the thing and thus wouldn't really be going out of their way to help with the project.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true I suppose, it does state it's merely a theory afterall<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, the in between part is about the other inheritances, I don't see what it has to do with the incarnate theory some Talassi Beast have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:32:37-08:00","id":1269246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1269239#post1269239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, the in between part is about the other inheritances, I don't see what it has to do with the incarnate theory some Talassi Beast have</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Such a destiny is more easily spoken or imagined than actually achieved, but that never stops a Captor from trying. However, every failure sets the Family that much further back. To further compound the issue, the frustration the Talassii curse causes feeds into itself all too easily.&quot;<br /> <br /> The entire Inheritance section proceeding from that theory is an extended look at <i>how thoroughly that Anathema has wormed its way into the Family's mythical makeup</i>. They are not separate observations just because they are looking at different physical outcomes. The lesser Inheritances speak to despairing of ever reversing the curse and Incarnation talks about taking hold of it and incorporating it into their part of the psychic landscape, both of which address &quot;there are Captors who think Incarnation could hold the means to put the Family's legend back on the rails, but they sure have their work cut out for them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T12:34:03-08:00","id":1270662,"title":"","content":"Maybe somebody already asked this, but do you think the Atavism Titanic blow bypass Durability AND also Armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T00:06:29-08:00","id":1271059,"title":"","content":"So, let's say a beast meditates and exits it's lair into the temenos. In what for does he leave his lair? human or horror? furthermore, does his body stay in the physical world? does he really die or just suffers 0 willpower? What if he opens a burrow from temenos into underworld. does his body come through? doe she manifest as a spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T01:20:17-08:00","id":1271395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1271059#post1271059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say a beast meditates and exits it's lair into the temenos. In what for does he leave his lair? human or horror? furthermore, does his body stay in the physical world? does he really die or just suffers 0 willpower? What if he opens a burrow from temenos into underworld. does his body come through? doe she manifest as a spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I m not sure but my opinion is: <br /> The Beast body in the Lair remain fused with the Horror, her mind navigate the primordial dream and Temenos in dream form.<br /> If she wants to open a pathway to the underworld she must first return to the lair (and her body) and travel physically.<br /> If she find another kind of portal to the undereorld she would stay in dream form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T08:04:34-08:00","id":1271449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1271059#post1271059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say a beast meditates and exits it's lair into the temenos.In what for does he leave his lair? human or horror? furthermore, does his body stay in the physical world? does he really die or just suffers 0 willpower? What if he opens a burrow from temenos into underworld. does his body come through? doe she manifest as a spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to answer point by point, but they're all dependent on other answers so it's difficult to do.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how the Beast enters their Lair. If only in Dream Form (implied by them meditating, though I'm not sure that's something Beasts can do innately) then the body remains wherever it's left regardless of what you do with your Dream Form. When the Dream Form dies, you get Soul Shocked. (It can cause a drop to 0 WP, but no one automatically loses all their WP due to dying in their Dream Form.)<br /> Once the Beast leaves the Lair the Horror remains behind. The Horror never leaves the Lair and cannot be forced to leave it except through certain Inheritances or when it (without being merged) hunts because it's hungry.<br /> <br /> If you bodily enter the Lair you just bring your body with you wherever you go. The downside being that you die when killed.<br /> <br /> Edit: The only thing I'm not sure of is whether you can leave the Astral while in your Dream Form. Without a power that maintains a mental projection into non-dream realms you might not be able to enter them. Not sure whether you're just not capable of going through portals or if you simply just wake up instead (possibly with Soul-Shocked if your projection is destroyed in the process).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-28-2018, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:31:16-08:00","id":1271632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1271449#post1271449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you bodily enter the Lair you just bring your body with you wherever you go. The downside being that you die when killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading, given the aforementioned &quot;the Horror won't leave the Lair&quot; rule, the Dark Dream's abnormal relation to physicality, the necessity of bodily entering the Lair to be meaningfully there as a character instead of steering your Horror, and the fact that the rules for the Mother's Land still reference Dream Health specifically, is that if you leave the Lair for elsewhere in the Astral by physically exiting your Chambers, you exist as a Dream Form with Attributes calculated like a mortal's while your Lair holds down the burden of being your material checkpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T04:33:24-08:00","id":1271738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1271632#post1271632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading, given the aforementioned &quot;the Horror won't leave the Lair&quot; rule, the Dark Dream's abnormal relation to physicality, the necessity of bodily entering the Lair to be meaningfully there as a character instead of steering your Horror, and the fact that the rules for the Mother's Land still reference Dream Health specifically, is that if you leave the Lair for elsewhere in the Astral by physically exiting your Chambers, you exist as a Dream Form with Attributes calculated like a mortal's while your Lair holds down the burden of being your material checkpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the BPG. Good catch. Reading further it's also restated in the BPG that travellers whose Dream Form is destroyed wake up where they first took on the Dream Form, which would be the moment they unmerged from the Horror.<br /> It's honestly quite weird how it works with no mentions of whether they simply don't have a body during such travels or if it's still merged (without the Beast's mind) with the Horror. It also departs from how absolutely anyone else (including unmerged Beasts travelling through another Beast's Lair) would logically be bodily present in the Astral if bodily transported to a Lair and then taking a non-Primordial Pathway way out of the Lair.<br /> It's also weird how it's specified that the above rule only applies to exiting the Lair without taking Primordial Pathways, strongly implying that taking a Primordial Pathway to another part of the Astral would unmerge you and let you bodily enter instead of using your Dream Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T09:06:02-08:00","id":1273270,"title":"","content":"Has anyone here utilized the Vancouver setting for a game of Beast? I find it very intriguing, and would be curious to know how it went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T12:39:42-08:00","id":1273928,"title":"","content":"I tried to run a search for this but couldn't find what I was looking for<br /> <br /> When making a Hero, do I use a normal Mortal sheet, or is there a sheet for Heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24762-argeniat","name":"Argeniat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T13:36:38-08:00","id":1273942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argeniat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1273928#post1273928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to run a search for this but couldn't find what I was looking for<br /> <br /> When making a Hero, do I use a normal Mortal sheet, or is there a sheet for Heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just mortal, I think. They don't have stats like Lair, and only a few Gifts and inherent abilities to keep track of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T16:08:27-08:00","id":1273965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argeniat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1273928#post1273928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to run a search for this but couldn't find what I was looking for<br /> <br /> When making a Hero, do I use a normal Mortal sheet, or is there a sheet for Heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldl use a mortal sheet, but with legend and life instead of virtue and vice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T17:59:34-08:00","id":1274811,"title":"","content":"Not answering a question, but a handy reminder that Heroes are orthogonal to the way of things for Beasts. You want a bigger fish, go Insatiable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T07:29:27-08:00","id":1274884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1274811#post1274811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not answering a question, but a handy reminder that Heroes are orthogonal to the way of things for Beasts. You want a bigger fish, go Insatiable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you mean by orthogonal in this context? The dictionary definition I found seems like it's related metaphorically, but I can't parse the metaphor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T10:51:57-08:00","id":1274907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1274884#post1274884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by orthogonal in this context? The dictionary definition I found seems like it's related metaphorically, but I can't parse the metaphor</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Arcane, but I suspect he means that the two are mutually exclusive from each other...<br /> <br /> ...and if I'm wrong, I'll let him explain. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T12:43:08-08:00","id":1274935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1274884#post1274884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What do you mean by orthogonal in this context? The dictionary definition I found seems like it's related metaphorically, but I can't parse the metaphor</div> </div> </div> </div>To break that down, we need to understand the main framework at which Heroes are at right angles to Beasts as-namely, in a food web.<br /> <br /> In a conventional food web, with chains more or less running from the base provider to the top tier predators, you expect most of your problems to be from the predator class above you. Sure, you do have to worry about the adept defenders of the prey, they can mess you up, but as it goes, most of your sense of threat comes from above your head.<br /> <br /> Applying that to Beast, you may have to worry about humanity's defenders in the form hunters giving you trouble, but for the most part, your 'bigger fish' are other Beasts, supernaturals with more oomph than you, Horrors, Dreamborn, and Royal Avatars bigger than you, etc. etc. all the way up to the Dark Mother. Beast's ecology, while odd, mostly makes clear sense that way. (For the record, this gonna mean I actually rescind the Insatiable comment-they also have an orthogonal relationship to Beasts) You want to fight a monster, you bring in a bigger monsters.<br /> <br /> Heroes are not bigger fish. In fact, they have a fuzzy relationship to concepts of predator, prey, scavenger, etc. on the whole. On the one hand, they seem like they fall under that adept protector class of prey, except that their mindsets and metaphysical toolset skew highly predatorial-but they also aren't so well equipped to stand clearly as the ones who feast on Beasts. THey straddle this odd line between the two.<br /> <br /> This is the groundwork of some of their horror, because every logical sense that they should either calm the fuck down back down into protector sort of role or continue to ramp up until they become some kind of bigger fish over Beasts, with this middling approach seemingly working against them*, setting them up to get knocked down as they lack both herd advantage and greater predatorial advantage against monsters who know how to exploit that to high hell...except <i>it works</i>. It works so well that our history is littered with their tales.( Granted, Beast nature lets Heroic victory stand out more than Primoridal victory.)<br /> <br /> Ecologically, Heroes make no sense, and they seem like they should be punished by the basic rules of predacity-but there's this strange fatalistic force behind them that seems to ensure their victory against the odds, this writing on the wall of the cave defying the teeth, the claws, the sheer girth, the wings and fire of the Beast. Sure, Heroes have advantages, even specialized ones to help take Beasts down, but that should still lead to about an even win-loss rate. Beasts and Heroes can fight with the same degree of dirty tactics and vicious escalation, and a Beast theoretically always has a larger toolset to do so with, but for all of that, Heroes seem to win a whole lot more than they should.<br /> <br /> The horror of Heroes is not, nor should it be, that they are the bigger fish. Their horror is rooted in that they seem to win a whole lot, <i>and no one really gets why because the big picture doesn't make sense that way</i>. The most obvious alternative is, well.<br /> <br /> Fate and fatalism.<br /> <br /> *Normally this would be the point where I elucidate how humans are kind of top tier terminator-predator type, but in this case we run into Cornelius's Lament on an ecological level, namely Beasts are &quot;humans&quot; too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-14-2022, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T08:22:20-08:00","id":1278072,"title":"","content":"Strange but interesting question:<br /> It s possibile (theorically) to put the family ties comdition on Heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T08:53:19-08:00","id":1278082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1278072#post1278072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange but interesting question:<br /> It s possibile (theorically) to put the family ties comdition on Heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, no. They don't tap into the emotional tapestry of other supernaturals. Where all other monsters either prey on mankind or cause one of more fears that make them resonant to the Idea of Fear and thus, astrally speaking, all children of the Dark Mother, Heroes are more of a reaction to that, one which embodies different emotions and hopes.<br /> <br /> <i>That said:</i><br /> <br /> It's the kind of plot that can happen. The good old &quot;No unless it makes for a good story&quot;. Heroes can get scary, after all, and their ties to Beast offer all the chances to subvert the Monomyth that way. Might work only with a certain Hero who has developed a special relationship with a Begotten (and that would still be huge) or be the beginning of a giant change in the way the Primordial Dream works, but I'd say it's worth leaving the option open.<br /> <br /> Getting more personal, I've had it happen in one of my games. The players liked that Hero, they all learned to coexist and eventually managed to obtain the Dark Mother's wary yet intrigued blessing. She kinda went &quot;you know, you're both empowered by myths and dreams and care for each other. Have fun&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-02-2019, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:09:53-08:00","id":1278086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1278082#post1278082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, no. They don't tap into the emotional tapestry of other supernaturals. Where all other monsters either prey on mankind or cause one of more fears that make them resonant to the Idea of Fear and thus, astrally speaking, all children of the Dark Mother, Heroes are more of a reaction to that, one which embodies different emotions and hopes.<br /> <br /> <i>That said:</i><br /> <br /> It's the kind of plot that can happen. The good old &amp;quot;No unless it makes for a good story&amp;quot;. Heroes can get scary, after all, and their ties to Beast offer all the chances to subvert the Monomyth that way. Might work only with a certain Hero who has developed a special relationship with a Begotten (and that would still be huge) or be the beginning of a giant change in the way the Primordial Dream works, but I'd say it's worth leaving the option open.<br /> <br /> Getting more personal, I've had it happen in one of my games. The players liked that Hero, they all learned to coexist and eventually managed to obtain the Dark Mother's wary yet intrigued blessing. She kinda went &amp;quot;you know, you're both empowered by myths and dreams and care for each other. Have fun&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about it while building a villain Npc.<br /> The villain is a beast who has undergone the inversion and is a leader of a hero association, i am going to give him hero gift for slained beasts and i was wondering if he could have put family ties on his hero comrades","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:13:13-08:00","id":1278087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1278086#post1278086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking about it while building a villain Npc.<br /> The villain is a beast who has undergone the inversion and is a leader of a hero association, i am going to give him hero gift for slained beasts and i was wondering if he could have put family ties on his hero comrades</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that's a nasty one. It would cause all sort ot trouble to PCs, be a terrible threat and make the Dark Mother absolutely livid. Also break things a little.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Go for it.</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T10:31:42-08:00","id":1278102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1278087#post1278087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oooh, that's a nasty one. It would cause all sort ot trouble to PCs, be a terrible threat and make the Dark Mother absolutely livid. Also break things a little.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Go for it.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to see that someone likes the idea \u263a, i will also develope heroes kinship nightmare and merits, players will remember him for a long time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T20:08:55-08:00","id":1278490,"title":"","content":"Hey, Im away from home. Can someone send me the flavour text for the atavism &quot;Enemy Within&quot; from Beast Player Guide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T21:42:39-08:00","id":1278500,"title":"","content":"How well do humans really know one another? Evolution <br /> wired the human brain to pay close attention to only a handful <br /> of people. As populations grew, humans favored broad detail <br /> over intimate familiarity. The Inguma exploit this weak spot, <br /> slipping between the cracks of human programming and passing <br /> themselves off as someone familiar.<br /> <br /> here you go <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4793\" data-vbnamecard=\"4793\">HunterInTheNight</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T22:11:53-08:00","id":1278503,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:47:20-08:00","id":1279104,"title":"","content":"so I was reading the sundered world dark era and have a question. <br /> <br /> the book mentions that some pangeans became trapped in the world of flesh after the gauntlet formed, and then formed into myth, monsters of legend (it specifically says the words myth and legend)<br /> <br /> is this a possible creation of the first horrors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:51:14-08:00","id":1279105,"title":"","content":"Sure. Alternatively since Horrors (I've not read the latest Beast book) tend to be sort of particularly aggressive aspects of humanity's collective unconscious, they could be memories of actual Pangaeans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:57:09-08:00","id":1279106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1279104#post1279104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I was reading the sundered world dark era and have a question.<br /> <br /> the book mentions that some pangeans became trapped in the world of flesh after the gauntlet formed, and then formed into myth, monsters of legend (it specifically says the words myth and legend)<br /> <br /> is this a possible creation of the first horrors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, since the siderbar concerning the other supernaturals in the world at the time includes creatures who are most certainly Beasts.<br /> <br /> Now, did some of the Pangaeans becomes horrors or even Family Progenitors in the source of the Sundering?<br /> <br /> Maaaaybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T20:06:44-08:00","id":1279107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1279106#post1279106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, since the siderbar concerning the other supernaturals in the world at the time includes creatures who are most certainly Beasts.<br /> <br /> Now, did some of the Pangaeans becomes horrors or even Family Progenitors in the source of the Sundering?<br /> <br /> Maaaaybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should've said possible origins. I do like the idea of them becoming progenitors of families though.<br /> <br /> also, i wonder how much more powerful beast were then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T03:47:27-08:00","id":1282612,"title":"","content":"When a Beast uses the Under the bed ability, can she opt to stay in the mortal dream instead to reach his lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T09:08:27-08:00","id":1282656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1282612#post1282612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Beast uses the Under the bed ability, can she opt to stay in the mortal dream instead to reach his lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>The passageway is noted to be a warped and distorted version of the nightmare the target is suffering under that's more representational. There's nothing expressly forbidding it, but if I was STing then I would say no since its meant to be a passage with nightmare and the corridor being more representational of the Beast's own connection to their Lair/ The Primordial Dream. I'd allow a check to see what information you could glean about the victim while passing through, but I wouldn't allow wandering out of the corridor into the victim's dreams proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T05:18:40-08:00","id":1283486,"title":"","content":"Could a Beast extend immunity to a trait imposed outside the lair (by core it seems only to broodmates and with a willpower point cost but the player guide contradict that) ?<br /> <br /> AND<br /> <br /> Can a Beast impose a broodmate lair trait inside her lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T19:19:03-08:00","id":1283623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1283486#post1283486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Beast extend immunity to a trait imposed outside the lair (by core it seems only to broodmates and with a willpower point cost but the player guide contradict that) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reading of the core implies that one's immunity to an element of the Lair trait doesn't work with just any instance of it. The chosen example was that a Beast could not squeeze through an overly cramped air duct even if they had the cramped Lair trait unless they first imposed their Lair on the area. Going with that logic, I'd say people who have standing invites into your Lair, like your Broodmates, would be protected because they are normally protected from the harmful effects of your Lair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1283486#post1283486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast impose a broodmate lair trait inside her lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume by the context we're talking a trait that isn't shared between the two of your Lairs. In which case, no.You don't gain any influence over a broodmate's Lair, the connection offered only protects you from the traits of their own Lair, but you wouldn't be able to use their own traits due to it being them and not you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T22:30:44-08:00","id":1283660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1283623#post1283623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume by the context we're talking a trait that isn't shared between the two of your Lairs. In which case, no.You don't gain any influence over a broodmate's Lair, the connection offered only protects you from the traits of their own Lair, but you wouldn't be able to use their own traits due to it being them and not you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can <i>impose</i> a broodmate's Lair Trait just fine; the fact that doing so would come out of your per-scene limit rather than from your free control over your own Traits within your own Lair doesn't mean you can't use the presence of a Lair Trait to pull in another one the normal way just because you're in a Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T23:15:09-08:00","id":1283662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1283660#post1283660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you can <i>impose</i> a broodmate's Lair Trait just fine; the fact that doing so would come out of your per-scene limit rather than from your free control over your own Traits within your own Lair doesn't mean you can't use the presence of a Lair Trait to pull in another one the normal way just because you're in a Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this is the way i intended it but on the core it s not very clear.<br /> What do you think about the first question?<br /> nalak42 interpretation seems good to me but i m not sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:48:30-08:00","id":1284133,"title":"","content":"This is maybe more a reading comprehension on my part but...does a collector's hoard <i>do </i>anything once they have it?<br /> <br /> That is, does disrupting/damaging/stealing it affect the beast in any way, or does having a particularly big or impressive help them?<br /> <br /> It feels very much like it <i>should</i>, thematically speaking, and i'm sure i remember seeing that mechanic somewhere, but i can't see any indication in the book. Maybe i just dreamt it (ironically) but i would like to make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T10:20:37-08:00","id":1284157,"title":"","content":"the hungers dont provide bonuses besides how you fulfill hunger, so no extra effects (though, it would be cool if hungers had their own mechanics)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T15:32:10-08:00","id":1284226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1284133#post1284133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is maybe more a reading comprehension on my part but...does a collector's hoard <i>do </i>anything once they have it?<br /> <br /> That is, does disrupting/damaging/stealing it affect the beast in any way, or does having a particularly big or impressive help them?<br /> <br /> It feels very much like it <i>should</i>, thematically speaking, and i'm sure i remember seeing that mechanic somewhere, but i can't see any indication in the book. Maybe i just dreamt it (ironically) but i would like to make sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does whatever such a collection would normally do, and if your Horror's tastes and Things That Are Important To You Personally happen to be aligned then replacing a lost trinket might make for a particularly good meal, but otherwise not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Typo. 02-01-2019, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T01:39:40-08:00","id":1284302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1284133#post1284133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is maybe more a reading comprehension on my part but...does a collector's hoard <i>do </i>anything once they have it?<br /> <br /> That is, does disrupting/damaging/stealing it affect the beast in any way, or does having a particularly big or impressive help them?<br /> <br /> It feels very much like it <i>should</i>, thematically speaking, and i'm sure i remember seeing that mechanic somewhere, but i can't see any indication in the book. Maybe i just dreamt it (ironically) but i would like to make sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you are talking about the hoard lair trait in player guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T17:21:10-08:00","id":1285739,"title":"","content":"So one thing I'm not totally clear on. I know when a beast enters their lair they merge with their horror. Does that mean they have to take its form or can they maintain a human appearance. I ask because stuff like the Well Stocked Lair or the Connected Lair ( The one that allows internet and phone signals I the lair) trait seem kinda pointless to non humanoid beasts. So unless the beast gets a lot of visitors what's the point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T17:49:15-08:00","id":1285746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1285739#post1285739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one thing I'm not totally clear on. I know when a beast enters their lair they merge with their horror. Does that mean they have to take its form or can they maintain a human appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>If their Horror is Slumbering or otherwise prevented from reaching the Begotten as alluded to on page 151 of the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I ask because stuff like the Well Stocked Lair or the Connected Lair ( The one that allows internet and phone signals I the lair) trait seem kinda pointless to non humanoid beasts. So unless the beast gets a lot of visitors what's the point? </div> </div> </div>Literally more than a quarter of the wordcount for Well-Stocked Lair is dedicated to addressing the prospect of using it to supply guests and long-term tenants, and Connected Lair allows two-way reach in a fashion that doesn't preclude Horrors with an informational bent even if you don't have guests or a Horror in a food coma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T18:18:28-08:00","id":1285754,"title":"","content":"There is also the possibility of more humanoid Horrors, not to the extent of requiring one's own supplies but it might work out to your benefit to have them even then. Heck a thing I'd had planned for a game that never happened was for my Beast to be a Doppleganger, so his &quot;relaxed&quot; state when prowling his own Lair would be wearing the human side's form. (This also provided the potentially fun benefit of being able to pretend the Horror was slumbering if you get the merger when no one was looking and thus able to spend the whole time pretending that you totally aren't your own Horror pretending to be you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:07:05-08:00","id":1286694,"title":"","content":"Do someone have a good idea for a medieval version of the direct dial merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T09:20:08-08:00","id":1286744,"title":"","content":"The first thing that came to my mind is earlier than medieval, but the reference should be widely understood in Judeo-Christian Europe.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belshazzar%27s_feast\" target=\"_blank\">Belshazzar's feast</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T13:43:04-08:00","id":1286831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1286744#post1286744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing that came to my mind is earlier than medieval, but the reference should be widely understood in Judeo-Christian Europe.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belshazzar%27s_feast&amp;quot;]Belshazzar's</a> feast[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting option, maybe with Animal ken or Survival as a prerequisite in order to &quot;write&quot; with insect or natural elements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T06:55:22-08:00","id":1288245,"title":"","content":"My apologies if this has been covered before, but: could someone help me out with the Pestilence Condition (Beast Player's Guide, page 86). It comes from the Satiety-expenditure portion of the Plague Bearer Atavism. I'm specifically confused about what sort of rolls the victim makes -- the &quot;cure&quot; part is clear, but I'm not sure what sort of rolls the victim should be making as the disease progresses. I'm assuming it's pulling off of the Normal version of the Atavism, where people make their resistance roll ever 12-[Lair] hours, and Pestilence's details on damage and severity overriding the Normal versions' details, but I'm not 100% on that. <br /> <br /> FWIW, this is stemming from one of my players using this in a hospital/almshouse in 1758's Caribbean.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for your help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:39:40-08:00","id":1288341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1288245#post1288245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologies if this has been covered before, but: could someone help me out with the Pestilence Condition (Beast Player's Guide, page 86). It comes from the Satiety-expenditure portion of the Plague Bearer Atavism. I'm specifically confused about what sort of rolls the victim makes -- the &quot;cure&quot; part is clear, but I'm not sure what sort of rolls the victim should be making as the disease progresses. I'm assuming it's pulling off of the Normal version of the Atavism, where people make their resistance roll ever 12-[Lair] hours, and Pestilence's details on damage and severity overriding the Normal versions' details, but I'm not 100% on that.<br /> <br /> FWIW, this is stemming from one of my players using this in a hospital/almshouse in 1758's Caribbean.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for your help!</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Condition is referring to the rules for Disease on page 171 of Beast's corebook: Resisting the damage inflicted by a disease requires a reflexive Stamina + Resolve roll. This roll is not contested but it is modified by the severity of the disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T09:51:24-08:00","id":1292517,"title":"","content":"Quick question:<br /> Spending Satiety is a reflexive action, there are no limits given on how much Satiety can be spent in one turn. Does that mean a Beast got spent 1 Satiety on Skin Deep, another on Cyclopean Strength, one on Eye of Heaven and a fourth on Limb From Limb to literally hulk out and go ballistic on someone?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:22:28-08:00","id":1292545,"title":"","content":"Well, you can do only one instant action per turn, so i would check what kind of action each atavism requires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:05:15-08:00","id":1292561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1292545#post1292545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can do only one instant action per turn, so i would check what kind of action each atavism requires</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, but spending Satiety is reflexive. So let's go with an example of a hypothetical Lair 1 Beast with 2/2/2 Strength/Dexterity/Stamina and 2 Brawl.<br /> Spending Satiety on Skin Deep would buff up your physical stats by one each +1 in let's say strength plus some bonuses (we're gonna go with something that is irrelevant and doesn't further add to the situation). So now its 4/3/3. No Instant Action used yet.<br /> Spending Satiety on Cyclopean Strength gives a +Lair modifier on successful Strength rolls. Still no Instant Action used.<br /> Spending Satiety on Eye of Heaven gives the Rote quality to the next attack roll. Still no Instant action.<br /> Spending Satiety on Limb From Limb gives the next unarmed attack a +1 Aggravated modifier.<br /> If you now roll your attack, it'd be a dicepool of 6, Rote. If you roll 1 Success, you deal 3 Aggravated.<br /> <br /> My question is: would spending Satiety like that work, spreading it out over multiple different Atavisms? (Stacking so many modifiers like here is up to the ST I guess, but couldn't come up with an alternative right now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T15:55:19-08:00","id":1292634,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm aware that's rules as intended, and the crazy power it grants is limited by the fact that you just spent half your maximum usable pool to pull that off. Better hope you started with 9 and don't need to do it more than twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T06:52:59-08:00","id":1292751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1292561#post1292561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, but spending Satiety is reflexive. So let's go with an example of a hypothetical Lair 1 Beast with 2/2/2 Strength/Dexterity/Stamina and 2 Brawl.<br /> Spending Satiety on Skin Deep would buff up your physical stats by one each +1 in let's say strength plus some bonuses (we're gonna go with something that is irrelevant and doesn't further add to the situation). So now its 4/3/3. No Instant Action used yet.<br /> Spending Satiety on Cyclopean Strength gives a +Lair modifier on successful Strength rolls. Still no Instant Action used.<br /> Spending Satiety on Eye of Heaven gives the Rote quality to the next attack roll. Still no Instant action.<br /> Spending Satiety on Limb From Limb gives the next unarmed attack a +1 Aggravated modifier.<br /> If you now roll your attack, it'd be a dicepool of 6, Rote. If you roll 1 Success, you deal 3 Aggravated.<br /> <br /> My question is: would spending Satiety like that work, spreading it out over multiple different Atavisms? (Stacking so many modifiers like here is up to the ST I guess, but couldn't come up with an alternative right now)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a hypothetical Beast with four specific Atavisms tied to four different Families meaning two of them are bought as Out-of-Family. Minmaxed characters will always be able to do extreme stuff in all of the gamelines. The only thing you can do to stop it is to tell your players to not minmax, if you're uncomfortable with such characters.<br /> And a small correction: Limb From Limb's Satiety Expenditure option doesn't give you a +1A attack. It makes your next unarmed attack (regardless of its damage modifier) deal aggravated damage, which means +0A in most cases. -1A in the case of biting. A single success attack in your example would deal 2 aggravated damage (1 from the success, +1 from the extra success granted by Cyclopean Strength).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T11:11:31-08:00","id":1292816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1292751#post1292751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a hypothetical Beast with four specific Atavisms tied to four different Families meaning two of them are bought as Out-of-Family. Minmaxed characters will always be able to do extreme stuff in all of the gamelines. The only thing you can do to stop it is to tell your players to not minmax, if you're uncomfortable with such characters.<br /> And a small correction: Limb From Limb's Satiety Expenditure option doesn't give you a +1A attack. It makes your next unarmed attack (regardless of its damage modifier) deal aggravated damage, which means +0A in most cases. -1A in the case of biting. A single success attack in your example would deal 2 aggravated damage (1 from the success, +1 from the extra success granted by Cyclopean Strength).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, mixed up the low satiety with the satiety expenditure there (+Lair Lethal turned into +Lair Agg in my head). Not uncomfortable with such characters, just wasn't sure whether spending satiety like that would work or not. It does change the dynamic of possible fights or social interactions a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:30:50-08:00","id":1293875,"title":"","content":"The satiety minigame in Beast is very cool. Satiety expenditure on atavisms are very cool, but they definitely cramp the style on using Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1292751#post1292751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And a small correction: Limb From Limb's Satiety Expenditure option doesn't give you a +1A attack. It makes your next unarmed attack (regardless of its damage modifier)</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth mentioning that RAW is your next attack, not your next unarmed attack. Low Satiety is the only one that stipulates unarmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 03-04-2019, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T09:07:43-08:00","id":1294079,"title":"","content":"Welp. It's only the Low Satiety effect that specifies unarmed attacks. Imagine that combo with a fire axe that is +3 damage and has 9-Again. &quot;Here's Johnny!&quot; except most of the door disappeared after the first swing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:52:37-08:00","id":1294537,"title":"","content":"There's a Nemesis cop who flat out blows people's arms or legs of with each shot from his pistol. Absolutely nasty customer in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:05:28-08:00","id":1295008,"title":"","content":"About Inverted beasts, do you think they still roll<br /> Attribute+satiety (so only attribute for them) for nightmare activation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:11:55-07:00","id":1297064,"title":"","content":"Some Atavism-questions: Shadowed Soul makes you immune to the Blinded Tilt regardless of source - does that mean that they see even when simply closing their eyes?<br /> Can you stack the normal effects of Monster from the Deep and Limb from Limb (specific example, would you be able to ignore 1/2 Lair rounded up, and due to the additional success get to inflict Arm wreck)?<br /> Does Storm-Lashed make you immune to a Promethean's Arc Alembic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T13:51:03-07:00","id":1297076,"title":"","content":"No, yes, and probably yes, though it's Torment filled nature might mitigate that or at least make it really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T11:22:58-07:00","id":1297298,"title":"","content":"Can minor spalt like Ghouls, Wolf Blooded or Proximi undergo the Devouring ? And if so does the Devouring shatters things like Blood bond addictions or that sort of things ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T11:29:37-07:00","id":1297299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1297298#post1297298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can minor spalt like Ghouls, Wolf Blooded or Proximi undergo the Devouring ? And if so does the Devouring shatters things like Blood bond addictions or that sort of things ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A clean yes for the first question. It's the sort of thing that gives you a quick and ready cool situation to deal with. For the second, I'd personally go for a &quot;probably yes, but also no depending on how interesting it would make the situation&quot;. I tend to go with both, because I like each Devouring to be its own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-16-2019, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T11:30:28-07:00","id":1297300,"title":"","content":"Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that opens up nice background possibilities","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T16:48:58-07:00","id":1297385,"title":"","content":"So I don't have a good grasp on the homebrews, but I was reminded of an old idea I'd had way before I'd actually finished reading the backer draft of Beast. (So yeah, a while back.) Back then from what I'd read I'd gotten the idea that Heroes were going to be a template that added on to other things. IE the concern Beasts had back then was the idea of creating a Hero with the potential threat that said Hero wouldn't just be a baseline human or a Hunter, but the concern of a nightmare scenario where one ends up creating a Werewolf Hero, a Vampire Hero, a Changeling Hero, etc.<br /> <br /> Any decent homebrews that went with that kind of idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T21:14:14-07:00","id":1297636,"title":"","content":"Do Beasts dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T00:13:42-07:00","id":1297652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1297636#post1297636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Beasts dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what i can desume from the core book, when they sleep their dream form &quot;merge&quot; with the horror, but the horror retains control.<br /> When they awake the memories of this &quot;merging&quot; could be clear or dreamlike, i m not sure<br /> <br /> For reference, see page 51 of core book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 03-18-2019, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:29:19-07:00","id":1298859,"title":"","content":"Probably been asked for, and I even feel like I answered this, but I can't it and my thinker box is fuzzy, ergo:<br /> <br /> Insatiable using Obcasus Rites. That a thing we find feasibly possible or noooooo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T00:12:18-07:00","id":1298869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1298859#post1298859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably been asked for, and I even feel like I answered this, but I can't it and my thinker box is fuzzy, ergo:<br /> <br /> Insatiable using Obcasus Rites. That a thing we find feasibly possible or noooooo?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um.... Well, the Obcasus Initiate merit has being a Beast as a prerequisite, and that you have experienced Guidance as described on page 141 of the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> The Player's Guide only mentions the Insatiable in a small sidebar on page 157 and it's not in any context of them being considered Beasts.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd say &quot;No, as Insatiable are different, if similar, creatures to Beasts and would have a different connection to the Dark Mother.&quot; I don't think the Insatiable really work together, either, so Obcasus Rites as how Beasts use them as social things, probably wouldn't fit very well. But Obcasus Rites, twisted as individual endeavors for an Insatiable, might be a good springing off point for interesting powers they could bring to bear.<br /> <br /> That help at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T00:18:00-07:00","id":1298871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1298859#post1298859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably been asked for, and I even feel like I answered this, but I can't it and my thinker box is fuzzy, ergo:<br /> <br /> Insatiable using Obcasus Rites. That a thing we find feasibly possible or noooooo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna say it doesn't seem that feasible. Insatiable seem to view themselves as having a different progenitor than the Dark Mother and since she's the power one is supposed to commune with when using one of the rites that doesn't seem as probable. Also add in the bit about the one leading needing to function as a shaman representing all Beasts present make me disinclined towards the standard idea. Probably also not helped by the bit pointing out that a non-captive Hero showing up at a temple profanes the site, and considering Beasts tend to be less friendly with the Insatiable than Heroes I'm not seeing that helping.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd probably totally have an Insatiable pull one off if I thought my group would use the normal stuff just for their responses when it works, but comes off with things that don't happen in the normal versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T20:20:00-07:00","id":1301214,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s is Devouring? It\u2019s a choice but not really a Choice. Because if you refuse they\u2019ll eat your soul anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T20:33:20-07:00","id":1301216,"title":"","content":"no it wont. it specifically says if they refuse, nothing will happen. they will continue to be human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T20:42:23-07:00","id":1301218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1301214#post1301214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s is Devouring? It\u2019s a choice but not really a Choice. Because if you refuse they\u2019ll eat your soul anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of a matter of how rough do you want it to go. The Player's Guide gives a bit more of the impression that the you don't get a choice aspect is more the side effect of some other Beasts getting involved and forcing the issue. Whereas with others it just ends up being that your Horror will keep confronting you until you accept the conclusion that the both parties are the same individual.<br /> <br /> Think of it more like forced confrontation with an unpleasant truth. (Which makes me think there's probably a few Namtaru that love it when they can force the Devouring for their more stubborn kin.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T21:11:31-07:00","id":1301221,"title":"","content":"she confronts her Horror for the very first time, seeing it <br /> this once as it stands alone. The dreamer has one final chance <br /> to flee here, though she will suffer a hollow and tormented <br /> existence without her soul if she does, and she will never escape <br /> the knowledge of what she was truly meant to be. If a particularly <br /> cruel or secretive Beast initiated her Devouring, she may become <br /> just another victim of his Hunger, should she reject her heritage. <br /> Once the Devouring has commenced, most prospective Beasts <br /> have made up their minds, and accepted their lot as Begotten.<br /> <br /> well damn. I'm sorry for lashing out @Konradleijon<br /> <br /> but anyway, what makes the devouring worse than the embrace, being a mummy (as in participating in the rite of return to become a slave), or being a captured by a keeper? the devouring is simply something that happens to humans with a deep connection to the dream meet their true soul. it's horrible they cant truly reject it, but why should beasts be the one supernatural that's just able to say &quot;no I dont want to&quot;? even mages have an inexplicable pull to the supernatural before awakening","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-31-2019, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:39:01-07:00","id":1301328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1301218#post1301218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of a matter of how rough do you want it to go. The Player's Guide gives a bit more of the impression that the you don't get a choice aspect is more the side effect of some other Beasts getting involved and forcing the issue. Whereas with others it just ends up being that your Horror will keep confronting you until you accept the conclusion that the both parties are the same individual.<br /> <br /> Think of it more like forced confrontation with an unpleasant truth. (Which makes me think there's probably a few Namtaru that love it when they can force the Devouring for their more stubborn kin.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So why did they replace the Homecoming? I mess it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:55:33-07:00","id":1301332,"title":"","content":"ok this I cant apologize for. konrad, you have voiced your opinion on the devouring before and how much you wish the devouring did not replace Homecoming. everyone has gone over this discussion before quite in depth.<br /> <br /> basically, you can keep your opinion, but dont beat it like a dead horse, by which I mean bringing it up again WITHOUT taking in past arguments","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:57:41-07:00","id":1301334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1301328#post1301328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why did they replace the Homecoming? I mess it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically they rolled it into the Devouring and changed the name. Even in the core it's mentioned that some Beghotten insist that their Devouring was more coming to grips with something that was always there. The Player's Guide expands on it a bit more with some more discussion, its basically the smoother option on the Devouring. <br /> <br /> As for why on the change, I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:15:08-07:00","id":1301339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1301328#post1301328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why did they replace the Homecoming? I mess it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've come to appreciate what the Devouring brings to the table and the stories and character involvement it carries along but, as others are saying, the circumstances of the Homecoming can still happen, with the core hinting at it and the Player's Guide giving more details.<br /> <br /> My personal suggestions is to call it something along the line of &quot;Spontaneous Devouring&quot;, keep in mind it can happen, but also that it's not the the only way Beast can merge with their Horror. It's alright, more options are rarely a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:49:07-07:00","id":1301413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1301328#post1301328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why did they replace the Homecoming? I mess it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just have the Homecoming for your games. It's what I'm doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:16:55-07:00","id":1301424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1301413#post1301413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just have the Homecoming for your games. It's what I'm doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>probably the best answer. just tell your storyteller you would like the devouring to be like homecoming (which is already is for some beasts). if he says no...well the storyteller needs to examine what's he's doing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T00:08:15-07:00","id":1303726,"title":"","content":"Idly fun question: What do you think are the most likely Path(s) each Family would appear as when using Family Resemblance to pass as mages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T00:36:33-07:00","id":1303729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1303726#post1303726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idly fun question: What do you think are the most likely Path(s) each Family would appear as when using Family Resemblance to pass as mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to give the boring answer: I think they'd all appear as Mastigos with various odd Legacies. This is because Nightmares are clearly Mind effects, the Family Resemblance is Space, and Lair is a combination of Mind (it's Temenos adjacent) and Space (it has/can form connections to real world places that resemble a chamber).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T01:14:59-07:00","id":1303731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1303726#post1303726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idly fun question: What do you think are the most likely Path(s) each Family would appear as when using Family Resemblance to pass as mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly less boring answer: Mastigos at high Satiety, Thyrsus at low Satiety.<br /> <br /> <br /> To check my latest understanding of a particular set of Lair mechanics that I've been sporadically grappling with over the years:<br /> \u2022 Hold the Door operates under the assumption that the space you've used to open a Primordial Pathway is &quot;an entrance to your Lair,&quot; and is the only means by which visitors to your Lair may receive the protections afforded to a guest (aside from Be My Guest, which works ).<br /> \u2022 Separate from this, anyone attempting to leave the while a Primordial Pathway is open finds themselves in the Beast's Lair, moving through one of their Burrows to another Chamber (presumably regardless of what the normal route to access that Burrow is within the open Chamber).<br /> \u2022 This isn't usually a huge problem because (besides the usual exercises of common sense that mean most Beasts aren't going to have unintended visitors slipping into their souls on a frequent basis) every Beast has the capacity to sustain at least two Chambers whose collapse does not end their lives, a single free pass through the front door doesn't make any other transition less difficult, Chambers are the Horror's favored hunting grounds (and the Horror is immune to its own Lair Traits and doesn't have to struggle to move between Chambers), and it's textual that most Beasts structure their Lairs in such a way that the Heart is the most distant Chamber from any entrances.<br /> \u2022 Be My Guest grants a character the ability to open Primordial Pathways as though they were the Beast whose permission they received, rolling Wits + Resolve along with any modifiers as normal.<br /> <br /> Does that sound about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T09:25:01-07:00","id":1303790,"title":"","content":"Who responds to &quot;idly fun question&quot;s with boring answers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:20:52-07:00","id":1304010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1303790#post1303790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who responds to &quot;idly fun question&quot;s with boring answers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I... honestly would've guessed that you'd bear the Passing Resemblance of the supernatural creature you have Family Ties with?<br /> <br /> Like, if you know a Winter Court Changeling, you'd peg as a Winter Court Changeling, because that is <i>what you know</i>. Plus, it makes interactions with the local communities a little more... Applicable, I think? Like, it would mean if you did something and other Changelings went asking to the local Winter Court...<br /> <br /> Alternatively... You just don't. You only peg as the overall supernatural type and not to any specific affiliations because they're not applicable to you. So you would register as a Changeling with no particular Court or Seeming noted. Or a Vampire of no particular Clan. And that could be suspicious or mysterious and leaves questions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like answers that provide avenues to more potential conflict.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, what supernatural effects determine your Auspice/Tribe, Court/Seeming, Path/Order, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 04-10-2019, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:33:09-07:00","id":1304012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304010#post1304010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I... honestly would've guessed that you'd bear the Passing Resemblance of the supernatural creature you have Family Ties with?<br /> <br /> Like, if you know a Winter Court Changeling, you'd peg as a Winter Court Changeling, because that is <i>what you know</i>. Plus, it makes interactions with the local communities a little more... Applicable, I think? Like, it would mean if you did something and other Changelings went asking to the local Winter Court...<br /> <br /> Alternatively... You just don't. You only peg as the overall supernatural type and not to any specific affiliations because they're not applicable to you. So you would register as a Changeling with no particular Court or Seeming noted. Or a Vampire of no particular Clan. And that could be suspicious or mysterious and leaves questions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like answers that provide avenues to more potential conflict.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, what supernatural effects determine your Auspice/Tribe, Court/Seeming, Path/Order, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is more fun.<br /> <br /> (though, yes, I am shamelessly asking something along the lines of &quot;So Anakim would likely come across as Obrimos/Moros&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:33:58-07:00","id":1304013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1303731#post1303731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slightly less boring answer: Mastigos at high Satiety, Thyrsus at low Satiety.<br /> <br /> <br /> To check my latest understanding of a particular set of Lair mechanics that I've been sporadically grappling with over the years:<br /> \u2022 Hold the Door operates under the assumption that the space you've used to open a Primordial Pathway is &quot;an entrance to your Lair,&quot; and is the only means by which visitors to your Lair may receive the protections afforded to a guest (aside from Be My Guest, which works ).<br /> \u2022 Separate from this, anyone attempting to leave the while a Primordial Pathway is open finds themselves in the Beast's Lair, moving through one of their Burrows to another Chamber (presumably regardless of what the normal route to access that Burrow is within the open Chamber).<br /> \u2022 This isn't usually a huge problem because (besides the usual exercises of common sense that mean most Beasts aren't going to have unintended visitors slipping into their souls on a frequent basis) every Beast has the capacity to sustain at least two Chambers whose collapse does not end their lives, a single free pass through the front door doesn't make any other transition less difficult, Chambers are the Horror's favored hunting grounds (and the Horror is immune to its own Lair Traits and doesn't have to struggle to move between Chambers), and it's textual that most Beasts structure their Lairs in such a way that the Heart is the most distant Chamber from any entrances.<br /> \u2022 Be My Guest grants a character the ability to open Primordial Pathways as though they were the Beast whose permission they received, rolling Wits + Resolve along with any modifiers as normal.<br /> <br /> Does that sound about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be perfectly honest, I'm really not sure how Hold The Door and Be My Guest are supposed to interact with Primordial Pathways or the Lair.<br /> <br /> Re-reading Hold The Door, it seems like a valid interpretation that if a Beast opens a Primordial Pathway and people flee the area, then they don't run into the Lair unless the Beast explicitly Holds The Door for them to do it. That seems to counter what Primordial Pathways says, though, and I'm not sure that's the <i>right</i> interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:39:43-07:00","id":1304015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304012#post1304012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this is more fun.<br /> <br /> (though, yes, I am shamelessly asking something along the lines of &quot;So Anakim would likely come across as Obrimos/Moros&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would they, though?<br /> <br /> Passing Resemblance only says &quot;Passing Resemblance automatically fools passive abilities that identify creature type, such as a vampire's instinctual recognition of another vampire.&quot; I don't think the vampire instinct identifies Clan. So what exactly is the scope of &quot;creature type&quot;? Uncertain, probably up to the Storyteller to define. The power explicitly notes that nothing about you changes, unless you have a high Satiety rating (7+) which makes convincing illusory elements such as turning pale and appearing not to breathe while imitating a vampire. That's not really information that gives Clan or whatnot. Faerie Mein might give clues, but that's called out as being based on the Horror.<br /> <br /> I think I'd just give little information out, and let the players (and the characters) puzzle it out.<br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, I'm not asking &quot;Why would they?&quot; to shut down the idea. But to ask &quot;Why?&quot; If you want Beasts to be able to easily pass through another supernatural culture, that's a valid and good answer to &quot;Why?&quot; Personally, I don't want my Beasts to be &quot;perfect&quot; with their deceptions using Passing Resemblance, and so I tailor my interpretation to have Passing Resemblance be more for evading casual notice, but when a Beast is under a microscope, the jig is probably up. Because I want my Beasts to be confronted eventually or when they're not being careful. I want that conflict. And that's why my answer of &quot;Why?&quot; might be different.<br /> <br /> Different goals for different games and play styles. Perfectly fine, in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 04-10-2019, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:46:07-07:00","id":1304017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304015#post1304015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why would they, though?<br /> <br /> Passing Resemblance only says &quot;Passing Resemblance automatically fools passive abilities that identify creature type, such as a vampire's instinctual recognition of another vampire.&quot; I don't think the vampire instinct identifies Clan. So what exactly is the scope of &quot;creature type&quot;? Uncertain, probably up to the Storyteller to define. The power explicitly notes that nothing about you changes, unless you have a high Satiety rating (7+) which makes convincing illusory elements such as turning pale and appearing not to breathe while imitating a vampire. That's not really information that gives Clan or whatnot. Faerie Mein might give clues, but that's called out as being based on the Horror.<br /> <br /> I think I'd just give little information out, and let the players (and the characters) puzzle it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying they would. That's not the goal of my question though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:54:07-07:00","id":1304020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304017#post1304017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying they would. That's not the goal of my question though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I hadn't thought of before... Thicker Than Water is still working when you're using Passing Resemblance... I hadn't really thought about what that means before, honestly. Are Beasts the Social Engineers of supernatural communities? Amusing thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:07:18-07:00","id":1304025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304020#post1304020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something I hadn't thought of before... Thicker Than Water is still working when you're using Passing Resemblance... I hadn't really thought about what that means before, honestly. Are Beasts the Social Engineers of supernatural communities? Amusing thought...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a big part of the point, yeah.<br /> <br /> Beasts are communities unto themselves, that's not too surprising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T20:24:47-07:00","id":1304090,"title":"","content":"Beasts love to meddle with the other splats stuff, from gaining chambers from locations of supernatural activities, having convenient family dinners, for fighting for the roll of apex, hell tbh from the games I've played interacting with the other supernaturals makes it so much easier to fulfill Hungers other then just feeding off their feeding, are a Tyrant? join the political mess that is the Danse Macabre, a Predator? join a werewolf pack against their prey. Collector? Join a Mage expedition though do not raid a Mummy's tomb if you know whats good for you.... unless you were to say have a mummy on you side....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T00:09:27-07:00","id":1304769,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> Just how are Hold The Door and Be My Guest supposed to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T10:54:52-07:00","id":1304842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304769#post1304769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...<br /> <br /> Just how are Hold The Door and Be My Guest supposed to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean mechanically or in universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T11:59:45-07:00","id":1304853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304842#post1304842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean mechanically or in universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. There's no mention of people being able to open Primordial Pathways in Be My Guest, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T14:15:11-07:00","id":1304878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304853#post1304853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both. There's no mention of people being able to open Primordial Pathways in Be My Guest, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't give them the ability to open Pathways, just protection in your Lair. Think of it like having a friend who you've let know the code to turn off your security on your house, but not their own key for your place. So they won't have to deal with security when they show up, even if you're not there, but if you aren't personally letting them in then they might not be able to get in anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T14:40:09-07:00","id":1304883,"title":"","content":"Be My Guest allows the recipient to &quot;enter the Lair just as the Beast does.&quot; The exact intent could be clearer, but I think the most natural reading is that it gives the person the ability to spend a willpower and roll Wits + Resolve +/- appropriate modifiers. <br /> <br /> Someone who moves through a Primordial Pathway will end up in the Lair regardless of whether Hold The Door is used, I think. The main difference is that without Hold The Door they won't be protected from the dangers of the Lair and they can't leave by their own choosing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T14:59:32-07:00","id":1304885,"title":"","content":"So... That's two very different interpretations of the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T15:41:06-07:00","id":1304897,"title":"","content":"Since Be My Guest allows the recipient to come and go from the Lair as she pleases, as per the text under \u2018Effect\u2019, I\u2019d allow the \u2018Guest\u2019 to attempt to open a Primordial Pathway to the Lair just as the Beast does. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d also suggest that the Guest has no inherent knowledge of the workings behind this and probably won\u2019t be as flexible as the Beast himself. If the Beast teaches the Guest how to open the Pathway in a given location, the Guest won\u2019t know that this could also work on a similar location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:22:20-07:00","id":1304980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1304013#post1304013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-reading Hold The Door, it seems like a valid interpretation that if a Beast opens a Primordial Pathway and people flee the area, then they don't run into the Lair unless the Beast explicitly Holds The Door for them to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My read of the two &quot;hospitality&quot; abilities is, as both nalak and Helms seem to agree, that their main function is to let you host people in the Lair without turning off deterrent Traits rather than to let them get into the Lair at all \u2014 it's textually not an impenetrable fortress, after all.<br /> <br /> At the moment the thing I'm most uncertain of boils down to a combination of whether the Uninvited Guests text on how long it takes to get through a Burrow applies to people attempting to leave and whether a Burrow counts as a separate space for the purposes of being in the Chamber when the Pathway closes; presently my read is &quot;yes&quot; to both, because the default state of being stuck in a secret passage that doesn't exist until another Pathway opens or you luck into brute-forcing your way into the next Chamber feels both secure enough and low-key enough to be run with.<br /> <br /> So trying to leave a Beast's hospital Chamber while a Primordial Pathway to it is open dumps you into the road Burrow linking it to their factory Chamber right away, but you can't proceed to the factory Chamber without spending the Willpower and beating the Horror's contested roll, which takes turns that may exceed the turns that the Pathway is open; once the Pathway's closed, you're on the road (unless you went back to the Chamber in time and &quot;stayed&quot; in the real hospital) and can either continue to try and force your way into the factory or go back to the hospital Chamber and contend with the dangers therein while you wait for the hospital to link back up with reality. Notably, as long as you're on the road it's consistently going to link the hospital and the factory in the way it was designed to do, which may force the issue for the Beast if their Lair can't kill you directly and the Horror somehow can't get at you in its own territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T10:51:01-07:00","id":1308486,"title":"","content":"Say a PC Beast has successfully become the Apex of the local Hive.<br /> <br /> Is one of their existing Lair traits elevated to being the Hive Trait?<br /> Or do they get a new, additional Trait that fills that role, essentially granting Apex Beasts an extra Trait to draw on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T13:59:40-07:00","id":1308520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1308486#post1308486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a PC Beast has successfully become the Apex of the local Hive.<br /> <br /> Is one of their existing Lair traits elevated to being the Hive Trait?<br /> Or do they get a new, additional Trait that fills that role, essentially granting Apex Beasts an extra Trait to draw on?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hive Trait should represent the Apex. If the Beast didn't have the Hive Trait before becoming Apex then it wouldn't really be representative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:05:31-07:00","id":1308599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1308520#post1308520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Beast didn't have the Hive Trait before becoming Apex then it wouldn't really be representative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This presumes that the number of Lair Traits that could be representative of a certain Beast is always exactly equivalent to the number of Lair Traits that they currently have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T22:19:42-07:00","id":1308604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1308599#post1308599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This presumes that the number of Lair Traits that could be representative of a certain Beast is always exactly equivalent to the number of Lair Traits that they currently have.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If the Apex is a Beast, the hive reflects that Beast's Lair; if the Apex is a Makara, for example, a river might run through the Chambers of a hive, becoming swollen and raging when the Apex is angry.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you don't have a Lair Trait in your personal chunk of the Primordial Dream, it's almost certainly not going to represent you as a Hive Trait in the bigger chunk of the Primordial Dream you claim spiritual dominion over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}]