t</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unchained are not kin, but they can trigger family resemblance</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I thought not kin cant be subject to anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T23:30:41-07:00","id":1313793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1313760#post1313760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I thought not kin cant be subject to anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the core book.<br /> Demons have supplemental rules for it.<br /> But yes, much of the others kinship abilities doesn t work on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T04:22:31-07:00","id":1315419,"title":"","content":"Hi<br /> I need to build a guardian creature for a beast lair, with a power level of a rank 4 or 5 ephemeral creature.<br /> How many level of the beast guide merit well stocked lair are necessary for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T21:15:51-07:00","id":1316190,"title":"","content":"Do Beast have a Z-Spat? Like Lodges for Werewolves or Vampire Bloodlines? I mean, I couldn't find so I'm asking if there is any that might be on the works or something<br /> <br /> And can a Beast or at least its Horror be a pack totem? I think I saw something alluding to it in the Player's Guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 06-03-2019, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T01:57:32-07:00","id":1316211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1316190#post1316190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Beast have a Z-Spat? Like Lodges for Werewolves or Vampire Bloodlines? I mean, I couldn't find so I'm asking if there is any that might be on the works or something</div> </div> </div> </div>Inheritance is the closest thing so far, but it\u2019s not really the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1316190#post1316190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And can a Beast or at least its Horror be a pack totem? I think I saw something alluding to it in the Player's Guide</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, but maybe. I\u2019d say definite no to having a Beast as a pack totem, but maybe a Horror. Uratha bind to spirits of the Hisil as totems as they have the right \u2018shape\u2019 to fit with whatever mystical forces werewolves use to make the pack bond. It\u2019s possible that this could extend to other ephemeral entities as well, with a bit of effort. The complicating factor to the Horror is that it\u2019s already bound to the Beast in ways stronger and tighter than the pack bond. The ability to link to other creatures is already used up as it occupies the place of a soul rather than being a free spirit. That said, strange things happen and whatever works for your game is the bottom line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T03:32:26-07:00","id":1316219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1316211#post1316211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, but maybe. I\u2019d say definite no to having a Beast as a pack totem, but maybe a Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Beast Player Guide </b>seems to not agree with you on that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> BPG, p. 135</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lodge of the Red Owl is dedicated to reverence and mastery of the hunt. The Final Peace serves as the de facto totem of an Iron Master pack, and teaches her human followers how to hunt with a werewolf\u2019s savage efficiency and cunning. Her flock\u2019s greatest calling is to pass these methods on to fellow hunters, even if that means making them prey first.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T05:18:54-07:00","id":1316227,"title":"","content":"*sigh* What you have in that section, as per its heading \u201cCults and Cultists\u201d and the pages it describes about how a Beast pulls together a cult, is the Beast recruiting werewolves as part of her cult. Here she serves as the central persona inspiring the cult around her in the hunt. As it\u2019s written under a section specifically talking about the different reasons why Beasts might build cults, it\u2019s demonstrating how a Beast can assimilates an aspect important to another supernatural and turn that to her own needs. Serving as a patron to the Uratha and using her powers to assist them helps them in the hunt, but more importantly to the Beast, she inspires a flock of humans to go out and hunt and kill in her name, harvesting the Satiety and benefits from it. <br /> <br /> What it doesn\u2019t mean is that the Beast has all the abilities and expectations of an actual totem. If the Final Peace was the same as an actual totem, the text would have said \u201cThe Final Peace serves as the totem of the pack\u201d, not \u201cde facto totem\u2019. She\u2019s occupying a position of centrality around which the pack finds purpose, much like an actual totem. It doesn\u2019t mean she is one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T06:45:58-07:00","id":1319039,"title":"","content":"About hive trait the core book says <br /> &quot;The Apex (if a Beast, or otherwise able to access the Primordial Dream) can use that trait to move in and out of any Chambers in the hive. Likewise, if the Apex grants a Beast immunity to the Hive Trait, or if the Hive Trait happens to match one of the Lair Traits of a Beast, that Beast can move throughout the hive with impunity&quot;<br /> What does it mean?<br /> The apex can open a passage to every chamber of the hive even with no similarity with his lair chambers?<br /> Or it refers to this passage &quot; If a Beast doesn\u2019t know exactly where she wants to go, she can feel for and open a Pathway to somewhere random but still resonant within a specified world. &quot; meaning that the apex can open a pathway to a random location in the hive (again what about chambers similarity?) because they are all resonant with the hive trait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T23:50:46-07:00","id":1320905,"title":"","content":"Is there an official errata for the KS book? I've seen somewhere (Noble Knight Games, I think), that there were two different printings of the core. How do I know if I have 1st or 2nd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T10:12:42-07:00","id":1320982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1320905#post1320905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an official errata for the KS book? I've seen somewhere (Noble Knight Games, I think), that there were two different printings of the core. How do I know if I have 1st or 2nd?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a unfinishied, white page, black text, no borders or art version, you have the 99% version. If it looks like an actual gaming book, you have the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T12:11:48-07:00","id":1321008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1320982#post1320982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a unfinishied, white page, black text, no borders or art version, you have the 99% version. If it looks like an actual gaming book, you have the final version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there not an advance PDF of the core complete with art, etc but pre-errata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T12:30:16-07:00","id":1321010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1321008#post1321008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there not an advance PDF of the core complete with art, etc but pre-errata?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the differences caused by the errata are not enough to warrant a conversation about different cores. Let's be frank, the question being asked is between the initial Kickstarter draft and the final product(which I will here define my meaning as saying &quot;mostly the text as it existed from the rewrites to what you can now get on DTRPG&quot;).<br /> <br /> The only book worth talking about errata differences is Geist 1st.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T02:45:53-07:00","id":1321138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1321008#post1321008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there not an advance PDF of the core complete with art, etc but pre-errata?</div> </div> </div> </div>Search for \u2018p. XX\u2019 in the pdf, if you get more than a couple of hits (some slip through at times) you\u2019ve got the backer-release, pre-final pdf. But if you have that version legitimately, you got it from Drivethru and it\u2019s in your library waiting for you to go download the final version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T12:28:59-07:00","id":1321220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147655841/Beast---The-Primordial-1st-Printing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/Content/images/fp/nkg-og-homepage-v1-1200x630.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147655841/Beast---The-Primordial-1st-Printing\" target=\"_blank\"> Beast - The Primordial (1st Printing) - RPG - Onyx Path Publishing from Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147655841/Beast---The-Primordial-1st-Printing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147655841/Beast---The-Primordial-1st-Printing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The World's Largest Selection of tabletop games! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147633974/Beast---The-Primordial-2nd-Printing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/Content/images/fp/nkg-og-homepage-v1-1200x630.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147633974/Beast---The-Primordial-2nd-Printing\" target=\"_blank\"> Beast - The Primordial (POD, Standard Color) - RPG - Onyx Path Publishing from Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147633974/Beast---The-Primordial-2nd-Printing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.nobleknight.com/P/2147633974/Beast---The-Primordial-2nd-Printing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The World's Largest Selection of tabletop games! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> According to them, there is a 10pg difference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T16:55:18-07:00","id":1321557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>endou_kenji</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1321220#post1321220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to them, there is a 10pg difference</div> </div> </div> </div>What can I say? Short version - Noble Knight has it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T08:28:53-07:00","id":1321726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1321557#post1321557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What can I say? Short version - Noble Knight has it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>seems reasonable, lol <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T20:00:01-07:00","id":1327523,"title":"","content":"So, I'm playing the Apex of a region, and want to use the Hive Trait to scout out the Chambers in the Hive.<br /> How do I, uhh...do that exactly?<br /> <br /> Do I open a Primordial Pathway with a +2 bonus (+1 for the Hive Trait, +1 for the destination being the Dream)? <br /> If so, do I still need to worry about the second table of penalties for narrative etc similarity?<br /> If so, does that mean that I can't actually functionally open Pathways to Chambers that aren't similar to my own, outside of the base similarity provided by the Hive Trait?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T21:26:13-07:00","id":1327532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1327523#post1327523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I open a Primordial Pathway with a +2 bonus (+1 for the Hive Trait, +1 for the destination being the Dream)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, do I still need to worry about the second table of penalties for narrative etc similarity? </div> </div> </div>By <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1305137-unpacking-the-lair\">my current understanding of the rules</a>, at least, no, though you may be better off walking back to your Lair if the Chamber in question isn't a result of your handiwork.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, does that mean that I can't actually functionally open Pathways to Chambers that aren't similar to my own, outside of the base similarity provided by the Hive Trait? </div> </div> </div>The way BPG establishes Themes work in the Temenos inclines me to at minimum interpret &quot;similar to an existing Chamber&quot; somewhat broadly, combined with the threshold-oriented means of using Primordial Pathways into the Lair to actually remain within the lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T01:39:31-07:00","id":1327702,"title":"","content":"You Must Obey dont have an exceptional successes row?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T12:04:18-07:00","id":1327773,"title":"","content":"So I've been staring at the Killer Instinct merit recently, and I was wondering if someone could help answer a few questions for me.<br /> <br /> First off, once you assess a target to actually activate the merit, is it permanently activated against that target for the rest of the scene, or do you have to re-assess them before every attack?<br /> <br /> And second, it says that you can divide your dots in the merit among any of its effects, but can you choose an effect more than once to stack it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25525,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25525-breezysatina","user":"BreezySatina","date":". 07-27-2019, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25525-breezysatina","name":"BreezySatina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25525_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T13:20:11-07:00","id":1327788,"title":"","content":"I believe the base version only applies to one attack, and then you have to spend another turn to reactivate it. Yes, I think you can stack the same effect up to three times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T14:37:29-07:00","id":1327800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1327788#post1327788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the base version only applies to one attack, and then you have to spend another turn to reactivate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I'm not so sure about that is because the wording states, &quot;when making an attack against that target&quot; and not &quot;on your next attack against that target&quot; like the Aim action, which makes it sound like it stays active instead of resetting when you attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25525,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25525-breezysatina","user":"BreezySatina","date":". 07-27-2019, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25525-breezysatina","name":"BreezySatina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25525_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T02:24:52-07:00","id":1327871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BreezySatina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1327773#post1327773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, once you assess a target to actually activate the merit, is it permanently activated against that target for the rest of the scene, or do you have to re-assess them before every attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that it's on <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">permanently. Like, mundane Killer Instinct has more or less the same wording. Then Advanced KI makes it always on. If KI needed activating every other turn, then that would be a massive step-up.<br /> <br /> It might be something to watch out for in a game.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T05:35:48-07:00","id":1327889,"title":"","content":"That would fit the pattern of other advanced merits though. Mundane Striking looks is a +2 dice bonus, advanced adds rote. The significant power jump is what makes advanced merits so desirable and why they're restricted to Beasts while the base effects are available to anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T13:52:43-07:00","id":1328154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1327889#post1327889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would fit the pattern of other advanced merits though. Mundane Striking looks is a +2 dice bonus, advanced adds rote. The significant power jump is what makes advanced merits so desirable and why they're restricted to Beasts while the base effects are available to anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I think Killer Instinct advanced already adds a significant power boost.<br /> <br /> Plus, if it were a one-shot ability then I think simply making that always on would be a massive jump on it's own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T13:15:23-07:00","id":1330796,"title":"","content":"Any particular merits/skills/atavisms/etc you think are a must-have for a black widow type of beast? Thinking a seduce-trap-consume modus operandi, still ironing out the details. This is my first Beast character so trying to figure out what're the good stuff and what're the stuff that just seems good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T15:33:03-07:00","id":1330842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1330796#post1330796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular merits/skills/atavisms/etc you think are a must-have for a black widow type of beast? Thinking a seduce-trap-consume modus operandi, still ironing out the details. This is my first Beast character so trying to figure out what're the good stuff and what're the stuff that just seems good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, access to Atavisms varies a little depending on the Family you decide to pick, but here's my two cents:<br /> <br /> - Attributes &amp; Skills are rather straightforward. Presence and Manipulation are mandatory, but others like Wits, Resolve and Composure will likely come in handy with the concept you have in mind. As for Skills, Persuasion, Subterfuge, Empathy and Socialize are the first which come to mind.<br /> <br /> -Merits somewhat depend on the details (and give you more details as well), but stuff like Alternate Identity, Barfly, Striking Looks and Trained Observer are good starting points for you to look at. Allies, Contacts and Resources also help.<br /> <br /> - Atavisms. Alien Allure is a given. Basilisk Touch gives you poison, which classically fits the concept, as does From the Shadows. Need Must can help find and track target and Siren's Treacherous Song helps to charm others too, in its own way. If you want to go with a literal black widow as Horror concept, Infestation is always fun and, if you have access to the Player's Guide, Caught in the Web does exactly what its name describes. A combination of Inguma and Talassi Atavisms from that same book would likely provide something for what you have in mind.<br /> <br /> -Nightmares can be costumized a lot, but some like Bugs Everywhere!, You Are Alone and You Cannot Run seem appropriate right from the bat.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-13-2019, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:31:41-07:00","id":1331847,"title":"","content":"I'm really sorry if this has been answered before, but I couldn't find a good answer for this and I though I had an idea of how did this work but reading the book again I saw that I didn't have a good grasp of how did it work.<br /> <br /> What am I talking about? Imposing Lair traits, could you walk me through the permutations for it? or give me a link to a post where it has been answered?<br /> <br /> I'm confused when the book mentions that a trait is Resonant, can the Beast just will a number or lair traits as per Lair rating with no roll or cost involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:48:02-07:00","id":1331850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1331847#post1331847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused when the book mentions that a trait is Resonant, can the Beast just will a number or lair traits as per Lair rating with no roll or cost involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the case in any permutation of the action.<br /> <br /> If one of your Lair Traits is already present in a scene, you can invoke as many of the others as allowed by your Lair without a cost or a roll.<br /> <br /> If you're in the location one of your Chambers is based on or a location similar to it, you can spend a point of Satiety and roll Wits + Resolve modified by the degree to which the location matches the original site; if you're not using the initial basis for the Chamber itself, this also costs a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> A space being resonant requires it to have one of your Lair Traits present, and is both a requirement for incorporating a new Chamber into your Lair as well as the means by which you can spend Willpower to use the Satiety Expenditure effects of your Atavisms a limited number of times per scene; for the latter purpose, your Lair itself always counts as resonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:23:15-07:00","id":1331860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1331850#post1331850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If one of your Lair Traits is already present in a scene, you can invoke as many of the others as allowed by your Lair without a cost or a roll.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally what I meant above, so let's use an example, my beast has a smoke grenade and the trait Fog in the form of a haze of smoke, using the grenade would make any location resonant with the Fog trait and allow the beast to then use a number lair traits within the limits imposed by my beast current Lair rating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:39:37-07:00","id":1331866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1331860#post1331860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally what I meant above, so let's use an example, my beast has a smoke grenade and the trait Fog in the form of a haze of smoke, using the grenade would make any location resonant with the Fog trait and allow the beast to then use a number lair traits within the limits imposed by my beast current Lair rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The area has been made resonant by the presence of the Trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:53:13-07:00","id":1331869,"title":"","content":"Ok, I understand now, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-23T08:28:18-07:00","id":1332289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1330796#post1330796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular merits/skills/atavisms/etc you think are a must-have for a black widow type of beast? Thinking a seduce-trap-consume modus operandi, still ironing out the details. This is my first Beast character so trying to figure out what're the good stuff and what're the stuff that just seems good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alien Allure + Basilisk\u2019s Touch + Ravenous Maw is your basic bed-\u2018em-kill-\u2018em-eat-\u2018em Atavism combo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T10:49:19-07:00","id":1332449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1332289#post1332289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alien Allure + Basilisk\u2019s Touch + Ravenous Maw is your basic bed-\u2018em-kill-\u2018em-eat-\u2018em Atavism combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caught in the Webs wouldn't go amiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-25-2019, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T13:13:37-07:00","id":1333156,"title":"","content":"What family would a Giant Wasp creature horror be in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25438-justasplanned","name":"JustAsPlanned","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T13:51:27-07:00","id":1333163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JustAsPlanned</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1333156#post1333156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What family would a Giant Wasp creature horror be in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which part it emphasises. That it's a giant? Anakim. That it flies? Ugallu. That it's a big fuck-off bug? Namtaru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T13:59:00-07:00","id":1333164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JustAsPlanned</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1333156#post1333156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What family would a Giant Wasp creature horror be in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... if it is a <b>Giant</b> Wasp that just comes for you huge and imposing making you see the hopelesness of trying to fight or resist it then it is Anakim.<br /> <br /> If it is a Giant <b>Wasp</b> that looks upon you with it\u2019s compound eyes, legs twitching and its stinger dripping foul venom it is a Namtaru.<br /> <br /> If it is a Giant Wasp whose buzzing you constantly hear and are unable to escape because it always catches up and sees you then it is an Ugallu.<br /> <br /> If it despite it\u2019s size always creepy up on you, stinging you when you least expect it then it could be an Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> So all in all it can be many things, almost any family can suit it depending on what kind of terror it inspires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T13:09:04-07:00","id":1333292,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was flitting between those three. Namtaru seems to fit what I had in mind most. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25438-justasplanned","name":"JustAsPlanned","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T13:17:08-07:00","id":1333427,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit on Satiety expenditure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25600-redtooth-redtooth","name":"Redtooth-Redtooth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T16:02:09-07:00","id":1333439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redtooth-Redtooth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-que