uote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1338602#post1338602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That make sense, point taken!<br /> Thanks Neos01!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem \ud83d\udc4d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T11:26:13-08:00","id":1352653,"title":"","content":"If a Beast with the Minions or Thralls Lair Trait is Slumbering, do the Minions/Thralls still obey the human part of the Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:18:02-08:00","id":1352713,"title":"","content":"Probably not, given that the human half of the Beast is not immune to their Lair Traits under those circumstances","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T17:41:34-08:00","id":1355728,"title":"","content":"Can we expect more books for Beast or the ones we have are the ones we get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T00:07:09-08:00","id":1362806,"title":"","content":"So, how would you go about forging platonic metals as a beast? I mean, you could open a door into twilight and move metal in-and-out till it 'melts' down into it's platonic form?<br /> <br /> Beyond that either Anakim or Eshmaki should be able to use atavisms like titanic strenngnth, dragonfire, and mimir's wisdom to further shape it if needed?<br /> <br /> That also opens way for further astral forging, like trying to merge astral archetypes with pefect metals, or using Salamander fires in the process. <br /> <br /> How would you go about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T17:25:58-08:00","id":1362974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1355728#post1355728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we expect more books for Beast or the ones we have are the ones we get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eventually sure, but I will admit not being aware of any off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362806#post1362806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how would you go about forging platonic metals as a beast? I mean, you could open a door into twilight and move metal in-and-out till it 'melts' down into it's platonic form?<br /> <br /> Beyond that either Anakim or Eshmaki should be able to use atavisms like titanic strenngnth, dragonfire, and mimir's wisdom to further shape it if needed?<br /> <br /> That also opens way for further astral forging, like trying to merge astral archetypes with pefect metals, or using Salamander fires in the process.<br /> <br /> How would you go about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>First things first, what are platonic metals in this sense? Only thing I was able to get were like, tin, lead, and copper; which if you wanted to forge as a Beast I don't see why you'd need more than the normal methods. (Maybe using the Lair tricks to bypass security to a good forge or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T17:34:32-08:00","id":1362976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1355728#post1355728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we expect more books for Beast or the ones we have are the ones we get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Working on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T17:35:39-08:00","id":1362977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362974#post1362974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First things first, what are platonic metals in this sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">perfected metals</a>.<br /> <br /> Barring some dramatic paradigm shift that might involve mummies, you can't open a door into Twilight with the tools available to you as a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T17:58:38-08:00","id":1362981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362977#post1362977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/&quot;]perfected</a> metals[/URL].<br /> <br /> Barring some dramatic paradigm shift that might involve mummies, you can't open a door into Twilight with the tools available to you as a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can open one into the Shadow, though, which would also satisfy the 'convert to ephemera and back' thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T18:08:07-08:00","id":1362983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362977#post1362977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">perfected metals</a>.<br /> <br /> Barring some dramatic paradigm shift that might involve mummies, you can't open a door into Twilight with the tools available to you as a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, hadn't heard the term before myself.<br /> <br /> I mean you technically could, but it would require a few hoops like having a Lair Chamber in the Twilight or a gate that opens into the Twilight. (Same principle for the Shadow and Underworld.) Neither option are really practical though as it'll eat through your Willpower fast.<br /> <br /> Though I didn't see anything in the entry saying the perfected metals can't be forged with in ways that aren't normal aside from traits. You wouldn't be able to make amalgams with them, heramium's desire to mix with everything aside. Aside from that seems like it would be normal use of Beast tricks to forge stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T02:11:00-08:00","id":1363047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362977#post1362977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring some dramatic paradigm shift that might involve mummies, you can't open a door into Twilight with the tools available to you as a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, iirc, a Beast can physically enter the Astral, and the Astral is an ephemeral realm. The only question is if the WYSIWYG principles of the Astral might interfere with the material/ephemeral conversion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362983#post1362983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean you technically could, but it would require a few hoops like having a Lair Chamber in the Twilight or a gate that opens into the Twilight. (Same principle for the Shadow and Underworld.) Neither option are really practical though as it'll eat through your Willpower fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason Satchel mentioned a paradigm shift involving mummies is because mummies are the only ones that interact with Twilight as if it was a different location, and notably only as a means to reach a place to which they are metaphysically bound. For everyone else Twilight is simply how you interact with the world rather than a world of its own, and thus you shouldn't be able to create a Chamber in Twilight. It'd just be a Chamber of that physical location. It'd only include Twilight of the relevant &quot;frequency&quot;. (Which actuallly sounds pretty interesting for Beasts who have ghosts or spirits as Lair inhabitants, and even more interesting if it's the &quot; frequency&quot; tied to Dreamborn as the Horror would then be in Twilight within its own Lair.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-24-2020, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T04:23:25-08:00","id":1363053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362977#post1362977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sheer-perfection-signs-of-sorcery-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">perfected metals</a>.<br /> <br /> Barring some dramatic paradigm shift that might involve mummies, you can't open a door into Twilight with the tools available to you as a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeap sorry<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. that's the stuff. I was thinking 'perfected metals' myself, but then remembered that there is 'practice of perfecting' and thought I was remembering it wrong. Taking into account what the Perfected Metals are, 'Platonic Metals' came to mind. After all those things are indeed idealized materials, pushed to their perfect expressions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1362983#post1362983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, hadn't heard the term before myself.<br /> <br /> I mean you technically could, but it would require a few hoops like having a Lair Chamber in the Twilight or a gate that opens into the Twilight. (Same principle for the Shadow and Underworld.) Neither option are really practical though as it'll eat through your Willpower fast.<br /> <br /> Though I didn't see anything in the entry saying the perfected metals can't be forged with in ways that aren't normal aside from traits. You wouldn't be able to make amalgams with them, heramium's desire to mix with everything aside. Aside from that seems like it would be normal use of Beast tricks to forge stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's just quite a few splats have their own 'technology'. be it mage enchantments, werewolf fetishes, and whatever mummies and sin eaters use. In addition, many Anakim legends are closely linked to crafting (mostly metalwork) like giants and cyclops. So was thinking about the 'technology' beasts could make.<br /> Now, ancasus artifacts are a given, but those things are more of a part of spells then anything else. So what I came up with were astral forging and perfected metals.<br /> <br /> Perfected metals arre actually pretty easy to make as long as you can move things into ephemeral state. Considering how mobile beasts are, they should be able to do that. First of all, doesn't beast layer count as an 'ephemeral state' itself? so bringing those metals in the layer and leaving them in there to 'melt' down should be enough. barring that, you could move them to Shadow and back a dozen times. Taking into account Beasts aren't mages, making it that slow would be appropriate. So a beast would have to move metal between realms a few dozen times to purify it.<br /> <br /> If needed a forging process could be summarized with 'Forge' merit with 1-5 points? that could include small portal to 'smelt' the metal, instruments and maybe some helpers like small metal spirits, nightmares of industry or maybe at the top level a Salamander homeboy? Salamanders are Dreaming Earth rank 4 fire elemental that can also live in the spirits attuned with forging (prerequisite high craft?) and can both reach into real world and actually purify metals into 'platonic' (not perfected) form that is easy to enchant. <br /> <br /> The next step would be to incorporate perfected metals into abcasus rights, or maybe for making astral fetishes or something like that. Would be nice way to introduce a way to make unique equipment for beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 01-24-2020, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T17:10:40-08:00","id":1364643,"title":"","content":"Thing I'm toying with doing, and wondering if we have one and/or if it would be something people would be interested in. In character introduction to being a Beast. Don't have a character in mind or anything and only barebones framework just wondering on opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:05:09-08:00","id":1366629,"title":"","content":"Is there any default rule to how Beasts resolve conditions like Addicted that have the resolution of &quot;Gain integrity, lose integrity, or exceptional a breaking point&quot;? By a strict 1 to 1, that'd mean spending or gaining Satiety would resolve it, but that doesn't seem right to me (it's too easy). Is that covered in the books at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T14:21:12-08:00","id":1366634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1366629#post1366629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any default rule to how Beasts resolve conditions like Addicted that have the resolution of &quot;Gain integrity, lose integrity, or exceptional a breaking point&quot;? By a strict 1 to 1, that'd mean spending or gaining Satiety would resolve it, but that doesn't seem right to me (it's too easy). Is that covered in the books at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not believe this is ever addressed. One potential solution could be &quot;Gain and then resolve either the Slumbering or Ravenous Condition.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T17:59:08-08:00","id":1369067,"title":"","content":"so yall know how Horrors can come into form from modern fears and emerging cultures? do yall think it's possible that there is a Makara Horror that is Sharktopus? this is a serious question","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T18:17:42-08:00","id":1369070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1369067#post1369067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so yall know how Horrors can come into form from modern fears and emerging cultures? do yall think it's possible that there is a Makara Horror that is Sharktopus? this is a serious question</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T18:19:38-08:00","id":1369071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1369070#post1369070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Absolutely.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you. I was kinda afraid I was the only one who had this thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T18:28:14-08:00","id":1369073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1369071#post1369071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thank you. I was kinda afraid I was the only one who had this thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anything showing up in a horror movie, or horror-comedy movie, can definitely qualify. What Horrors are, are supposed to be nightmares. And people can have nightmares over a wide variety of things. None of them need to physically exist.<br /> <br /> If you've got questions as to &quot;How can this be scary?&quot; Well... Ask the player. They should be able to answer that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T17:03:51-08:00","id":1369930,"title":"","content":"About the Inverted from the Player's Guide (I'm guessing there's nothing official on these, so I'm just fishing for other people's thoughts): <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They lose their Satiety Pool, should that mean they're reduced to just the base Attribute when using Nightmares? This feels like Nightmares would be so weak as to almost be not worth mentioning...</li> <li>Could they acquire new Nightmares and/or Atavisms? I think learning Nightmares makes sense, but the Horror doesn't seem likely to undergo the mutation necessary to gain new Atavisms while it's busy being impaled.</li> <li>&quot;The Inverted\u2019s Lair persists, though he can\u2019t make it larger&quot;. The obvious meaning is that they can't add new Chambers, but does it also mean they can never increase their Lair rating?</li> <li>Kinship isn't mentioned at all. Should they still be able to establish Family-Ties and use Kinship abilities not dependent on Satiety expenditure?</li> <li>Is the idea of an Inverted player-character problematic? (Yes, the answer is yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.)</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T00:10:18-08:00","id":1369989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1369930#post1369930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Inverted from the Player's Guide (I'm guessing there's nothing official on these, so I'm just fishing for other people's thoughts): <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They lose their Satiety Pool, should that mean they're reduced to just the base Attribute when using Nightmares? This feels like Nightmares would be so weak as to almost be not worth mentioning...</li> <li>Could they acquire new Nightmares and/or Atavisms? I think learning Nightmares makes sense, but the Horror doesn't seem likely to undergo the mutation necessary to gain new Atavisms while it's busy being impaled.</li> <li>&amp;quot;The Inverted\u2019s Lair persists, though he can\u2019t make it larger&amp;quot;. The obvious meaning is that they can't add new Chambers, but does it also mean they can never increase their Lair rating?</li> <li>Kinship isn't mentioned at all. Should they still be able to establish Family-Ties and use Kinship abilities not dependent on Satiety expenditure?</li> <li>Is the idea of an Inverted player-character problematic? (Yes, the answer is yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.)</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>In the chronicle i m currently running i houseruled that inverted can place family ties only on heroes.<br /> This gives them access to special nightmares and kinship merits.<br /> One of this merits give the ability to devour the heart chamber of a diying beast, allowing you to add it to your lair and to use exp to increase the lair score","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T02:31:02-08:00","id":1370009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1369930#post1369930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They lose their Satiety Pool, should that mean they're reduced to just the base Attribute when using Nightmares? This feels like Nightmares would be so weak as to almost be not worth mentioning...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, just the Attribute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could they acquire new Nightmares and/or Atavisms? I think learning Nightmares makes sense, but the Horror doesn't seem likely to undergo the mutation necessary to gain new Atavisms while it's busy being impaled. </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The obvious meaning is that they can't add new Chambers, but does it also mean they can never increase their Lair rating? </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kinship isn't mentioned at all. Should they still be able to establish Family-Ties and use Kinship abilities not dependent on Satiety expenditure? </div> </div> </div>No, their Horror is almost dead and their connection to the Primordial Dream all but gone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the idea of an Inverted player-character problematic? (Yes, the answer is yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.) </div> </div> </div>Unless the character is in a very particular type of game with a specific story around wanting to murder as many Beasts as possible before dying in a blaze of glory (or forgotten in a back alley), yes.<br /> <br /> The Inverted aren\u2019t really any kind of \u2018win\u2019 condition, except for the personal satisfaction of refusing to follow the burdens upon you and choosing your own, very brief and outnumbered, path. Any player who wants to run an Inverted should have a serious conversation with their ST about what they\u2019re looking for in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T07:05:36-08:00","id":1370047,"title":"","content":"<i>What</i> are and <i>where</i> are in <b>Beast</b> <b>Player's Guide</b> are Inverted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T07:56:45-08:00","id":1370053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1370047#post1370047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>What</i> are and <i>where</i> are in <b>Beast</b> <b>Player's Guide</b> are Inverted?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 161. It's a weird Inheritance where the Beast puts their Horror in a half-dead state so that they don't have to feed it any more, but they keep some of it's powers so they can hunt other Beasts. They end up as a weird Beast-Hero hybrid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 02-24-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T19:27:38-07:00","id":1374040,"title":"","content":"Alright, my inner power-gamer keeps bugging me about this:<br /> <br /> Obcasus Rites probably should <i>not </i>benefit from mundane merits like Patient or Good Time Management, correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T19:38:38-07:00","id":1374044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1374040#post1374040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, my inner power-gamer keeps bugging me about this:<br /> <br /> Obcasus Rites probably should <i>not </i>benefit from mundane merits like Patient or Good Time Management, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ....Why not? Legitimate question back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T20:33:58-07:00","id":1374053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1374044#post1374044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....Why not? Legitimate question back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly because there's a note in VtR 2e's Blood Sorcery section that specifies that unless a Merit that applies to extended actions specifically calls out blood sorcery it doesn't benefit the roll.<br /> <br /> If that is the case, it's worth noting that blood sorcery is the only form of extended ritual magic so far that adds a third component to its roll; Obcasus Rites have very stringent requirements for where they can be performed, come with built-in penalties that need a variety of circumstances to mitigate, and run on a two-component dicepool that uses the lower of two Skills; Shadow Rites likewise only use a two-component dicepool (albeit a more flexible one) and <i>automatically fucks up their interactions with the Shadow for a bit</i> if the performance is interrupted.<br /> <br /> Other gamelines' ritual magic is resolved as an instant action with a time investment, but between Vampire, Werewolf, and Beast, there's little to indicate that the gameline where ritual magic is in and of itself <i>a religious practice</i> is going to have particularly much go bad if you can spend a little longer or work a little faster in the consecrated space of the temple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T20:59:01-07:00","id":1374056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1374044#post1374044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ....Why not? Legitimate question back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because an ability to &quot;manage deadlines&quot; doesn't seem like it would help you call down the eldritch powers of the Dark Mother any faster. There's no other mechanical means of speeding up the process, so it'd be weird for this one dot mundane merit to cut the time in half. And I'm always wary of allowing a ability obviously meant for mundane activities to be used for supernatural ones. Similar reservations apply for the Patient merit.<br /> <br /> And now I'm picturing the Dark Mother looming over an initiate like &quot;It's okay pumpkin, take all the time you need!&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Just occurred to me that there is in fact a built in way of speeding up the rites...namely having a better die pool so you finish in fewer rolls. Maybe I'm just overly suspicious of my own power-gaming tendencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 03-11-2020, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T22:03:01-07:00","id":1374064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1374056#post1374056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because an ability to &quot;manage deadlines&quot; doesn't seem like it would help you call down the eldritch powers of the Dark Mother any faster. There's no other mechanical means of speeding up the process, so it'd be weird for this one dot mundane merit to cut the time in half. And I'm always wary of allowing a ability obviously meant for mundane activities to be used for supernatural ones. Similar reservations apply for the Patient merit.<br /> <br /> And now I'm picturing the Dark Mother looming over an initiate like &quot;It's okay pumpkin, take all the time you need!&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Just occurred to me that there is in fact a built in way of speeding up the rites...namely having a better die pool so you finish in fewer rolls. Maybe I'm just overly suspicious of my own power-gaming tendencies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't worry about it too much. If it is an extended roll, then I absolutely would allow Merits that affect extended rolls to affect these rolls. If there is no calling out of specific exceptions...<br /> <br /> And yeah, I can see an ability to &quot;manage deadlines&quot; as helping. I don't strictly see it as &quot;calling down the eldritch powers of the Dark Mother faster&quot; so much as simply being more efficient with your approach. You get any equipment you need lined up and ready. Any sacrifices are already acquired. You've got written notes to help keep yourself organized and prepared on what steps to take.<br /> <br /> Seems like simple project management to me. Yeah, I'd let my players make use of those merits for these rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T02:16:13-07:00","id":1375043,"title":"","content":"Extended actions are such an utter nuisance in cofd, that encourage optimizing as hard as you can, that I am all for taking whatever advantage you can by RAW to make the tediousness go by faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T13:11:09-07:00","id":1375138,"title":"","content":"Just a little thematic question. So Eshmaki, fear of the darkness, of the horrors in the darkness. How does Relentless hunter fit in as a Family Atavism? I have trouble seeing how it's not Anakim instead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T14:53:39-07:00","id":1375150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1375138#post1375138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a little thematic question. So Eshmaki, fear of the darkness, of the horrors in the darkness. How does Relentless hunter fit in as a Family Atavism? I have trouble seeing how it's not Anakim instead</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fond of denoting the core five Families in terms of their relative position, e.g. the Ugallu are fears from above, the Makara are fears from below, etc.<br /> <br /> The Anakim are frontal sorts of terror. The Eshmaki are fears from <i>behind.</i><br /> <br /> The Lurkers are frightening because they come out of your blindspot and you don't know how long you can evade them -- they're arguably the best-fit Family for the Hunger for Prey, and being able to resume pursuit an arbitrary amount of time after taking a mortal blow feeds into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixing mobile autocorrect. 03-16-2020, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T16:45:29-07:00","id":1375172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1375150#post1375150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fond of denoting the core five Families in terms of their relative position, e.g. the Ugallu are fears from above, the Makara are tears from below, etc.<br /> <br /> The Anakim are frontal sorts of terror. The Eshmaki are fears from <i>behind.</i><br /> <br /> The Lurkers are frightening because they come out of your blindspot and you don't know how long you can evade them -- they're arguably the best-fit Family for the Hunger for Prey, and being able to resume pursuit an arbitrary amount of time after taking a mortal blow feeds into that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it feeds into the idea that the no matter how much much damage you do to the monster, it will simply retreat back into the unknowable dark, and come back as if you did nothing. It's less &quot;it doesn't matter what I do, it just tanks through it&quot; and more &quot;every damn time we get close to killing it, it just runs away and comes back as fine as ever. And none of us are brave enough to follow it into the dark&quot;. Correct?<br /> <br /> Also, that's a nice way of denoting them, I've never thought of them that way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T17:39:39-07:00","id":1375185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1375172#post1375172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it feeds into the idea that the no matter how much much damage you do to the monster, it will simply retreat back into the unknowable dark, and come back as if you did nothing. It's less &quot;it doesn't matter what I do, it just tanks through it&quot; and more &quot;every damn time we get close to killing it, it just runs away and comes back as fine as ever. And none of us are brave enough to follow it into the dark&quot;. Correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. As literal monsters out of nightmare whose powers are themed around their home-field advantage, most Beasts don't play fair, but the Eshmaki in particular are built to make people jump at shadows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, that's a nice way of denoting them, I've never thought of them that way </div> </div> </div>The introduction of the Talassi and the Inguma makes it a little less useful as a simplest-terms metric, but the Captors coming at you from either side rounds out the straightforward exterior set, and the Outsiders being fear-from-inside-other-people makes for a nice complement to the Namtaru's fear-from-inside-yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T17:46:37-07:00","id":1375188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1375185#post1375185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. As literal monsters out of nightmare whose powers are themed around their home-field advantage, most Beasts don't play fair, but the Eshmaki in particular are built to make people jump at shadows.<br /> <br /> The introduction of the Talassi and the Inguma makes it a little less useful as a simplest-terms metric, but the Captors coming at you from either side rounds out the straightforward exterior set, and the Outsiders being fear-from-inside-other-people makes for a nice complement to the Namtaru's fear-from-inside-yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the comparison you draw with the Inguma and Namtaru<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I tend to think of Eshmaki too much as in terms of &quot;darkness=stealth&quot; rather than the fear of darkness representing the idea of hidden, unknown dangers that lurk just beyond us, hoping we get close (or us hoping they dont come out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:36:55-07:00","id":1391902,"title":"","content":"Core book says that a beast in the hedge can shape it as a changeling with high wyrd does.<br /> Now, with changeling 2ed out, do you think it would be fair to allow beast to hedgespin using satiety instead of glamour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:42:01-07:00","id":1391911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1391902#post1391902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core book says that a beast in the hedge can shape it as a changeling with high wyrd does.<br /> Now, with changeling 2ed out, do you think it would be fair to allow beast to hedgespin using satiety instead of glamour?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300369#post1300369\">Did this one last year</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T23:11:07-07:00","id":1392129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1391911#post1391911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1300369#post1300369&amp;quot;]Did</a> this one last year[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>It s a good way to handle it.<br /> As an alternative, do you think that it would be interesting to let the beast roll and spend one satiety to gain the benefit of the resonant option of the primordial cult merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T14:17:37-07:00","id":1392315,"title":"","content":"The way I handle it is that the Hedge spins itself when the Beast enters or does things that would normally trigger that, tending towards making changes conducive to the Beast's nature (but not always directly beneficial).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T08:05:24-07:00","id":1396680,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit curious about Beast but what does a standard game looks like?<br /> <br /> Like if I'm going to let the characters do personal stuff and take it easy between two &quot;spikes&quot; in terms of drama and opposition, what kind of routine stuff would Beasts be up to?<br /> <br /> <b>Example: </b>Say the Beasts have shown the error of their ways to a brutal crime family and I've got an idea for an epic monster slayer in the Greek mythological style to come after them. But between these two kind of &quot;spikes&quot; I want something that's more routine to let them develop characters, do some personal side stuff for their characters, develop some relations with NPCs they got interested in and so on. But I don't want it to be so calm that they'll get bored. So what could be thrown in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T16:52:38-07:00","id":1396749,"title":"","content":"A big theme in Beast for our group is the found family dynamic. Our PC's all have very different lifestyles and opinions on what being a beast means so much of the tension in the game comes from this family drama. For example my character (Makara Punisher) is trying to have a family with a police officer and has a ten-year old child. She has to deal with the split between this life and her Legend, which she previously pursued through her job as a Prosecutor until she lost her job. By comparison her &quot;brother&quot; is a homeless Wendigo (Anakim Hunter) who is building a serial killer cult of personality. They often disagree, but between &quot;spikes&quot; as you put it both are trying to build their legend in different ways, sometimes helping each other and sometimes interfering. The Player Guide has a good optional rule to guide this in the form of the Four Paths (page 162.) When there is no opposition it provides a mechanical incentive to explore some themes of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T20:30:23-07:00","id":1396795,"title":"","content":"I'm the storyteller for the game Strictura is in and I pretty much agree with what they said but with a little bit more emphasis on what they only touched on and that's theme. Theme is going to be the the question or the idea you always come back to in your chronicle and it's going to determine what scenes and dialogue you're going to prepare for and steer your players towards. I want to take your example and with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1396680#post1396680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Example: </b>Say the Beasts have shown the error of their ways to a brutal crime family and I've got an idea for an epic monster slayer in the Greek mythological style to come after them. But between these two kind of &quot;spikes&quot; I want something that's more routine to let them develop characters, do some personal side stuff for their characters, develop some relations with NPCs they got interested in and so on. But I don't want it to be so calm that they'll get bored. So what could be thrown in?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in your example, you want to follow up your mafia-style game with an epic monster slayer in the Greek style, this is going to have more of focus on Heroes, Beasts, and possibly the people that are subject to both their whims. Another concept is that of tragedy in Greek mythology for both the Hero and the Beast, the idea that their lives were always subject to fate and there was nothing really they could do even when they fight harder against it. But with all Greek myths, they have some kind of setup, a prophecy that needs fulfilling but is ignored, powerful monster-slaying relics, and the torment in which the people are subjected to either by your characters Beasts or someone else. These are just some ideas you can play off that are relatively low stakes but can establish your next chronicle while exploring your player's characters.<br /> <br /> Another question you asked was what a standard Beast game looks like. Like any of the other supernatural game lines in WoD this really depends on the storyteller, but I would direct your attention to the tagline that the game has &quot;A storytelling game of endless hunger.&quot; This, I believe, is what makes Beast the Primordial and is the connecting concept in all the games. The Beasts hunger for fear, The Heroes hunger for recognition, The Dark Mother hungers for something we cannot possibly understand, but even everyday people want something and this takes centre stage in most games. Why do the characters in the game do this is what makes the story and that's definitely something I focus on in my game as Strictura has said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T03:14:48-07:00","id":1396842,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13329_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13329\" data-vbnamecard=\"13329\">Strictura</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13444_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13444\" data-vbnamecard=\"13444\">zannmato</a> <br /> <br /> Thanks guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This has given some food for thought and perspective on the matter and I will keep chewing on this and come back if I've got more questions.<br /> <br /> The part on endless hunger is of course interesting and I suppose its the great temptation to abandon the teaching part of the Beast's existance and just give in to being a, well, monster until taken down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T14:08:27-07:00","id":1397575,"title":"","content":"Please confirm or correct my understanding here. If a Beast *wants* their beast &quot;form&quot; to be shown.. to show a giant etc.. for a while, is that possible either when physical or in dream/lair?<br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5930-deathchipmunk","name":"DeathChipmunk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T15:49:45-07:00","id":1397587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathChipmunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397575#post1397575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please confirm or correct my understanding here. If a Beast *wants* their beast &amp;quot;form&amp;quot; to be shown.. to show a giant etc.. for a while, is that possible either when physical or in dream/lair?<br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>The beast enters his Horror form upon entering his Lair. Otherwise he cannot do so<br /> <br /> Upon using atavisms in the physical world, supernatural creatures will be able to see the Horror from superimposed over the human form. Regular Mortals wont see anything except a man somehow breathing fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T17:10:17-07:00","id":1397594,"title":"","content":"The Nightmare &quot;Behold my True Form&quot; does this, but in deadly fashion. Beasts have the innate ability to mimic and pass for other supernatural creatures as per the Family Resemblance ability on page 88 of the core rule book so it seems Beasts are designed to blend in with other descendants of the Dark Mother rather than reveal themselves (not to say they can't.) But they are expressly hidden from Mortals most of the time. To riff on what was originally posted by DeathChipmunk: Anakim have the Looming Presence Atavism which does make them Giant, but to the Mortals subconscious.<br /> <br /> Successfully reaching some of the &quot;end-game&quot; states can make the Horror manifest in the real world, for example the Beast Rampant, but although these states are achievable in game they are also pretty unplayable.<br /> <br /> If your intent is to reveal what you really are to a Mortal for a reason other than feeding a story path to this would be to make them not mortal anymore, with all the attached baggage of say: having your vampire BFF embrace your love interest or have your mage friend turn your mother into a Sleepwalker etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T18:06:26-07:00","id":1397599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397594#post1397594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nightmare &quot;Behold my True Form&quot; does this, but in deadly fashion. Beasts have the innate ability to mimic and pass for other supernatural creatures as per the Family Resemblance ability on page 88 of the core rule book so it seems Beasts are designed to blend in with other descendants of the Dark Mother rather than reveal themselves (not to say they can't.) But they are expressly hidden from Mortals most of the time. To riff on what was originally posted by DeathChipmunk: Anakim have the Looming Presence Atavism which does make them Giant, but to the Mortals subconscious.<br /> <br /> Successfully reaching some of the &quot;end-game&quot; states can make the Horror manifest in the real world, for example the Beast Rampant, but although these states are achievable in game they are also pretty unplayable.<br /> <br /> If your intent is to reveal what you really are to a Mortal for a reason other than feeding a story path to this would be to make them not mortal anymore, with all the attached baggage of say: having your vampire BFF embrace your love interest or have your mage friend turn your mother into a Sleepwalker etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could bring them into the Lair, I mean holding the door would preserve them from the dangers there and all that while the Beast merges with their other half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T02:05:30-07:00","id":1397643,"title":"","content":"Also a good point nalak42. There was a particularly memorable moment in our campaign where I swallowed a group of NPCs using Ravenous Maw. Saved them from danger and no doubt traumatised them for life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T12:20:54-07:00","id":1397787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397643#post1397643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a good point nalak42. There was a particularly memorable moment in our campaign where I swallowed a group of NPCs using Ravenous Maw. Saved them from danger and no doubt traumatised them for life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh true doesn't Ravenous Maw's satiety spend send things you swallow to the Lair?<br /> <br /> That would be a hell of a way to prove it. &quot;I'm actually a monster.&quot;<br /> &quot;No you're not.&quot;<br /> <i> Grabs person and shoves them into their mouth like an oreo and swallows them. Shows up in Nightmare Lair a couple minutes later.</i><br /> &quot;Now do you believe me?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T16:03:22-07:00","id":1397837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397787#post1397787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh true doesn't Ravenous Maw's satiety spend send things you swallow to the Lair?<br /> <br /> That would be a hell of a way to prove it. &quot;I'm actually a monster.&quot;<br /> &quot;No you're not.&quot;<br /> <i> Grabs person and shoves them into their mouth like an oreo and swallows them. Shows up in Nightmare Lair a couple minutes later.</i><br /> &quot;Now do you believe me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it'd definitely be at least slightly traumatizing, especially if the NPC your coming out to is particularly close (such as a best friend). I mean, wouldn't <i>you</i> be terrified if your bestie revealed themselves to be a monster via swallowing you whole and sending you to a nightmare realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T00:41:03-07:00","id":1397908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397787#post1397787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh true doesn't Ravenous Maw's satiety spend send things you swallow to the Lair?<br /> <br /> That would be a hell of a way to prove it. &quot;I'm actually a monster.&quot;<br /> &quot;No you're not.&quot;<br /> <i> Grabs person and shoves them into their mouth like an oreo and swallows them. Shows up in Nightmare Lair a couple minutes later.</i><br /> &quot;Now do you believe me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarifying.<br /> <br /> Your friend would split from the roof of their mouth to the bottom of their genitals into a gigantically wide and probably toothy vertical maw that the human mind is not used to perceiving because verticality is not something we're biologically prepared for mouth-wise, be shoved into said vertical hell maw, and arrive bewilderingly Not Dead(?<sup>tm</sup>) in a hostile environment Your Friend Almost Assuredly Did Not Invite Them In For.<br /> <br /> There are problems to address following this instance regardless of benevolent, malevolent, or indifferent intent.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually making a point, I'm just amused by how the action is horrifying regardless of context in that twisted way I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:34:35-07:00","id":1397996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397908#post1397908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your friend would split from the roof of their mouth to the bottom of their genitals into a gigantically wide and probably toothy vertical maw that the human mind is not used to perceiving because verticality is not something we're biologically prepared for mouth-wise, be shoved into said vertical hell maw, and arrive bewilderingly Not Dead(?<sup>tm</sup>) in a hostile environment Your Friend Almost Assuredly Did Not Invite Them In For.<br /> <br /> There are problems to address following this instance regardless of benevolent, malevolent, or indifferent intent.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually making a point, I'm just amused by how the action is horrifying regardless of context in that twisted way I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! I agree. Especially since a Beast's Lair is a portion of the Primordial Dream that said Begotten has claimed as their territory and modified to fit with their Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T16:02:36-07:00","id":1398077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1397908#post1397908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarifying.<br /> <br /> Your friend would split from the roof of their mouth to the bottom of their genitals into a gigantically wide and probably toothy vertical maw that the human mind is not used to perceiving because verticality is not something we're biologically prepared for mouth-wise, be shoved into said vertical hell maw, and arrive bewilderingly Not Dead(?<sup>tm</sup>) in a hostile environment Your Friend Almost Assuredly Did Not Invite Them In For.<br /> <br /> There are problems to address following this instance regardless of benevolent, malevolent, or indifferent intent.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually making a point, I'm just amused by how the action is horrifying regardless of context in that twisted way I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the birght side you can probably claim that spot as a Lair chamber rather easily at that point, so going in won't take too long. You may have to pay therapy bills though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T21:14:14-07:00","id":1398284,"title":"","content":"Hahahaha. It was... great. Especially since the rest of the family were waiting in that chamber to say hi, so to extend the above delicious description from ArcaneArts they would also wake up being looked at curiously by a gargantuan white serpent with red eyes, a slavering Wendigo, a shifting humanoid mass of worms and a sludgy glowing mass of radioactive concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":13329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","user":"Strictura","date":". 06-23-2020, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T06:36:11-07:00","id":1398344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1398284#post1398284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahahaha. It was... great. Especially since the rest of the family were waiting in that chamber to say hi, so to extend the above delicious description from ArcaneArts they would also wake up being looked at curiously by a gargantuan white serpent with red eyes, a slavering Wendigo, a shifting humanoid mass of worms and a sludgy glowing mass of radioactive concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeyup, definitely traumatizing. Also, what does your Horror look like? Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"Terro