tent":"I m confused by the way heroic tracking and stalking is supposed to work.<br /> Let s say in a medium city, 8km of diameter, a Beast creates a disturbance by inflicting nightmare rules (pag 99).<br /> The Hero arrives to the victim, who probably have never meet the Beast, an then what?<br /> With a lair of 2 or 3 the Beast could be literally anywhere in the city, and the Hero has no way or power to restrict the research area as i remember.<br /> Am i missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T06:53:26-07:00","id":1411342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411331#post1411331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m confused by the way heroic tracking and stalking is supposed to work.<br /> Let s say in a medium city, 8km of diameter, a Beast creates a disturbance by inflicting nightmare rules (pag 99).<br /> The Hero arrives to the victim, who probably have never meet the Beast, an then what?<br /> With a lair of 2 or 3 the Beast could be literally anywhere in the city, and the Hero has no way or power to restrict the research area as i remember.<br /> Am i missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hero is now within a range of the Beast and has begun investigating a type of monster that runs on infamy.<br /> <br /> Unless the character is extremely lucky, the switch to Heroic Stalking is going to reveal that she has used Atavisms or Nightmares in places or been nearby; Heroic Stalking, like Demonic spoofing in reverse, is an uncontested and unresisted roll whose only available counter-influence comes in the form of what modifiers you can bring to bear (i.e. stay high-Satiety, don't be super-Famous, don't gather multiple Beasts in one place, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T09:49:36-07:00","id":1411363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411342#post1411342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hero is now within a range of the Beast and has begun investigating a type of monster that runs on infamy.<br /> <br /> Unless the character is extremely lucky, the switch to Heroic Stalking is going to reveal that she has used Atavisms or Nightmares in places or been nearby; Heroic Stalking, like Demonic spoofing in reverse, is an uncontested and unresisted roll whose only available counter-influence comes in the form of what modifiers you can bring to bear (i.e. stay high-Satiety, don't be super-Famous, don't gather multiple Beasts in one place, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but stalking rolls costs 1 willpower and the book doesn t define the range.<br /> Also it can detect power usage in the last 24 hours.<br /> From what i can read a Hero could exhaust himself for months without detecting anything in a city if the power range is too short.<br /> With a very long range instead the Hero would feel the beast but identify her within a city block would be almost impossible.<br /> In a rural area maybe it would be easier, but within the city of the example i don t understand how it is supposed to work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T20:10:43-07:00","id":1411458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411363#post1411363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but stalking rolls costs 1 willpower and the book doesn t define the range.<br /> Also it can detect power usage in the last 24 hours.<br /> From what i can read a Hero could exhaust himself for months without detecting anything in a city if the power range is too short.<br /> With a very long range instead the Hero would feel the beast but identify her within a city block would be almost impossible.<br /> In a rural area maybe it would be easier, but within the city of the example i don t understand how it is supposed to work</div> </div> </div> </div>Computer ate my previous attempt to post this, but:<br /> <br /> <i>If a Hero is Stalking you, they know you by name, physical description, or personal encounter.</i> If they have been drawn to an area by your activity and you are not yet aware of their presence they are able to gather information about you by asking around, listening to rumors, leveraging followers, and so on.<br /> <br /> Heroic Tracking works by drawing a Hero to the relevant person or location in a region of a Beast's activity. It is not difficult to infer a similar level of &quot;accuracy&quot; (albeit narrower in range) for Stalking's ability to suss out the presence of nearby Beasts or recent activity in the Primordial Dream of the same general area; pinning it down from within a neighborhood or a block or an apartment complex isn't out of sorts with the role the power plays in the narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T23:03:00-07:00","id":1411477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411458#post1411458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Computer ate my previous attempt to post this, but:<br /> <br /> <i>If a Hero is Stalking you, they know you by name, physical description, or personal encounter.</i> If they have been drawn to an area by your activity and you are not yet aware of their presence they are able to gather information about you by asking around, listening to rumors, leveraging followers, and so on.<br /> <br /> Heroic Tracking works by drawing a Hero to the relevant person or location in a region of a Beast's activity. It is not difficult to infer a similar level of &quot;accuracy&quot; (albeit narrower in range) for Stalking's ability to suss out the presence of nearby Beasts or recent activity in the Primordial Dream of the same general area; pinning it down from within a neighborhood or a block or an apartment complex isn't out of sorts with the role the power plays in the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if i understand it rightly you think that once inside the city of my example the hero could use heroic stalking in any part of the city and the power would pinpoint to a specific neighboorhood?<br /> Also do you think that stalking range gets narrower as the hero gets closer to the beast. ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 09-02-2020, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T23:21:11-07:00","id":1411479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411477#post1411477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if i understand it rightly you think that once inside the city of my example the hero could use heroic stalking in any part of the city and the power would pinpoint to a specific neighboorhood?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fundamentally misunderstanding the point of Heroic Stalking if you have to use it to figure out what neighborhood a character lives in.<br /> <br /> Again, a Hero does not progress to Stalking until they have a name, physical description, or personal observation to go on \u2014 Heroic Tracking is everything from the first ping to gathering information from locals and rumor, and Stalking only comes into play when they've gotten close enough to start confirming their target.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also do you think that stalking range gets narrower as the hero gets closer to the beast. ? </div> </div> </div>I think it's inherently narrower than the [Lair] miles/&quot;within the same region&quot; range that prompts the initial bout of Heroic Tracking, which is as fuzzy as it needs to be for as much ground as a Beast covers in any given story. A Hero who is Stalking a Beast has a lead and is now doing the smart thing by feeling out their target instead of immediately leaping to open conflict with a powerful foe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T05:42:38-07:00","id":1411493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411479#post1411479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fundamentally misunderstanding the point of Heroic Stalking if you have to use it to figure out what neighborhood a character lives in.<br /> <br /> Again, a Hero does not progress to Stalking until they have a name, physical description, or personal observation to go on \u2014 Heroic Tracking is everything from the first ping to gathering information from locals and rumor, and Stalking only comes into play when they've gotten close enough to start confirming their target.<br /> I think it's inherently narrower than the [Lair] miles/&amp;quot;within the same region&amp;quot; range that prompts the initial bout of Heroic Tracking, which is as fuzzy as it needs to be for as much ground as a Beast covers in any given story. A Hero who is Stalking a Beast has a lead and is now doing the smart thing by feeling out their target instead of immediately leaping to open conflict with a powerful foe.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then... why doesn t peaceful or lazy Beasts feeds only by letting their horrors inflicting nightmares?<br /> If they are careful going to ravenous is very unlikely, and even when they gain an eceptional success the only clue that the hero could gain is the visual appearance of the horror, described by a victim who doesn t know the beast, and nobody else could give a clue about a beast who doesn t feed openly.<br /> Also, the book says that Beasts cannot run this kind of lifestyle for fear of Hero retributions, but with those mechanics and the Beast living even in a small city for a hero it would be very hard to gain the details of the beast necessary to progress to stalking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T07:45:40-07:00","id":1411505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411493#post1411493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then... why doesn t peaceful or lazy Beasts feeds only by letting their horrors inflicting nightmares?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, for one thing, &quot;lazy&quot; falls on the other side of the Satiety scale from &quot;Horror is feeding on its own&quot; and &quot;peaceful&quot; is not going to easily describe a character who saw the true shape of their soul and decided &quot;nightmare monster inflicted upon the world&quot; was a thing they could accept being and expanded their Lair to the point where their victims aren't being drawn purely from within a mile or two of where they sleep.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are careful going to ravenous is very unlikely, </div> </div> </div>What &quot;careful&quot; is there to be in doing nothing to feed your Horror yourself?<br /> <br /> If you only feed through Inflicting Nightmares, you're going to fail rolls eventually and drop to Ravenous \u2014 or worse, eat the wrong person's soul and fall to Slumbering \u2014 and in the meantime you're incentivized to use your more obvious powers and feed your Hunger in petty ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and even when they gain an eceptional success the only clue that the hero could gain is the visual appearance of the horror, </div> </div> </div>This is a hell of an assumption to make. A nightmare is more than just the monster that shows up at the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> described by a victim who doesn't know the beast, </div> </div> </div>This is also a hell of an assumption to make. It feeds on a random available person within range, jumping to the first person within range if they're not available, and the examples suggest &quot;random&quot; still favors people relevant to the story by their acquaintance with the Beast. Either you're hitting someone you know or you're creating a series of incidents that narrow the field to where you sleep at night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and nobody else could give a clue about a beast who doesn t feed openly. </div> </div> </div>Another hell of an assumption. Beasts have an Anchor built around being scary in a particular way, interact with strange people and real estate, and benefit from being Known to a moderate degree, including deliberately raising their Lair rating. It may take a little longer, but the process of investigation will eventually develop a lead, because this is a storytelling game where this plot is introduced at the Storyteller's discretion and players are presumably playing Beasts because they wanted to play Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the book says that Beasts cannot run this kind of lifestyle for fear of Hero retributions, but with those mechanics and the Beast living even in a small city for a hero it would be very hard to gain the details of the beast necessary to progress to stalking. </div> </div> </div>Again, Beasts can't run the kind of lifestyle where they <i>set their Horror on human enemies</i> because there tends to be a connection to follow for any Hero who comes knocking.<br /> <br /> <br /> The basic social contract of &quot;we agree to play the damn game&quot; is in effect \u2014 if you're playing Beast and you're running a character who ignores the entire set of mechanics around Satiety as a roleplaying guide and otherwise runs their character as a human with a Lair that they expand but barely use and an unruly pet heart-monster that they don't want to feed, it should be obvious that there will be problems that force the Storyteller to rely on characters' offscreen awareness of your unconscious behaviors to lead a Hero to the alarm you're setting off in the Primordial Dream by starving yourself.<br /> <br /> This is not a simulation. Attracting a Hero brings a threat to the area that makes feeding yourself more dangerous because they're in the area and looking for you. You can skip town or spend a couple weeks crashing on your broodmate's couch or take your chances gambling on repeat feedings or tap into the hive to disperse the signal with Willpower, but it's become a thing you have to deal with until the Hero's gone. That's the point of the mechanic: The Hero is in town and that makes things marginally more difficult for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T09:22:50-07:00","id":1411514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1411505#post1411505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, for one thing, &amp;quot;lazy&amp;quot; falls on the other side of the Satiety scale from &amp;quot;Horror is feeding on its own&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;peaceful&amp;quot; is not going to easily describe a character who saw the true shape of their soul and decided &amp;quot;nightmare monster inflicted upon the world&amp;quot; was a thing they could accept being and expanded their Lair to the point where their victims aren't being drawn purely from within a mile or two of where they sleep.<br /> What &amp;quot;careful&amp;quot; is there to be in doing nothing to feed your Horror yourself?<br /> <br /> If you only feed through Inflicting Nightmares, you're going to fail rolls eventually and drop to Ravenous \u2014 or worse, eat the wrong person's soul and fall to Slumbering \u2014 and in the meantime you're incentivized to use your more obvious powers and feed your Hunger in petty ways.<br /> <br /> This is a hell of an assumption to make. A nightmare is more than just the monster that shows up at the end.<br /> <br /> This is also a hell of an assumption to make. It feeds on a random available person within range, jumping to the first person within range if they're not available, and the examples suggest &amp;quot;random&amp;quot; still favors people relevant to the story by their acquaintance with the Beast. Either you're hitting someone you know or you're creating a series of incidents that narrow the field to where you sleep at night.<br /> <br /> Another hell of an assumption. Beasts have an Anchor built around being scary in a particular way, interact with strange people and real estate, and benefit from being Known to a moderate degree, including deliberately raising their Lair rating. It may take a little longer, but the process of investigation will eventually develop a lead, because this is a storytelling game where this plot is introduced at the Storyteller's discretion and players are presumably playing Beasts because they wanted to play Beasts.<br /> <br /> Again, Beasts can't run the kind of lifestyle where they <i>set their Horror on human enemies</i> because there tends to be a connection to follow for any Hero who comes knocking.<br /> <br /> <br /> The basic social contract of &amp;quot;we agree to play the damn game&amp;quot; is in effect \u2014 if you're playing Beast and you're running a character who ignores the entire set of mechanics around Satiety as a roleplaying guide and otherwise runs their character as a human with a Lair that they expand but barely use and an unruly pet heart-monster that they don't want to feed, it should be obvious that there will be problems that force the Storyteller to rely on characters' offscreen awareness of your unconscious behaviors to lead a Hero to the alarm you're setting off in the Primordial Dream by starving yourself.<br /> <br /> This is not a simulation. Attracting a Hero brings a threat to the area that makes feeding yourself more dangerous because they're in the area and looking for you. You can skip town or spend a couple weeks crashing on your broodmate's couch or take your chances gambling on repeat feedings or tap into the hive to disperse the signal with Willpower, but it's become a thing you have to deal with until the Hero's gone. That's the point of the mechanic: The Hero is in town and that makes things marginally more difficult for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must disagree on the &quot;hell of an assumption&quot;.<br /> Even if a Beast starts with all of the &quot;good&quot; intention, his Horror hungers could bring her to a point in which she refuses to feed anymore.<br /> It s one of the key assumptions for introducing the 3 new kinds of inheritances in the player guide and also this kind of inner conflict could lead to a good narration in fact.<br /> Also from Conquering hero, when the Sheperd gaze gift is described we can infer that a hero only gets a bonus for identifying the beast from watching a nightmare.<br /> But i also agree with you on the very key point of the matter that in fact solves anything.<br /> We can also infer from the core book example of mrs winters that the inflicting nightmare target is not totally a random guy, but at least a person with whom the Beast has interacted.<br /> If a hero know this the disturbances caused by inflicting nightmare rolls becames much more dangerous.<br /> Thank you for the insight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T20:29:40-07:00","id":1420068,"title":"","content":"Say a Beast enters the Astral via some means other than their Lair, such that their body is unconscious somewhere in the physical, while their consciousness is a Dream Form in the Astral. They then open a Primordial Pathway and enter their Lair, as a Dream Form. They then open a Pathway back to the physical. When they leave the second Pathway, what happens? Do they snap back to their body, regardless of their relative location? Do they stay as a Dream Form, probably in Astral-phase Twilight? Or is the Dream From simply blocked from exiting the Pathway into the physical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T18:08:10-07:00","id":1420189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420068#post1420068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a Beast enters the Astral via some means other than their Lair, such that their body is unconscious somewhere in the physical, while their consciousness is a Dream Form in the Astral. They then open a Primordial Pathway and enter their Lair, as a Dream Form. They then open a Pathway back to the physical. When they leave the second Pathway, what happens? Do they snap back to their body, regardless of their relative location? Do they stay as a Dream Form, probably in Astral-phase Twilight? Or is the Dream From simply blocked from exiting the Pathway into the physical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick question for clarification. Are you asking if a Beast enters the astral but as an entity seperate from their body and their Horror, or are scenarios where the beghotten just enters the astral through a portal made by someone else viable for your scenario?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 10-25-2020, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T18:33:24-07:00","id":1420192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420189#post1420189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick question for clarification. Are you asking if a Beast enters the astral but as an entity seperate from their body and their Horror, or are scenarios where the beghotten just enters the astral through a portal made by someone else viable for your scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former, I think.<br /> <br /> The actual scenario that came up in play had a Beast using Skeleton Key on a Synese, which are a kind of Astral portal from Mage. They &quot;provide direct access to an Astral Realm. Synesi allow anyone with the Key or another means of entrance to enter the linked realm while sleeping or meditating. Travelers don\u2019t physically enter the Astral through a Synese, but enter the usual trance state for Astral journeys.&quot; So the Beast hacked his way through the Synese, leaving his body unconscious on the floor, while his mind as a Dream Form got up to some shenanigans in the Tenemos. He had to retreat from some angry cat dreamborn (long story), so opened a Pathway back to his Lair. Rather than trek across the Nightmare to get back to the Tenemos and then leave through the Synese, he opened another Pathway back to his body in the physical. At which point I realized I wasn't sure what would happen when his Dream Form and body started existing on the same metaphysical layer of reality. (The situation is especially trippy because one of his Chambers is based on the physical site of the Synese. Though I don't think that changes the outcome.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T19:28:29-07:00","id":1420196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420192#post1420192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual scenario that came up in play had a Beast using Skeleton Key on a Synese, which are a kind of Astral portal from Mage. They &quot;provide direct access to an Astral Realm. Synesi allow anyone with the Key or another means of entrance to enter the linked realm while sleeping or meditating. Travelers don\u2019t physically enter the Astral through a Synese, but enter the usual trance state for Astral journeys.&quot; So the Beast hacked his way through the Synese, leaving his body unconscious on the floor, while his mind as a Dream Form got up to some shenanigans in the Tenemos. He had to retreat from some angry cat dreamborn (long story), so opened a Pathway back to his Lair. Rather than trek across the Nightmare to get back to the Tenemos and then leave through the Synese, he opened another Pathway back to his body in the physical. At which point I realized I wasn't sure what would happen when his Dream Form and body started existing on the same metaphysical layer of reality. (The situation is especially trippy because one of his Chambers is based on the physical site of the Synese. Though I don't think that changes the outcome.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in this case there's cause to conclude that the Beast entered bodily, given the usual use-context of Skeleton Key, the usual use-context of Synesi, and the fact that Beasts don't have any innate sense for magical gateways to expand the use of Skeleton Key; a Synese is more like a locus than a Hedge Gate in this fashion, and I wouldn't treat a Locus the same as a Shadowed Door for the purposes of Skeleton Key, either.<br /> <br /> &quot;This shouldn't have happened&quot; is a bit of a too-late thing to say here, but unless you actually want to explore complications from this string of events as an in-game thing it would probably be wise to just elide past the fact that being in an altered state is a non-negotiable part of using a Synese and lean into the fact that every use of Skeleton Key (including the one that doesn't actually get you into the thing that's normally on the other side of the threshold) allows you bodily entry into the Primordial Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T20:50:03-07:00","id":1420212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420196#post1420196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in this case there's cause to conclude that the Beast entered bodily...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd considered that possibility, but ultimately went with having the Synese function &quot;normally&quot; because it's a Beast NPC in a party of Mages, so I wanted the astral travel to function, more-or-less, on typical Mage terms. (Evidently I failed to be consistent in this regard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.) Rather than continue to bog down the discussion with the weird circumstances of my chronicle, sufficeth to say that the possibility of Dream Forms leaving the astral via Pathway was a legitimate question that arose.<br /> <br /> So, without all the fluff, the question is simply: What happens to a Dream Form when it travels from the Astral to the Physical via a Primoridal Pathway?<br /> <br /> Edit: Barring a ruling with better citations, I think I'll go with the following: if the external end of the Pathway contains the traveler's body, the Dream Form merges with the body and &quot;wakes up&quot;, similar to how a Beast merges with it's Horror in a Pathway. Otherwise, the Dream Form enters astral-Twilight, similar to Dreamborn during the odd case when they are pulled into the physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 10-26-2020, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T21:33:41-07:00","id":1420214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420212#post1420212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, without all the fluff, the question is simply: What happens to a Dream Form when it travels from the Astral to the Physical via a Primoridal Pathway?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, unless this scenario has gotten even more convoluted and the Beast being in his Lair didn't merge his Dream Form with his Horror because of Slumbering or other very specific circumstances. Beasts can get away with this \u2014 their approach to the Astral is fundamentally different to how the Awakened experience it, after all, the root example of which is &quot;these people can enter the Astral bodily.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shakier ground may be found for what would happen to any astral-projected mages ejected from an open Pathway into the material, but that's more of a question for the Mage version of this thread. The Beast is opening a Pathway from his Lair to the location of his physical body while (presumably) merged with his Horror, so the worst case scenarios that spring to mind are all relatively minor things like losing a dot of Satiety or suffering the side-effects of the Dark Mother's Guidance or taking a Condition that drives him to fulfill his Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T23:07:29-07:00","id":1420217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420192#post1420192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The former, I think.<br /> <br /> The actual scenario that came up in play had a Beast using Skeleton Key on a Synese, which are a kind of Astral portal from Mage. They &quot;provide direct access to an Astral Realm. Synesi allow anyone with the Key or another means of entrance to enter the linked realm while sleeping or meditating. Travelers don\u2019t physically enter the Astral through a Synese, but enter the usual trance state for Astral journeys.&quot; So the Beast hacked his way through the Synese, leaving his body unconscious on the floor, while his mind as a Dream Form got up to some shenanigans in the Tenemos. He had to retreat from some angry cat dreamborn (long story), so opened a Pathway back to his Lair. Rather than trek across the Nightmare to get back to the Tenemos and then leave through the Synese, he opened another Pathway back to his body in the physical. At which point I realized I wasn't sure what would happen when his Dream Form and body started existing on the same metaphysical layer of reality. (The situation is especially trippy because one of his Chambers is based on the physical site of the Synese. Though I don't think that changes the outcome.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, so I checked the player's guide as that has the whole section on trying to leave the Lair while merged with a Horror and there's not much else about a Beghotten having a form in the astral. It kind of runs into the issue that the Devouring is stated to be the last time a Beghotten Dreams and the Horror eating and replacing their soul/whatever passed for a soul essnetially leads to the bit that the Horror would be the dream form the Beghotten would take.<br /> <br /> This is a complication since the Horror can't leave the Lair, so technically what this would likely do is dreamform the mages into the Astral Realm or whatever and the Beghotten would &quot;wake up&quot; being their Horror wandering the Lair. Considering the dreamform wouldn't normally exist I'd say entering the Lair of course leads to merger and returning to the material plane would result in just a snap back to the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T09:30:19-07:00","id":1420276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420217#post1420217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so I checked the player's guide as that has the whole section on trying to leave the Lair while merged with a Horror and there's not much else about a Beghotten having a form in the astral...</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 151, Leaving the Lair: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a Beast leaves her Lair without using a Primordial Pathway, she separates from her Horror and leaves it behind in her Chambers while she wanders the wider dreamscape as a Dream Form. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420214#post1420214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't, unless this scenario has gotten even more convoluted and the Beast being in his Lair didn't merge his Dream Form with his Horror because of Slumbering or other very specific circumstances. Beasts can get away with this \u2014 their approach to the Astral is fundamentally different to how the Awakened experience it, after all, the root example of which is &quot;these people can enter the Astral bodily.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shakier ground may be found for what would happen to any astral-projected mages ejected from an open Pathway into the material, but that's more of a question for the Mage version of this thread. The Beast is opening a Pathway from his Lair to the location of his physical body while (presumably) merged with his Horror, so the worst case scenarios that spring to mind are all relatively minor things like losing a dot of Satiety or suffering the side-effects of the Dark Mother's Guidance or taking a Condition that drives him to fulfill his Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>After the Player's Guide, my understanding that it's only when in a Lair/Chamber/Pathway that the normal Astral mechanics of Dream Form get sidestepped. As soon as the Beast (and presumably anyone else physically in the Lair) exits the Lair into the Astral proper, they leave their body behind like 90% of other means of astral travel. In any case, the Core book makes it sound like it's not that uncommon for Dream Forms (Beast or otherwise) to end up inside a Lair (Dream Form section page 99).<br /> <br /> I phrased my question initially to apply to Beasts, since I thought that would be the most generally applicable version of the question (though it raised the question of getting a Beast into their Lair as a Dream Form in the first place), but the thrust of the scenario in my Chronicle is that the players were rescuing a mortal who'd been trapped in the Astral without natural means to return to his body. So the ultimate concern was what would happen to the dream form of the mortal when pathway-ed back to the physical. While that scenario is a bit niche, I still think the question is a valid one, since the Core explicitly says that Dream Forms in the Lair is a thing that happens.<br /> <br /> I did think about the question from the Mage perspective, where their general rule for Astral entities is that, on the rare occasion they leave the Astral, they enter Twilight. So far as I know, Mage does not actually have much precedent for things physically entering or leaving the Astral. In any case, Beast doesn't seem to have actually considered the question either, so I'll stick with my ruling for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T09:50:19-07:00","id":1420280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1420276#post1420276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, Beast doesn't seem to have actually considered the question either, so I'll stick with my ruling for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the scenario has gotten even weirder, because Beast's primary way of addressing foreign Dream Forms in the Lair is that they're food and someone getting &quot;killed&quot; while in Dream Form outside of their own dreams wakes up with the Soul-Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> Like, the book doesn't necessarily address this situation directly in the same way that the mechanics of how easy or hard it is for strangers to get into your Lair are a little unclear, but basic door security and the fact that you have to dedicate conscious attention to marking people as guests and making your Horror not do as it pleases in the Lair means Astral intruders are generally going to be dispatched in short order well before being dumped into the material world is a problem.<br /> <br /> Prior examples of the Golden Road suggest your reading is probably the way to handle this particular conundrum, but either this wasn't a simple question or the consequences of Astral death were being drastically overestimated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T08:50:44-08:00","id":1422430,"title":"","content":"Aha! Behold, Changeling 2e:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Occasionally, an oneiropomp careens all the way back to the mortal world \u2014 if she was in dream form at the time, she exists in Twilight and must return to her body before her player can make the roll to wake her up. </div> </div> </div>(I came across this completely randomly. Why was I reading Changeling when I've already said I'm running a Mage game? Reasons. Reasons is why.) Assuming the metaphysics of a Dream Form originating from the Gate of Ivory are much the same as an Astral Dream Form, I think this is our answer: Dream Forms that wind up in the physical enter the appropriate phase of Twilight, and must return to their body before they can make the usual role to &quot;wake up&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 11-07-2020, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T17:48:10-08:00","id":1422519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1422430#post1422430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aha! Behold, Changeling 2e:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (I came across this completely randomly. Why was I reading Changeling when I've already said I'm running a Mage game? Reasons. Reasons is why.) Assuming the metaphysics of a Dream Form originating from the Gate of Ivory are much the same as an Astral Dream Form, I think this is our answer: Dream Forms that wind up in the physical enter the appropriate phase of Twilight, and must return to their body before they can make the usual role to &quot;wake up&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel this is correct. This scenario actually happened in a recent Changeling game I ran where several of the Player characters ended up falling out of a collapsing dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T05:27:26-08:00","id":1426228,"title":"","content":"Do you think it s possible to use Basilisk touch to poison the tip of an arrow/blade and then injecting the poison with an attack of the weapon in the following turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T20:51:16-08:00","id":1426280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1426228#post1426228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it s possible to use Basilisk touch to poison the tip of an arrow/blade and then injecting the poison with an attack of the weapon in the following turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it depends on the level you're using the atavism at. Technically nothing in actual wording of the ability says that's possible, so this is very much an ST call. From my own I might allow it at the Satiety expenditure level, due to the thematic mention of the Beast dripping poison and such. That said I'm iffy on the tactic as a whole because the ability is inherantly a touch attack, and so there isn't really a point to it in my mind. I mean the point of applying poison to a weapon would be to get the poison into a person's system when other methods don't work, but since all you need is physical contact the blade isn't necessary as a delivery option, especially as you can Basilisk Touch turn one and slash turn two as opposed to the proposed plan which requires two turn to accomplish the plan assuming the roll goes to plan.<br /> <br /> So the only advantage to being able to envenom other objects would be to either A) Gain a large supply of poison that basically can't be taken from you, or detected on you. And B) turning it into a ranged power, which again your ST might object to based on how much of a problem the Tilts the ability applies would be for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T23:25:14-08:00","id":1426291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1426280#post1426280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, it depends on the level you're using the atavism at. Technically nothing in actual wording of the ability says that's possible, so this is very much an ST call. From my own I might allow it at the Satiety expenditure level, due to the thematic mention of the Beast dripping poison and such. That said I'm iffy on the tactic as a whole because the ability is inherantly a touch attack, and so there isn't really a point to it in my mind. I mean the point of applying poison to a weapon would be to get the poison into a person's system when other methods don't work, but since all you need is physical contact the blade isn't necessary as a delivery option, especially as you can Basilisk Touch turn one and slash turn two as opposed to the proposed plan which requires two turn to accomplish the plan assuming the roll goes to plan.<br /> <br /> So the only advantage to being able to envenom other objects would be to either A) Gain a large supply of poison that basically can't be taken from you, or detected on you. And B) turning it into a ranged power, which again your ST might object to based on how much of a problem the Tilts the ability applies would be for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but considering that it s possible to buy or craft a poison of similar toxicity with the Streetwise or Science/medicine skill the ST should not be worried about the Tilts impact.<br /> Another thing is that if you have dots in athletic or weaponry but not brawl the power could be more versatile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 11-27-2020, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T17:02:22-08:00","id":1426883,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the Players Guide yet, so I apologize if this is directly answered there, but.. the discussion on here has made me wonder. Can a Beast have Chambers in it's Lair from all around the globe? More specifically, can an Apex?<br /> <br /> I run a DC comics based RP group, and I didn't have an Apex for Gotham and the Metropolis in the past (Batman is the modern day one, despite the big secret that it is human). When the new families and hungers were revealed, I decided on a Lair 10 Inguma Whisper, the Phantom Stranger. His design is perfect (even if I have yet to actually read some of his powers or even his x and y splat write-up), but one feature I gave him was that each of his seven Chambers was from a different part of the globe. He is a wanderer, settling down and creating ripples and often chaos wherever he goes, revitalizing his legend, then a few days later is across the world in a different place doing the same thing. In my head, he was the Apex of at least a majority of the cities where his Chambers spawned from, and he is known among supernatural and mortals alike. <br /> <br /> However, after reading this thread, I'm not sure if having Chambers that far apart is appropriate, especially for an Apex. Can someone clarify this for me? Is it possible? If so, does his Lair effectively link ALL the Hives in his seven cities? Can he do this, but only be Apex of one Hive? Is the whole thing against the RAW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T18:16:00-08:00","id":1426889,"title":"","content":"Disregarding some of the homebrew, the short answer is that yes, a Beast can have chambers across the whole world-and even across different worlds (Chambers in the Shadow/Underworld/Hedge/Odd corners of the cosmology), can serve as the Apex of multiple Hives, and as such would be the wheel hub of all those Hives.<br /> <br /> The longer answer is the same....with a notation that this is a <i>lot</i> of heavy lifting for a Beast to get up to. While their Lair is collective, the Beast effectively has to become a whispered big deal in all those cities-You don't get to be Apex without having a reputation, and building the Lair necessary for that span of real estate likewise for that number of chambers means that's a lot of legend building. The main reason a lot of Beasts focus on one area is that it's easier to cultivate coherent and prominent Legend/Lair while still having time to attend to their Life or, you know. Have some time off. A Beast whose establishing their Lair in multiple cities has to account for whether or not those have synergy of story spread-If you have seven chambers across NYC, Boston, Baltimore and a few other New ENgland cities, it's not impossible for those to flow more synergistically with each other, but if a Beast has one chamber in NYC and another in Tokyo, conventionally those are not going to help feed each other organically, or at least easily. The nature of the astral allowing for magnified waves and the global effect of the news and the internet definitely help, but if a Beast is operating globally, they're still basically having to run all over the place to keep themselves prominent urban legends and nightmares despite those advantages.<br /> <br /> The final interesting twist is the effect being an Apex across multiple cities and therefore uniting different Hives together would have, but since we lack written text on that, it's the realm of speculation/storyteller judication.<br /> <br /> So TL;DRing all of that, it basically means that while it's doable, it's a <i>lot of work</i> to establish and maintain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T18:55:55-08:00","id":1426894,"title":"","content":"More prosaically:<br /> <br /> The book indicates in one or two places that Beasts tend to feel uncomfortable spreading themselves too thin, Lair-wise, and your personal Chambers are technically as much vulnerabilities as places of power for you specifically. Every Chamber is a place where someone can more easily get into your Lair, and the more you use them, the more likely someone is to cotton onto that. Heightened defensibility is one of the more obvious reasons for a common Lair structure being one &quot;front door&quot; and a bunch of more obscure Chambers that you don't typically use for transport, and that's a lot harder to pull off without particularly convoluted Burrow management if you're splitting that role between seven different areas.<br /> <br /> Maintaining the geographic Apex in multiple locales is a requirement that makes this harder still, because Destabilization is going to make that either a full-time job or given up as a loss outright. You can more easily be the Apex of one city with Chambers in other areas, but that only connects those hives in the same way that any Lair would. Even the Old Man of the Mountains doesn't fuck around to that degree, not least because there's no definite point to risking your Incarnation on that kind of flex.<br /> <br /> Inguma being what they are, you could definitely manage something with international crime/fixing/etc, but you don't need outright overseas Chambers for that \u2014 that's what hunting to build up a better similarity modifier is for, and it works as well for connecting transAtlantic wharves to each other as it does for linking your forest to the woods on the other side of town. (If there's an Antarctic Chamber, though, that's definitely a strong candidate for insulating the Heart without dipping into other dimensions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T13:47:24-08:00","id":1427024,"title":"","content":"Thank you. Arc and Satchel, you two have always been my favorites,and I appreciate the insight. So it all boils down to whether the Phantom Stranger can maintain Apex status in a world without Internet to help spread his legend..<br /> <br /> He definitely does the legwork. I imagine he's always at low Satiety except in rare occasions, because a Lair 10 beast is hard to keep fed. As a Whisper, he doesn't usually have to worry about hiding bodies or dealing with huge legal ramifications, especially back in 1912. Plus, his Atavisms are almost unfair. He can ignore the need to eat, drink, or sleep, provided he is stalking someone to gain their dirty secrets. Is it a glitch or a meant feature, that having Eyes of Heaven and Mimit's wisdom means he can just... Know those secrets by being around people, and thus feed his hunger without even really trying?; I found it odd that I think Mimit's Wisdom let's you touch someone and find out their secrets, and Whispers need that to feed.it almost seems OP, unless I am reading it wrong and it somehow breaks the RAW. <br /> <br /> So long and short of it, as a non-Apex,he is most certainly still possible, but as Apex of multiple cities, the caveat is that he has to sufficiently annoy/disrupt/affect all of these cities on a regular basis, and will have little &quot;downtime&quot; doing so? I don't often design a powerstat 10 Npc, but it seemed to fit him, and as a character concept of the literal embodiment of the stranger that shows up and knows everything, I think that's possible. He's not outright a douche, but he had a habit of just showing up and telling people the secrets they need to keep the story going, then disappears, letting people ask &quot;who the f was that guy...&quot;. And he does it often, at least daily for his feeding. And across the globe. And in every city,he is still a foreigner, an alien, and nobody besides a few learned monsters know how he knows what he knows. Does that qualify him, if most monsters and police/criminals are half excited and half afraid he can just show up at any time and spoiler their plans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T19:01:30-08:00","id":1427082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1427024#post1427024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a glitch or a meant feature, that having Eyes of Heaven and Mimit's wisdom means he can just... Know those secrets by being around people, and thus feed his hunger without even really trying?; I found it odd that I think Mimit's Wisdom let's you touch someone and find out their secrets, and Whispers need that to feed.it almost seems OP, unless I am reading it wrong and it somehow breaks the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember the way feeding works \u2014 feeding the Hunger for Secrets requires the target to <i>know that someone knows their secret</i>, you don't make a feeding roll unless the Satiety potential is above your current Satiety, base Satiety potential scales proportionately with difficulty, and the roll happens at the end of the scene unless you spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> The Stranger, like many high-Lair-low-average-Satiety Beasts, is going to have to make a lot of little rolls often, tilt his Aspirations toward his Hunger, rope in other monsters for Family Dinner, lean hard into his Legend, Life, and/or Myth, and make use of Lair resonance for the Satiety Expenditure effects of his Atavisms to keep up with the demands of Lair 10 with or without Incarnation safeguarding him from becoming fully Ravenous, on top of being a fairly constant beacon for Heroic attention in his area (which might not be a problem for him personally, but will definitely make trouble for any other Beasts active in the area).<br /> <br /> At the very least, his shtick seems like it would strongly benefit from maintaining some Horrorspawn (particularly if he's not going to be using that top half of his Satiety track anyway), but those present their own tricky balancing act to manage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So long and short of it, as a non-Apex,he is most certainly still possible, but as Apex of multiple cities, the caveat is that he has to sufficiently annoy/disrupt/affect all of these cities on a regular basis, and will have little &quot;downtime&quot; doing so? I don't often design a powerstat 10 Npc, but it seemed to fit him, and as a character concept of the literal embodiment of the stranger that shows up and knows everything, I think that's possible. He's not outright a douche, but he had a habit of just showing up and telling people the secrets they need to keep the story going, then disappears, letting people ask &quot;who the f was that guy...&quot;. And he does it often, at least daily for his feeding. And across the globe. And in every city,he is still a foreigner, an alien, and nobody besides a few learned monsters know how he knows what he knows. Does that qualify him, if most monsters and police/criminals are half excited and half afraid he can just show up at any time and spoiler their plans? </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a character you're going to have to paint around as much as with \u2014 if this guy's not just an Apex but Incarnate then he's sharing a level of storied infamy with the likes of Bigfoot and Nessie while sporting a Hunger that people aren't likely to want to talk specifics about if they don't have to, which means probably engaging with some Elf-On-The-Shelf Santa's-Watching-You levels of inspired paranoia and implicit or explicit conspiracy that practically demands leveraging some degree of symbolism.<br /> <br /> There's a reason a lot of the things Beasts resonate with in mythology are temple guardians \u2014 if he's gone worldwide in the years before American commercial airlines, it's not inconceivable that on some distant shore, a band of thieves with no personal affiliation to him keeps a little wall fixture bearing his mark around as an apotropaic against double-dealing or snitching or attending meetings undisguised, because his Legend is such that he's become a kind of patron saint of secret-keeping. (He's not a Nemesis, but neither are most Beasts who partake of lesson culture, and most humans don't know the difference, much less the ones consuming the whisper-down-the-lane fringes of a Myth.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T20:10:49-08:00","id":1435145,"title":"","content":"Kind of wondering something aftter a discussion I had with fellow players on a game, you know how Geist, Changeling and Werewolf have group specific merits? you know, Motley, Pack and Krewe merits, do Beasts have any of those?<br /> <br /> To be honest I could only think of Obcasus Rites since those work better with a Brood, I could maybe make a case for shared lairs in a brood and Lair Merits, but I can't recall there being anything saying that they can be shared by the brood if any of the brood gets them.<br /> <br /> So the question would be, are there any Brood specific merits? was it ever going to be a thing for them at all?<br /> <br /> I not saying that there aren't thing already there for helping broods, plenty of stuff is already innate with the Lair Trait immunity being the first one that comes to mind, just wondering if there were ideas for some Brood merits....or am I not understanding some of the merits in the Player's Guide? (Can't think of any specific merits for broods in the Core)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T22:46:32-08:00","id":1435158,"title":"","content":"Just like with Mortals the storyteller can allow some merits to be shared (Safe Place, Allies, Status etc.) In our Beast Game the PC's all have a stake in a Community Center that forms a joined pathway to their shared Lairs (i.g. one has a Chamber linked to the Theater, another to the alley behind it etc.) As part of the time invested in creating this place by deliberately causing fear to make chambers, Safe Place also applies to the mundane amenities and security of the building.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any beast specific merits though. Doesn't mean a story teller can't make a ruling. Primordial Cult (from the Players Guide) for example is built from the ground up to be about one Beast. But since Beast's represent stories about heros confronting the things that go bump in the night I would allow players with two very strongly conjoined beasts to take it together. Two Beasts tying their legends together is a big thing - that would be a big part of a story in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T14:13:27-08:00","id":1437388,"title":"","content":"So, I have been considering coming up with custom lair traits, but the rules for making new ones are kind of...unclear to say the least, unless I missed my mark, rules for making new traits can be found in Pg. 101 of the Beast core book, below you can see what the book says on those, I can't find anything else, if you know of somewhere else I would like to know because I want to know about Traits that give skill or attribute bonus<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">Minor:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Lair Traits are always possible in the physical world </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">without the use of magic. They may provide dice penalties or </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">bonuses to Skills, or count as Extreme Environments </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">(see p. </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">171 )</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> up to level 2.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">Major:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Lair Traits may (but don\u2019t always) impose Tilts that </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">aren\u2019t physically possible; anything from turning the skin of </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">victims to salt to acidic rain. They may provide dice penalties or </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">bonuses to Attributes or derived traits like Speed and Defense, </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">or count as Extreme Environments up to level 4</span><br /> <br /> My main question here, is how much of a bonus can a Lair Trait give for either Minor or Major lair traits, besides those two texts I haven't been able to find any more details and not to beat on it again, but it's a rather vague ruling here and not quite clear.<br /> <br /> I mean, what are the limits? how much is too much when trying to give bonus using lair traits specially when it comes to Major traits?<br /> <br /> Like, plenty of stuff weakens a target, like Infected giving -3 to stamina, what if you come up with a beast that has a legend for healing, so out come the Healing lair trait that gives minor regeneration healing Lethal in hours rather than days to all involved for a Major trait, or you come up with a beast whose legend is about empowering their minions and allies, so he get the Invigorating lair trait giving +X bonus to Strength. I mean, I get the ideas but don't know how to set the limits or where they are at all<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T14:52:15-08:00","id":1437393,"title":"","content":"Thematically Lair traits are about the Beast's Lair being a hostile environment for their enemies. I feel they wouldn't help others heal, or the Beast heal for that matter - that is the purview of spending Satiety or an Atavism. A Lair trait about healing is more likely to be one that prevents it, or causes uncontrolled and damaging cell growth or mutations. When looking to make my own I took the average effects of the existing ones, the bonuses or penalties they levy, and the example extreme environments as the guide on what is balanced. Ultimately playing with them in combination with other traits and abilities in the game is going to be the real test but as long as the ST and all the Players agree it can be used, then have at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T15:22:49-08:00","id":1437397,"title":"","content":"And there aren't places that creatures can draw power from? that instead of a harmful trait it turns to be a possitive one for the creature? Like a Locus for Werewolves or a Demesne (is that the word?) for a Mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T20:04:34-08:00","id":1437418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437388#post1437388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, what are the limits? how much is too much when trying to give bonus using lair traits specially when it comes to Major traits?</div> </div> </div> </div>The modifier is presumably the same, because a modifier to Skill rolls and a modifier to Attribute rolls or derived traits are substantially different in scope. Assume, as with Circumstance and Equipment, anything flatly adding or subtracting more than three dice is a Big Fucking Deal, like the Darkness Lair Trait representing it being pitch dark in the affected areas. It's likewise safe to assume (for reasons discussed anon) that any bonuses a Lair Trait offers are just things about the environment that someone could exploit against vulnerable targets, like how Wanton, Competitive, and Bestial make it easier for certain actions rolled against you to be exceptionally successful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437397#post1437397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there aren't places that creatures can draw power from? that instead of a harmful trait it turns to be a possitive one for the creature? Like a Locus for Werewolves or a Demesne (is that the word?) for a Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>are</i> places that creatures can draw power from, but the qualities of those places don't represent themselves directly through mortal experience the way the various stage hazards common to Begotten soulscapes do. Humans don't know that there's a locus of pain in the werewolves' territory that's been ritually strengthened to make everyone on the beach uncomfortable near the rock where an unfortunate swimmer stumbled upon a float of box jellyfish, but they sure can tell that the water and sand there is Stinging to the touch.<br /> <br /> Of the published Lair Traits, five aren't direct hazards (all of them from the Player's Guide); two of them are upgrades of another two, three of them are just ways to draw the Horror's attention to a particular character, and the remaining two are ways to give your Lair native inhabitants that aren't the Horror. The trend is consistent: Lair Traits make the Beast more powerful by being dangerous things they can bring into a scene without fear of direct harm to themselves, because they are part of the hunting ground that their Horror uses to bring down its prey.<br /> <br /> Until you get into the realm of Incarnation, the Legend a Beast embodies is a creature of nightmare who brings some form of harm or ill upon the people it directs its hunger toward. Boons in the standard Begotten toolkit skew toward making other monsters' magical powers work better through Kinship and terrifying people into particular forms of effectiveness through Nightmares. More involved fare requires borrowing from unique phenomena or outside sources or throwing yourself into the part of the endgame that lets you rewrite the narrative in your favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-28-2021, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T02:22:51-08:00","id":1437448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437397#post1437397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there aren't places that creatures can draw power from? that instead of a harmful trait it turns to be a possitive one for the creature? Like a Locus for Werewolves or a Demesne (is that the word?) for a Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>While the physical location represented by a Chamber might've been a Locus or anything else of a supernatural nature, the Chamber is still a copy of a traumatised human's experiences. If a human was traumatised by Supernal manifestations inside a Verge, the Lair Traits you might develop from that Chamber will only recreate the effects of the Verge as relevant to the traumatic experiences of that human. Any Supernal entity that manifested within the Verge would be represented by awful hallucinations or a Dreamborn copy of that entity, and you simply wouldn't get any bonuses to spellcasting.<br /> That is assuming Lair Traits can be developed from a Beast's Chambers. As far as I can tell, a Beast is free to gain basically any Lair Traits they want, but even in the case of spontaneous Lair Traits they really have no business recreating supernatural places of power. They're an extension of the Horror's nature imposed on the world, and thus supposed to be horrific and hostile towards everyone else. Creating a supernatural place of power is simply not what Beasts are built for, and in many cases places of power can be used by others because they're linked up to something specific, like a different place or plane of existence or a specific individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-01-2021, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T08:04:37-08:00","id":1437479,"title":"","content":"First of all thanks for the responses, but I'm not quite satisfied with the answers, that being said I'm not trying to be contrarian but I'll be pointing out holes in the reasons you are giving me.<br /> <br /> And, OK I have to agree that Lair traits are going to be harmful for regular mortals most if not all the time but what I meant is that for the Beast a trait could be directly benefitial and still be something traumatic at the end of the tale for the mortal involved, or something that can be used to lord over them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There <i>are</i> places that creatures can draw power from, but the qualities of those places don't represent themselves directly through mortal experience the way the various stage hazards common to Begotten soulscapes do. Humans don't know that there's a locus of pain in the werewolves' territory that's been ritually strengthened to make everyone on the beach uncomfortable near the rock where an unfortunate swimmer stumbled upon a float of box jellyfish, but they sure can tell that the water and sand there is Stinging to the touch. </div> </div> </div>While in that particular case I can agree with you, what happens when you switch the resonance to something bening like Joy, give it a nicer story about being a place where all children come to play and have fun and you get a whole different experience, maybe harder to get a traumatic experience here than in other places but it depends on how you pitch it forward.<br /> <br /> Since you want me to make it a traumatic experience, let's provide an example then, say you start in that same place and you get an exceptional success with a nightmare thus forming a chamber, the nightmare you used was Flying and Falling so you get them feeling elated just until the fall comes, out comes a new trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Joyful</b><br /> <br /> The lair is a seemingly joyful and fun place, the victims feel happy, content and safe, everyone enjoys a +3 in all rolls to keep the fun going and make sure everyone is happy, but anything that would distract them of the fun suffers that same bonus as a penalty to be noticed.<br /> <br /> Let's take it to the next level then if you don't think that is scary enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Soporific</b><br /> <br /> Much like with Joyful the lair is seemgly a nice place to have fun in, this trait makes it easy to ignore anything harmful, under this lair trait effects the beast and its target can ignore pain and the effects of harmful physical tilts, they still take damage they just ignore it unless they make a successful roll resolve+composure roll with a -3 penalty, furthermore they lose sense of time and of their health unless they get a succesful roll, a dancer will dance until they bleed and won't stop there they will continue to dance until they die unless stopped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the physical location represented by a Chamber might've been a Locus or anything else of a supernatural nature, the Chamber is still a copy of a traumatised human's experiences. If a human was traumatised by Supernal manifestations inside a Verge, the Lair Traits you might develop from that Chamber will only recreate the effects of the Verge as relevant to the traumatic experiences of that human. Any Supernal entity that manifested within the Verge would be represented by awful hallucinations or a Dreamborn copy of that entity, and you simply wouldn't get any bonuses to spellcasting. </div> </div> </div>See the above examples, but you can still forget one aspect of a place of power, they have a lure to them that works on those that seek to take advantage of that power, and one of the traits that are available already exemplifies this point, take a look at the Hoard trait, it offers a promise of riches and if you play your cards right you can get the gold and valuables sell them if you are fast enough and can avoid the hungry Horror, it's a trap yeah, the horror knows you took something from it and he'll go hunting for it.<br /> <br /> Let's take this very concept to the Healing trait I put forward when I started this discussion and write it down as an insidious lair trait taking a bit of inspiration from the Hoard trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Healing</b><br /> <br /> Inside the lair there is a special place, maybe a pond, or maybe it's the horror itself whatever it is, inside one of the lair chambers all healing times are halved, furthermore any type of damage can be healed through enough exposure so a person could regrow a limb is he heals all damage inside the lair, the counterpoint is that they know without any room for doubt that the monster that makes the chamber its home is the cause of the healing, no monster, no healing.<br /> <br /> And just with that, I created a lure and a problem for visitors, even more, I make the Beast valuable, now you can get a Primordial Cult going here making offerings to a Horror to keep it distracted, or a Tyrant might dangle the power over a community, or a Predator uses it lure the desperate to itself. It's not by any means a sure thing, you can get a fanatical Hero to just burn everything down and destroy the chamber consequences be damned just so long as the beast dies but its followers might not be so zealous.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just an example of what I mean with positive traits, maybe I wasn't as clear when I first made my question and I apologize for that, but maybe you can see how seemingly bening traits can still be part of the Legend for a hungry monster that feeds on the fears of humanity.<br /> <br /> Either way, I still feel that I need help figuring out the limits of how beneficial a Lair trait can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T09:07:14-08:00","id":1437492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437479#post1437479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all thanks for the responses, but I'm not quite satisfied with the answers, that being said I'm not trying to be contrarian but I'll be pointing out holes in the reasons you are giving me.<br /> <br /> And, OK I have to agree that Lair traits are going to be harmful for regular mortals most if not all the time but what I meant is that for the Beast a trait could be directly benefitial and still be something traumatic at the end of the tale for the mortal involved, or something that can be used to lord over them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While in that particular case I can agree with you, what happens when you switch the resonance to something bening like Joy, give it a nicer story about being a place where all children come to play and have fun and you get a whole different experience, maybe harder to get a traumatic experience here than in other places but it depends on how you pitch it forward.<br /> <br /> Since you want me to make it a traumatic experience, let's provide an example then, say you start in that same place and you get an exceptional success with a nightmare thus forming a chamber, the nightmare you used was Flying and Falling so you get them feeling elated just until the fall comes, out comes a new trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Joyful</b><br /> <br /> The lair is a seemingly joyful and fun place, the victims feel happy, content and safe, everyone enjoys a +3 in all rolls to keep the fun going and make sure everyone is happy, but anything that would distract them of the fun suffers that same bonus as a penalty to be noticed.<br /> <br /> Let's take it to the next level then if you don't think that is scary enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Soporific</b><br /> <br /> Much like with Joyful the lair is seemgly a nice place to have fun in, this trait makes it easy to ignore anything harmful, under this lair trait effects the beast and its target can ignore pain and the effects of harmful physical tilts, they still take damage they just ignore it unless they make a successful roll resolve+composure roll with a -3 penalty, furthermore they lose sense of time and of their health unless they get a succesful roll, a dancer will dance until they bleed and won't stop there they will continue to dance until they die unless stopped.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See the above examples, but you can still forget one aspect of a place of power, they have a lure to them that works on those that seek to take advantage of that power, and one of the traits that are available already exemplifies this point, take a look at the Hoard trait, it offers a promise of riches and if you play your cards right you can get the gold and valuables sell them if you are fast enough and can avoid the hungry Horror, it's a trap yeah, the horror knows you took something from it and he'll go hunting for it.<br /> <br /> Let's take this very concept to the Healing trait I put forward when I started this discussion and write it down as an insidious lair trait taking a bit of inspiration from the Hoard trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Healing</b><br /> <br /> Inside the lair there is a special place, maybe a pond, or maybe it's the horror itself whatever it is, inside one of the lair chambers all healing times are halved, furthermore any type of damage can be healed through enough exposure so a person could regrow a limb is he heals all damage inside the lair, the counterpoint is that they know without any room for doubt that the monster that makes the chamber its home is the cause of the healing, no monster, no healing.<br /> <br /> And just with that, I created a lure and a problem for visitors, even more, I make the Beast valuable, now you can get a Primordial Cult going here making offerings to a Horror to keep it distracted, or a Tyrant might dangle the power over a community, or a Predator uses it lure the desperate to itself. It's not by any means a sure thing, you can get a fanatical Hero to just burn everything down and destroy the chamber consequences be damned just so long as the beast dies but its followers might not be so zealous.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just an example of what I mean with positive traits, maybe I wasn't as clear when I first made my question and I apologize for that, but maybe you can see how seemingly bening traits can still be part of the Legend for a hungry monster that feeds on the fears of humanity.<br /> <br /> Either way, I still feel that I need help figuring out the limits of how beneficial a Lair trait can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first looks like the effect of a Nightmare, while the second one... i think it could work, but with something like &quot;the healing process is so unsettling that for every scene spent in the chamber a mortal would roll for a breaking point&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T09:34:22-08:00","id":1437494,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying it isn't possible to turn Lair Traits into benefits for some characters. The most obvious example is a Lair Trait (say Darkness) which only affects one side in a conflict because the other side happens to be immune (because they don't rely on sight) or are made immune to the effects thanks to the Beast. It's not directly affecting anyone in a beneficial sense, but can absolutely be made beneficial through circumstances.<br /> So I'm really not opposed to Lair Traits that can be used to people's advantage, but they still need to be a hindrance or danger first and foremost. You brought up Hoard. The main effect is that interacting with the Hoard attracts the Horror. The fact that you could, if fast enough, carry some of the false treasure away and spend it is a side effect that requires effort to facilitate. Note that the treasure is still false. You're never actually wealthier by stealing it; you're just able to pass it off as real for a short while.<br /> Your Healing example, however, is the exact opposite. It's a beneficial effect that can be used as a tool for horror if the Beast sets up the right circumstances for it. Unlike Hoard, the &quot;treasure&quot; is absolutely real and by itself it's almost always a purely positive effect. The Beast needs to put in a lot of effort to gain anything thematically relevant from it. (It's also not a particularly good lure since it's only noticeable for a small subset of the people it can affect, and only if they experience prolonged exposure to the Lair Trait. Basically, only people with amputated limbs who <i>live within your Lair</i> will notice the lure.)<br /> <br /> I do like the Joyful example, though, but that's because the way I see it the main effect is that it's distracting for the victim. Much like Hoard it's turning something that's often seen as positive (joy/treasure) into a direct and tangible drawback (distraction/attracting the Horror).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-01-2021, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T09:47:45-08:00","id":1437497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first looks like the effect of a Nightmare, while the second one... i think it could work, but with something like &quot;the healing process is so unsettling that for every scene spent in the chamber a mortal would roll for a breaking point&quot; </div> </div> </div>Why would it matter if a Nightmare or an Atavism could do the same?<br /> <br /> I mean, you have Traits like Toxic, Noxious Gases, Diseased, with powers like Basilisk's Touch, Plague Bearer, Bugs Everywhere!, They Put Something in Your Food, from what you are saying I could take that you think the Hurricane trait shouldn't be in the list because Storm Lashed is an atavism.<br /> <br /> But why wouldn't I want both the nightmare and the lair trait? say I work a crowd with a nightmare that makes everybody happy drunks, Drugged Tilt to happy feelings just to set an example, Fear is Contagious to help affect more people, my Beast takes the time to work the crowd, get a bunch of happy drunks and get the mood Joyful and fun, there I managed to get a subtle Trait resonance going and can then subtly add more lair traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T10:50:46-08:00","id":1437505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437497#post1437497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would it matter if a Nightmare or an Atavism could do the same?<br /> <br /> I mean, you have Traits like Toxic, Noxious Gases, Diseased, with powers like Basilisk's Touch, Plague Bearer, Bugs Everywhere!, They Put Something in Your Food, from what you are saying I could take that you think the Hurricane trait shouldn't be in the list because Storm Lashed is an atavism.<br /> <br /> But why wouldn't I want both the nightmare and the lair trait? say I work a crowd with a nightmare that makes everybody happy drunks, Drugged Tilt to happy feelings just to set an example, Fear is Contagious to help affect more people, my Beast takes the time to work the crowd, get a bunch of happy drunks and get the mood Joyful and fun, there I managed to get a subtle Trait resonance going and can then subtly add more lair traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, a negative effect with a beneficial side effect is more like some Nightmares are structured.<br /> I see lair traits as something more simplier, in the joyful example i would prefer to build it as a tilt that give penalities to perception rolls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T11:07:21-08:00","id":1437509,"title":"","content":"Perhaps directly beneficial lair features would be better modeled as Merits rather than Lair Traits? The Players Guide has a few examples of these, like Well-Stocked Lair. By my understanding, Lair Traits are less \u201cthings inside the Lair\u201d and more \u201cways that the environment is trying to scare and/or kill you\u201d. Whereas the Lair Merits seem to cover \u201cnifty thing inside the Lair that may or may not be supernatural in origin\u201d. <br /> <br /> For example, if I had a player who had a Hallow inside their Lair (for whatever reason), I\u2019d just price it as the normal Hallow merit. Spitballing, I\u2019d probably price that healing trait as two dots for the increased healing factor, with a four dot option to also grant limb regeneration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T19:53:27-08:00","id":1437568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437509#post1437509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps directly beneficial lair features would be better modeled as Merits rather than Lair Traits? The Players Guide has a few examples of these, like Well-Stocked Lair. By my understanding, Lair Traits are less \u201cthings inside the Lair\u201d and more \u201cways that the environment is trying to scare and/or kill you\u201d. Whereas the Lair Merits seem to cover \u201cnifty thing inside the Lair that may or may not be supernatural in origin\u201d.<br /> <br /> For example, if I had a player who had a Hallow inside their Lair (for whatever reason), I\u2019d just price it as the normal Hallow merit. Spitballing, I\u2019d probably price that healing trait as two dots for the increased healing factor, with a four dot option to also grant limb regeneration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The discussion I'm having and the questions I have been asking for are in reference to Lair Traits, please do not derail the discussion by talking about merits.<br /> <br /> The dicussion and questions I'm making are about these lines bellow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Minor: Lair Traits are always possible in the physical world without the use of magic. They may provide dice penalties or bonuses to Skills, or count as Extreme Environments (see p. 171 ) up to level 2.<br /> <br /> Major: Lair Traits may (but don\u2019t always) impose Tilts that aren\u2019t physically possible; anything from turning the skin of victims to salt to acidic rain. They may provide dice penalties or bonuses to Attributes or derived traits like Speed and Defense, or count as Extreme Environments up to level 4 </div> </div> </div>These lines are taken from Page 101 of the Beast Core Book, they literally say you can get bonus from traits directly to attributes, skills or derived traits.<br /> <br /> I have been trying to come up with new positive traits following some of the advise I have recieved, but I feel like I'm banging my head against a wall here finding way to accomodate others while still doing what I want, and what I want is to take advantage of these rules while staying withing the themes of the game and perhaps to add some clarity about the limits of these rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437494#post1437494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm really not opposed to Lair Traits that can be used to people's advantage, but they still need to be a hindrance or danger first and foremost.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you say but I have yet to hear from you how it should be mechanically expresed, maybe with the Healing trait I'm taking it too far, but I don't agree that the traits need to be a direct hindrance first, let's come up with another new trait, I seem to be doing that a lot just to prove a point.<br /> <br /> Tall Grass<br /> Despite the name of the trait, this can manifest in many ways, the chamber can be office full of cubicles or just tall grass from a maize field or stalagmites in a cave, by themselves they don't hinder anyone under the effects of this trait, they offer however places to hide that the Beast can move through without alerting his prey, the Beast gains a +3 to stealth rolls to remain hidden.<br /> <br /> You know how there is Bad Angles, how about this then?<br /> <br /> Good Angles<br /> Space behaves strangely in the lair, the Beast always can find a good angle to get a bead on their prey, the Beast benefits from full aiming bonus for any ranged attack when this trait is active.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T20:43:47-08:00","id":1437570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437568#post1437568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The discussion I'm having and the questions I have been asking for are in reference to Lair Traits, please do not derail the discussion by talking about merits.<br /> <br /> I have been trying to come up with new positive traits following some of the advise I have recieved, but I feel like I'm banging my head against a wall here finding way to accomodate others while still doing what I want, and what I want is to take advantage of these rules while staying withing the themes of the game and perhaps to add some clarity about the limits of these rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you may want to consider that the solution might not be to try and lean on the part of the game with an attached rule called &quot;Environmental Immunity&quot; for beneficial character aspects instead of the part of the generalized framework where bonuses that aren't managed by other purchaseable Traits go.<br /> <br /> Beast's corebook has some problems with it, being the first edition of a new gameline whose initial development was not as together as it could have been with systems that were still relatively new to the overall mechanical structure; it is not difficult to extrapolate that, given two big batches of Lair Traits at either end of a three-year release span, the corebook mentioning bonuses is a mistake. Taking the one-off mention of non-negative modifiers as guidance for coming up with new Lair Traits is obviously not going to help you in this context.<br /> <br /> Lair Traits are things about the environment that make the Lair the favored hunting ground of the Beast and other monsters like them. The ones that represent natural phenomena work like those natural phenomena, down to replicating their increased or decreased effectiveness against beings for whom those phenomena would be more or less effective; the ones that don't represent natural phenomena are minions, methods of denying respite, and ways to target the Horror's reach and attention further.<br /> <br /> The presence of Lair Traits makes a Beast's Atavisms \u2014 the supernatural qualities representing more-or-less bodily aspects of the Begotten's Horror \u2014 easier to leverage without burning fuel. They are not themselves the things to use for &quot;the Beast is better in this one circumstance,&quot; because that is not an environmental quality in the same way a Hollow being a changeling's Home Turf or a city block being a vampire's Feeding Grounds is; a Beast derives advantage from their Lair by being able to live in it where most others would not \u2014 it is a place in the collective soul of humanity set aside for them as close to the mind-scouring breath of the world-soul as mortal minds can exist without constant exposure to the Mother's Land.<br /> <br /> It is <i>geography</i>, and that means it doesn't provide personalized boons or direct mental effects, because those are what Atavisms and Nightmares and Kinship abilities are for in the Begotten toolbox. Trying to bend the Chamber-agnostic qualities of the Lair into bonuses is going to give you trouble in a game where the core of your magic comes from filtering down the power of a land that communicates in pain and hunger and fear into a cryptid/urban legend descended from Fear Herself.<br /> <br /> Bonuses personalized to the Beast are Merits or Atavisms. That is what those things are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T21:16:20-08:00","id":1437571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437388#post1437388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My main question here, is how much of a bonus can a Lair Trait give for either Minor or Major lair traits, besides those two texts I haven't been able to find any more details and not to beat on it again, but it's a rather vague ruling here and not quite clear.<br /> <br /> I mean, what are the limits? how much is too much when trying to give bonus using lair traits specially when it comes to Major traits?<br /> <br /> Like, plenty of stuff weakens a target, like Infected giving -3 to stamina, what if you come up with a beast that has a legend for healing, so out come the Healing lair trait that gives minor regeneration healing Lethal in hours rather than days to all involved for a Major trait, or you come up with a beast whose legend is about empowering their minions and allies, so he get the Invigorating lair trait giving +X bonus to Strength. I mean, I get the ideas but don't know how to set the limits or where they are at all<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To try and address your root question about balancing Traits: there isn't a lot of guidance on how to design them in general. The best guide is to just look at the official traits. However, this is more difficult if you want to frame the Traits as beneficial, since there aren't really any official beneficial traits. That said, when it comes to direct bonuses, you're probably safe with just inverting the penalties that similar Traits give. So I think a +3 to Stealth rolls (like you mention above) is well within the bounds of what a Minor Trait could give, probably even on the low side. However, this is less helpful if you want to include more unique effects like the aforementioned healing. Part of the reason I suggested using Merits is that it's easier to price a particular effect in dots than it is to cram said effect into the loosely defined Minor and Major Trait categories.<br /> <br /> To repeat, Lair Traits in general don't have brilliant design guidelines, so creating custom ones, beneficial or not, is going to be more art than science. Trying ideas out in play, and getting other's options, is the best way of achieving balance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T21:58:06-08:00","id":1437573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437570#post1437570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you may want to consider that the solution might not be to try and lean on the part of the game with an attached rule called &quot;Environmental Immunity&quot; for beneficial character aspects instead of the part of the generalized framework where bonuses that aren't managed by other purchaseable Traits go.<br /> <br /> Beast's corebook has some problems with it, being the first edition of a new gameline whose initial development was not as together as it could have been with systems that were still relatively new to the overall mechanical structure; it is not difficult to extrapolate that, given two big batches of Lair Traits at either end of a three-year release span, the corebook mentioning bonuses is a mistake. Taking the one-off mention of non-negative modifiers as guidance for coming up with new Lair Traits is obviously not going to help you in this context.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can accept more easily, I can acknowledge that my whole point was based on what the book said about minor and major lair traits, maybe it was clarified before, if you guys did, then I missed it completely and a bit of a stubborn streak of my own made me want to defend my point a bit strongly, so my apoligies for that.<br /> <br /> Without a hill to stand on, my arguments are invalid so I can see now what everybody has been saying about Traits being primarily enviromental hazards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1437571#post1437571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To try and address your root question about balancing Traits: there isn't a lot of guidance on how to design them in general. The best guide is to just look at the official traits. However, this is more difficult if you want to frame the Traits as beneficial, since there aren't really any official beneficial traits. That said, when it comes to direct bonuses, you're probably safe with just inverting the penalties that similar Traits give. So I think a +3 to Stealth rolls (like you mention above) is well within the bounds of what a Minor Trait could give, probably even on the low side. However, this is less helpful if you want to include more unique effects like the aforementioned healing. Part of the reason I suggested using Merits is that it's easier to price a particular effect in dots than it is to cram said effect into the loosely defined Minor and Major Trait categories.<br /> <br /> To repeat, Lair Traits in general don't have brilliant design guidelines, so creating custom ones, beneficial or not, is going to be more art than science. Trying ideas out in play, and getting other's options, is the best way of achieving balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this is another part of what I want to get a more clear idea of, what are the limits that I can hit with minor or major traits? Specially with Major traits when they can be a lot less natural about their effects.<br /> <br /> With my new acceptance of how traits works, and taking the idea of healing, I can come up with something like this, now aiming for a Major trait, let me know if I take it too far.<br /> <br /> Mutating<br /> Those affected by this trait, heal faster in the lair at a rate of Bashing in 1 minute and Lethal in 1 hour, aggravated damage however is unaffected, despite this all healing is done wrongly, the ones affected by this lair trait gain a persistant negative physical tilt or condition of the storytellers choice.<br /> <br /> Great for turning a regeneration power into a problem but it also leaves a lasting mark on a victim of the Beast feeding<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 03-02-2021, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-02T23:27:59-07:00","id":1442464,"title":"","content":"Excuse me, I was wondering if it\u2019s correct that Unfettered Horrors of high-Lair Beasts (Lair 6+) will become astral gods (Rank 6+), even though they are roughly at best as powerful as Rank 5 ephemeral entities while in their Lairs (if calculating their attributes as described in core rulebook p.99).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","name":"agrelletto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T05:20:32-07:00","id":1442487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>agrelletto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1442464#post1442464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me, I was wondering if it\u2019s correct that Unfettered Horrors of high-Lair Beasts (Lair 6+) will become astral gods (Rank 6+), even though they are roughly at best as powerful as Rank 5 ephemeral entities while in their Lairs (if calculating their attributes as described in core rulebook p.99).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that but they can also reach Rank 9 or 10, which is above the most powerful known gods who use the Rank system. To put it into perspective: Luna and Helios, the two most powerful entities in Werewolf: The Forsaken, are Rank 8. The Aeons, the Astral gods of the Arcana in Mage: The Awakening, are Rank 8. The scale could've basically just ended at 8.<br /> And at the other end of the scale we can end up with Unfettered Horrors with Rank 1, which is actually <i>less</i> than the Rank of larval Horrors who's not yet gone through with the Devouring (Player's Guide says they are Rank 2).<br /> <br /> Unfettered Horrors are a cool concept and otherwise I do like the rules for them, but equating Lair with Rank was extremely ill-thought-out. If I were to redesign it, I would've made it something like this:<br /> Lair 1 = Rank 2 (the Horror neither gains nor loses power this early)<br /> Lair 2-3 = Rank 3<br /> Lair 4-5 = Rank 4<br /> Lair 6-7 = Rank 5<br /> Lair 8-9 = Rank 6<br /> Lair 10 = Rank 7","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T06:33:04-07:00","id":1442490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1442487#post1442487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only that but they can also reach Rank 9 or 10, which is above the most powerful known gods who use the Rank system. To put it into perspective: Luna and Helios, the two most powerful entities in Werewolf: The Forsaken, are Rank 8. The Aeons, the Astral gods of the Arcana in Mage: The Awakening, are Rank 8. The scale could've basically just ended at 8.<br /> And at the other end of the scale we can end up with Unfettered Horrors with Rank 1, which is actually <i>less</i> than the Rank of larval Horrors who's not yet gone through with the Devouring (Player's Guide says they are Rank 2).<br /> <br /> Unfettered Horrors are a cool concept and otherwise I do like the rules for them, but equating Lair with Rank was extremely ill-thought-out. If I were to redesign it, I would've made it something like this:<br /> Lair 1 = Rank 2 (the Horror neither gains nor loses power this early)<br /> Lair 2-3 = Rank 3<br /> Lair 4-5 = Rank 4<br /> Lair 6-7 = Rank 5<br /> Lair 8-9 = Rank 6<br /> Lair 10 = Rank 7</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! The chart you provide is great!<br /> <br /> Since Death, as one of the mightiest beings in Temenos, is Rank 7, it seems that astral beings born from collective consciousness of humanity won\u2019t be as powerful as souls of celestial bodies and universal phenomena (and thus their maximum power scale is Rank 7). I don\u2019t know if this statement still applies in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23765-agrelletto","name":"agrelletto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T19:15:21-07:00","id":1443551,"title":"","content":"So regarding the information revealed in the PG on the Primordial Dream...<br /> <br /> Was it that the Primordial Dream, if you went further in enough, lead to the Temenos, that the Primordial Dream and Temenos were one and the same, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T19:39:11-07:00","id":1443553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1443551#post1443551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So regarding the information revealed in the PG on the Primordial Dream...<br /> <br /> Was it that the Primordial Dream, if you went further in enough, lead to the Temenos, that the Primordial Dream and Temenos were one and the same, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Dream is in the Temenos, but Beasts and people led by a Beast navigate it in a geographically prosaic fashion compared to the Bright Dream beyond the Day.<br /> <br /> The Temenos is the Dark Dream and the Bright Dream minus Oneiroi; the Bright Dream is Oneiroi and the Temenos minus the Primordial Dream. There's a Venn diagram at work here, but nothing in that continuum is in the Mother's Land/Anima Mundi (which Beasts experience largely as just the Dreamtime).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T09:01:46-07:00","id":1449121,"title":"","content":"Balance check: is the following a reasonable application of the Normal Effect of Storm-Lashed?<br /> <br /> Strike: the Beast can launch loose objects at dangerous speeds, or simply pummel a foe directly with a compressed burst of air. The requires an attack roll of Dexterity + Athletics \u2013 the target\u2019s Defense, and inflicts bashing damage equal to successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T23:19:46-07:00","id":1449228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1449121#post1449121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balance check: is the following a reasonable application of the Normal Effect of Storm-Lashed?<br /> <br /> Strike: the Beast can launch loose objects at dangerous speeds, or simply pummel a foe directly with a compressed burst of air. The requires an attack roll of Dexterity + Athletics \u2013 the target\u2019s Defense, and inflicts bashing damage equal to successes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems underpowered if anything depending on what range this works at which is not specified in the above. That is the thrown weapons dice pool (Dex+Ath-Def) and ranged weapons have ranges (short, medium and long.) A thrown weapon can be lethal instead of bashing and would therefore be better than the Strike attack in every way except for repeatability and range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T08:58:30-07:00","id":1449259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1449228#post1449228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seems underpowered if anything depending on what range this works at which is not specified in the above. That is the thrown weapons dice pool (Dex+Ath-Def) and ranged weapons have ranges (short, medium and long.) A thrown weapon can be lethal instead of bashing and would therefore be better than the Strike attack in every way except for repeatability and range.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have the same range as the rest of the Normal effect (5 yards per dot of Lair), which means it will probably be shorter range than thrown weapons. I'm less concerned with how powerful it is overall, and more with how well it fits within the vanilla options for Storm-Lashed. For example, adding Lair as a weapon modifier would, I think, make it too similar to the Normal effect of Dragonfire, considering you'd still have all of the versatility of the vanilla applications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T13:27:45-07:00","id":1449280,"title":"","content":"So, would the evil within (video game) be considered good inspiration for what Lairs would look like and operate? I recommended it for a friend who will be running a beast game with his group, but I don't want to mislead him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 05-22-2021, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T17:06:02-07:00","id":1449293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1449259#post1449259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would have the same range as the rest of the Normal effect (5 yards per dot of Lair), which means it will probably be shorter range than thrown weapons. I'm less concerned with how powerful it is overall, and more with how well it fits within the vanilla options for Storm-Lashed. For example, adding Lair as a weapon modifier would, I think, make it too similar to the Normal effect of Dragonfire, considering you'd still have all of the versatility of the vanilla applications.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As an additional effect of an Atavism, rather than replacing part of an atavism, it seems fine from a balance perspective then. I think they designed it the way they did to place the damaging component with Satiety Expenditure but I would allow that in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T11:42:55-07:00","id":1453386,"title":"","content":"I have a question about starting Nightmares. Apologies if it's already been asked and answered, but 84 pages is a lot to dig through.<br /> <br /> The text in the book says &quot;Choose two starting Nightmares. If you start play with Kinship established with another supernatural creature, you have your character begin play with a Kinship Nightmare based in that creature's type.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm a bit unclear here. Does the Kinship Nightmare count as one of the two starting Nightmares, or is it an extra bonus Nightmare? Further, is a Beast who begins play with Kinship *required* to take a Kinship Nightmare, or is it just an option available to them? Especially if it counts as one of the two, and the player already has two Nightmares picked out, neither of which are Kinship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","name":"RuNoMai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T12:07:45-07:00","id":1453389,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure the word &quot;may&quot; accidentally got omitted (as in &quot;you may have your character begin play&quot; etc.). You always start with two Nightmares. They can be, but are not required to be, Kinship Nightmares if you begin play with the appropriate established Kinship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T12:15:45-07:00","id":1453390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1453389#post1453389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure the word &amp;quot;may&amp;quot; accidentally got omitted (as in &amp;quot;you may have your character begin play&amp;quot; etc.). You always start with two Nightmares. They can be, but are not required to be, Kinship Nightmares if you begin play with the appropriate established Kinship.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, but wasn't really sure. Just wanted to ask in case this section of text was cleared up or corrected in errata or later printings.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarification!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","name":"RuNoMai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T19:45:28-07:00","id":1457670,"title":"","content":"1) Would Playful work as a Legend?<br /> 2) Can a Horror have a weapon as part of it\u2019s nature? <br /> 3) Has anyone made kinship merits or nightmares for fetches?<br /> 4) Can a Inguma be something like a urban legend serial killer?<br /> 5) When people fear Artificial Intelligence, would you say it\u2019s more fear of something inhuman being in control of our tech, or the vast power it weird from that tech? To phrase another way, Anakim or Inguma?<br /> 6) What hunger would setting up elaborate pranks on people be?<br /> 7) How useful is Alien Mindset in practice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T20:06:56-07:00","id":1457674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457670#post1457670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Would Playful work as a Legend?<br /> 2) Can a Horror have a weapon as part of it\u2019s nature? <br /> 3) Has anyone made kinship merits or nightmares for fetches?<br /> 4) Can a Inguma be something like a urban legend serial killer?<br /> 5) When people fear Artificial Intelligence, would you say it\u2019s more fear of something inhuman being in control of our tech, or the vast power it weird from that tech? To phrase another way, Anakim or Inguma?<br /> 6) What hunger would setting up elaborate pranks on people be?<br /> 7) How useful is Alien Mindset in practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Well, cats have been known to play with prey\u2026 so do fairies and demons. <br /> <br /> 2) I\u2019d say yes, but focus on simpler ones, like an Oni holding an iron club, or a Kraken swinging anchors. <br /> <br /> 4) I\u2019d say yes, but the Horror itself probably looks more like Slenderman or CHUD.<br /> <br /> 5) Ugallu for me, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T20:26:24-07:00","id":1457676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457674#post1457674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Well, cats have been known to play with prey\u2026 so do fairies and demons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457674#post1457674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I\u2019d say yes, but focus on simpler ones, like an Oni holding an iron club, or a Kraken swinging anchors.</div> </div> </div> </div> So just a simple knife would work. That would be a power+ finesse roll, same a a claw or bite with no weapon rating?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457674#post1457674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) I\u2019d say yes, but the Horror itself probably looks more like Slenderman or CHUD.</div> </div> </div> </div> So if I wanted a masked figure slasher horror, would I be better off with another family? I was thinking of the mask actually being the face, while the body and clothes changes to suit the horrors needs. I\u2019m not sure if that effects anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457674#post1457674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Ugallu for me, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, huh. Not what I expected. Do you mind explaining why? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T20:39:42-07:00","id":1457678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457670#post1457670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) When people fear Artificial Intelligence, would you say it\u2019s more fear of something inhuman being in control of our tech, or the vast power it weird from that tech? To phrase another way, Anakim or Inguma?</div> </div> </div> </div>Makara, if I'm to indulge the high-concept approach to building a type of monster that is typically more bluntly-stated in its fear-factor.<br /> <br /> &quot;Artificial intelligence&quot; is a thing people fear as a cipher for a number of different fears depending on the person, but the Anakim are a frontal assault and the Inguma wears a human face. As an abstract phenomenon it's more in tune with the topological skews of the Leviathans or the Raptors, who force you to confront an entire extra dimension in which you are unprepared for their ascendance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T20:48:47-07:00","id":1457679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457676#post1457676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So just a simple knife would work. That would be a power+ finesse roll, same a a claw or bite with no weapon rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the simple way. Anything more, I\u2019d ask for a Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I wanted a masked figure slasher horror, would I be better off with another family? I was thinking of the mask actually being the face, while the body and clothes changes to suit the horrors needs. I\u2019m not sure if that effects anything. </div> </div> </div>And <i>that</i> sounds like Namtaru to me. I think the Masked Killer archetype is rather humane and less Primordial\u2026 which usually means not \u201cDon\u2019t do it\u201d but \u201cAnything could fit with enough brain gymnastics\u201d to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, huh. Not what I expected. Do you mind explaining why? </div> </div> </div><i>They\u2019re watching us.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T21:07:47-07:00","id":1457680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457678#post1457678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makara, if I'm to indulge the high-concept approach to building a type of monster that is typically more bluntly-stated in its fear-factor.<br /> <br /> &quot;Artificial intelligence&quot; is a thing people fear as a cipher for a number of different fears depending on the person, but the Anakim are a frontal assault and the Inguma wears a human face. As an abstract phenomenon it's more in tune with the topological skews of the Leviathans or the Raptors, who force you to confront an entire extra dimension in which you are unprepared for their ascendance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, resides in a realm completely alien from human experience, takes strange shapes we possibly cannot comprehend, thinks thoughts unknowable to us, some may be very charming indeed, the better to fool us\u2026 I think we have a winner. Sold on Makara at least. Perhaps I need to review Ugallu, because I still don\u2019t understand why they fit. With social media and cameras, they know everything about you, thus being under exposure? Thank you for that perspective, it was most informative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T23:25:32-07:00","id":1457693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457670#post1457670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Would Playful work as a Legend?<br /> 2) Can a Horror have a weapon as part of it\u2019s nature?<br /> 3) Has anyone made kinship merits or nightmares for fetches?<br /> 4) Can a Inguma be something like a urban legend serial killer?<br /> 5) When people fear Artificial Intelligence, would you say it\u2019s more fear of something inhuman being in control of our tech, or the vast power it weird from that tech? To phrase another way, Anakim or Inguma?<br /> 6) What hunger would setting up elaborate pranks on people be?<br /> 7) How useful is Alien Mindset in practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes. An example would be something along the lines of:<br /> <br /> (Modeled from Relentless) <b>Playful:</b> Regain one point of Willpower if your character delays gratification when interacting with a target. Regain all Willpower if she knows that by not instantly satisfying her urges she is raising the chances of a dangerous situation occurring, such as a Hero interrupting.<br /> <br /> (Modeled from Vicious) <b>Playful: </b>Regain one point of Willpower when your character goes over-the-top in dealing with someone, whether physically or emotionally, such as letting them run through a maze of your own devising, or taking the time to orchestrate a betrayal amongst their cohort. Regain all Willpower when doing this unnecessarily to prolong enjoyment, or when developing the conditions of a feed to increase the amount of satiety obtained.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes again, they are however intrinsic to the Horror in the same way that claws are to a tiger.<br /> <br /> 3) Not that I am aware of, but have a look at the corresponding threads<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares\"> Homebrew Nightmares - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Because, surprisingly, there wasn't already a thread for this, even though Nightmares are literally designed to be homebrewed. Here until we get a Beast forum. Ideas or fully crunched mechanics are both fine, as are Nightmares based on homebrew templates. You Are Not Prepared (General): The nightmare of </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\"> Homebrew Beast Merits - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Yep. Here's my Beast edition for Homebrew Merits. Expect a lot of the Beast (and Hero stuff) that Arcanist and I are brewing up to appear here in this thread. As </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 4) Whatever you can think of can usually fit the template of the Families. Inguma is just a fear of the other, this can be serial killers.<br /> <br /> 5) Depends. I can agree with 21C Hermit, but the fear of technology can fit into any of the nightmares that the Families produce. Just think of the fear that it produces e.g. does it make you feel hopeless, exposed, etc.<br /> <br /> 6) I guess this is another it depends question. But, judging from what you've asked, your attempting to make some sort of trickster Beast. I'd say Ruin, cause 'some people just want to watch the world burn.'<br /> <br /> 7) Incredibly. Super-versatile when it comes to feeding and gaining willpower and leaves others in the dark and confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;To succeed, planning alone is insufficient. One must improvise as well.&quot; - Salvor Hardin, Foundation</span></span></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13444-zannmato","name":"zannmato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T13:31:56-07:00","id":1457730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457693#post1457693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Yes. An example would be something along the lines of:<br /> <br /> (Modeled from Relentless) <b>Playful:</b> Regain one point of Willpower if your character delays gratification when interacting with a target. Regain all Willpower if she knows that by not instantly satisfying her urges she is raising the chances of a dangerous situation occurring, such as a Hero interrupting.<br /> <br /> (Modeled from Vicious) <b>Playful: </b>Regain one point of Willpower when your character goes over-the-top in dealing with someone, whether physically or emotionally, such as letting them run through a maze of your own devising, or taking the time to orchestrate a betrayal amongst their cohort. Regain all Willpower when doing this unnecessarily to prolong enjoyment, or when developing the conditions of a feed to increase the amount of satiety obtained.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wow, this is perfect. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457693#post1457693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Not that I am aware of, but have a look at the corresponding threads<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares\"> Homebrew Nightmares - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Because, surprisingly, there wasn't already a thread for this, even though Nightmares are literally designed to be homebrewed. Here until we get a Beast forum. Ideas or fully crunched mechanics are both fine, as are Nightmares based on homebrew templates. You Are Not Prepared (General): The nightmare of </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...w-beast-merits</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, kinda skimmed these before, but I\u2019ll have to look over them in detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457693#post1457693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Whatever you can think of can usually fit the template of the Families. Inguma is just a fear of the other, this can be serial killers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I\u2019m not attached to a family for the concept. I\u2019m mostly trying see how I can make the concept work right now. I like the idea of horrors styled after modern terrors, like mutants and slashers, and aliens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457693#post1457693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Depends. I can agree with 21C Hermit, but the fear of technology can fit into any of the nightmares that the Families produce. Just think of the fear that it produces e.g. does it make you feel hopeless, exposed, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s part of the problem I guess, I don\u2019t really feel exposed from the ghost in the machine. I might be frightened because it\u2019s otherworldly in a way I can\u2019t begin to understand, or because it\u2019s strong, or because it wants to do me harm. It barley registers that it can get me from a unexpected way. I don\u2019t know, I guess I\u2019m used to the idea that anyone, if they were so inclined could see my search history or hack my bank account.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457693#post1457693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) I guess this is another it depends question. But, judging from what you've asked, your attempting to make some sort of trickster Beast. I'd say Ruin, cause 'some people just want to watch the world burn.'</div> </div> </div> </div> hehe, caught me. I want to make a AI that trolls people in mostly harmless ways, but that still makes it clear that it had the power to hurt them if it really wanted to. Kinda in that sociopathic style from certain parts of the internet. I liked the Inguma birthright that lets you text people even when they disconnect their computers from power, and put phones on airplane mode. Maybe hack someone\u2019s bank account and buy them something they hate with a note telling them they need better security. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zannmato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457693#post1457693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) Incredibly. Super-versatile when it comes to feeding and gaining willpower and leaves others in the dark and confused.</div> </div> </div> </div> Great, the AI will take that then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T14:04:03-07:00","id":1457732,"title":"","content":"New Questions!<br /> 1) Is there a way to make a nice adjacent Tempter? That hunger seems rather hard to make a positive spin out of. I know part of the point of Beast is Monstrousness nature, but getting someone to cheat on their spouse seems rather horrible for a mid tier meal.<br /> 2) Would a Horror that represents the fear of insanity be valid? Something like a Mooneborn Changeling?<br /> 2.5)Any Avatisms besides Alien Mindset good for this concept?<br /> 3) Is it possible to try to intentionally send the Horror into people\u2019s nightmares for it to feed, in the event of it\u2019s hungers either being too impractical at that point in time or simply being against the human parts morality?<br /> 3.5) Is it practical to do so?<br /> 4) Would being with a loyal group of followers count as being within the Minions or Thralls lair traits for Lair Resonance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 08-26-2021, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T17:28:54-07:00","id":1457742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457732#post1457732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is there a way to make a nice adjacent Tempter? That hunger seems rather hard to make a positive spin out of. I know part of the point of Beast is Monstrousness nature, but getting someone to cheat on their spouse seems rather horrible for a mid tier meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enablers who're trying to play out their needs in a positive fashion have the uncomfortable requirement of intimately knowing their victims' boundaries. Setting aside how fucked up that can get, <a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/655925306248527872\" target=\"_blank\">that's a time investment that you might not have</a>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Would a Horror that represents the fear of insanity be valid? Something like a Mooneborn Changeling? </div> </div> </div>This would be that &quot;high-concept&quot; thing again \u2014 figuring out what your Horror &quot;represents&quot; is the process of Legend-building in a nutshell. You can steer your reputation toward &quot;'madness' is bad news&quot; easily enough, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1399503-the-astral-ideal-of-monsters-and-its-relation-to-hunters?p=1401624#post1401624\">I would advise against trying to play Lovecraft Lite with the Begotten</a> when the irrationality of the world is so much more the Insatiable's cup of ichor.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Is it possible to try to intentionally send the Horror into people\u2019s nightmares for it to feed, in the event of it\u2019s hungers either being too impractical at that point in time or simply being against the human parts morality?<br /> 3.5) Is it practical to do so? </div> </div> </div>Short of getting extremely lucky or having a very particular geographical distance you can arrange for while you're Starving, not really. If your Hunger is impractical it's usually because you're fed beyond the threshold of mere satiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T03:57:49-07:00","id":1457776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457732#post1457732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Questions!<br /> 1) Is there a way to make a nice adjacent Tempter? That hunger seems rather hard to make a positive spin out of. I know part of the point of Beast is Monstrousness nature, but getting someone to cheat on their spouse seems rather horrible for a mid tier meal.<br /> 2) Would a Horror that represents the fear of insanity be valid? Something like a Mooneborn Changeling?<br /> 2.5)Any Avatisms besides Alien Mindset good for this concept?<br /> 3) Is it possible to try to intentionally send the Horror into people\u2019s nightmares for it to feed, in the event of it\u2019s hungers either being too impractical at that point in time or simply being against the human parts morality?<br /> 3.5) Is it practical to do so?<br /> 4) Would being with a loyal group of followers count as being within the Minions or Thralls lair traits for Lair Resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 you could target people with habits that you find despicable.<br /> For example a member of a fanatical sect, you could feed by making him betray his ethics.<br /> 3 simply put your Satiety below 4, then wait and go to sleep.<br /> To select a specific target you can use the Hunting ground Lair trait or enter in the victim oneiros before going to sleep (both explained in player s guide)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T04:06:01-07:00","id":1457777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457732#post1457732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Questions!<br /> 1) Is there a way to make a nice adjacent Tempter? That hunger seems rather hard to make a positive spin out of. I know part of the point of Beast is Monstrousness nature, but getting someone to cheat on their spouse seems rather horrible for a mid tier meal.<br /> 2) Would a Horror that represents the fear of insanity be valid? Something like a Mooneborn Changeling?<br /> 2.5)Any Avatisms besides Alien Mindset good for this concept?<br /> 3) Is it possible to try to intentionally send the Horror into people\u2019s nightmares for it to feed, in the event of it\u2019s hungers either being too impractical at that point in time or simply being against the human parts morality?<br /> 3.5) Is it practical to do so?<br /> 4) Would being with a loyal group of followers count as being within the Minions or Thralls lair traits for Lair Resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>2.5 Infestation could work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T06:56:42-07:00","id":1457783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457776#post1457776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 you could target people with habits that you find despicable.<br /> For example a member of a fanatical sect, you could feed by making him betray his ethics.</div> </div> </div> </div> Paying evil unto evil? I guess, but it doesn\u2019t sit well with me. Looks like the best way involves a lot planning, or have Needs Must and Eye of Heaven. Is it possible to feed by getting someone shy to stand up for themselves? Would convincing warlords that murder is wrong, or attacking that city was morally wrong, and to make reparations for the damage they have done work?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457776#post1457776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 simply put your Satiety below 4, then wait and go to sleep.<br /> To select a specific target you can use the Hunting ground Lair trait or enter in the victim oneiros before going to sleep (both explained in player s guide)</div> </div> </div> </div> oh, I saw hunting ground, must of missed specifically going to their Oneiros. I\u2019ll look for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looks like Nobody answered question 4, is that because the is no set answer, or the question was phrased poorly and nobody understood it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 08-27-2021, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T07:39:15-07:00","id":1457789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457732#post1457732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Would being with a loyal group of followers count as being within the Minions or Thralls lair traits for Lair Resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel with Thralls and Minions the trick there is at what points it stops being a swarm. I reckon, just as an initial judgement, it would depend on the disposition of the group. Minions would need to be small subservient beings, so thinking animals and the like, but it'd be tricky to impose. Same for Thrall, but I think that might be a bit easier to Impose, as the Thrall condition does work.<br /> <br /> My own general rule of thumb is this: Don't rely on Thrall or Minions for resonance purposes, the general parameters are very difficult to conceive. If you need something easier to Impose or Resonate with, your best bet is the likes of Poor Light, Jagged etc, as these can be fairly easy to forcibly recreate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27033-syantor","name":"syantor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T08:36:52-07:00","id":1457794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457783#post1457783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is it possible to feed by getting someone shy to stand up for themselves? Would convincing warlords that murder is wrong, or attacking that city was morally wrong, and to make reparations for the damage they have done work?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As long as the victim feels a little guilty,&quot; &quot;enough to cause the victim shame, or invite rebuke from her peers,&quot; &quot;it should be at odds with their self-image,&quot; and &quot;fundamentally transgress his beliefs&quot; all suggest no.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety meals for Enablers can be acquired by something as petty as instigating gossip or breaking curfew. You don't have to go full Life-Destroying Bad Decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T09:04:13-07:00","id":1457795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457732#post1457732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Questions!<br /> 2) Would a Horror that represents the fear of insanity be valid? Something like a Mooneborn Changeling?<br /> 2.5)Any Avatisms besides Alien Mindset good for this concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would be more specific than \u201cinsanity\u201d. Is it the fear that you can\u2019t trust your senses? That you might lose control of your actions? That you might get attacked by an insane person? Forbidden knowledge that drives you insane? You can go for a vague lovecraftian sanity-eater (in which case just take your pick of the Makara atavisms), but then it becomes more about being a hideous monster then the fear of insanity, per say. <br /> <br /> For example, I have an Inguma Whisperer npc who\u2019s the fear that you are secretly crazy, and that you might be found out by another person who is secretly even crazier. So besides Alien Mindset, stealth and information gathering atavisms suit him, like From the Shadows, Enemy Within, Needs Must, etc. But, in general, Nightmares give better ammo for screwing with people\u2019s minds than Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457732#post1457732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 4) Would being with a loyal group of followers count as being within the Minions or Thralls lair traits for Lair Resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say yes. Some Lair traits can be ridiculously easy to access in combination with other Traits, like using Death of Light to impose Poor Light. So it wouldn\u2019t be unbalanced to allow something like Allies to trigger Minions, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T11:57:06-07:00","id":1457805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457794#post1457794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;As long as the victim feels a little guilty,&quot; &quot;enough to cause the victim shame, or invite rebuke from her peers,&quot; &quot;it should be at odds with their self-image,&quot; and &quot;fundamentally transgress his beliefs&quot; all suggest no.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety meals for Enablers can be acquired by something as petty as instigating gossip or breaking curfew. You don't have to go full Life-Destroying Bad Decision.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. Maybe for those characters that don\u2019t want to go father than they have to to feed, investment in the merits that let get you more out of a feeding is warranted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457795#post1457795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I would be more specific than \u201cinsanity\u201d. Is it the fear that you can\u2019t trust your senses? That you might lose control of your actions? That you might get attacked by an insane person? Forbidden knowledge that drives you insane? You can go for a vague lovecraftian sanity-eater (in which case just take your pick of the Makara atavisms), but then it becomes more about being a hideous monster then the fear of insanity, per say.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really haven\u2019t gotten very far with the character idea, just was thinking about what people fear happening to them. That being said, I kinda like the idea of invading someone\u2019s dreams, and just kinda sticking there while the go through their day, whispering to them. Really, both the fear of sensory deception and the loss of control are actually pretty terrifying. Being attacked by a crazy person is really in my mind the same fear as being attacked by a wild animal. The forbidden knowledge angle seems interesting, but I almost want that to be a separate character. Thanks, you have given me much to ponder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457795#post1457795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I have an Inguma Whisperer npc who\u2019s the fear that you are secretly crazy, and that you might be found out by another person who is secretly even crazier. So besides Alien Mindset, stealth and information gathering atavisms suit him, like From the Shadows, Enemy Within, Needs Must, etc. But, in general, Nightmares give better ammo for screwing with people\u2019s minds than Atavisms.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s a great npc! Will remember when I come back to this character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457795#post1457795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say yes. Some Lair traits can be ridiculously easy to access in combination with other Traits, like using Death of Light to impose Poor Light. So it wouldn\u2019t be unbalanced to allow something like Allies to trigger Minions, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Great! I take it that a Primordial Cult would work for Minions, but would the main part of the Cult work for Thralls? Is the presence of the Herald alone enough for Thralls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 08-27-2021, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T13:12:40-07:00","id":1457819,"title":"","content":"Last question, for now<br /> Can there be lair traits that are distractingly pleasant to be in, like a garden so beautiful that makes one one want to stay forever, or a drugged atmosphere that clouds one\u2019s mind? I know Hoard is in theme, but it doesn\u2019t quite do it in the way I want. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T15:58:34-07:00","id":1457838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457819#post1457819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last question, for now<br /> Can there be lair traits that are distractingly pleasant to be in, like a garden so beautiful that makes one one want to stay forever, or a drugged atmosphere that clouds one\u2019s mind? I know Hoard is in theme, but it doesn\u2019t quite do it in the way I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get to the Primordial Dream from the Bright Dream by navigating toward places that are scary and less likely to have people in them. The Begotten's mental powers that provide a benefit to their subject do so through fear. The cultural tendency of these monsters occupying the oldest part of the human psyche is to portray themselves honestly in the deepest parts of their sanctuary/hunting-ground. The resonance necessary to expand that hunting ground is partially managed by the presence of Lair Traits. The Horror hunts uninvited guests unless the Beast prevents it from doing so by using its form to do something else.<br /> <br /> You can have stuff in your Lair that's distracting and/or pleasant, but making those things able to be reproduced elsewhere through the basic resonance daisy-chain quickly risks turning a Beast into something other than an image-conscious nightmare-cryptid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T16:03:13-07:00","id":1457839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1457819#post1457819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last question, for now<br /> Can there be lair traits that are distractingly pleasant to be in, like a garden so beautiful that makes one one want to stay forever, or a drugged atmosphere that clouds one\u2019s mind? I know Hoard is in theme, but it doesn\u2019t quite do it in the way I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lair traits are designed in such a way that the mechanics are fairly understandable, in that they almost always impose penalties to attributes or inflict conditions. So you could, for example, choose a trait like Stench and explain it as overwhelmingly pleasant smells caused by flowers in the lair. The penalty to exertion becomes one of apathy or a desire not to stop smelling. Or Maze and the Int + Comp roll is to shake of the effect and leave. This is all briefly addressed on page 102 of the core book. What is more important to consider than the mechanics though is the way the description works with similarities for imposing traits or accessing the Lair. In this extended example it would be pretty obvious that the Beast could use a florist, a garden in bloom, a perfume counter at a retail store. They themselves also gain immunity to naturally occurring instances of this trait. To my knowledge none of the books give explicit rules for the limits of trait beyond the statement &quot;they may provide dice penalties or bonuses to Skills, or count as Extreme Environments.&quot; However, in trying to design some of my own by tabulating all the existing ones and what they do I came to the realisation that everything I was thinking of could be better done re-flavouring the ones that exist rather than making new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T10:59:46-07:00","id":1459318,"title":"","content":"What Family and Hunger would you call for Mytha, the Baneful Queen from Dark Souls 2? Is she the rare Namtaru with Alien Allure? Is that even possible? The player's guide says &quot;No matter what amalgam of features a Namtaru may possess, no alien beauty arises from gazing upon him&quot;. For context, I'm trying to place most of the Monsters I see in the context of Beast. I find most of bosses form Dark Souls are Anakim, but there are exceptions. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/JyLfKdbh.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/JyLfKdbh.png</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T16:49:59-07:00","id":1459707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459318#post1459318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Family and Hunger would you call for Mytha, the Baneful Queen from Dark Souls 2? Is she the rare Namtaru with Alien Allure? Is that even possible? The player's guide says &quot;No matter what amalgam of features a Namtaru may possess, no alien beauty arises from gazing upon him&quot;. For context, I'm trying to place most of the Monsters I see in the context of Beast. I find most of bosses form Dark Souls are Anakim, but there are exceptions. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/JyLfKdbh.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/JyLfKdbh.png</a></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>The link is broken, I can't see that image<br /> <br /> Anyway, there is a legend of the white ladies, some ghostly ladies that are increadibly beautiful ghost right until they aren't and pounce on their prey turning hideus right before they kill their prey, normally a guy that fell for her charms...come to think of it, that trailer of the witcher where Gerald fights a monter lady and kills her by poisoning his own blood is a good example of a Namtaru with Allien Allure<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T22:09:10-07:00","id":1459722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459707#post1459707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The link is broken, I can't see that image</div> </div> </div> </div> Sigh. Is this better?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://igorgrechanyi.cgsociety.org/4klv/mytha-the-baneful-qu\" target=\"_blank\">https://igorgrechanyi.cgsociety.org/...the-baneful-qu</a><br /> <br /> Basically, in case the link still doesn\u2019t work, Mytha looks like a serpent centaur, or lamia. She also carries her own severed head. She resides in a bathhouse designed to pump what in game is only known as poison to enhance her \u201cbeauty\u201d. She even heals from the poisons touch. She did this to herself, to try and attract the attention of her love that spurned her. Fromsoft can and has done very effective nightmare fuel. They chose to make her sort of conventionally attractive. I\u2019m not phased by snakes, but I know a lot of people are. This makes it hard for me to place her family. She isn\u2019t really about hopelessness, or hidden and unseen. She definitely has nothing to do with exposure or confinement. Leaves Makara, Namtaru, Inguma. Makara is shaky in my mind, because she really doesn\u2019t have any symbolism of the depths around her, besides maybe having Alien Allure. Her most defining lair traits are Toxic, and Thralls. Doesn\u2019t really invoke the lair of a Makara, which is way more naturally alien to human existence. Inguma is a decent fit, but only in the way Inguma fits literally all monsters descended from humans. Also no Atavisms fit her from Inguma. Finally we have Namtaru. She shares some symbolism with Medusa, but differs in many more. She might be disgusting to some, but I\u2019m sure just as many have no problem with her. The other thing is that the rest of her potential Atavisms are from here. So I\u2019m stuck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459707#post1459707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, there is a legend of the white ladies, some ghostly ladies that are increadibly beautiful ghost right until they aren't and pounce on their prey turning hideus right before they kill their prey, normally a guy that fell for her charms...come to think of it, that trailer of the witcher where Gerald fights a monter lady and kills her by poisoning his own blood is a good example of a Namtaru with Allien Allure</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I will look this up. Edit: If you have a link I would be much obliged<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 09-12-2021, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T23:14:57-07:00","id":1459726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459722#post1459722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sigh. Is this better?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://igorgrechanyi.cgsociety.org/4klv/mytha-the-baneful-qu&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://igorgrechanyi.cgsociety.org/...the-baneful-qu</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Namtaru with Alien Allure and Basilisk Touch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T08:22:18-07:00","id":1459752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459726#post1459726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Namtaru with Alien Allure and Basilisk Touch?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what I would assume, but I keep having doubts. Only other Atavism I would give her is Unbreakable. At least her hunger is easy to place. She is easily a Tyrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T14:42:26-07:00","id":1459770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459752#post1459752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s what I would assume, but I keep having doubts. Only other Atavism I would give her is Unbreakable. At least her hunger is easy to place. She is easily a Tyrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>She\u2019s a beheaded snake thing \u2014 it should be repulsive enough for most to count as Namtaru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T15:11:10-07:00","id":1459774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459752#post1459752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s what I would assume, but I keep having doubts. Only other Atavism I would give her is Unbreakable. At least her hunger is easy to place. She is easily a Tyrant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overthinking this. A lot.<br /> <br /> Alien allure doesn't have to due with beauty, namtaru don't have some special revulsion to having it. Alien allure simply means SOMETHING about the horror attracts people to it.<br /> <br /> Also, realistically, almost every single mortal seeing her jn real life would DEFINITELY have am issue with the appearance. Like if you don't then you've seen some shit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T15:39:37-07:00","id":1459779,"title":"","content":"So after a quick look up the character, She becomes a decapitated Naga because she drank some poison to try and make herself more beautiful after finding out her husband was thinking of moving on because her beauty wasn't enough(or, more clearly, he was moving on because of other problems with his wife and the beatuy was not enough of a perk to keep at it, and Mytha took that as &quot;Damn gurl, y can't u be mor beautifullers?&quot;), and her aesthetic is a decapitated naga. On all levels she's a Namtaru, <i>probably</i> a Collector since her balm ot her fears is to accumulate and cultivate more of the posion in question.<br /> <br /> The Namtaru can and do possess things like the Striking Looks Merit and the Alien Allure Atavism-what kind of bronze-gothic horror game would this be if there was no gothic romance of decay-but the point of that for the Namtaru is to understand that entropic romanticism <i>is</i> a response to that decaying of physical, psychic, and spiritual forms. That society marches towards it's taboos is no surprise, and that some fear responses include the fetishization and submission to that frightful thing is not particularly controversial. It's clear that at some point, Mytha's standards changed and accepted this current state.<br /> <br /> I&quot;m not sure I would call her a <i>Beast</i>, though. Obviously because a) Dark Souls is not going to neatly line up with other game's outlook on things, but also b) a big part of what the Devouring is is learning that your fears are a part of of you, getting to real roots of that fear, and learning to embrace that as a part of yourself while cutting out the more superficial and more useless reads of &quot;Why this scares me?&quot; Mytha doesn't strike me as having internalized anything-if anything, she seems consumed by her fears in a way that's more befitting the Insatiable (and boy howdy is Dark Souls a great game series to find Insatiable) or the not-book-canon-at-all instance of where a nascent Beast skips Beastdom and is instead devoured straight into becoming a Rampant. But that's all academic.<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm not one to question a person's sense of aesthetics or their fetishes and kink, I'll freely admit &quot;Oh yeah baby, you got some kind of Alien Allure going on there&quot; was not a response I had the first few times I looked at the pictures in question. Different strokes for different folks, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-12-2021, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T17:28:43-07:00","id":1459796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459774#post1459774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're overthinking this. A lot.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it wouldn\u2019t be the first time. Definitely won\u2019t be the last.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459774#post1459774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alien allure doesn't have to due with beauty, namtaru don't have some special revulsion to having it. Alien allure simply means SOMETHING about the horror attracts people to it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459774#post1459774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, realistically, almost every single mortal seeing her jn real life would DEFINITELY have am issue with the appearance. Like if you don't then you've seen some shit</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess I\u2019m jaded then? Because I frankly would be a lot more worried about the spear than her appearance. I don\u2019t know, she doesn\u2019t seem that horrifying. The decapitation is pretty weird, but in the moment I doubt I would even notice.Then again, I\u2019ve have a gun pointed at me and I didn\u2019t really have much of a reaction at the time, or really ever. (I accidentally trespassed while at night, and drove off the road. Got lucky they stayed calm.) So maybe I\u2019m not a good metric on how normal people react.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459779#post1459779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So after a quick look up the character, She becomes a decapitated Naga because she drank some poison to try and make herself more beautiful after finding out her husband was thinking of moving on because her beauty wasn't enough, and her aesthetic is a decapitated naga. On all levels she's a Namtaru, <i>probably</i> a Collector since her balm ot her fears is to accumulate and cultivate more of the posion in question.</div> </div> </div> </div> Great point! I was thinking about how she started requiring her servants to be veiled, and made her creations headless so they could not gaze on her, but that\u2019s a really good point about her gathering poison to herself.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459779#post1459779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Namtaru can and do possess things like the Striking Looks Merit and the Alien Allure Atavism-what kind of bronze-gothic horror game would this be if there was no gothic romance of decay-but the point of that for the Namtaru is to understand that entropic romanticism <i>is</i> a response to that decaying of physical, psychic, and spiritual forms. That society marches towards it's taboos is no surprise, and that some fear responses include the fetishization and submission to that frightful thing is not particularly controversial. It's clear that at some point, Mytha's standards changed and accepted this current state.</div> </div> </div> </div> Clearly, I\u2019ve not read enough Gothic Horror. I\u2019m not used to the idea of romanticized entropy, but I guess it must exist. Hmm, I wonder if the fetishization of fear explains some of the stranger things I\u2019ve seen. Like the not completely untrue memes of being attracted to the Dead by Daylights killers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459779#post1459779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I&quot;m not sure I would call her a <i>Beast</i>, though. Obviously because a) Dark Souls is not going to neatly line up with other game's outlook on things, but also b) a big part of what the Devouring is is learning that your fears are a part of of you, getting to real roots of that fear, and learning to embrace that as a part of yourself while cutting out the more superficial and more useless reads of &quot;Why this scares me?&quot; Mytha doesn't strike me as having internalized anything-if anything, she seems consumed by her fears in a way that's more befitting the Insatiable (and boy howdy is Dark Souls a great game series to find Insatiable) or the not-book-canon-at-all instance of where a nascent Beast skips Beastdom and is instead devoured straight into becoming a Rampant. But that's all academic.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think she fits a self-made Deviant more than anything, but yeah. Dark Souls doesn\u2019t really fit Beast well at all, but this started as a exercise to try and see Monsters through a Beast lens. Dark Souls likes to draw from Mythical symbolism, so I thought it would be fun to start there. The Insatiable are in Conquering Heroes, right? Clearly I need to pick that up to see the difference between them and Beasts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459779#post1459779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while I'm not one to question a person's sense of aesthetics or their fetishes and kink, I'll freely admit &quot;Oh yeah baby, you got some kind of Alien Allure going on there&quot; was not a response I had the first few times I looked at the pictures in question. Different strokes for different folks, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Truthfully, I really don\u2019t get which creatures should have Alien Allure. I\u2019ve just been going with whether or not I think a particular thing is being played for fan service. Other bosses are more warped from normal human standards. That she looks vaguely human, and has lots of references to having made herself look \u201cbeautiful\u201c is enough for me. I\u2019ve also seen references that people like her. Part of the problem is that I don\u2019t really have a good sense of positive aesthetics.<br /> Honestly, I don\u2019t get why mermaids, sirens, any other \u201cbeautiful\u201d monster are considered such. What exactly is supernatural beauty? Like, is it a illusion like glamor? Are the monsters just supposed to be human enough where \u201cbeauty\u201d applies? Is it mind control? Am I overthinking it, or fundamentally misunderstanding it? Probably.<br /> <br /> Edited: Because it probably provides too much personal information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 09-12-2021, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T18:27:12-07:00","id":1459799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459796#post1459796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, it wouldn\u2019t be the first time. Definitely won\u2019t be the last.<br /> <br /> Oh, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> I guess I\u2019m jaded then? Because I frankly would be a lot more worried about the spear than her appearance. I don\u2019t know, she doesn\u2019t seem that horrifying. The decapitation is pretty weird, but in the moment I doubt I would even notice.Then again, I\u2019ve have a gun pointed at me and I didn\u2019t really have much of a reaction at the time, or really ever. (I accidentally trespassed while at night, and drove off the road. Got lucky they stayed calm.) So maybe I\u2019m not a good metric on how normal people react.<br /> <br /> Great point! I was thinking about how she started requiring her servants to be veiled, and made her creations headless so they could not gaze on her, but that\u2019s a really good point about her gathering poison to herself.<br /> Clearly, I\u2019ve not read enough Gothic Horror. I\u2019m not used to the idea of romanticized entropy, but I guess it must exist. Hmm, I wonder if the fetishization of fear explains some of the stranger things I\u2019ve seen. Like the not completely untrue memes of being attracted to the Dead by Daylights killers.<br /> I think she fits a self-made Deviant more than anything, but yeah. Dark Souls doesn\u2019t really fit Beast well at all, but this started as a exercise to try and see Monsters through a Beast lens. Dark Souls likes to draw from Mythical symbolism, so I thought it would be fun to start there. The Insatiable are in Conquering Heroes, right? Clearly I need to pick that up to see the difference between them and Beasts.<br /> Truthfully, I really don\u2019t get which creatures should have Alien Allure. I\u2019ve just been going with whether or not I think a particular thing is being played for fan service. Other bosses are more warped from normal human standards. That she looks vaguely human, and has lots of references to having made herself look \u201cbeautiful\u201c is enough for me. I\u2019ve also seen references that people like her. Part of the problem is that I don\u2019t really have a good sense of positive aesthetics.<br /> Honestly, I don\u2019t get why mermaids, sirens, any other \u201cbeautiful\u201d monster are considered such. What exactly is supernatural beauty? Like, is it a illusion like glamor? Are the monsters just supposed to be human enough where \u201cbeauty\u201d applies? Is it mind control? Am I overthinking it, or fundamentally misunderstanding it? Probably.<br /> <br /> Edited: Because it probably provides too much personal information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just focusing on the reply to me. I sincerely think that if you were to see her in real life, you'd be disgusted. It's easy to see something in a video game so much it don't matter, but in real life it's WAY different. Like not even comparable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T19:03:59-07:00","id":1459805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459799#post1459799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just focusing on the reply to me. I sincerely think that if you were to see her in real life, you'd be disgusted. It's easy to see something in a video game so much it don't matter, but in real life it's WAY different. Like not even comparable</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely. Maybe I\u2019m wrong. But my past experience says I under react to things. *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T19:16:40-07:00","id":1459808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459796#post1459796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, I\u2019ve not read enough Gothic Horror. I\u2019m not used to the idea of romanticized entropy, but I guess it must exist. Hmm, I wonder if the fetishization of fear explains some of the stranger things I\u2019ve seen. Like the not completely untrue memes of being attracted to the Dead by Daylights killers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a good idea to get into gothic/Romantic(not romantic) literature, goth cinema, and the gothic subculture on the whole the longer one relates to and experiences the Chronicles- and World- of Darkness franchise, though not neccesary. I (and many other writers) read Byron and watched The Crow so you don't have to.<br /> <br /> Also, because it's loosely related to this topic and I love it:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.redd.it/ld5zu2ocp8741.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.