ey vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T07:59:28-07:00","id":1459848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1459816#post1459816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Thank you, ArcaneArts.<br /> Edit: oh your signature says you would prefer Arcane.<br /> Thank you, Arcane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kelly or Sean work, as is comfortable for you to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-13-2021, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T05:10:58-07:00","id":1460633,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, I had a question regarding the Legendary Horror merit introduced in the BPG, not so much its function however.<br /> <br /> What numina would you say the Horror would be able to access? The general ones as described in the main corebook, potentially the Unfettered numina etc, I've always been puzzled at what could and could not go when selecting the merit for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27033-syantor","name":"syantor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:11:20-07:00","id":1464765,"title":"","content":"So I really can't find a definitive by searching google, has there been a consensus on how to calculate a Horror's health? Is a Horror always a dream form creature essentially and therefore its size doesnt impact it's health or is it actually present/ephemeral and it's health is resistance + size? Unfettered are said to be Ephemeral beings which to me almost implies Horrors are ephemeral to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-21-2021, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:46:10-07:00","id":1464776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1464765#post1464765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I really can't find a definitive by searching google, has there been a consensus on how to calculate a Horror's health? Is a Horror always a dream form creature essentially and therefore its size doesnt impact it's health or is it actually present/ephemeral and it's health is resistance + size? Unfettered are said to be Ephemeral beings which to me almost implies Horrors are ephemeral to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>THe horror's Health is calculated with the same rules for Ephemeral Entities (Chapter 4), and keys primarily off of your (effective/)size, keeping in mind the added points mentioned on pg 99 in the The Horror Itself sidebar and any Atavisms or Merits that would effect that.<br /> <br /> A Horror does count as a ephemeral being and follows the rules that apply in the corebook, though if you possess the Beast Player's Guide, Goetia are understood as the Dreamborn iwthin Beast parlance, and Horrors are a class apart from them, the rules in Chapter 5 for them superceding the rules for Goetia/Dreamborn the rules in the core as it applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-21-2021, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:50:52-07:00","id":1464778,"title":"","content":"So yea, that seems to say clearly to me that Horrors use size for health. Odd that most things you find when searching for horror stats on google says the exact opposite with quite a bit of support. Regardless, I appreciate the answer and the ability to spend your extra points when you merge on size makes alot more sense now. Its a do or die entirely situation to fight in your Lair, they should be able to get some crazy levels of health given what a Horror represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T11:19:35-07:00","id":1464780,"title":"","content":"That raises one more question though, is there a maximum attribute for these extra points? They mentioned unfettered use the beast's lair as their rank but Lair can go to 10 and they say rank 6+ ephemeral beings are basically chronicle spanning big bads essentially. So second question, does that mean that any beast at Lair 6+ who spawns a unfettered has created a powerful monster that is basically campaign definingly strong? Aka rank 6+?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T12:13:58-07:00","id":1464785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1464780#post1464780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That raises one more question though, is there a maximum attribute for these extra points? They mentioned unfettered use the beast's lair as their rank but Lair can go to 10 and they say rank 6+ ephemeral beings are basically chronicle spanning big bads essentially. So second question, does that mean that any beast at Lair 6+ who spawns a unfettered has created a powerful monster that is basically campaign definingly strong? Aka rank 6+?</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Ephemeral Entites Rules as normal&quot; and basically, yeah. Honestly, any Beast at 6+ Lair is probably a campaign defining feature, whether they've claimed an Inheritance or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T18:35:47-07:00","id":1465230,"title":"","content":"So quick question: the books seem to suggest it's possible for Beasts to enter people's dreams directly from their Lair (presumably through the Tenemos/Primordial Dream) and feed on them in their dreams (similar to how the Horror does it of its own accord when you're starving/ravenous). How does that work exactly, though? I mean... I suppose they just open a Primordial Pathway to areas of the Astral, but how do Beasts find Oneiros (or whatever they call the area for people's dream) ? Do they just wander into the Astral until they find an Oneiros by accident, or do they have some way to directly get to an Oneiros if they know what they're looking for?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because it honestly sounds like a really fun way of feeding for Beasts, and one of my players wants to do that quite often, but I'm never quite sure how to handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 10-24-2021, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T20:12:28-07:00","id":1465237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1465230#post1465230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quick question: the books seem to suggest it's possible for Beasts to enter people's dreams directly from their Lair (presumably through the Tenemos/Primordial Dream) and feed on them in their dreams (similar to how the Horror does it of its own accord when you're starving/ravenous). How does that work exactly, though? I mean... I suppose they just open a Primordial Pathway to areas of the Astral, but how do Beasts find Oneiros (or whatever they call the area for people's dream) ? Do they just wander into the Astral until they find an Oneiros by accident, or do they have some way to directly get to an Oneiros if they know what they're looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Player's Guide goes into more detail, but the process essentially runs:<br /> <br /> 1. Be in your Lair.<br /> 2. Leave one of your Chambers without using a Burrow or Primordial Pathway, placing you in the larger dreamscape of the Primordial Dream, which mostly mirrors the material world (don't try this from your Heart or more esoteric Chambers, you will have further to travel).<br /> 3. The dreamscape is not a populated space; move towards places where more people should be (based on where you currently are) to cross the Horizon called the Day and enter the Bright Dream/Temenos.<br /> 4. Navigate between realms in the Bright Dream (largely mechanically identical to the rules for navigating the Temenos in <i>Astral Realms</i>), bridging your way conceptually toward a specific person to reach their Oneiros.<br /> 5. (Optional) Open a Primordial Pathway back to your Lair (possible in any part of the Bright Dream if one of your Lair Traits matches its Theme, which the Begotten always know) to deliberately target an individual for your Horror to feed from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:13:56-07:00","id":1465265,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Satchel^^ that's very helpful.<br /> <br /> I swear, it's a shame so many people ignore the Beast player guide. It added so much to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T15:00:43-08:00","id":1469130,"title":"","content":"Quick question about Insatiable: can they heal damage by spending Satiety the way Beasts do in their Lair, and if yes how does it work? Do they need to Subvert a Lair or create one, or since they're pretty much walking horrors to begin with, can they do it anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T12:20:46-08:00","id":1469187,"title":"","content":"I don't remember anything saying they can do so and would say considering their own origins and format in the setting you're probably justified in saying they can't do that with stolen lairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T13:37:57-08:00","id":1474436,"title":"","content":"Hey, everyone. Hope you have been having a good day. So I've had some questions gnawing on me for a bit, mostly about Beast's relation to dreams, and a few miscellaneous others.<br /> <br /> So, the Players guide to the Contagion Chronicles states that the Horror actually reaches the Bastion of the dreamer it's affecting, which seems to suggest that Dreams are reachable from the Astral. The same passage then goes on to say there is no passage from the Astral to Faerie...which I think means Arcadia/the Hedge. In the Player's Guide, opening Primordial Pathway into the Oneiros has the Horror specially target that individual for feeding when starving, which seems to suggest that everything stays in the Astral. So, what's actually happening when the Horror goes off and inflicts nightmares? Is the Bastion in the Oneiros, or is the Horror messing with the underlying currents that forms the Bastion?<br /> <br /> Can Beasts follow the path their Horror take in order to break into dreams on their own? Is this a Primordial Pathway, or a normal astral jaunt? <br /> <br /> If a Beast can make it into a Bastion, should they interact with it like a Changeling and use dreamweaving rules, or would that be a Kinship Merit?<br /> <br /> Can a Beast feed from scenarios created from dreamweaving or their own equivalent?<br /> <br /> and as for the miscellaneous questions<br /> <br /> What Hungers feed from spreading plagues, and the like? <br /> <br /> What can feed from spreading incredibly beautiful, but disturbing artwork around anonymously? Like making a monument appear in the middle of town overnight, that has eye watering engravings spelling out dooms for the town.<br /> <br /> What would you consider good family/hunger for doll/marionette/ect type horrors? From what I understand, the uncanny valley seems like the source of people's fears about dolls and stuff, which suggests Inguma to me, but I've seen a few things where the doll wants to make everyone dance on strings...which seems like a Talassii thing to me. What do Y'all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T14:03:00-08:00","id":1474437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474436#post1474436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Players guide to the Contagion Chronicles states that the Horror actually reaches the Bastion of the dreamer it's affecting, which seems to suggest that Dreams are reachable from the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll answer the rest of this after the shower, but making clear I'm looking at the same segment as you, toss up the page and section, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T14:40:40-08:00","id":1474440,"title":"","content":"To answer these specific parts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474436#post1474436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Hungers feed from spreading plagues, and the like?<br /> <br /> What can feed from spreading incredibly beautiful, but disturbing artwork around anonymously? Like making a monument appear in the middle of town overnight, that has eye watering engravings spelling out dooms for the town.<br /> <br /> What would you consider good family/hunger for doll/marionette/ect type horrors? From what I understand, the uncanny valley seems like the source of people's fears about dolls and stuff, which suggests Inguma to me, but I've seen a few things where the doll wants to make everyone dance on strings...which seems like a Talassii thing to me. What do Y'all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think any Hunger could feasibly be associated with either method, depending on how they're employed and the specifics involved, though Ravager springs to mind considering the potentially indiscriminate nature of spreading plagues/leaving up mind-bending artwork around town. They also sound most like the setpieces for a Namtaru-type feeding (or potentially Inguma, again depending on the particulars).<br /> <br /> As for doll-Horrors, Inguma and Talassii both seem like good fits. It's important to remember that any given monster could potentially fit into any Family depending on what the focus is; a doll could be an Eshmaki if the fear comes from an easily overlooked creature that leaps out of the shadows to attack, a Makara if you play up the puppetmaster angle of an antagonist that can only be discovered by peeling back layers of proxies and deceptions, or even an Anakim for an implacable automaton not moved by human sentiment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T14:49:17-08:00","id":1474441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474437#post1474437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll answer the rest of this after the shower, but making clear I'm looking at the same segment as you, toss up the page and section, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, so, very sorry for the delay. I didn't think anyone would answer so quickly. I'm using pg 22 &quot;The Hedge and The Astral &quot; in the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicles, pg 99 &quot;Inflicting Nightmares&quot; in the core Beast rulebook, and a little of pg 153 and &quot;the Bright Dream&quot; 's second paragraph. The rest is what I remember from Changeling 2e, in that a Bastion is a Dream, and rests on the Dreaming Roads, which is part of the Hedge...I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T14:50:21-08:00","id":1474442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474436#post1474436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Players guide to the Contagion Chronicles states that the Horror actually reaches the Bastion of the dreamer it's affecting, which seems to suggest that Dreams are reachable from the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordial Pathways can reach anywhere. But you're kinda right in that dreams are connected to the Astral because they're the stepping stone for anyone who needs to meditate into the Astral. But when someone meditates into the Astral, they kinda just appear in their Oneiros and their dreams presumably end because they're no longer dreaming. There's no passageway for anyone else to use when you're just dreaming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same passage then goes on to say there is no passage from the Astral to Faerie...which I think means Arcadia/the Hedge. </div> </div> </div>No natural passage, at least. See above about Primordial Pathways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Player's Guide, opening Primordial Pathway into the Oneiros has the Horror specially target that individual for feeding when starving, which seems to suggest that everything stays in the Astral. </div> </div> </div>The only mention of Primordial Pathways into an Oneiros in the BPG is about Larval Horrors. They seek out souls, not dreams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what's actually happening when the Horror goes off and inflicts nightmares? Is the Bastion in the Oneiros, or is the Horror messing with the underlying currents that forms the Bastion? </div> </div> </div>From the same paragraph you've mentioned in the PGttCC:<br /> &quot;A Bastion <i>is</i> a human dream and functions as one for any supernatural being who can see or manipulate dreams.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Beast can make it into a Bastion, should they interact with it like a Changeling and use dreamweaving rules, or would that be a Kinship Merit? </div> </div> </div>The next sentence in the same paragraph:<br /> &quot;A Horror intruding on a sleeping character\u2019s dreams can run into a changeling who broke into that character\u2019s Bastion, as they\u2019re both inside the same dream, and they interact with that dream in their own usual ways.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T15:25:16-08:00","id":1474447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474442#post1474442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primordial Pathways can reach anywhere. But you're kinda right in that dreams are connected to the Astral because they're the stepping stone for anyone who needs to meditate into the Astral. But when someone meditates into the Astral, they kinda just appear in their Oneiros and their dreams presumably end because they're no longer dreaming. There's no passageway for anyone else to use when you're just dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's why I'm trying not to involve Primordial Pathways, they kinda don't answer the question unless it happens that the Horror is using them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474442#post1474442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only mention of Primordial Pathways into an Oneiros in the BPG is about Larval Horrors. They seek out souls, not dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is literally true...because the passage I read uses the phrases &quot;individuals\u2019 personal soul&quot;, and &quot;a soul realm&quot; instead of Oneiros. Please look at pg 153 of the BPG.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474442#post1474442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the same paragraph you've mentioned in the PGttCC:<br /> &quot;A Bastion <i>is</i> a human dream and functions as one for any supernatural being who can see or manipulate dreams.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is great, but I'm asking if the Horror is still on the Astral side when it does it's thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474442#post1474442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next sentence in the same paragraph:<br /> &quot;A Horror intruding on a sleeping character\u2019s dreams can run into a changeling who broke into that character\u2019s Bastion, as they\u2019re both inside the same dream, and they interact with that dream in their own usual ways.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Unfortunately, I'm unclear as to what Beast's usual way is. Is it dreamweaving like Changelings? or do the Nightmare Shamans have their own system? Beasts don't exactly have the Glamor to spend like a Changeling does in order to Dream-Weave, but their powers can inflict nightmares, but as far as I'm aware, every instance of those powers are external to the dream, not actually from inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-11-2022, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T16:03:50-08:00","id":1474450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474447#post1474447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally true...because the passage I read uses the phrases &quot;individuals\u2019 personal soul&quot;, and &quot;a soul realm&quot; instead of Oneiros. Please look at pg 153 of the BPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad.<br /> The base fact is that a connection to a person's Oneiros allows the Horror to target that individual for feeding. I think this is supposed to tie into the Horror going hunting when Starving/Ravenous, but <i>that's</i> in turn too underexplained in the core book for me to say anything with certainty. Maybe it's expanded somewhere in the BPG and I've missed it.<br /> According to what I've read in the core book: when a Horror hunts it ventures out into the Astral and from there somehow enters the dreams of someone who's physically nearby. Having made a connection to someone's Oneiros might waive the physical proximity requirement for the Horror, allowing it to target people from afar, and/or make it prioritise such targets over others with no such connection. But that's completely hypothetical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is great, but I'm asking if the Horror is still on the Astral side when it does it's thing. </div> </div> </div>The question I quoted and answered was: &quot;<i>Is the Bastion in the Oneiros[..]?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, I'm unclear as to what Beast's usual way is. Is it dreamweaving like Changelings? or do the Nightmare Shamans have their own system? Beasts don't exactly have the Glamor to spend like a Changeling does in order to Dream-Weave, but their powers can inflict nightmares, but as far as I'm aware, every instance of those powers are external to the dream, not actually from inside. </div> </div> </div>Dreamweaving is specific for changelings.<br /> Beasts and Horrors interact with dreams as described in the BtP books. (If they contain such descriptions. I don't recally reading anything other than Dream Forms.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T16:23:01-08:00","id":1474453,"title":"","content":"Welp, everyone else has answered, but here we go anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474436#post1474436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, everyone. Hope you have been having a good day. So I've had some questions gnawing on me for a bit, mostly about Beast's relation to dreams, and a few miscellaneous others.<br /> <br /> So, the Players guide to the Contagion Chronicles states that the Horror actually reaches the Bastion of the dreamer it's affecting, which seems to suggest that Dreams are reachable from the Astral. The same passage then goes on to say there is no passage from the Astral to Faerie...which I think means Arcadia/the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so the Hedge and Faerie/Arcadia are two different dimensions with the Hedge being a barrier to between Faerie/Arcadia and Ironside/the mortal world.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is also the Astral Barrier that most anyone else has to pay a toll to cross, and from how it's been explained, the Astral is one side of a universal fork in the road, with Arcadia on the other side.<br /> <br /> Beast's can't form a Pathway to Arcadian Domains on account of not having made or become the beneficiary of the pledges that basically allow for &quot;hospitality&quot;, ie access and basic survival needs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Player's Guide, opening Primordial Pathway into the Oneiros has the Horror specially target that individual for feeding when starving, which seems to suggest that everything stays in the Astral. So, what's actually happening when the Horror goes off and inflicts nightmares? Is the Bastion in the Oneiros, or is the Horror messing with the underlying currents that forms the Bastion? </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, a Horror that is Inflicting Nightmares is opening Pathways into a target's dreams, which is both in a person's head and in a Bastion. One assumes a Horror <i>could</i> open up into a person's Oneiros, but the goings-on there are a little too substantial to just fit into their mouths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Beasts follow the path their Horror take in order to break into dreams on their own? Is this a Primordial Pathway, or a normal astral jaunt? </div> </div> </div>If a Horror is Inflicting Nightmares, they've already followed, but more on, yes, so long as a dream has resonance with a Beast's Lair, a Beast could open a Primordial Pathway into it. Naturally, the biggest problem of this is knowing if someone is dreaming in Trait-adjacent terms, but if your Horror has been razing it a lot recently, it's a safe bet that recurring dreams are keeping up a presence of resonance.<br /> <br /> A Beast could also get there by way of reverse Astral Jaunting, but that's time consuming, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Beast can make it into a Bastion, should they interact with it like a Changeling and use dreamweaving rules, or would that be a Kinship Merit? </div> </div> </div>Notably, there is no inherent ability to commit to dreamweaving, but the impact Beast's have on the Hedge carries over to dreams, and of course a Beast can daisy chain a Lair Trait into a Dream from the original Trait that was resonant in the first place.<br /> <br /> A Kinship Merit would very feasibly allow for the low scale of dreamweaving. You could also make a decent argument about Nightmares translating into full blown environmental tilts or crude dreamweaving effects in dreams<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can a Beast feed from scenarios created from dreamweaving or their own equivalent? </div> </div> </div>A Beast feeds off the shock of the individual experiencing the Beast as a psychospiritual presence of itself, regardless whether they experience it in a dream or not. It's how Inflicting Nightmares works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Hungers feed from spreading plagues, and the like? </div> </div> </div>Directly? Power, Prey, Punishment, Ruin. There's also a decent argument for Transgression if you're working with the target to spread the plague.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What can feed from spreading incredibly beautiful, but disturbing artwork around anonymously? Like making a monument appear in the middle of town overnight, that has eye watering engravings spelling out dooms for the town. </div> </div> </div>What, like an Arisen?<br /> <br /> Such an act could feed Power, Punishment, arguably Ruin, and Secrets easily. I imagine with some creativity, it could also feed into Prey and otherwise decently facilitate Transgression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would you consider good family/hunger for doll/marionette/ect type horrors? From what I understand, the uncanny valley seems like the source of people's fears about dolls and stuff, which suggests Inguma to me, but I've seen a few things where the doll wants to make everyone dance on strings...which seems like a Talassii thing to me. What do Y'all think? </div> </div> </div>Dolls and Marionettes? Hrm.<br /> <br /> Dolls and marionettes are more a formal subject than an actionable one, so with just that, there's less focus on Hunger and more on Family. The Uncanny Valley and themes of control do indeed neatly tie into Inguma and Talassii, but that uncanny valley can ramp up into grotesquerie in it's own way, so the Namataru have a nominal space to play with the icon. While not directly relating to the icon itself, the Nightmares of Darkness and Hopelessness can find some thin mileage with the icon, but I'd reserve that for if you really want o fuck with expectations and not just get the full blow of the icon, to which Inguma or Talassii remain your best friends.<br /> <br /> There is also a version of a doll Horror as a Nightmare of Exposure that becomes more fucked up the more I think about it and I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T17:04:03-08:00","id":1474456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474436#post1474436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Players guide to the Contagion Chronicles states that the Horror actually reaches the Bastion of the dreamer it's affecting, which seems to suggest that Dreams are reachable from the Astral. The same passage then goes on to say there is no passage from the Astral to Faerie...which I think means Arcadia/the Hedge. In the Player's Guide, opening Primordial Pathway into the Oneiros has the Horror specially target that individual for feeding when starving, which seems to suggest that everything stays in the Astral. So, what's actually happening when the Horror goes off and inflicts nightmares?<br /> <br /> Is the Bastion in the Oneiros, or is the Horror messing with the underlying currents that forms the Bastion?</div> </div> </div> </div>The most frequently-changing part of the Oneiros, the realm that applies the Dreamquake Tilt to anyone inside it for more than a scene, reflects a character's active thoughts and dreams. Mages meditate to enter the Astral by stilling their thoughts and blocking out the outside world; the &quot;entrance&quot; to their Oneiros is shaped by their thoughts and feelings at the moment they're arriving at it. Mage 2e outright describes dreams as the shallows of the Astral, and Changeling 1e's big book on dreams contains several entities that are dream-level reflections of beings from the deeper Astral, some of them emerging to that level due to supernatural tampering on either side of the interface. A Horror interacts with the outside world by overlapping the Lair with other locations, and it's a traumatic being to confront in the first place.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say that the Bastion is in dreams, but the Horror is there through the interface of the Pathway and it would be messing with the underlying currents that form the Bastion either way. A nightmare inflicted by a Horror is a particularly powerful dream that happens to have an inhabitant not derived from the dreamer's own unconscious mind, and changelings interact with it like they would any other nightmare Bastion just like the Horror interacts with it like a normal dream-hunt where it's a Dream Form with supernatural powers and influence over the terrain.<br /> <br /> If you're already in the Astral and make your way to someone's Oneiros, you can open the door for your Horror to get at their dreams from the inside, which sidesteps the problems of needing to have prescient-mind-reader-level instincts for when to open the Pathway and outgoing Pathways not bringing the Horror along with you; actions in the Oneiros lay the groundwork for dreams to happen later, if nothing else, due to the Bright Dream's narrative logic allowing for a monster to show up in your emotional metaphor because a monster showed up in your emotional metaphor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Beasts follow the path their Horror take in order to break into dreams on their own? Is this a Primordial Pathway, or a normal astral jaunt? </div> </div> </div>The Horror takes a Primordial Path; the Beast would need some extreme luck or foresight to manage the timing on that feat, since the target dream is the outside end of the Pathway and therefore you need to be inside the Lair to seize that opening and you immediately separate from the Horror when you leave anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T17:41:20-08:00","id":1474459,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone! This was all extremely helpful. I think I have a much better grasp on things now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> Thank you, I never seem to have a good grasp on what Hunger or Families a particular monster is best suited for.<br /> \u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> Sorry, for misunderstanding the intent of your answer. Thank you for correcting me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Thanks, your post pretty much covered everything. The concept of a Doll as a Ugallu is perfect. I'm still laughing at the horrible images my brain has conjured.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Mage says that? I'll have to find it. Changeling has reflections of stuff from the Astral? Very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":".  I have got to stop making these things out of order 02-11-2022, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T17:57:42-08:00","id":1474461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474459#post1474459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Mage says that? I'll have to find it. Changeling has reflections of stuff from the Astral? Very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Astral Realms</i> and <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i>, respectively. The material on the Skein is somewhat obsolete with 2e's rearrangement of the cosmology, but there's multiple Aeons and a daimon in there, among other things, and <i>Astral Realms</i> remains the most in-depth look at its eponymous portion of the metaphysics so far.<br /> <br /> (Dreams as the shallows of the Astral is straight out of Mage 2e Core's World of Magic chapter. Page 246.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-11-2022, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T15:07:12-08:00","id":1474587,"title":"","content":"Minor questions for clarification\u2019s sake:<br /> <br /> The Doppelganger Atavism is certainly interesting, but I\u2019m uncertain about how long they are supposed to live. I understand they die when their template wakes, but what does being able to maintain doppelgangers mean? Is it just a limit on the total doppelgangers, or do people stay unconscious while their doppelganger is maintained? I have some skepticism about being able to reach the former with higher Lair, excepting coma patients and other very long term sleepers, because people wake after a relatively short time frame, and some templates would start to wake before you could acquire and finish more duplicates. The latter isn\u2019t explicitly stated, but I can kinda see that interpretation.<br /> <br /> When Crushing Coils says \u201cand adds Lair dots to any rolls or resistance against opposition\u201d, what does that mean? Is it just for grappling, or does it add dice when someone is resisting in general?<br /> <br /> Do Beasts use their mental stats to calculate dream form stats? I was under the impression they used the highest of their physical mental and social to calculate their traits, but I can\u2019t find anything to suggest that except the Horrors traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T16:29:33-08:00","id":1474590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474587#post1474587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Doppelganger Atavism is certainly interesting, but I\u2019m uncertain about how long they are supposed to live. I understand they die when their template wakes, but what does being able to maintain doppelgangers mean? Is it just a limit on the total doppelgangers, or do people stay unconscious while their doppelganger is maintained? I have some skepticism about being able to reach the former with higher Lair, excepting coma patients and other very long term sleepers, because people wake after a relatively short time frame, and some templates would start to wake before you could acquire and finish more duplicates. The latter isn\u2019t explicitly stated, but I can kinda see that interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recall the list of people who can be subject to Inflicting Nightmares; understand the breadth of options implicit in &quot;She must render her victim unconscious&quot; for a splat with the ability to do large amounts of damage or apply poisons or bring to bear Environmental Tilts and Extreme Environments that prevent bashing damage from healing.<br /> <br /> Maintaining doppelgangers means having that many at the same time. Have a cold-room or the right drugs or a powerful left hook and keep an eye on your victims' vitals; the power doesn't use Medicine for nothing, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When Crushing Coils says \u201cand adds Lair dots to any rolls or resistance against opposition\u201d, what does that mean? Is it just for grappling, or does it add dice when someone is resisting in general? </div> </div> </div>You keep your hold automatically under ordinary circumstances, and if you need to roll a Strength check to keep your hold on something or something subtracts your Stamina from rolls to try and get you to drop it, you add your Lair dots to those Traits. These are separate circumstances from grappling, such as climbing or attempting to retain the use of a tool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Beasts use their mental stats to calculate dream form stats? I was under the impression they used the highest of their physical mental and social to calculate their traits, but I can\u2019t find anything to suggest that except the Horrors traits. </div> </div> </div>My impression is that you calculate your Dream Form stats like a mortal does in the uncommon situation where you're in the Astral and not merged with the Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T11:07:26-08:00","id":1474745,"title":"","content":"Idly fun, if horrible, thing to do:<br /> <br /> Steal Shrouds of Observation from the Seers (which will <i>never</i> have consequences, <s><i>don't</i></s><i> trust me</i>.), be ready to condemn a few choice souls to a life of exploitation and finally death, keep a Hallow with some help,and make Dopplegangers for them. You'll have key figures forever in your pocket, a decent set of spy agents, and all you pay for it is being a giant asshole of questionable morals to your friends and the enmity of local agents of one of the most powerful and terrifying organizations in the world.<br /> <br /> Look, it's definitely more fun than it sounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T12:09:30-08:00","id":1474752,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, it'd make for one hell of a Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T18:23:52-08:00","id":1474766,"title":"","content":"Well, I have more questions:<br /> <br /> How does Shadow Stalker work? What can you do besides inflict Nightmares on your host? Could you talk to the Host?<br /> <br /> When imposing Mirages, Murmurs, an the like, does the Beast get to chose what form those take?<br /> <br /> How effective are the non-physical Lair Traits (Bad Angles, Isolated, Mirages, Murmurs) at defending the Lair?<br /> <br /> Would allowing the Horror to use Nightmares on it's own be a decent merit?<br /> <br /> Similarly, would a merit allowing to use of Nightmares on someone who is in a area resonant with the Beast's Lair, without looking them in the eye or touching them be fine?<br /> <br /> I saw while browsing that someone made a Atavism about being a telepathic relay, or being a hive mind in other words. The concept quite charmed me, but it was noted that the concept might work better as a Nightmare. What's your opinion on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T19:32:32-08:00","id":1474775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474766#post1474766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Shadow Stalker work? What can you do besides inflict Nightmares on your host? Could you talk to the Host?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're specifically silent, so not likely \u2014 the main advantage is that, in contrast to Shadowed Soul, you're mobile without abandoning the ruse. It's a stalking tool, which means it's best used to gather information while going undetected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When imposing Mirages, Murmurs, an the like, does the Beast get to chose what form those take? </div> </div> </div>They should probably fit the idiom of the Beast's Horror, Lair, or Legend, but yeah, that tracks; the main mechanical effect of those Traits is their penalizing of subsets of Perception roll and otherwise distracting the victims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How effective are the non-physical Lair Traits (Bad Angles, Isolated, Mirages, Murmurs) at defending the Lair? </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on how you're using the Lair. Like most predators, the Lair's best defense is to not be found before it can do its work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would allowing the Horror to use Nightmares on it's own be a decent merit? </div> </div> </div>To what end?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, would a merit allowing to use of Nightmares on someone who is in a area resonant with the Beast's Lair, without looking them in the eye or touching them be fine? </div> </div> </div>That seems more in line with a secondary Nightmare like The Walls Have Eyes or You Can't Wake Up or You Are Infected than a Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I saw while browsing that someone made a Atavism about being a telepathic relay, or being a hive mind in other words. The concept quite charmed me, but it was noted that the concept might work better as a Nightmare. What's your opinion on the matter? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220454#post1220454\">The Atavism in question</a> is almost entirely mental effects that alter other people; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220554#post1220554\">the alternate take</a> is a little closer to the scope of Atavisms as a mostly sensory effect, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Let's be plain: the Astral's primary demonstrations of shared consciousness aren't especially hivemind-y, and the more hivemind-y section of the Astral is the one that resonates better with Beasts who favor Nightmares over Atavism \u2014 the gestalt psyches of the Mother's Land can't stop their component ideas from acting according to their own natures, and Dreamborn from the Bright Dream either possess a single person or exert their influence across a bunch of people in less direct fashion.<br /> <br /> Atavisms are tools the Horror uses to fulfill its Hunger, and most of those rely on a separation between Self and Other for the shock; losing oneself is a more cerebral sort of fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T20:40:33-08:00","id":1474781,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474775#post1474775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're specifically silent, so not likely \u2014 the main advantage is that, in contrast to Shadowed Soul, you're mobile without abandoning the ruse. It's a stalking tool, which means it's best used to gather information while going undetected.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was afraid of that, but I suppose that\u2019s why it\u2019s a Eshmaki Atavism. I was hoping I could use it for whispering in a victim\u2019s ear, and manipulating them from there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474775#post1474775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends entirely on how you're using the Lair. Like most predators, the Lair's best defense is to not be found before it can do its work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s fair. The goal of this particular Lair is to break intruder\u2019s will long before they could ever reach the Heart. I think it does that pretty well, especially with Vast Lair and the like, but I\u2019m not sure if that would stop bigger threats than regular mortals who somehow wound up in the Lair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474775#post1474775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what end?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well\u2026I\u2019m trying (and failing) to come up with a appropriate Horror for a character. This would be a heavily Nightmare focused character, and it\u2019s kinda weird that such a character\u2019s Horror wouldn\u2019t be able to use some of their Nightmares. It just seems reasonable to me. It\u2019s not something most characters would take, but I could see certain Horrors being able to project the more direct \u201cpsychic sledgehammers\u201d to force uncooperative prey into more advantageous positions. It doesn\u2019t really have a use in gameplay, mostly a narrative one. I guess the Horror is slightly more able to defend it\u2019s self without a Beast guiding it. Though anything able to seriously injure the Horror probably won\u2019t be deterred by Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474775#post1474775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems more in line with a secondary Nightmare like The Walls Have Eyes or You Can't Wake Up or You Are Infected than a Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok. To be honest, I\u2019ve never understood why those were not Merits. It\u2019s fine they aren\u2019t, but I\u2019m a bit confused is all. You Can\u2019t Wake Up just sounds like a really interesting Nightmare on it\u2019s own, having it\u2019s victim\u2019s question if they are even awake. But maybe that\u2019s only a Nightmare I\u2019d be interested in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474775#post1474775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220454#post1220454\">The Atavism in question</a> is almost entirely mental effects that alter other people; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220554#post1220554\">the alternate take</a> is a little closer to the scope of Atavisms as a mostly sensory effect, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Let's be plain: the Astral's primary demonstrations of shared consciousness aren't especially hivemind-y, and the more hivemind-y section of the Astral is the one that resonates better with Beasts who favor Nightmares over Atavism \u2014 the gestalt psyches of the Mother's Land can't stop their component ideas from acting according to their own natures, and Dreamborn from the Bright Dream either possess a single person or exert their influence across a bunch of people in less direct fashion.<br /> <br /> Atavisms are tools the Horror uses to fulfill its Hunger, and most of those rely on a separation between Self and Other for the shock; losing oneself is a more cerebral sort of fear.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. Are there really no astral entities that do their thing as a pack entity with multiple bodies and one mind? I would argue though, that a hive mind is fundamentally other. We are singular, and live lives only in our own heads. People find people acting in perfect unison to be creepy, it\u2019s even a trope. People think all sorts of weird things about twins, and that\u2019s just people who look pretty similar and are close. Humanity doesn\u2019t understand that level synchronization, and fears it\u2026a little. You\u2019re not wrong about it being a more cerebral fear\u2026but it fundamentally comes from a trait of the Horror. I don\u2019t know, maybe I\u2019m wrong. I\u2019m not anywhere near the level of understanding Beast required to be able to argue in any sufficient capacity. It just seems like it doesn\u2019t really fit either Atavisms or Nightmares to me. Granted, this concept is probably better handed by Deviant in terms of themes and abilities of it\u2019s characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T21:53:42-08:00","id":1474782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474781#post1474781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s fair. The goal of this particular Lair is to break intruder\u2019s will long before they could ever reach the Heart. I think it does that pretty well, especially with Vast Lair and the like, but I\u2019m not sure if that would stop bigger threats than regular mortals who somehow wound up in the Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understand that the primary function of the Lair is to serve as the favored hunting grounds of the Horror. Distraction goes a long way in a war of attrition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well\u2026I\u2019m trying (and failing) to come up with a appropriate Horror for a character. This would be a heavily Nightmare focused character, and it\u2019s kinda weird that such a character\u2019s Horror wouldn\u2019t be able to use some of their Nightmares. It just seems reasonable to me. It\u2019s not something most characters would take, but I could see certain Horrors being able to project the more direct \u201cpsychic sledgehammers\u201d to force uncooperative prey into more advantageous positions. It doesn\u2019t really have a use in gameplay, mostly a narrative one. I guess the Horror is slightly more able to defend it\u2019s self without a Beast guiding it. Though anything able to seriously injure the Horror probably won\u2019t be deterred by Nightmares. </div> </div> </div>Your Horror lives in your Lair and does not act autonomously on anything that isn't in the Lair or overlapped with the Lair. It has the benefit of being able to leverage the full strength of its Atavisms and always being able to substitute Willpower for Satiety some number of times in the using of them. When it's more active, you're less able to manage the imaginative legerdemain necessary to open Primordial Pathways or use Nightmares in general, and the reverse is also true.<br /> <br /> If your Horror is given the ability to use Nightmares autonomously, it now has another way for you to lose Satiety without the benefits of Lair resonance or Low Satiety bonuses, and it is more likely to be worse at using them due to the way Nightmare dice pools are constructed and how Horror activity is determined. You already have the ability to take control of your Horror at any time and use Nightmares while doing so.<br /> <br /> I said this to a poster who kept trying to figure out ways to make their geist more prominent and the same advice holds true here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1240771-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-geist-edition?p=1440277#post1440277\">Play the half of your character that is a person, not the feral monster that they get their powers from.</a> Remember that a character equipped to use Nightmares well and often is a character whose Horror is usually acting as iconography more than as a literal threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok. To be honest, I\u2019ve never understood why those were not Merits. It\u2019s fine they aren\u2019t, but I\u2019m a bit confused is all. </div> </div> </div>They have High Satiety, Satiety Expenditure, and Exceptional Success effects as normal Nightmares do; some of them are Kinship Nightmares; the rules for Kinship Merits make them infeasible to render as Kinship Merits; and Merits are already the systems folder for &quot;granularly-priced widget that we aren't making a dedicated system for.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm. Are there really no astral entities that do their thing as a pack entity with multiple bodies and one mind? </div> </div> </div>There's weird stuff like the sentient play <i>The Kindly Stranger</i> from Dancers in the Dusk, but that's from the Temenos and works by drafting people into a shared dreamspace \u2014 and that's easy to mechanically attribute to Dreamborn having to allocate all of their Numina to Numina, because the Kindly Stranger has an &quot;actor&quot; that it manifests as, and dreamriding in Changeling 1e required you to change a dream in order for you to appear in it and change it again for you to look like something other than yourself. There's also the thing that inhabits Endymion's Legacy from Night Horrors: The Unbidden, which came from a damaged section of the Dreamtime and is fundamentally alien to human consciousness \u2014 that's closer to cosmic horror than Beast generally deals with, as I've discussed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1399503-the-astral-ideal-of-monsters-and-its-relation-to-hunters?p=1401624#post1401624\">elsewhere</a>.<br /> <br /> Dreamborn are ideas. They inhabit and shape minds, but most of them are not terribly concerned with having a body unless that's part of how an individual specimen works or somebody draws them down; the Astral is the one otherworld in the metaphysics that actually sustains its invisible inhabitants without their directed effort, so most goetia don't need to worry about Essence hunger so much as the encroaching of others on their conceptual territory (hence the Temenos being described as a realm of physicalized abstraction where culture wars can get bloody).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would argue though, that a hive mind is fundamentally other. We are singular, and live lives only in our own heads. People find people acting in perfect unison to be creepy, it\u2019s even a trope. People think all sorts of weird things about twins, and that\u2019s just people who look pretty similar and are close. Humanity doesn\u2019t understand that level synchronization, and fears it\u2026a little. You\u2019re not wrong about it being a more cerebral fear\u2026but it fundamentally comes from a trait of the Horror. I don\u2019t know, maybe I\u2019m wrong. I\u2019m not anywhere near the level of understanding Beast required to be able to argue in any sufficient capacity. It just seems like it doesn\u2019t really fit either Atavisms or Nightmares to me. Granted, this concept is probably better handed by Deviant in terms of themes and abilities of it\u2019s characters. </div> </div> </div>Let me re-phrase: If you are in a hivemind with something you have ceased to have as clear a division between Self and Other as you would from not directly sharing a mind with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-16-2022, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T11:10:13-08:00","id":1474998,"title":"","content":"What is important for resonance to the Isolated Lair Trait? Is it the physical act of being alone, or is the feeling of Isolation sufficient? (ie can I use Nightmares to create resonance?)<br /> <br /> What does Immunity to Isolation entail? Never feeling Lonely again?<br /> <br /> Similarly, what is important for resonance to Murmurs? Is the whispers of a crowd enough, or can the hallucination of whispers work? <br /> <br /> Does imposing Bottomless in the Waking World drop people and stuff into the Lair?<br /> <br /> Does Immunity to Bottomless grant Immunity to Fall Damage, or does it just allow a Beast to never fall off a Ledge if they don't want to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T12:23:33-08:00","id":1475001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1474998#post1474998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is important for resonance to the Isolated Lair Trait? Is it the physical act of being alone, or is the feeling of Isolation sufficient? (ie can I use Nightmares to create resonance?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, as a quality of the location \u2014 you can't use Nightmares to impose the resonance, because Nightmares are an effect on a person instead of a place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does Immunity to Isolation entail? Never feeling Lonely again? </div> </div> </div>You can hang out in places that feel Isolating without it making you feel Isolated, and supernatural attempts to apply the effect get a +2 to resist (or the opportunity to Clash, in unresisted cases). By a similar token, immunity to Bad Angles would mean that those forms of architecture don't get into your head like they do everybody else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Similarly, what is important for resonance to Murmurs? Is the whispers of a crowd enough, or can the hallucination of whispers work? </div> </div> </div>Lair Traits are environmental qualities. Anything that isn't a quality of the environment (temporary or otherwise) accessible to the senses of more than one materially-aware person isn't going to provide resonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does imposing Bottomless in the Waking World drop people and stuff into the Lair? </div> </div> </div>Nope. Bottomless makes it so that if you lose your footing upon entering Chamber with it, you need to take two points of lethal damage to stop your fall, and then any Burrows you could take out of the Chamber from there go to a random Chamber. Imposing it outside of the Lair simply doesn't have any mechanical effect, because there's no Chamber people are entering to trigger the roll to see if they lose their footing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does Immunity to Bottomless grant Immunity to Fall Damage, or does it just allow a Beast to never fall off a Ledge if they don't want to? </div> </div> </div>Falling damage is different from the damage you take to stop a fall in a Bottomless location \u2014 if you were actually falling any length reasonable to describe as &quot;forever&quot; you'd take a lot more than two points of lethal damage. If you have the Trait, you can enter other Bottomless Chambers without having to roll to avoid falling.<br /> <br /> It's worth remembering that some Lair Traits, especially Major Lair Traits or the more unusual ones from the Player's Guide, exist more as internal hazards and modifiers than as sources of Environmental Immunity or things to impose on the material world generally \u2014 your Hoard isn't going to draw your Horror one Chamber closer to anything if you're just applying the Trait without opening a Primordial Pathway for minutes at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T13:09:09-08:00","id":1475003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1475001#post1475001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter, as a quality of the location \u2014 you can't use Nightmares to impose the resonance, because Nightmares are an effect on a person instead of a place.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah. I don\u2019t suppose that the modification Nightmares can change that? I could see a argument that The Walls Have Eyes attaches an effect to the environment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1475001#post1475001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can hang out in places that feel Isolating without it making you feel Isolated, and supernatural attempts to apply the effect get a +2 to resist (or the opportunity to Clash, in unresisted cases). By a similar token, immunity to Bad Angles would mean that those forms of architecture don't get into your head like they do everybody else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. Well, thanks to spirits, and resonance, locations that feel Isolating should be more common than in the real world. Is there or could there be a Obcasus rite that keeps a minor Lair Trait in existence for a while? Like blanketing a ritual space with fog or strong wind unnaturally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T13:33:43-08:00","id":1475006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1475003#post1475003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah. I don\u2019t suppose that the modification Nightmares can change that? I could see a argument that The Walls Have Eyes attaches an effect to the environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Walls Have Eyes attaches the effect of &quot;you have this Nightmare if you sleep in this place,&quot; which is not the environmental quality implied by the Isolated Lair Trait. Nightmares affect one person, or a little over a double-handful with Fear Is Contagious and the right steering \u2014 nothing about them changes what the environment is like from an objective perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm. Well, thanks to spirits, and resonance, locations that feel Isolating should be more common than in the real world. Is there or could there be a Obcasus rite that keeps a minor Lair Trait in existence for a while? Like blanketing a ritual space with fog or strong wind unnaturally? </div> </div> </div>This is, to varying degrees, the literal effect of the Secret Ways and Kingdom of Nightmares Obcasus Rites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-19-2022, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T03:12:09-08:00","id":1475631,"title":"","content":"Hello.<br /> How much dots could be a Merit for make to Inflict Nightmare outside of starving/ravenouse Condition?<br /> <br /> Another questione : on BPG what Is the sense of &quot; The rewards for journeying this far are great, however; by opening a Primordial Pathway back to their Lair in a soul realm, a Beast can deliberately target an individual for their Horror to feed from.&quot; ?<br /> <br /> The Horror can target the victim on another time ? Horror can exit from the Lair and team up with their partner Beast?<br /> The Beast could open a Primordial Pathway at -1 with the victim oneiros?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 03-01-2022, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T05:26:00-08:00","id":1475633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1475631#post1475631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another questione : on BPG what Is the sense of &quot; The rewards for journeying this far are great, however; by opening a Primordial Pathway back to their Lair in a soul realm, a Beast can deliberately target an individual for their Horror to feed from.&quot; ?<br /> <br /> The Horror can target the victim on another time ? Horror can exit from the Lair and team up with their partner Beast?<br /> The Beast could open a Primordial Pathway at -1 with the victim oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Horror will feed on that individual specifically when Inflicting Nightmares while they're within the range determined by the Beast's Lair rating and/or the hive, as opposed to a random person, and will continue to do so unless the Beast changes their Horror's target by spending a point of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T06:55:49-08:00","id":1475635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1475633#post1475633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horror will feed on that individual specifically when Inflicting Nightmares while they're within the range determined by the Beast's Lair rating and/or the hive, as opposed to a random person, and will continue to do so unless the Beast changes their Horror's target by spending a point of Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks You! About target an individual Oneiros, what are the prerequisit? Know the target a bit, and roll wits + resolve at -1?<br /> This passage was not very clear for me.<br /> Idem, for open a Primordial Pathway on material realm , at whatever location wanted.<br /> <br /> I misses something, doubt that Is so Easy pull off this stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T08:47:18-08:00","id":1475640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1475635#post1475635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks You! About target an individual Oneiros, what are the prerequisit? Know the target a bit, and roll wits + resolve at -1?<br /> This passage was not very clear for me.<br /> Idem, for open a Primordial Pathway on material realm , at whatever location wanted.<br /> <br /> I misses something, doubt that Is so Easy pull off this stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to make your way to their Oneiros through the Bright Dream, then open a Primordial Pathway from a part of their Oneiros that at least has a Theme matching one of your Lair Traits, if it doesn't match one of your Chambers descriptively, narratively, spiritually, or exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T15:46:02-08:00","id":1476233,"title":"","content":"So, here is...sort of a question. I'm trying to come up with custom made atavisms for Inguma, but I'm having trouble with getting or more like, understanding the mindset that I need to come of with something fitting for the Inguma, I look at the ones that we already have available and they sort of easy to see how they fit with the whole Inguma stick of the Other, they are beautiful done for the concept of the horror of what makes the Inguma scary, but when I try to look into making extra stuff, I get sort of brain blocked becaue I want it to be a good fit and I can't seem to move past what is already there.<br /> <br /> I tried making one about them making better tools and messing around with the tools, leaning on the connection of humanity and their tools, with the main draw of the effect being the ability to imbue items with atavism, blessing (dice bonus) and curses (curse condition) to wielding them or stealing them, and the ability to just shut down all equipment with a Disruption like effect, magical tools included, like some monsters mess up with technology or outright render useless by their presence.<br /> <br /> So, anyway to not go in a too long tangent, what other themes could I explore for the Inguma when coming up with goodies for them?<br /> <br /> Can you help me point me out to fitting inspiration for an Inguma monster to go look at their powers and how they are scary?<br /> <br /> Are there other threads that have discussed the inguma before? I searched them and got three hits among titles only and none were particularly deep or had much a discussion<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T16:28:55-08:00","id":1476237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476233#post1476233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here is...sort of a question. I'm trying to come up with custom made atavisms for Inguma, but I'm having trouble with getting or more like, understanding the mindset that I need to come of with something fitting for the Inguma, I look at the ones that we already have available and they sort of easy to see how they fit with the whole Inguma stick of the Other, they are beautiful done for the concept of the horror of what makes the Inguma scary, but when I try to look into making extra stuff, I get sort of brain blocked becaue I want it to be a good fit and I can't seem to move past what is already there.<br /> <br /> I tried making one about them making better tools and messing around with the tools, leaning on the connection of humanity and their tools, with the main draw of the effect being the ability to imbue items with atavism, blessing (dice bonus) and curses (curse condition) to wielding them or stealing them, and the ability to just shut down all equipment with a Disruption like effect, magical tools included, like some monsters mess up with technology or outright render useless by their presence.<br /> <br /> So, anyway to not go in a too long tangent, what other themes could I explore for the Inguma when coming up with goodies for them?<br /> <br /> Can you help me point me out to fitting inspiration for an Inguma monster to go look at their powers and how they are scary?<br /> <br /> Are there other threads that have discussed the inguma before? I searched them and got three hits among titles only and none were particularly deep or had much a discussion</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 maybe something that gives them inhuman or outright unnatural bodily functions, especially for organs etc? The visceral counterpart of Alien Mindset.<br /> <br /> Subverting a victim\u2019s online persona and digital identity looks nice, but no idea how that\u2019d translate to Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T18:00:20-08:00","id":1476244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476233#post1476233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here is...sort of a question. I'm trying to come up with custom made atavisms for Inguma, but I'm having trouble with getting or more like, understanding the mindset that I need to come of with something fitting for the Inguma, I look at the ones that we already have available and they sort of easy to see how they fit with the whole Inguma stick of the Other, they are beautiful done for the concept of the horror of what makes the Inguma scary, but when I try to look into making extra stuff, I get sort of brain blocked becaue I want it to be a good fit and I can't seem to move past what is already there.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> So, anyway to not go in a too long tangent, what other themes could I explore for the Inguma when coming up with goodies for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Inguma are fear of the stranger, paranoia, monsters who specifically look like \u2014 or can temporarily pass for \u2014 human. Their published Atavisms allow them to be inscrutable and make themselves look like familiar faces or create things that are indistinguishable from other people apart from their loyalty to the Beast. Their published Birthrights revolve around blending into a crowd and gaslighting victims with unretrievable messages and sudden appearances and disappearances to fixate on. Their perspective of the Dark Mother is an alien thing apart from the world, coordinating her Children through a pane of glass.<br /> <br /> Their foundational Nightmare originates with the first cities. Where the Namtaru shock through the unclean and the naturally unsettling \u2014 scaly things, sickly things, slimy things, things with too many legs \u2014 the Inguma reveal themselves through incongruous features. Where the Lurkers are built on fear of the unseen, the Outsiders come from the sense that <i>one of these things is not like the others.</i> They're the terror of a spot-the-difference picture and the opening that creates for their Hunger.<br /> <br /> Go for unpleasant surprises. Be a suspicious individual. Make Atavisms that let the Beast infiltrate, impersonate, misdirect, and otherwise <i>walk among us</i>. Hide damning evidence, reveal nasty complications, keep them on their toes without tipping your hand entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T02:18:08-08:00","id":1476266,"title":"","content":"So I would like a slight clarification of the Lore : can there be Actors and Dreamborn in the Primordial Dream? Or are they exclusive to the Tenemos/Oneiros, and Horrors are the only thing that live naturally there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T05:34:22-08:00","id":1476269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476244#post1476244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inguma are fear of the stranger, paranoia, monsters who specifically look like \u2014 or can temporarily pass for \u2014 human. Their published Atavisms allow them to be inscrutable and make themselves look like familiar faces or create things that are indistinguishable from other people apart from their loyalty to the Beast. Their published Birthrights revolve around blending into a crowd and gaslighting victims with unretrievable messages and sudden appearances and disappearances to fixate on. Their perspective of the Dark Mother is an alien thing apart from the world, coordinating her Children through a pane of glass.<br /> <br /> Their foundational Nightmare originates with the first cities. Where the Namtaru shock through the unclean and the naturally unsettling \u2014 scaly things, sickly things, slimy things, things with too many legs \u2014 the Inguma reveal themselves through incongruous features. Where the Lurkers are built on fear of the unseen, the Outsiders come from the sense that <i>one of these things is not like the others.</i> They're the terror of a spot-the-difference picture and the opening that creates for their Hunger.<br /> <br /> Go for unpleasant surprises. Be a suspicious individual. Make Atavisms that let the Beast infiltrate, impersonate, misdirect, and otherwise <i>walk among us</i>. Hide damning evidence, reveal nasty complications, keep them on their toes without tipping your hand entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was really helpful, thank you, first idea that came up with is the concept of a scapegoat atavism, Enemy Within is good for taking their place and with some work you can do the same thing, as in shifting the blame away from you, but I though, why not give the other guy the tells of a monster, hero tracking pings first on this poor guy, magical senses get spoofed and actually find evidence of this guy being the monster, while the Inguma watches or does his thing away from the spotlight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T06:48:57-08:00","id":1476271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476266#post1476266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I would like a slight clarification of the Lore : can there be Actors and Dreamborn in the Primordial Dream? Or are they exclusive to the Tenemos/Oneiros, and Horrors are the only thing that live naturally there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actors can be found within the Day, and the Unfettered haunt the hives and wider dreamscape, but full Dreamborn belong to the Bright Dream and the Mother's Land, per the BPG's &quot;Here There Be Monsters&quot; section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T03:11:17-07:00","id":1476830,"title":"","content":"New question, sorry: what happens to Beasts when Insatiable steal the entirety of their Lair? Are they possessed by the Insatiable? Do they just lose access to their Lair and/or Atavisms? Do they become prisonners of the Insatiable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T03:36:30-07:00","id":1476831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476830#post1476830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question, sorry: what happens to Beasts when Insatiable steal the entirety of their Lair? Are they possessed by the Insatiable? Do they just lose access to their Lair and/or Atavisms? Do they become prisonners of the Insatiable?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming there's no official answer after all; maybe a variant of the Slumbering Condition, where the abilities of opening Primordial Pathways, conjuring of/immunity to Lair Traits, Supernatural Tolerance, etc are sealed off instead of the Atavisms + Nightmares + Beast-Merits + Birthrights combo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T09:23:01-07:00","id":1476848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476830#post1476830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question, sorry: what happens to Beasts when Insatiable steal the entirety of their Lair? Are they possessed by the Insatiable? Do they just lose access to their Lair and/or Atavisms? Do they become prisonners of the Insatiable?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Beast who hits 0 Lair <i>dies. </i>It's the same as if someone struck the Horror down, or destroyed the Heart.<br /> <br /> The Insatiable enjoys a hearty serving of Lair that takes a little more time to digest before going to pick off another one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-21-2022, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T10:58:41-07:00","id":1476858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476848#post1476848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Beast who hits 0 Lair <i>dies. </i>It's the same as if someone struck the Horror down.<br /> <br /> The Insatiable enjoys a hearty serving of Lair that takes a little more time to digest before going to pick off another one.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Holy crap. So <i>that</i>'s why so many supplements talk of Insatiables eating Beasts. That ability is scarier than I thought.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot Arcane^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T11:12:09-07:00","id":1476859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476858#post1476858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... Holy crap. So <i>that</i>'s why so many supplements talk of Insatiables eating Beasts. That ability is scarier than I thought.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot Arcane^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The Insatiable are the manifest fact that everything eventually returns to nature, and that the stars and void hear stories and only understand the silences. Nothing is larger than their biosphere.<br /> <br /> (They are also the manifest reason people who build on that are assholes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T21:41:34-07:00","id":1476918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476830#post1476830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New question, sorry: what happens to Beasts when Insatiable steal the entirety of their Lair? Are they possessed by the Insatiable? Do they just lose access to their Lair and/or Atavisms? Do they become prisonners of the Insatiable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different take:<br /> <br /> Per the book, the Beast ceases to be the primary owner of the Lair until the Insatiable relinquishes control or is driven out; Subversion of Hunger is noted as a method best used when the Horror is, well, hungry, and the Insatiable begins the process by entering the Lair while the Horror is out.<br /> <br /> There's some real issues with clarity in the section that can probably be chalked up to the usual reasons re: Beast's early confusion, such as talk of entrances to the Lair or Beasts being spoken of interchangeably with their Horrors or the general vagueness of how the Primordial Dream works, but it's pretty definite that as-written having your Lair completely Subverted by an Insatiable doesn't kill you, because the consequences of that happening are specifically framed as temporary.<br /> <br /> By a similar token, Subverting a Lair is how the Insatiable steal Atavisms without using the &quot;steal Beast powers&quot; Esurient, and the specific consistent language of &quot;steal&quot; indicates the Beast loses access to a stolen Atavism, but the mechanics of stealing an Atavism without Your Power Is Mine are not described, although the Insatiable can keep a stolen Atavism until its Lair falls to 0.<br /> <br /> The general takeaway, then, in attempting to fit this together in a way that makes sense, is that the Horror may be deprived of as many as all of its Atavisms and its extra Attribute dots from Lair while the Insatiable maintains control of the Lair, but &quot;primary owner&quot; does not entail &quot;sole owner,&quot; such that the Beast can still access the Lair through Primordial Pathways and retains their Environmental Immunities \u2014 the Lair still exists and won't fade away when the Insatiable leaves it, so anything that isn't a direct function of the numerical rating can be safely kept while the Beast deals with the process of driving out the usurper of their holy hunting ground inside the head of humanity. (The Insatiable probable won't kill the Horror, because it's the only thing keeping the Lair from collapsing, but keeping it weak is one way to maintain dominance.)<br /> <br /> Possession is the bailiwick of the other type of Subversion, and the Insatiable's inability to lock their Satiety at Slumbering is one thing forcing them to leave the Lair to feed and making that come-back-every-day requirement have some teeth to it.<br /> <br /> So &quot;prisoner of the Insatiable&quot; is the closest, though the Insatiable doesn't have direct influence over the Beast in this way save through the leverage of likely having their Horror at its mercy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T02:36:55-07:00","id":1476936,"title":"","content":"Well... now I'm just more confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T09:29:48-07:00","id":1476973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476936#post1476936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... now I'm just more confused.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't worry about it. Satchel is just proposing a different option they can derive from the text. Essentially Satchel's is that an Insatiable stealing the Lair, and until it hits 0, the Lair doesn't cease to exist and the Beast would still have access to non-stolen powers and things that don't derive numerically like the ability to use your Lair to become immune to enviromental tilts (though I'm less sure as I recall text saying that the stolen Lair warps as a result of the Insatiable usurping it.) Though I'm not as sure on Satchel's as it sounds more like a discussion about what happens to a PC when this is their conflict vis a vis while the Insatiable is in the process of stealing the Lair and not what happens after your Lair hits 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T11:13:06-07:00","id":1476984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476973#post1476973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't worry about it. Satchel is just proposing a different option they can derive from the text. Essentially Satchel's is that an Insatiable stealing the Lair, and until it hits 0, the Lair doesn't cease to exist and the Beast would still have access to non-stolen powers and things that don't derive numerically like the ability to use your Lair to become immune to enviromental tilts (though I'm less sure as I recall text saying that the stolen Lair warps as a result of the Insatiable usurping it.) Though I'm not as sure on Satchel's as it sounds more like a discussion about what happens to a PC when this is their conflict vis a vis while the Insatiable is in the process of stealing the Lair and not what happens after your Lair hits 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> I'm sure no one is surprised when I say that Beast frequently lacks clear or fully coherent explanation. I ran my read off text regarding Beast from the main core and the consequences of directly attacking the Lair (and it's myriad parts) and backed it up with the nihilistic thematics at work around the Insatiable. Satchel worked backwards from what the Insatiable text said and supported it with the narrative control thematics around the Begotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T15:12:36-07:00","id":1477028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1476973#post1476973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry about it. Satchel is just proposing a different option they can derive from the text. Essentially Satchel's is that an Insatiable stealing the Lair, and until it hits 0, the Lair doesn't cease to exist and the Beast would still have access to non-stolen powers and things that don't derive numerically like the ability to use your Lair to become immune to enviromental tilts (though I'm less sure as I recall text saying that the stolen Lair warps as a result of the Insatiable usurping it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly it's just that the Insatiable don't mechanically possess Lair Traits or Environmental Immunities and turning the Beast's stage hazards against them at the furthest point of the Satiety scale from when that usually happens is a bit excessive, given that\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I'm not as sure on Satchel's as it sounds more like a discussion about what happens to a PC when this is their conflict vis a vis while the Insatiable is in the process of stealing the Lair and not what happens after your Lair hits 0. </div> </div> </div>\u2026it's not explicitly stated what becomes of the Beast after Subversion reduces their Lair to zero, but my read relies on the fact that it doesn't make a whole lot of sense to talk about the Beast driving the Insatiable out of the Lair as a way to make the Insatiable stop being the primary owner of the Lair if the Beast is killed by the process of Subversion.<br /> <br /> Subversion of Hunger steals Lair <i>dots</i>, not discrete Chambers, so even before the Insatiable has seized control of the last bit of the Lair it's still not limiting the Beast's movement within the Lair. The counterpart process to Subversion of Hunger results in the Beast being possessed by a primeval jackass for a number of hours after winnowing down the character's Presence and Composure; killing a Beast by taking over its hunting grounds in a way that requires daily reinforcement doesn't really match that in mechanical weight.<br /> <br /> Make no mistake, the Insatiable mechanics in Conquering Heroes are extremely messy, but they seem pretty clear, at least, that Subversion is a temporary process that shows off the Insatiable's ability to break boundaries in a particularly upsetting way, not a mechanical statement that it's a pity the Begotten didn't know when they started their game of murder that the Insatiable were playing, too (they have blunter instruments for that lesson).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T15:07:49-07:00","id":1479562,"title":"","content":"Hey guys got a question on insatiable topic.<br /> <br /> If a insatisble try to subvert a lair , he needs enter on it and face the lair traits right? He gets any form of help in doing this? Because i only found a power who gives then tilt imunity,but Burning major trait its not listed as a tilt, so what would probably happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T09:44:34-07:00","id":1480296,"title":"","content":"Lore question: How distinct are the Beast and her Horror as entities? My impression is that they are closer of being the same person than a Geist and his Sin-Eater, but I ended up in debates on the topic with other people. Feels appropriate to ask here for a third party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T17:15:20-07:00","id":1480326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1480296#post1480296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore question: How distinct are the Beast and her Horror as entities? My impression is that they are closer of being the same person than a Geist and his Sin-Eater, but I ended up in debates on the topic with other people. Feels appropriate to ask here for a third party.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast has the most personal connection to the Horror as a creature that lives inside the soul of all humanity after migrating upward from the soul of all existence. Its hunger is the Beast's hunger, and the only ways the two are separated without killing them both entail Inheritance.<br /> <br /> Identity gets fuzzy when it comes to the Astral, but the Horror was never a person and its relation to the Beast is not the Bargain of the Bound \u2014 the Heart wants what it wants, and the strength of that desire's inclination to fulfill itself is a function of how sated it already is. It's a hungry concept from the deep subconscious, and the fact that you share a subconscious with everyone else doesn't make it not <i>your</i> subconscious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T21:57:41-07:00","id":1480338,"title":"","content":"Short version: It's your id-shadow, and that your id-shadow blankets the countryside and so acts as all's shadows does not divorce it from the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T16:39:51-07:00","id":1487802,"title":"","content":"A two part question:<br /> <br /> Can a Beast use Primordial Pathways to follow a mummy who\u2019s heading to Duat after a Descent?<br /> <br /> And if so, could a Beast have a Chamber in Duat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:45:03-07:00","id":1487815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1487802#post1487802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Beast use Primordial Pathways to follow a mummy who\u2019s heading to Duat after a Descent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Duat is not a consistent world engaged with through game mechanics, I would say no, much the same as they can't follow a Prospect along on their Awakening into the Supernal World or a vampire into their torpor dreams.<br /> <br /> The Oneiros contains powerful memories like the dreams that form Chambers, and the Dreaming Roads are protean enough to justify being where attempts to access the Hedge through Primordial Pathways end up, but Duat isn't visited by anyone whose psyche participates in the Bright or Primordial Dreams.<br /> <br /> It's a timeless Hell whose residents use images of themselves to breach containment. Plot devices might allow it, but there's multiple layers of justification you'd have to go through to get there and then you wouldn't be able to get out, since you're not rolling for anything there, including attempts to open a Primordial Pathway back home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:54:18-07:00","id":1487817,"title":"","content":"Ok! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T12:16:04-07:00","id":1487927,"title":"","content":"Well, then....if a Beast accompanies an archmaster into a Lustrum, could the Beast form a Chamber either in the mage\u2019s Golden Path or in the Lustrum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T14:06:33-07:00","id":1487936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1487927#post1487927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, then....if a Beast accompanies an archmaster into a Lustrum, could the Beast form a Chamber either in the mage\u2019s Golden Path or in the Lustrum?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lustrum ceases to exist once the archmaster stops being able to sustain it and the circumstances required to form a Chamber still apply. The Golden Road is more persistent, but the same caveat about forming Chambers applies with the further addition of &quot;what Lair Traits are you going to hang Chamber formation off of in a space where there's basically nothing there but the exits?&quot;<br /> <br /> A Chantry would be a different story, because a Chantry is a proper world to some degree (being formed from a seed location not entirely unlike how Chambers are), but &quot;a shining pathway of Pneuma stretching through a darkened landscape that flickers with emotional color and flashes with spellcasting&quot; doesn't give much space for things to happen on compared to the worlds it provides access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T17:46:47-07:00","id":1487955,"title":"","content":"I imagine Void Moment Insatiable would find it rather comforting, a Golden Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T16:32:49-07:00","id":1488615,"title":"","content":"What is the \u201creach\u201d of an Apex? A city? A region? How do I define where one Apex\u2019s dominion in the Primordial Dream ends and another Apex\u2019s begins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T17:58:32-07:00","id":1488631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1488615#post1488615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the \u201creach\u201d of an Apex? A city? A region? How do I define where one Apex\u2019s dominion in the Primordial Dream ends and another Apex\u2019s begins?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Apex affects a hive, and a hive corresponds to a population center. That might translate to a metropolitan area or a borough or a town. A reasonable reading would probably be &quot;within the range that people consider a place with a discrete unifying cultural identity.&quot; New York City and Chicago and other major cities with large culturally-recognized subdivisions might have Apexes for separate boroughs or major neighborhoods, and &quot;the outskirts&quot; or &quot;the edge of town&quot; might be close enough to demarcate the borders of the hive within the larger dreamscape, but individual streets and entire counties alike are probably too small or large, respectively. Building A Legend has the shifting interface between the Apexes of Minnesota's Twin Cities as a story hook, and also dedicates its entire first chapter and a not-insignificant portion of its second chapter to talking about the region in which a chronicle takes place.<br /> <br /> Since hives are made from Chambers and Chambers come from the Bright Dream by way of people, it's going to be a fuzzier boundary than you might get in a game that didn't have &quot;no neat little boxes&quot; as a running theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T17:12:26-07:00","id":1489375,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to create and play new, nonmythological beasts of our own imagination? I've always been intrigued with the idea of Changeling the Lost's myriad Kiths and Deviant the Renegade's all-you-can-eat buffet of supernatural creatures. I keep thinking that it should be the same with Beast, but I can't help but feel that it's mostly limited to mythology-only creatures. I'm intrigued by the setting of Beast, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T17:24:44-07:00","id":1489376,"title":"","content":"Sure! I once made up an Ugallu whose Horror was an all-per asive surveillance system in his city-Lair, very Orwellian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T18:31:21-07:00","id":1489378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1489375#post1489375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to create and play new, nonmythological beasts of our own imagination? I've always been intrigued with the idea of Changeling the Lost's myriad Kiths and Deviant the Renegade's all-you-can-eat buffet of supernatural creatures. I keep thinking that it should be the same with Beast, but I can't help but feel that it's mostly limited to mythology-only creatures. I'm intrigued by the setting of Beast, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The line's fiction anthology includes a character whose Horror is a freaky thing with IV lines running down its arms, the line's Ready-Made Characters include a character whose Horror is a crumbling mass of soot and dirt, and the Introduction of the corebook outright says that Horrors run the gamut from storied monsters of legend to forgotten tales from dead cultures to modern inventions.<br /> <br /> A Beast is the human point of contact for a being that is equal parts local cryptid and manifest communal anxiety; the Horror takes its shape from the bits of human culture that have been springing up around traumatic contact with the supernatural and the baneful elements of the world itself. Sometimes that's a dragon, sometimes it's a gremlin, sometimes it's a weird nest of eyes and mouths, sometimes it's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungavenhooter\" target=\"_blank\">a big crocodile that catches you when you're drunk, thrashes you into mist, and inhales you</a>. A well-established Doylist audience isn't a precondition for a Horror's form, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fearsome_critters\" target=\"_blank\">lord knows</a> there's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jersey_Devil\" target=\"_blank\">been</a> some <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vegetable_Lamb_of_Tartary\" target=\"_blank\">weird stuff</a> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_legendary_creatures_by_type\" target=\"_blank\">folklore and mythology</a> before.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Nope, go nuts if you've got something you think you can spin into an interesting story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T12:35:35-08:00","id":1496727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1487407-badass-splat-boasts?p=1496669#post1496669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Tyrannical gods, the world itself a Lie? Distant Cousin, do not deny all that is dark as some external force of evil. It is as natural as the light. And the limits you overcome every day mean nothing without it&quot;- a Beast to a mage</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's weird for me to be asking this, because I'm me, but somehow, despite having a notion that Beasts might get caught up in Awakenings and wanting to explore that, and otherwise knowing that, for as invisible the Invisible Tyrants are, Exarchial influence and effect do have ready presence in the world that a Beast can nominally come across and know about, I actually haven't considered how they would actually approach the idea of the Lie and the Exarchs-and I'm at work, so I can't do any deep dive thinking on it until later today.<br /> <br /> So, to kickstart said thinking-uh, yeah, how do y'all think the Begotten interact with this view of reality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T16:04:24-08:00","id":1496752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1496727#post1496727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to kickstart said thinking-uh, yeah, how do y'all think the Begotten interact with this view of reality?</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019m not going to claim any particular insight into the Begotten mindset, but my initial feeling is that their response would be incredibly divided over the matter. Like, way worse than even Mages. As I understand, the Lie can be summarized as \u201cthis is all there is\u201d. The longer version might be \u201cThere isn\u2019t enlightenment, the world is fundamentally uncontrollable and unknowable, and you can\u2019t do anything make things better\u201d. There are going to be Horrors who internal story revolves around such themes. Heck, some might feed by inducing such concepts into people. And plenty do the opposite. And some will say \u201cok, so what?\u201d. Or only care about it when their Mage kin are around. And a good chunk just won\u2019t really understand. The most unified response probably will be a polite refusal to talk about the Lie, so as not to anger anyone in the Family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T17:47:44-08:00","id":1496761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1496727#post1496727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's weird for me to be asking this, because I'm me, but somehow, despite having a notion that Beasts might get caught up in Awakenings and wanting to explore that, and otherwise knowing that, for as invisible the Invisible Tyrants are, Exarchial influence and effect do have ready presence in the world that a Beast can nominally come across and know about, I actually haven't considered how they would actually approach the idea of the Lie and the Exarchs-and I'm at work, so I can't do any deep dive thinking on it until later today.<br /> <br /> So, to kickstart said thinking-uh, yeah, how do y'all think the Begotten interact with this view of reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy that quote got a reaction lol.<br /> <br /> I actually only came up with it in the spot, but I've always felt Beasts beliefs on it would range from &quot;the exarchs represent harsh Truths, much like us.&quot;, to &quot;the Lie is not a good thing...if you're human&quot; to &quot;disgustingly similar to the breach of agency heroes represent, except in a scale even we can't imagine&quot;<br /> <br /> One very real possibility I see, is that Beasts come to their understanding of mages through the Astral Aeons alongside interacting with mages. I think one reaction possible is that Beasts see the Arcana as a natural aspect of humanity and its place in the collective consciousness, and may see exarchal influence as an artifical stamping out of true enlightenment and self determinations Beasts may see themselves as representative of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh and of course, the viewpoint of the beast in the quote, that exarchal influence is really a natural consequence of human behavior (as they are invested in the Fallen, and the way ministries spread exarchal influence is ultimately with methods reflective of humanity as a whole, and thus reflected in the Astral and Primordial dream). That said, I am assuming this view with beast poijt of view bias AND lack of understanding as mages do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 11-10-2022, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T17:56:58-08:00","id":1496763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1496761#post1496761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Happy that quote got a reaction lol.<br /> <br /> I actually only came up with it in the spot, but I've always felt Beasts beliefs on it would range from &quot;the exarchs represent harsh Truths, much like us.&quot;, to &quot;the Lie is not a good thing...if you're human&quot; to &quot;disgustingly similar to the breach of agency heroes represent, except in a scale even we can't imagine&quot;<br /> <br /> One very real possibility I see, is that Beasts come to their understanding of mages through the Astral Aeons alongside interacting with mages. I think one reaction possible is that Beasts see the Arcana as a natural aspect of humanity and its place in the collective consciousness, and may see exarchal influence as an artifical stamping out of true enlightenment and self determinations Beasts may see themselves as representative of.</div> </div> </div> </div>It bugged me when I read it, and I was about to go &quot;Why would they disbelieve the idea of the Lie and the Exarchs or otherwise get defensive about it?&quot; and was about to just explain what was wrong with that-and then got stopped by realizing I had never actually thought about it and did not have a half-articulated response to flesh out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T20:22:15-08:00","id":1496775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1496763#post1496763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It bugged me when I read it, and I was about to go &amp;quot;Why would they disbelieve the idea of the Lie and the Exarchs or otherwise get defensive about it?&amp;quot; and was about to just explain what was wrong with that-and then got stopped by realizing I had never actually thought about it and did not have a half-articulated response to flesh out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Again, it was just a quote I thought of for coolness sake<br /> <br /> If I were to think on what has caused that Beast to view the Lie in such a way as complementary to itself. The Begotten's place in the world is as monsters born of humanity, to test them and reveal to them why their fears are tor good reason. The Lie and perhaps exarchs as the Begotten may see them, are born not of human fears, but of human evils. Evils that humanity can overcome, yet must understand as coming from their own souls. All said, this is strictly from a beast point of view. If I were to do a Cross-over I would focus on themes of self actualization between the splats, rather than questions regarding the state of humanity and relationship of those who Dreamed in the sleeping Lie to those of the supernal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T16:21:52-08:00","id":1498480,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a Beast to have the soul of small, ordinary creatures that would be considered mythological? For example, ravens and magpies, such as Odin's ravens Munnin and Huginn, and Apollo's white raven (which could be Ugallu?) Or could any ordinary creature be applicable since it's called <i>Beast</i>: The Primordial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T16:37:16-08:00","id":1498482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1498480#post1498480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a Beast to have the soul of small, ordinary creatures that would be considered mythological? For example, ravens and magpies, such as Odin's ravens Munnin and Huginn, and Apollo's white raven (which could be Ugallu?) Or could any ordinary creature be applicable since it's called <i>Beast</i>: The Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1489378#post1489378\">Same answer</a>. Cryptids run the gamut from bizarre to plain-but-famous, albeit with time they're bound to get a bit weird as the story picks up extra angles.<br /> <br /> Human imagination and anxiety mixed with the trend for spiritual power to correlate to Size and the Primordial Dream's ability to mess with a Horror's effective size for the purposes of navigating its own hunting grounds mean most Horrors will not actually be small \u2014 they're the same Size as their human counterparts, and even a Size 4 Small-Framed Horror is big enough to be menacing in its context \u2014 but Beasts can absolutely have Horrors whose horror doesn't come from overt supernatural qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T16:41:32-08:00","id":1498483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1498480#post1498480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a Beast to have the soul of small, ordinary creatures that would be considered mythological? For example, ravens and magpies, such as Odin's ravens Munnin and Huginn, and Apollo's white raven (which could be Ugallu?) Or could any ordinary creature be applicable since it's called <i>Beast</i>: The Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div>While there are no particular Atavisms that might mythologically take advantage of smallness (Well, Infestation a little bit), nothing precludes the Horror from being a small thing.<br /> <br /> People get a little hung up on &quot;game about mythological creatures&quot; in some ways. While dragons and phoenixes and giant squids are certainly on the list, the mythos extends beyond what we might consider fictional and into realms both historical and personal. The rat who bore the black plague, the cat you accidentally killed trying to help it, the eagle rendered icon for a highly troubled nation*-all of these are mytholgoical in their own ways, and so a Horror born from atavistic humanity may wear any of these faces.<br /> <br /> *If I ever get to do a section on Astral Gods as Beasts appraoch the subject, you can bet your bottom dollar I'm putting in the Imperial Eagle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T22:18:42-08:00","id":1503110,"title":"","content":"So, uh, guess this thread wasn't closed. That's neat. <br /> Unfortunately, this question is a kinda a rehash of a bunch of questions I've already asked. Kinda wish I had something more important to mark the occasion, but oh well.<br /> <br /> Would y'all consider it a valid use of the Skeleton Key power to pass through the Astral Barrier like a Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T22:55:28-08:00","id":1503111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1503110#post1503110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh, guess this thread wasn't closed. That's neat.<br /> Unfortunately, this question is a kinda a rehash of a bunch of questions I've already asked. Kinda wish I had something more important to mark the occasion, but oh well.<br /> <br /> Would y'all consider it a valid use of the Skeleton Key power to pass through the Astral Barrier like a Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. None?<br /> <br /> The general idea is that Skeleton Key works on Portals( For every lock, a key; for every door, a lock, for every key, a door), and the Astral Barrier (as the Astral Barrier, as opposed to the Astral Barrier as the Hedge) doesn't really have a Portal to work on. The main way that a Beasts cross it is by way of Primordial Pathway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T08:10:15-08:00","id":1504362,"title":"","content":"If Beasts A and B are in the same location, and B opens a Primordial Pathway to their Lair and thus fuse with their Horror, what happens to A? Do they remain in human form? Do they automatically assume Horror Form but do not benefit from their Lair Traits since they are in another Beast's Lair? And what happens after said Primordial Pathway closes? Assuming Beast A automatically assumes Horror Form, does A's Horror take a while to return to its Lair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T11:05:49-08:00","id":1504373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1504362#post1504362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Beasts A and B are in the same location, and B opens a Primordial Pathway to their Lair and thus fuse with their Horror, what happens to A? Do they remain in human form? Do they automatically assume Horror Form but do not benefit from their Lair Traits since they are in another Beast's Lair? And what happens after said Primordial Pathway closes? Assuming Beast A automatically assumes Horror Form, does A's Horror take a while to return to its Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Beast only merges with their Horror in their own Lair or a brood Lair that their Lair is part of. If Beast A does not share a brood Lair with Beast B, their Horror cannot leave their own Lair to reach them to merge with Beast A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T11:11:59-08:00","id":1504374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1504362#post1504362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Beasts A and B are in the same location, and B opens a Primordial Pathway to their Lair and thus fuse with their Horror, what happens to A? Do they remain in human form? Do they automatically assume Horror Form but do not benefit from their Lair Traits since they are in another Beast's Lair? And what happens after said Primordial Pathway closes? Assuming Beast A automatically assumes Horror Form, does A's Horror take a while to return to its Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do A and B share a Lair? If yes, then Beast A would assume their Horror's Form. If no, then they would remain human.<br /> <br /> Beast's only assume their Horror's Form when they are in their own Lair, and likewise their Lair traits only come in when available. THe most interesting cases are when a location has enough similarities to the two's Chambers that both could open a Pathway-the Beast who doesn't still isn't going to have their Horror's Form but can start daisy chaining in Lair Traits, but if both do, fun time o' clock is here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T12:32:31-07:00","id":1506517,"title":"","content":"Since Spirits do not have Virtues nor Vices, what does Eye of Heaven reveal as a substitute? Is there even a substitute? Would Eye of Heaven reveal an absence of Virtue and Vice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T14:10:35-07:00","id":1506530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1506517#post1506517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Spirits do not have Virtues nor Vices, what does Eye of Heaven reveal as a substitute? Is there even a substitute? Would Eye of Heaven reveal an absence of Virtue and Vice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since spirits get Willpower from gaining Essence through harvesting and theft, I'd say the Atavism tells you the spirit's Influences and/or that it's a spirit with the universal Vice of &quot;Essence.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T09:58:44-07:00","id":1508900,"title":"","content":"Ok, weird hypothetical time. If a Beast comes across the body of a Mage who is astrally jaunting, and thus currently not available for a conversation, what happens if the Beast uses a Nightmare on the person? Does it only affect the body? Or does the dream form of the mage suddenly get attacked by bugs or something from their perspective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:10:13-07:00","id":1509210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1508900#post1508900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, weird hypothetical time. If a Beast comes across the body of a Mage who is astrally jaunting, and thus currently not available for a conversation, what happens if the Beast uses a Nightmare on the person? Does it only affect the body? Or does the dream form of the mage suddenly get attacked by bugs or something from their perspective?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026my gut ruling is that the mage\u2019s mind isn\u2019t \u201cthere\u201d for the Nightmare to target, so it just wouldn\u2019t work. But I could see an argument that the mage\u2019s state is tantamount to dreaming, so it would have the same effect as triggering a Nightmare on a sleeping victim\u2026but honestly what that actually does has never been clear to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T10:42:44-07:00","id":1509215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1509210#post1509210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm\u2026my gut ruling is that the mage\u2019s mind isn\u2019t \u201cthere\u201d for the Nightmare to target, so it just wouldn\u2019t work. But I could see an argument that the mage\u2019s state is tantamount to dreaming, so it would have the same effect as triggering a Nightmare on a sleeping victim\u2026but honestly what that actually does has never been clear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the purpose of the question a thought experiment was to figure out what \u201clayer\u201d of reality Nightmares affect. For example, does targeting the mage\u2019s body have the effect happen to them in the astral? Does that mean Behold, My True Form! can kill the dream form from the body? Or if it only targets the body, does the body take the damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T13:32:44-07:00","id":1513227,"title":"","content":"Can a Collector steal in abstract ways and gain Satiety? Some examples of what I mean:<br /> <br /> 1: A serial homewrecker that feeds from the fear of being cheated on (Stealing another person's lover/spouse)<br /> 2: A Beast that forces established powers to serve them (Stealing Power from established rulers)<br /> 3: Absorbing other supernaturals' territories into yours (Stealing territory/land)<br /> 4: Forcing others to serve them (Stealing freedom)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T14:15:55-07:00","id":1513231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1513227#post1513227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Collector steal in abstract ways and gain Satiety? Some examples of what I mean:<br /> <br /> 1: A serial homewrecker that feeds from the fear of being cheated on (Stealing another person's lover/spouse)<br /> 2: A Beast that forces established powers to serve them (Stealing Power from established rulers)<br /> 3: Absorbing other supernaturals' territories into yours (Stealing territory/land)<br /> 4: Forcing others to serve them (Stealing freedom)</div> </div> </div> </div>The sum answer is found on pg. 38 of the core:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast: the Primordial, pg. 38</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though every Collector hungers for physical things, hoards vary drastically from Beast to Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>To address what these actually are.<br /> <br /> 1. This is more likely a case of the Hunger of Power (taking another's person's partner as an assertion of social dominance), Ruin (the destruction of the trust the partnership is founded on), Secrets (for the cheating partner trying to have it both ways by not being honest about), or Transgression (also for the cheating partner in crossing the line of the trust they established).<br /> 2. Clearly Hunger for Power.<br /> 3. This one can fall under the Hunger for Hoard. It also works as an expression of Power, and certain expressions of Punishment.<br /> 4. Power, as it's stated, and Punishment again under certain expressions. Kidnapping people as a disruption to the security of targets by way of their social circles/expressions of power and dominance could fall under Hoard, though-early drafts even included the dragon kidnapping fair maidens as an example until enough consensus was put up that it was kind of a &quot;yikes&quot; example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:38:58-07:00","id":1513327,"title":"","content":"1. Do humans with supernatural merits count as kin?<br /> <br /> 2. Do sorcerers from Mummy the Cursed count as kin?<br /> <br /> 3. Do non-sapient supernaturals (Maniticores, Ghouled Animals, Humanity 0 Vampires etc.) count as kin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:09:26-07:00","id":1513329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1513327#post1513327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Do humans with supernatural merits count as kin?<br /> <br /> 2. Do sorcerers from Mummy the Cursed count as kin?<br /> <br /> 3. Do non-sapient supernaturals (Maniticores, Ghouled Animals, Humanity 0 Vampires etc.) count as kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) As a general rule, yes. Certain merits like Cursed give me pause, but the grand majority absolutely count.<br /> 2) This is one of those interesting cases where the questions of &quot;Does knowledge of how to make a supernatural thing happen make one magical?&quot; needs to be addressed, but given that the Ritual Sorcerer Merit grants resistance to Sybaris and the ability to interpret Sybaratic Omens innately, this pretty firmly makes them Kin.<br /> 3) Yep. How a Beast might take advantage of that Family Tie with the barrier of non-sapiency is another subject, but the metaphysics are in place (thank god for the &quot;Horror's are World Soul Dreamborn stewed in Humanity's Soul&quot; clarification).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T22:07:27-07:00","id":1514548,"title":"","content":"Ok, so when Beast came out it had some rules for the Begotten in the Hedge....but that was 1st edition Changeling's Hedge. <br /> Essentially it said Beasts could Hedgespin using their Lair as the dicepool. But Hedgespinning doesn't work that way anymore. <br /> <br /> So how does it work now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T07:55:45-07:00","id":1514576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1514548#post1514548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so when Beast came out it had some rules for the Begotten in the Hedge....but that was 1st edition Changeling's Hedge.<br /> Essentially it said Beasts could Hedgespin using their Lair as the dicepool. But Hedgespinning doesn't work that way anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that most of the 1e rules referenced amounted to ease of tracking based on the cosmetic effects, it's practical to say that that under 2e's rules the Begotten provide the same tracking bonus to fae creatures as a changeling with Wyrd equal to their Lair and that the Hedge's own Hedgespinning tends to reflect the Beast's Family and Hunger. Between that, Lair Traits, and Primordial Pathways, a well-established Beast asserting dominance over the local Hedge can pretty well manage to do as the Lost do.<br /> <br /> (The referenced paragraph starting with &quot;can warp the psychoactive landscape of the Hedge by their very presence&quot; and then saying that high-Lair Beasts might find cosmetic reflections of their Atavisms leaking into physical reality indicates to me that that mechanic is largely meant to be referencing the unconscious influence describe in Shaping The Hedge rather than a Hedgespinning analogue.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T11:42:27-07:00","id":1517508,"title":"","content":"Questions about people's readings of the Alien Mindset atavism from the Player's Guide:<br /> <br /> The Normal Effect: the description says the penalty applies to supernatural abilities, but that they provoke a Clash of Wills. Does this mean that the Beast has to win the Clash before the penalty will apply to the incoming effect? Or that any such effects have to beat the Best in the Clash to take effect at all (and still suffer the penalty if they win?)? The former reading seems the most plausible to me, but also the more mechanically dubious.<br /> <br /> The Low Satiety Effect: is the second Legend locked in when the Beast acquires the atavisim? The word &quot;malleable&quot; suggests otherwise, but doesn't specify a criteria when/how the secondary Legend can change. My guess would be that they pick the secondary Legend anew each time they reach Low Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T12:04:53-07:00","id":1517510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1517508#post1517508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Normal Effect: the description says the penalty applies to supernatural abilities, but that they provoke a Clash of Wills. Does this mean that the Beast has to win the Clash before the penalty will apply to the incoming effect? Or that any such effects have to beat the Best in the Clash to take effect at all (and still suffer the penalty if they win?)? The former reading seems the most plausible to me, but also the more mechanically dubious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also read it as the former, given that the latter would be the reading I would make if the effect was &quot;attempts automatically fail&quot; instead of &quot;attempts suffer a penalty.&quot; Basically a supernatural effect Clashes with the persistent Atavism to determine whether it rolls with a penalty, and then if it fails that penalty makes it more likely for them to fail (or dramatically fail and become Confused).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Low Satiety Effect: is the second Legend locked in when the Beast acquires the atavisim? The word &quot;malleable&quot; suggests otherwise, but doesn't specify a criteria when/how the secondary Legend can change. My guess would be that they pick the secondary Legend anew each time they reach Low Satiety. </div> </div> </div>My reading aligns with your guess here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T12:49:53-07:00","id":1517514,"title":"","content":"What hunger and family would best represent a beast who represents the fear of ridicule/mockery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T16:24:33-07:00","id":1517521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1517514#post1517514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What hunger and family would best represent a beast who represents the fear of ridicule/mockery?</div> </div> </div> </div>At a first glance, Ugallu for me. Being exposed to ridicule by a literal Mocking-bird.<br /> <br /> Hunger would need a more specific image of what the Beast in question is like, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T19:58:02-07:00","id":1517531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1517521#post1517521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At a first glance, Ugallu for me. Being exposed to ridicule by a literal Mocking-bird.<br /> <br /> Hunger would need a more specific image of what the Beast in question is like, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea I was having would be a person who's good at psychoanalyzing people and pushing their buttons. Their favorite targets would be boastful people, ESPECIALLY ones that like to make themselves seem greater or more important than they are. Some examples of how they would feed would be exposing a pseudo-intellectual's stupidity, making a respected leader look like a buffoon, or heckling a mocker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T20:09:46-07:00","id":1517532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1517531#post1517531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea I was having would be a person who's good at psychoanalyzing people and pushing their buttons. Their favorite targets would be boastful people, ESPECIALLY ones that like to make themselves seem greater or more important than they are. Some examples of how they would feed would be exposing a pseudo-intellectual's stupidity, making a respected leader look like a buffoon, or heckling a mocker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm. Gonna have to be more specific on <b>why</b> the Beast does all that, but at a glance that sounds like a Nemesis or Enabler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T20:18:54-07:00","id":1517533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1517532#post1517532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmm. Gonna have to be more specific on <b>why</b> the Beast does all that, but at a glance that sounds like a Nemesis or Enabler.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Horror represents the fear of mockery/ridicule, which the beast fulfills by humiliating arrogant people. They're preferred targets are powerful people, but when hungry anyone who's too full of themselves can do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T22:13:17-07:00","id":1517537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1517533#post1517533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe Horror represents the fear of mockery/ridicule, which the beast fulfills by humiliating arrogant people. They're preferred targets are powerful people, but when hungry anyone who's too full of themselves can do</div> </div> </div> </div>Power and Secrets(if the mockery is rooted in real facets of the victim) are the obvious ones. Ruin's a stretch, but in the same way killing a pillar of the community could satisfy, arguably a community that relies on the reputation of an individual could be devastated enough that it could satisfy it.<br /> <br /> That said, I think someone needs to mention that the idea of rooting a Horror in <i>just</i> mockery and ridicule is a little weak, so here's me doing that. A Social Tyrant isn't just going to mock and ridicule, they're going to destroy a person's reputation viscerally and violently. A Whisper isn't going to just mock and jape, they're going to make the victim's whole picture painfully obvious to absolutely the wrong people. The Ravager take basically demands that you can't stop on the concept.<br /> <br /> Beasts and their Horrors tap into deeper senses of displacement and existential angst, on the psychological angle, rather than simple discomfort or jump scares-it's a factor that separates them from the Autumn Court and Nosferatu, who can engage with both ends of the depth scale but don't have to and certainly don't need to connect the two dots. Mockery and ridicule are preludes towards the idea that something shameful and horrible about the victim is always going to leak out, or that something about the victim means they're always going to invite this sort of response, that these things, valid or not, are always going to tear them down and will always create rifts between them, others, and their own sense of self-worth. As a prelude, that can apply to a lot of things-I think the Ugallu are the best fit, but you could make a case of the Anakim, the Namtaru, and the Talasii as well-and the fact that's true indicates you might wanna dig more into what it is about the idea of mockery and ridicule an angle you want to explore fear and the way they can destroy a person's sense of security before trying to build a Horror around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T15:19:20-07:00","id":1518327,"title":"","content":"Am I right that passive \u201cfeedings\u201d, such as ephemeral entities gaining Essence from spending a day in an appropriate Condition, aren\u2019t generally going to be suitable for Family Dinner?<br /> <br /> I was thinking about how having Family Ties with a ghost would be nifty, but necrophagia seems like the only decent candidate for Family Dinner they have. And finding other ghosts for them to chew on sounds like more trouble than it\u2019s worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T17:14:20-07:00","id":1518333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1518327#post1518327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right that passive \u201cfeedings\u201d, such as ephemeral entities gaining Essence from spending a day in an appropriate Condition, aren\u2019t generally going to be suitable for Family Dinner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, on account of that being neither hunting nor feeding \u2014 its closest equivalent is Astral beings regaining Essence for being in the Astral, which, given that &quot;you have Dreamborn in your Lair&quot; is a Lair Trait, should be all the evidence one needs even without the alternative example of being around a Promethean when the sun rises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking about how having Family Ties with a ghost would be nifty, but necrophagia seems like the only decent candidate for Family Dinner they have. And finding other ghosts for them to chew on sounds like more trouble than it\u2019s worth. </div> </div> </div>You'd want to angle for ectophagia, deliberate incitement of remembrance, or the Memory trade, or else lean on Vice for the narrative beats Family Dinner relies on, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T19:57:04-07:00","id":1522731,"title":"","content":"I'm not the most familiar with Beast but I saw an idea on Reddit and wanted to know if it fit how Beast works. The idea is someone who either pulls other people into another realm or who lures them into the other realm. The other realm is designed like a wrestling arena and the character is a professional wrestler. Could that work for a Beast and it's lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T06:49:37-07:00","id":1522791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1522731#post1522731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the most familiar with Beast but I saw an idea on Reddit and wanted to know if it fit how Beast works. The idea is someone who either pulls other people into another realm or who lures them into the other realm. The other realm is designed like a wrestling arena and the character is a professional wrestler. Could that work for a Beast and it's lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics wise it can be done easily enough, there are merits and lair traits that allow for it, Bottomless lair trait for example at the top of my head, trap door merit I think it was called, Sealed exit so they can't escape the fighting arena, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T10:35:03-08:00","id":1525565,"title":"","content":"Is it mentioned in any book if the Dark Mother and the God-Machine have some kind of rivalry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T13:24:09-08:00","id":1525570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1525565#post1525565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it mentioned in any book if the Dark Mother and the God-Machine have some kind of rivalry?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not, beyond the Unchained's origins with the Machine being the attributed reason why Family Resemblance interacts with their nature as it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T15:59:15-08:00","id":1527579,"title":"","content":"What exactly is different for a whisper beast from a secret collector? Was it just a continuity error or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T18:35:54-08:00","id":1527586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1527579#post1527579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is different for a whisper beast from a secret collector? Was it just a continuity error or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the explicit statement that the default assumption is that Collectors take physical things for their Hoard, a Whisper reveals to their victim that they know about a lie they've told or a secret they thought was secure. A Collector of nonphysical things <i>steals those things.</i><br /> <br /> Setting aside the possibility that Nancy from the corebook could be an artifact of the revision process that slipped through the cracks, the explicit function of her Hunger is to <i>have privileged knowledge</i> rather than to <i>be poised to commit blackmail</i>. There's overlap between those things, but for Whispers the point is that the victim knows their secret isn't safe and for Collectors the point is that a person/monster that takes things has taken something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T09:11:49-08:00","id":1528595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1527579#post1527579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is different for a whisper beast from a secret collector? Was it just a continuity error or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collectors keep what they collect, whisper reveal the secrets they collect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28231-thenightmarechild","name":"TheNightmareChild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T19:12:01-08:00","id":1530001,"title":"","content":"How does Beast make Other Supernatual Trust them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-04T21:11:35-08:00","id":1530004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1530001#post1530001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Beast make Other Supernatual Trust them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same ways people make other people trust them. Being competent and reliable and helpful goes a long way, as does keeping confidence with regards things they can't talk with other people about and otherwise signaling that they belong to the same in-group. Thicker Than Water offers a foot in the door for this, and the way Family Dinner works further incentivizes the Begotten to do what they can to ensure their kin can be fed without needless complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T01:04:44-08:00","id":1530010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1530001#post1530001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Beast make Other Supernatual Trust them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being useful, the more the better, having common interests or similarities in each person's situation also helps depending on the case and obviously not being a risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T09:47:24-08:00","id":1531363,"title":"","content":"A not so simple question, how diverse can beasts be? From the descriptions, many look like creatures from legends or large animals and some even look like something mechanical, but could they take on other appearances, like macabre toys? beings that resemble weapons? or military vehicles? They don't have to be big, they can be small but terrifying creatures too? Maybe even made up of a swarm, like a humanoid made up of several smaller insects? Could they have multiple heads? Do they look like a cartoon like Toon Cat? What is their limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T11:12:40-08:00","id":1531368,"title":"","content":"They can be as diverse as mankind's nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T13:14:27-08:00","id":1531378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1531363#post1531363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A not so simple question, how diverse can beasts be? From the descriptions, many look like creatures from legends or large animals and some even look like something mechanical, but could they take on other appearances, like macabre toys? beings that resemble weapons? or military vehicles? They don't have to be big, they can be small but terrifying creatures too? Maybe even made up of a swarm, like a humanoid made up of several smaller insects? Could they have multiple heads? Do they look like a cartoon like Toon Cat? What is their limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1489378#post1489378\">come up</a> a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1498482#post1498482\">couple times</a> before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T03:26:14-08:00","id":1532281,"title":"","content":"Horrorspawn can also use something like a statue or a car as a physical body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T06:18:57-08:00","id":1532287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1532281#post1532281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horrorspawn can also use something like a statue or a car as a physical body?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Physical Form&quot; seems to indicate that without a rite to form something out of the Dream the things the Horrorspawn can inhabit are living or dead bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T15:56:19-07:00","id":1532457,"title":"","content":"I know specific numbers of monsters tends to get verboten, but in general how big of a population do you think a beast needs to be able to successfully hide? And does it scale straight, like 1 beast needs X population and 2 beasts need 2X or is it more of a curve after the first where maybe 2 beasts only need 1.7X?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T18:04:59-07:00","id":1532463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1532457#post1532457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know specific numbers of monsters tends to get verboten, but in general how big of a population do you think a beast needs to be able to successfully hide? And does it scale straight, like 1 beast needs X population and 2 beasts need 2X or is it more of a curve after the first where maybe 2 beasts only need 1.7X?</div> </div> </div> </div>This varies because the larger a beast's lair, the faster it loses satiety and the more frequently it feeds and depending on the method, it doesn't even need humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T19:26:09-07:00","id":1532472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1532457#post1532457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know specific numbers of monsters tends to get verboten, but in general how big of a population do you think a beast needs to be able to successfully hide? And does it scale straight, like 1 beast needs X population and 2 beasts need 2X or is it more of a curve after the first where maybe 2 beasts only need 1.7X?</div> </div> </div> </div>Framing in terms of what kind of population numbers are needed to hide is tricky for the simple reason that beasts have more methods of feeding that aren't obviously supernatural than ones that are; even without accounting for Family Dinner or discounting the fact that the Horror doesn't have any innate visual connection to the beast to make the victims of the nightmares it spreads at low Satiety draw a connection between the two, normal feeding being achievable through mundane activities means comparison to criminal enterprises is about as close as one is likely to get.<br /> <br /> The breadth of Hungers and hunting/feeding kin further complicates matters, because how renewable the resources a feeding taps are will vary and that in turn may or may not make it impossible for two or more beasts to peacefully coexist. The Begotten are relatively rare and the Devouring has no guarantees for Family or Hunger, and collaboration helps keep everyone's Satiety up for practical reasons, but if two different Nemeses both have the same favorite flavor and can't stand each other that puts a bit of potential strain on the table that doesn't exist between a Tyrant and a Collector with a bet-your-life's-work-on-this-fight racket.<br /> <br /> Baseline assumption would be &quot;enough of a population for a person to hide chronic criminal activity in,&quot; modified further by circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T13:20:23-07:00","id":1535493,"title":"","content":"Does the Scaly Hide option of ther Skin Deep atavism works like ballistic armor by downgrading lethal damage while it is being inflicted, or does it continually downgrade damage that has been inflicted previously, like a form of regeneration?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-12T18:25:14-07:00","id":1535499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1535493#post1535493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Scaly Hide option of ther Skin Deep atavism works like ballistic armor by downgrading lethal damage while it is being inflicted, or does it continually downgrade damage that has been inflicted previously, like a form of regeneration?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's named for a surface feature and if it worked like regeneration it would be better than the Atavism whose primary effect is regeneration. &quot;Downgrade&quot; is pretty clearly being used in the same sense as it's used in the Iron Skin and Iron Skin (Advanced) Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T01:54:39-07:00","id":1535548,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks.<br /> Other question: Could a Legendary Horror become a werewolf's or werewolf's pack's totem? Perhaps using the Usurp Numina? What about an Unfettered Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T04:44:01-07:00","id":1535552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1535548#post1535548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other question: Could a Legendary Horror become a werewolf's or werewolf's pack's totem? Perhaps using the Usurp Numina? What about an Unfettered Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1506138-unique-totems?p=1506419#post1506419\">You could try to set something up, but Legendary Horror doesn't exactly help on that front.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T21:50:13-08:00","id":1546625,"title":"","content":"Does Beast need to eat normal food? Or can they survive using their Hunger system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T22:42:09-08:00","id":1546627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1546625#post1546625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Beast need to eat normal food? Or can they survive using their Hunger system?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the Low Satiety effect of Relentless Hunter suspends the character's need for food, drink, and rest as long as they are actively pursuing a Satiety increase seems a very direct implication that they do not have the ability to sustain themselves on fear alone by default, to say nothing of there being no such quality described in the overall description of what innate abilities one gets from simply being a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T03:41:06-08:00","id":1546633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1546625#post1546625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Beast need to eat normal food? Or can they survive using their Hunger system?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Satchel said, but merits can modify this (like Sanguivore on player guide)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T17:44:36-08:00","id":1546669,"title":"","content":"Does Beast have any Nightmare from a Kinship with Hunter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T20:57:33-08:00","id":1546673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1546669#post1546669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Beast have any Nightmare from a Kinship with Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most hunters are just ordinary humans and therefore cannot have the Family Ties necessary to develop Kinship Nightmares, which is the probable reason there are no published Kinship Nightmares directly based on hunters.<br /> <br /> The corebook and the Player's Guide both provide advice for developing your own Kinship Nightmares, which are as applicable to a suitable hunter as they are to a psychic or medium (which fall under the &quot;Fundamentally Human&quot; subset of Kinship), and you likewise might use such a hunter as the basis for learning a published Kinship Nightmare whose direct inspiration comes from something else with a similar power or thematic root.<br /> <br /> Without some sort of unnatural power or quality to them like the Lucifuge have, though, a run-of-the-mill person whose distinguishing connection to the supernatural is being on the Vigil isn't going to be enough of a monster for the Begotten to start playing copycat with their narrative beats until they die and leave behind a ghost, lose the last of their Integrity and become a slasher, or otherwise gain supernatural powers that can shake the Integrity of normal people's self-concept and understanding of the world to see in reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T21:45:05-08:00","id":1546677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1546673#post1546673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most hunters are just ordinary humans and therefore cannot have the Family Ties necessary to develop Kinship Nightmares, which is the probable reason there are no published Kinship Nightmares directly based on hunters.<br /> <br /> The corebook and the Player's Guide both provide advice for developing your own Kinship Nightmares, which are as applicable to a suitable hunter as they are to a psychic or medium (which fall under the &quot;Fundamentally Human&quot; subset of Kinship), and you likewise might use such a hunter as the basis for learning a published Kinship Nightmare whose direct inspiration comes from something else with a similar power or thematic root.<br /> <br /> Without some sort of unnatural power or quality to them like the Lucifuge have, though, a run-of-the-mill person whose distinguishing connection to the supernatural is being on the Vigil isn't going to be enough of a monster for the Begotten to start playing copycat with their narrative beats until they die and leave behind a ghost, lose the last of their Integrity and become a slasher, or otherwise gain supernatural powers that can shake the Integrity of normal people's self-concept and understanding of the world to see in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't the Core Rule Book say that if a Hunter were to go on a hunt in the Primodial Dream, that they could be counted as Kin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T05:15:25-08:00","id":1546685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1546677#post1546677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't the Core Rule Book say that if a Hunter were to go on a hunt in the Primodial Dream, that they could be counted as Kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as anything more than speculation and hearsay:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP Core Rulebook, Page 228</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But where vampires and witches and their ilk share a common descent from the Dark Mother, hunters are by and large pure human. <b>Even hunters with surgical augmentation, such as the Cheiron Group\u2019s Thaumatechnology, or induced psychic phenomena, like VASCU\u2019s telepathic agents, aren\u2019t inherently monstrous enough to count as anything but human. That largely bars them from forming Kinship bonds and fully joining a Brood \u2014 at least without drastic actions.</b> Beasts tell stories of dream-quests and sacred hunts deep into the Primordial Dream that awaken just enough of a human\u2019s Bestial aspect to become Kin to Beasts. Hunters with Endowments stemming from their bloodline, like the Lucifuge, can form Kinship bonds without the ordeal \u2014 and more disturbingly, so can slashers, even if they were born as bog-standard normal humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T06:21:47-08:00","id":1547197,"title":"","content":"What are the rules you use when Merging with your Horror? The paragraph about it in the corebook is... frustratingly vague, only explaining how Atavisms and Nightmares function. Mostly I wish to ask the followings specifically:<br /> * Do you use the Dream Form rules (and thus calculate Health based on Lair), or Physical rules (and thus calculate Health based on Size?) And if the former, what purpose does increasing Size serve?<br /> * Can you use Skills along with your Horror's Attributes while merged with your Horror?<br /> * Are you permanently in monster form or can you shift between human and Horror form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-23T09:20:21-08:00","id":1547201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1547197#post1547197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Do you use the Dream Form rules (and thus calculate Health based on Lair), or Physical rules (and thus calculate Health based on Size?)</div> </div> </div> </div>While you are merged with your Horror, you use its Dream Health and the most severe damage on the two of you is used, healing separately accordingly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if the former, what purpose does increasing Size serve? </div> </div> </div>Multiple Anakim-affinity Atavisms reference the character's Size for effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Can you use Skills along with your Horror's Attributes while merged with your Horror? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Are you permanently in monster form or can you shift between human and Horror form? </div> </div> </div>Unless you are Slumbering or otherwise prevented from merging with your Horror, you stay merged with your Horror until you leave your Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T05:05:16-07:00","id":1552302,"title":"","content":"How does the &quot;You Must Obey&quot; Nightmare actually make people obey? It says it causes a Breaking Point if the victim doesn't obey, but is the choice between obedience and facing the Breaking Point something the victim is aware of, or does it just happen with no warning if they ignore an order?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T07:01:30-07:00","id":1552303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873180-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-beast-edition?p=1552302#post1552302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the &quot;You Must Obey&quot; Nightmare actually make people obey? It says it causes a Breaking Point if the victim doesn't obey, but is the choice between obedience and facing the Breaking Point something the victim is aware of, or does it just happen with no warning if they ignore an order?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that breaking points are also how the Vinculum works in Requiem 2e, it's safe to say the Nightmare imposes an understanding that disobeying the order is in the same broad category of Bad Idea as committing murder or willingly sitting down to be tortured \u2014 not done lightly and requiring the demands of the Nightmare to contradict one's sense of self-preservation to more easily override.<br /> <br /> It would also be very weird for You Must Obey, a power that puts a perceptual/emotional payload from the Primordial Dream into someone's head, to allow a Beast to expand their Lair by triggering it on a target who then casually ignores whatever the Beast tells them to do. Breaking points are narratively significant and the fiction reflects this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T23:40:42-07:00","id":1552352,"title":"","content":"Overall, anything related to Breaking Points, Virtue, Vice and Aspirations should be intuitively understood by the character, always.<br /> <br /> Those mechanics don't punish or reward behavior out of the blue. It isn't so much that the character is aware of them (they're not in an objective sense), but that they represent the psychological/emotional state of the character at any given time.<br /> <br /> If something is a Vice, the character is attracted to doing it. If something is a Virtue, the character feels that's the person they'd like to be. If something is an Aspiration, the character feels it's a worthy goal. If something is a Breaking Point, the character feels a strong revulsion by the imminent thought of actually doing it (which isn't to say they're against it as a pure conjecture, just as most people feel enough anger to desire someone else dead in from time to time, but won't really be able to commit murder without terrible trauma).<br /> <br /> What's the secret here is to understand those are feelings, hence them being mechanics for psychological reward/punishment. But yes, while the character doesn't know how this works mechanically, it does represent their emotional state and tendency to behave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}